/-
RSX LOWER — the reference lowering rsx → scm (hole 14, plan/PHASE1-BOUNDARY.md §14,
"lower: rsx -> scm (erasure, then defunctionalization, then fuel)"), its `#guard`
controls, and the per-construct adequacy statements.

Pipeline (each stage a total, executable, fueled definition; `Rsx.Lower.lowerF`):

  1. erasure       `Expr Nat → LExpr`   types, type formers and proofs become `□`
                                         (`LExpr.box`); binder types are dropped;
                                         transparent constants are unfolded (δ) and
                                         their bodies erased in the empty context.
  2. defunctionalization `LExpr → DExpr × List Code`  every λ becomes a first-order
                                         closure record `clo ℓ [captured]` and every
                                         application an `apply` node; `Code ℓ` is the
                                         λ's body over `arg :: captured` (flat closures).
  3. fuel          `run : List Code → Nat → …`  the first-order `apply` loop of the
                                         defunctionalized program, made total by fuel
                                         (fuel-out is `none`, never a value).
  4. emission      `DVal → BootExpr S G t`  the value is emitted at the requested scm
                                         type `t` (literal → `litI`, constructor →
                                         `inj ⟨ref⟩ (list fields)`, erased fields
                                         dropped); anything not representable at `t`
                                         is the refusing expression `unwrapSome noneE`
                                         (evaluates to `none`).

`Rsx.lower E : Expr Nat → BootExpr S [] t` is `lowerF E 0 defaultFuel t`.

Partial definitions (step 5, semantics/Rsx/Partial.rsd): erasure takes a global table
`gi`; a partial constant becomes `LExpr.glob i` / `DExpr.glob i`, resolved by `run` from
code entry `i` at one fuel tick per resolution, never inlined. The total lowering passes
`noGlobals`, so it never produces `glob` (`Rsx.Partial.lowerPF_nil`).

Sources (PREAMBLE item 7: ported, not invented):
- Erasure: P. Letouzey, "A New Extraction for Coq", TYPES 2002, LNCS 2646 — the `□`
  translation of the logical and type-level parts of CIC terms (the informative test:
  a term is erased when its type is an arity or its type's type is `Prop`).
  M. Sozeau, S. Boulier, Y. Forster, N. Tabareau, T. Winterhalter, "Coq Coq Correct!
  Verification of Type Checking and Erasure for Coq, in Coq", POPL 2020 — MetaCoq's
  `erase` (same test, `tBox`) and its correctness observation on first-order values,
  which is the shape of `Rsx.adequacyStatement` (Adequacy.rsd). Lean 4.14's own code generator
  makes the same cut: `src/library/compiler/erase_irrelevant.cpp` (types and proofs to
  the neutral value, binder types dropped) and, in the LCNF pipeline,
  `src/Lean/Compiler/LCNF/ToLCNF.lean` (`isProof` / type formers → `.erased`).
- Defunctionalization: J. C. Reynolds, "Definitional Interpreters for Higher-Order
  Programming Languages", Proc. ACM Annual Conference 1972 (repr. HOSC 11(4), 1998),
  §8: each functional value becomes a record tagged by the λ it came from, carrying its
  free variables, and application becomes a call of one `apply` that dispatches on the
  tag. O. Danvy, L. R. Nielsen, "Defunctionalization at Work", PPDP 2001 (the
  correspondence with closure conversion; flat closures: the record holds exactly the
  λ's free variables, in first-occurrence order).
- Fuel: the totalization rsdc uses for every definition (a leading fuel `Nat`), and
  evalLF's own call-only fuel (N6c, `Residua/Bootstrap/Semantics.lean`).

Scope notes (facts, each witnessed by a control below; reports/rsxlower/GAPS.md):
- the statement Adequacy.rsd carried until 2026-11-18 (now `adequacyStatementWeak`) is
  provable for EVERY `lower`: its fuels are existential and both `eval … 0 …` and
  `scmValOf E 0 …` are `none` (`Rsx.adequacyStatement_vacuous`). The official
  `Rsx.adequacyStatement` is now the strong form: rsx value fixed, scm fuel existential,
  lowering fuel eventual, and the scm value is `some w`.
- `BootExpr` is intrinsically typed with no recursive type and homogeneous lists, so a
  constructor value whose fields mix literals and constructors, or whose depth exceeds
  the requested type, has no scm term of that type; `valFits` names the representable
  values and the strong statement assumes it (control `gap_heterogeneous`).
- `scmValOf` keeps proof fields; erasure drops them (`relevantSpine` premise).
- a value of a Prop inductive (`True.intro : True`) is data for `DataTy` and `scmValOf`,
  and erasure maps it to `□`: the step-4 statement (`adequacyStatementNoRoot`) is false
  for this lowering (`lowerF_not_adequate_noRoot`); the statement on main assumes
  `irrelevant E n [] v = false` (session 7).
- literals beyond i64 refuse (`litI` range), while `scmValOf` returns `.int t`
  (control `gap_i64`).
- `lower` needs the environment `E` (δ bodies, constructor classes); the strong
  statement quantifies a lowering family `Rsx.Lowering S` that reads `E`, `n`, its fuel
  and the requested type, so `Rsx.lower E` is the family member at `n = 0`,
  `F = defaultFuel`.

Recipe (inner loop, one file plus its imports):

    { echo "import Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics";
      cat semantics/Rsx/Core.rsd semantics/Rsx/Norm.rsd
          semantics/Rsx/Adequacy.rsd semantics/Rsx/Lower.rsd; } > /tmp/rsx-lower.lean \
      && cd lean/rsd-cert && lake build Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics \
      && lake env lean /tmp/rsx-lower.lean

Expected: exit 0; every `#guard` passes; `#print axioms` lists nothing beyond
`propext`, `Quot.sound`.

closure_claim = 0.
-/

namespace Rsx
namespace Lower

open Residua.Bootstrap.IR Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics
open Residua.Bootstrap.EvalBootSeparators (inI64Range)

/-! ## Stage 1: erasure (Letouzey 2002; MetaCoq `erase`; Lean `erase_irrelevant`) -/

/-- erased λ-terms: de Bruijn, untyped; `box` is Letouzey's `□`. Constants left after
    δ are constructors (`ctor`) or rigid heads (`rigid`: axioms, opaques, recursors). -/
inductive LExpr : Type
  | bvar : Nat → LExpr
  | box : LExpr
  | lit : Nat → LExpr
  | ctor : Nat → LExpr
  | rigid : Nat → LExpr
  | app : LExpr → LExpr → LExpr
  | lam : LExpr → LExpr
  | letE : LExpr → LExpr → LExpr
  /-- a reference to global `i` of the program's partial definitions (Partial.rsd), resolved
      at run time, never inlined: its body may call itself. The total lowering has none. -/
  | glob : Nat → LExpr
  deriving DecidableEq, Repr

/- The relevance test is `Rsx.irrelevant` (Adequacy.rsd): Letouzey's informative test
   read off the certified syntactic checker `inferT` — `e` is erased when its type is an
   arity or the type of its type is `Prop`; a term the checker cannot type is kept
   (erasure only ever errs toward keeping). It lives in Adequacy.rsd because the
   statement's proof-free side condition `relevantSpine` reads the same test. -/

def isCtor (E : ResolvedEnv) (r : Nat) : Bool :=
  match E.members r with
  | some m => decide (m.mclass = .constructorM)
  | none => false

/-- erasure, parametric in the relevance test `irr` (the reference instance is
    `irrelevant E n`; the controls plant a wrong one) and in the global table `gi`
    (`gi r = some i`: constant `r` is the `i`-th partial definition, erased to `glob i`
    and resolved at run time; the total lowering passes `noGlobals`). Fuel bounds depth
    plus δ. -/
def eraseWith (irr : LCtx → Expr Nat → Bool) (gi : Nat → Option Nat) (E : ResolvedEnv) :
    Nat → LCtx → Expr Nat → Option LExpr
  | 0, _, _ => none
  | _ + 1, _, .sort _ => some .box
  | _ + 1, _, .pi _ _ => some .box
  | _ + 1, _, .lit k => some (.lit k)
  | _ + 1, Γ, .bvar i => if irr Γ (.bvar i) then some .box else some (.bvar i)
  | f + 1, Γ, .const r ls =>
      if irr Γ (.const r ls) then some .box
      else
        match gi r with
        | some i => some (.glob i)
        | none =>
            match transparentBody E r ls with
            | some b => eraseWith irr gi E f [] b
            | none => some (if isCtor E r then .ctor r else .rigid r)
  | f + 1, Γ, .app g a =>
      if irr Γ (.app g a) then some .box
      else
        match eraseWith irr gi E f Γ g, eraseWith irr gi E f Γ a with
        | some g', some a' => some (.app g' a')
        | _, _ => none
  | f + 1, Γ, .lam A b =>
      if irr Γ (.lam A b) then some .box
      else (eraseWith irr gi E f (.assumption A :: Γ) b).map .lam
  | f + 1, Γ, .letE A v b =>
      if irr Γ (.letE A v b) then some .box
      else
        match eraseWith irr gi E f Γ v, eraseWith irr gi E f (.letBinding A v :: Γ) b with
        | some v', some b' => some (.letE v' b')
        | _, _ => none

/-- the empty global table: the total lowering has no partial definitions. -/
def noGlobals : Nat → Option Nat := fun _ => none

def erase (E : ResolvedEnv) (n : Nat) : Nat → LCtx → Expr Nat → Option LExpr :=
  eraseWith (irrelevant E n) noGlobals E

/-! ## Stage 2: defunctionalization (Reynolds 1972 §8; Danvy–Nielsen 2001) -/

/-- the defunctionalized first-order language: `clo ℓ xs` builds the record of λ `ℓ`
    from the environment slots `xs`; `apply` is Reynolds' single dispatch. -/
inductive DExpr : Type
  | var : Nat → DExpr
  | box : DExpr
  | lit : Nat → DExpr
  | ctor : Nat → DExpr
  | rigid : Nat → DExpr
  | clo : Nat → List Nat → DExpr
  | apply : DExpr → DExpr → DExpr
  | letE : DExpr → DExpr → DExpr
  /-- global `ℓ`: run the closed code entry `ℓ` (a partial definition's body) in the empty
      environment; one fuel tick per resolution (the compiler-inserted fuel). -/
  | glob : Nat → DExpr
  deriving DecidableEq, Repr

/-- the body of λ `ℓ`, over the environment `arg :: captured` (`ncap` captured slots). -/
structure Code where
  ncap : Nat
  body : DExpr
  deriving DecidableEq, Repr

def addUniq (xs : List Nat) (x : Nat) : List Nat :=
  if xs.contains x then xs else xs ++ [x]

def unionL (xs ys : List Nat) : List Nat := ys.foldl addUniq xs

/-- free de Bruijn indices `≥ c`, shifted down by `c`, in first-occurrence order. -/
def freeVars (c : Nat) : LExpr → List Nat
  | .bvar i => if c ≤ i then [i - c] else []
  | .app f a => unionL (freeVars c f) (freeVars c a)
  | .lam b => freeVars (c + 1) b
  | .letE v b => unionL (freeVars c v) (freeVars (c + 1) b)
  | _ => []

def idxOf (x : Nat) : List Nat → Option Nat
  | [] => none
  | y :: ys => if x = y then some 0 else (idxOf x ys).map (· + 1)

/-- renaming under a `let`: slot 0 is the bound value. -/
def liftRen (ρ : Nat → Nat) : Nat → Nat
  | 0 => 0
  | i + 1 => ρ i + 1

/-- renaming inside a λ body: slot 0 is the argument, slot `1 + k` the `k`-th captured
    variable; a variable not captured maps past the environment (lookup fails). -/
def capRen (fs : List Nat) : Nat → Nat
  | 0 => 0
  | i + 1 => (idxOf i fs).getD fs.length + 1

/-- closure conversion + defunctionalization, parametric in the λ-body renaming `cr`
    (reference `capRen`). Labels are positions in the code table, inner λs first. -/
def convWith (cr : List Nat → Nat → Nat) (ρ : Nat → Nat) (code : List Code) :
    LExpr → DExpr × List Code
  | .bvar i => (.var (ρ i), code)
  | .box => (.box, code)
  | .lit k => (.lit k, code)
  | .ctor r => (.ctor r, code)
  | .rigid r => (.rigid r, code)
  | .glob i => (.glob i, code)
  | .app f a =>
      let p := convWith cr ρ code f
      let q := convWith cr ρ p.2 a
      (.apply p.1 q.1, q.2)
  | .lam b =>
      let fs := freeVars 1 b
      let p := convWith cr (cr fs) code b
      (.clo p.2.length (fs.map ρ), p.2 ++ [{ ncap := fs.length, body := p.1 }])
  | .letE v b =>
      let p := convWith cr ρ code v
      let q := convWith cr (liftRen ρ) p.2 b
      (.letE p.1 q.1, q.2)

def defunc (l : LExpr) : DExpr × List Code := convWith capRen id [] l

/-! ## Stage 3: fuel (the defunctionalized `apply` loop, totalized) -/

/-- first-order values: no meta-level functions anywhere. -/
inductive DVal : Type
  | box : DVal
  | lit : Nat → DVal
  | ctor : Nat → List DVal → DVal
  | rigid : Nat → List DVal → DVal
  | clo : Nat → List DVal → DVal

/-- the environment machine of the defunctionalized program, parametric in how `apply`
    binds the argument (reference: `a :: captured`). Fuel-out is `none`. -/
def runWith (bind : DVal → List DVal → List DVal) (code : List Code) :
    Nat → List DVal → DExpr → Option DVal
  | 0, _, _ => none
  | _ + 1, env, .var i => env.get? i
  | _ + 1, _, .box => some .box
  | _ + 1, _, .lit k => some (.lit k)
  | _ + 1, _, .ctor r => some (.ctor r [])
  | _ + 1, _, .rigid r => some (.rigid r [])
  | _ + 1, env, .clo l caps => (caps.mapM (fun i => env.get? i)).map (.clo l)
  | f + 1, _, .glob l =>
      match code.get? l with
      | some c => runWith bind code f [] c.body
      | none => none
  | f + 1, env, .apply g a =>
      match runWith bind code f env g, runWith bind code f env a with
      | some (.clo l caps), some av =>
          match code.get? l with
          | some c => runWith bind code f (bind av caps) c.body
          | none => none
      | some (.ctor r args), some av => some (.ctor r (args ++ [av]))
      | some (.rigid r args), some av => some (.rigid r (args ++ [av]))
      | some .box, some _ => some .box
      | _, _ => none
  | f + 1, env, .letE v b =>
      match runWith bind code f env v with
      | some vv => runWith bind code f (vv :: env) b
      | none => none

def bindArg (a : DVal) (caps : List DVal) : List DVal := a :: caps

def run (code : List Code) : Nat → List DVal → DExpr → Option DVal :=
  runWith bindArg code

/-! ## Stage 4: emission into the scm IR (`BootExpr`, evalLF's input) -/

/-- the refusing scm term at every type: `unwrapSome noneE` evaluates to `none`. -/
def refuse {S : SigTable} {G : Ctx} {t : BootTy} : BootExpr S G t := .unwrapSome .noneE

def listOf {S : SigTable} {G : Ctx} {τ : BootTy} :
    List (BootExpr S G τ) → BootExpr S G (.list τ)
  | [] => .emptyList
  | e :: es => .listAppend (.listSingleton e) (listOf es)

/-- constructor fields after erasure: `□` fields (parameters, proofs) are dropped, as
    Lean's constructor layout drops irrelevant fields. -/
def relevantArgs (args : List DVal) : List DVal :=
  args.filter (fun v => match v with | .box => false | _ => true)

/-- emission at the requested type, parametric in the field selection (reference
    `relevantArgs`). Convention (the one `scmValOf` fixes): literal `k` ↦ `.int k`;
    constructor `r` ↦ summand `r` of a sum whose summand `r` is `list τ`. -/
def emitWith (fields : List DVal → List DVal) {S : SigTable} {G : Ctx} :
    Nat → (t : BootTy) → DVal → BootExpr S G t
  | 0, _, _ => refuse
  | _ + 1, .i64, .lit k =>
      if inI64Range (Int.ofNat k) then .litI (Int.ofNat k) else refuse
  | f + 1, .sum ts, .ctor r args =>
      if h : r < ts.length then
        match hτ : ts.get ⟨r, h⟩ with
        | .list τ =>
            .inj ⟨r, h⟩ (cast (congrArg (BootExpr S G) hτ.symm)
              (listOf ((fields args).map (emitWith fields f τ))))
        | _ => refuse
      else refuse
  | _ + 1, _, _ => refuse

def emit {S : SigTable} {G : Ctx} : Nat → (t : BootTy) → DVal → BootExpr S G t :=
  emitWith relevantArgs

/-! ## The lowering -/

/-- the four stages composed; every stage is a parameter so a planted mutant is the
    same composition with one stage replaced. -/
def pipeline {S : SigTable} (eraseS : Nat → LCtx → Expr Nat → Option LExpr)
    (defuncS : LExpr → DExpr × List Code)
    (runS : List Code → Nat → List DVal → DExpr → Option DVal)
    (emitS : Nat → (t : BootTy) → DVal → BootExpr S [] t)
    (F : Nat) (t : BootTy) (e : Expr Nat) : BootExpr S [] t :=
  match eraseS F [] e with
  | none => refuse
  | some l =>
      match runS (defuncS l).2 F [] (defuncS l).1 with
      | some v => emitS F t v
      | none => refuse

/-- the reference lowering at universe context `n` and fuel `F`. -/
def lowerF (E : ResolvedEnv) (n F : Nat) {S : SigTable} (t : BootTy) (e : Expr Nat) :
    BootExpr S [] t :=
  pipeline (erase E n) defunc run emit F t e

def defaultFuel : Nat := 10000

end Lower

/-- `Rsx.lower`: the reference lowering rsx → scm with the brief's signature
    (`E` supplies δ bodies and constructor classes). -/
def lower (E : ResolvedEnv) {S : Residua.Bootstrap.IR.SigTable} {t : Residua.Bootstrap.IR.BootTy}
    (e : Expr Nat) : Residua.Bootstrap.IR.BootExpr S [] t :=
  Lower.lowerF E 0 Lower.defaultFuel t e

-- provenance: ours, extending r1 (semantics/Rsx/Lower.rsd; FRONTEND-BOOT-1 F3)
namespace Lower

/-! ## RSX R2 reference lowering (`eraseR2`, `runR2`, `lowerR2WithEmit`)
    Placed beside untouched `r1` (`erase`, `defunc`, `run`, `emit`, `lowerF`).
    Covers pinned unfolding equations (`f.eq_def`), non-recursive `casesOn`
    (unused IH binders stripped, 0-arity arms thunked), and `Ext/Lit` `Nat`
    primitives over uniform `valueWords` (tag + LEB128 / length-prefixed frames). -/

def boxTag : Int := 0
def literalTag : Int := 1
def ctorTag : Int := 2
def rigidTag : Int := 3
def closureTag : Int := 4

def literalWords (n : Nat) : List Int :=
  literalTag :: Rsx.lebEncInt n

mutual
  def valueWords : DVal → List Int
    | .box => [boxTag]
    | .lit n => literalWords n
    | .ctor label args => ctorTag :: Int.ofNat label :: frameWords args
    | .rigid label args => rigidTag :: Int.ofNat label :: frameWords args
    | .clo label caps => closureTag :: Int.ofNat label :: frameWords caps

  def frameWords : List DVal → List Int
    | [] => []
    | x :: xs =>
        let words := valueWords x
        Int.ofNat words.length :: words ++ frameWords xs
end

def recTagStride : Nat := 100000000
def casesOnTag (r : Nat) : Nat := r + recTagStride

inductive NatBinOp : Type
  | add | sub | mul | pow | gcd | mod | div | xor
  deriving DecidableEq, Repr, BEq, Hashable

inductive NatBinPred : Type
  | beq | ble
  deriving DecidableEq, Repr, BEq, Hashable

def natBinOpEval : NatBinOp → Nat → Nat → Nat
  | .add => Nat.add
  | .sub => Nat.sub
  | .mul => Nat.mul
  | .pow => Nat.pow
  | .gcd => Nat.gcd
  | .mod => Nat.mod
  | .div => Nat.div
  | .xor => Nat.xor

def natBinPredEval : NatBinPred → Nat → Nat → Bool
  | .beq => Nat.beq
  | .ble => Nat.ble

structure LitRefs where
  natRef : Nat
  zeroRef : Nat
  succRef : Nat
  boolRef : Nat
  falseRef : Nat
  trueRef : Nat
  ops : List (Nat × NatBinOp) := []
  preds : List (Nat × NatBinPred) := []
  deriving DecidableEq, Repr

structure CasesCtorRule where
  ctorRef : Nat
  minorIdx : Nat
  ctorParamCount : Nat
  nfields : Nat
  nihs : Nat
  deriving DecidableEq, Repr, BEq, Hashable

structure CasesRule where
  recRef : Nat
  famRef : Nat
  arity : Nat
  propSingleton : Option (Nat × Nat)
  ctors : List CasesCtorRule
  deriving DecidableEq, Repr, BEq, Hashable

structure ExternRefs where
  mixHashRef : Option Nat := none
  stringHashRef : Option Nat := none
  platformBitsRef : Option Nat := none
  uint64MkRef : Nat
  bitVecOfFinRef : Nat
  finMkRef : Nat
  stringMkRef : Nat
  listNilRef : Nat
  listConsRef : Nat
  charMkRef : Nat
  uint32MkRef : Nat
  subtypeMkRef : Nat
  platformBits : Nat := 64
  deriving DecidableEq, Repr

def murmurMixHash64 (h value : UInt64) : UInt64 :=
  let m : UInt64 := 14313749767032793493
  let k := value * m
  let k := k ^^^ (k >>> 47)
  let k := k ^^^ m
  (h ^^^ k) * m

def murmurPackLE : List Nat → UInt64
  | [] => 0
  | b :: rest => (murmurPackLE rest <<< 8) ||| UInt64.ofNat (b % 256)

def murmurHashBlocks : Nat → UInt64 → List Nat → UInt64
  | 0, h, _ => h
  | fuel + 1, h, bs =>
      let m : UInt64 := 14313749767032793493
      if bs.length ≥ 8 then
        let w := murmurPackLE (bs.take 8)
        let k := w * m
        let k := k ^^^ (k >>> 47)
        let k := k * m
        let hNext := (h ^^^ k) * m
        murmurHashBlocks fuel hNext (bs.drop 8)
      else
        let hTail := if bs.isEmpty then h else (h ^^^ murmurPackLE bs) * m
        let h1 := hTail ^^^ (hTail >>> 47)
        let h2 := h1 * m
        h2 ^^^ (h2 >>> 47)

def murmurBytesHash64 (bs : List Nat) : UInt64 :=
  let m : UInt64 := 14313749767032793493
  let h0 : UInt64 := (11 : UInt64) ^^^ (UInt64.ofNat bs.length * m)
  murmurHashBlocks (bs.length + 1) h0 bs

def utf8BytesOfCodepoint (cp : Nat) : List Nat :=
  if cp < 128 then [cp]
  else if cp < 2048 then [192 + cp / 64, 128 + cp % 64]
  else if cp < 65536 then [224 + cp / 4096, 128 + (cp / 64) % 64, 128 + cp % 64]
  else [240 + cp / 262144, 128 + (cp / 4096) % 64, 128 + (cp / 64) % 64, 128 + cp % 64]

def extractCharCodepoint (E : ExternRefs) : DVal → Option Nat
  | .ctor cmR [.ctor u32R [.ctor bvR [_, .ctor fR [_, .lit cp, _]]], _] =>
      if cmR == E.charMkRef && u32R == E.uint32MkRef &&
         bvR == E.bitVecOfFinRef && fR == E.finMkRef then some cp else none
  | _ => none

def extractCharListUtf8 (E : ExternRefs) : DVal → Option (List Nat)
  | .ctor nilR [_] => if nilR == E.listNilRef then some [] else none
  | .ctor consR [_, chVal, tailVal] =>
      if consR == E.listConsRef then
        match extractCharCodepoint E chVal, extractCharListUtf8 E tailVal with
        | some cp, some rest => some (utf8BytesOfCodepoint cp ++ rest)
        | _, _ => none
      else none
  | _ => none

def extractUInt64DVal (E : ExternRefs) : DVal → Option Nat
  | .ctor u64R [.ctor bvR [_, .ctor fR [_, .lit v, _]]] =>
      if u64R == E.uint64MkRef && bvR == E.bitVecOfFinRef && fR == E.finMkRef then
        some (v % 18446744073709551616)
      else none
  | _ => none

def mkUInt64DVal (E : ExternRefs) (v : Nat) : DVal :=
  .ctor E.uint64MkRef
    [.ctor E.bitVecOfFinRef
      [.lit 64, .ctor E.finMkRef [.lit 18446744073709551616, .lit (v % 18446744073709551616), .box]]]

structure R2Env where
  lit : Option LitRefs := none
  casesRules : List (Nat × CasesRule) := []
  inlineRefs : List Nat := []
  extern : Option ExternRefs := none

def emptyR2 : R2Env := {}

def R2Env.findCases (r2 : R2Env) (r : Nat) : Option CasesRule :=
  (r2.casesRules.find? (fun p => p.1 == r)).map Prod.snd

def R2Env.findNatOp (r2 : R2Env) (r : Nat) : Option NatBinOp :=
  r2.lit.bind fun L => (L.ops.find? (fun p => p.1 == r)).map Prod.snd

def R2Env.findNatPred (r2 : R2Env) (r : Nat) : Option NatBinPred :=
  r2.lit.bind fun L => (L.preds.find? (fun p => p.1 == r)).map Prod.snd

def R2Env.isExternPrim (r2 : R2Env) (r : Nat) : Bool :=
  match r2.extern with
  | none => false
  | some E => E.mixHashRef == some r || E.stringHashRef == some r || E.platformBitsRef == some r

def R2Env.evalExtern (r2 : R2Env) (r : Nat) (allArgs : List DVal) : Option DVal :=
  match r2.extern with
  | none => none
  | some E =>
      if E.platformBitsRef == some r && allArgs.length == 1 then
        some (.ctor E.subtypeMkRef [.box, .box, .lit E.platformBits, .box])
      else if E.mixHashRef == some r then
        match allArgs with
        | [vh, vv] =>
            match extractUInt64DVal E vh, extractUInt64DVal E vv with
            | some h, some v =>
                some (mkUInt64DVal E (murmurMixHash64 (UInt64.ofNat h) (UInt64.ofNat v)).toNat)
            | _, _ => none
        | _ => none
      else if E.stringHashRef == some r then
        match allArgs with
        | [.ctor sMk [charList]] =>
            if sMk == E.stringMkRef then
              match extractCharListUtf8 E charList with
              | some bs => some (mkUInt64DVal E (murmurBytesHash64 bs).toNat)
              | none => none
            else none
        | _ => none
      else none

def R2Env.isLitPrim (r2 : R2Env) (r : Nat) : Bool :=
  (r2.findNatOp r).isSome || (r2.findNatPred r).isSome || r2.isExternPrim r

def R2Env.isInlineRef (r2 : R2Env) (r : Nat) : Bool :=
  r2.inlineRefs.contains r

def peelAllPis : Rsx.Expr Nat → List (Rsx.Expr Nat) × Rsx.Expr Nat
  | .pi d b =>
      let (ds, concl) := peelAllPis b
      (d :: ds, concl)
  | e => ([], e)

def levelAlwaysZero : Rsx.Level → Bool
  | .zero => true
  | .max a b => levelAlwaysZero a && levelAlwaysZero b
  | .imax _ b => levelAlwaysZero b
  | _ => false

private def findLastSortDomIdx (doms : List (Rsx.Expr Nat)) : Option Nat :=
  (List.range doms.length).foldl (fun acc idx =>
    match doms.get? idx with
    | some d =>
        match (peelAllPis d).2 with
        | .sort _ => some idx
        | _ => acc
    | none => acc) none

def extractCasesRules (E : Rsx.ResolvedEnv) (recRefs : List Nat) : List (Nat × CasesRule) :=
  recRefs.filterMap fun r =>
    match E.members r with
    | some m =>
        if m.mclass = .recursorM then
          let (doms, body) := peelAllPis m.mtype
          let arity := doms.length
          let (head, bodyArgs) := Rsx.appsSpine body
          if arity ≥ 2 && !bodyArgs.isEmpty && arity ≥ bodyArgs.length + 1 then
            let nindices := bodyArgs.length - 1
            let preIdxCount := arity - 1 - nindices
            match head, doms.get? (arity - 1) with
            | .bvar _, some majorDom =>
                match (Rsx.appsSpine majorDom).1 with
                | .const famRef _ =>
                    let sharedDoms := doms.take preIdxCount
                    match findLastSortDomIdx sharedDoms with
                    | none => none
                    | some lastMotive =>
                        let prefixLen := lastMotive + 1
                        let minorPositions := (List.range (preIdxCount - prefixLen)).map (· + prefixLen)
                        let ctors : List CasesCtorRule :=
                          minorPositions.filterMap fun pos =>
                            match sharedDoms.get? pos with
                            | none => none
                            | some minorDom =>
                                let (mDoms, mConcl) := peelAllPis minorDom
                                let D := mDoms.length
                                match (Rsx.appsSpine mConcl).2.getLast? with
                                | none => none
                                | some ctorApp =>
                                    let (cHead, cArgs) := Rsx.appsSpine ctorApp
                                    match cHead with
                                    | .const ctorRef _ =>
                                        let paramCount := (cArgs.takeWhile fun a =>
                                          match a with | .bvar i => decide (i ≥ D) | _ => true).length
                                        let nfields := cArgs.length - paramCount
                                        if D < nfields then none
                                        else some ⟨ctorRef, pos, paramCount, nfields, D - nfields⟩
                                    | _ => none
                        if ctors.length != minorPositions.length then none
                        else
                          let isPropFam : Bool := match E.members famRef with
                            | some fm =>
                                match (peelAllPis fm.mtype).2 with
                                | .sort l => levelAlwaysZero l
                                | _ => false
                            | none => false
                          let propSing : Option (Nat × Nat) :=
                            match ctors with
                            | [c] => if isPropFam && c.nihs == 0 then some (c.minorIdx, c.nfields) else none
                            | _ => none
                          some (casesOnTag r, {
                            recRef := casesOnTag r
                            famRef := famRef
                            arity := arity
                            propSingleton := propSing
                            ctors := ctors })
                | _ => none
            | _, _ => none
          else none
        else none
    | none => none

def whnfCtx (E : Rsx.ResolvedEnv) (Γ : Rsx.LCtx) : Nat → Rsx.Expr Nat → Rsx.Expr Nat
  | 0, e => e
  | f + 1, e =>
      let (head, args) := Rsx.appsSpine e
      match head with
      | .lam _ b =>
          match args with
          | a :: rest => whnfCtx E Γ f (Rsx.foldApps (Rsx.instantiate0 a b) rest)
          | [] => e
      | .letE _ v b => whnfCtx E Γ f (Rsx.foldApps (Rsx.instantiate0 v b) args)
      | .bvar i =>
          match Rsx.lookupValue Γ i with
          | some v => whnfCtx E Γ f (Rsx.foldApps v args)
          | none => e
      | .const r ls =>
          match Rsx.transparentBody E r ls with
          | some b => whnfCtx E Γ f (Rsx.foldApps b args)
          | none => e
      | _ => e

def isArityCtx (E : Rsx.ResolvedEnv) (whnfBudget : Nat) :
    Nat → Rsx.LCtx → Rsx.Expr Nat → Bool
  | 0, _, _ => false
  | d + 1, Γ, T =>
      match whnfCtx E Γ whnfBudget T with
      | .sort _ => true
      | .pi A B => isArityCtx E whnfBudget d (.assumption A :: Γ) B
      | _ => false

def inferTR2 (E : Rsx.ResolvedEnv) (natRef : Option Nat) (whnfBudget : Nat) :
    Nat → Nat → Rsx.LCtx → Rsx.Expr Nat → Option (Rsx.Expr Nat)
  | 0, _, _, _ => none
  | _ + 1, n, _, .sort l =>
      if Rsx.levelBounded n l then some (.sort (.succ l)) else none
  | _ + 1, _, _, .lit _ =>
      match natRef with
      | some nr => some (.const nr [])
      | none => none
  | _ + 1, _, Γ, .bvar i => Rsx.lookupType Γ i
  | _ + 1, n, _, .const r ls =>
      match E.members r with
      | some m =>
          if ls.length == m.arity && ls.all (Rsx.levelBounded n) then
            some (Rsx.instantiateLevels ls m.mtype)
          else none
      | none => none
  | fuel + 1, n, Γ, .app g a =>
      match inferTR2 E natRef whnfBudget fuel n Γ g with
      | some Tg =>
          match whnfCtx E Γ whnfBudget Tg with
          | .pi _ B => some (Rsx.instantiate0 a B)
          | _ => none
      | none => none
  | fuel + 1, n, Γ, .lam A b =>
      match inferTR2 E natRef whnfBudget fuel n (.assumption A :: Γ) b with
      | some B => some (.pi A B)
      | none => none
  | fuel + 1, n, Γ, .pi A B =>
      match inferTR2 E natRef whnfBudget fuel n Γ A,
            inferTR2 E natRef whnfBudget fuel n (.assumption A :: Γ) B with
      | some TA, some TB =>
          match whnfCtx E Γ whnfBudget TA, whnfCtx E (.assumption A :: Γ) whnfBudget TB with
          | .sort u, .sort v => some (.sort (.imax u v))
          | _, _ => none
      | _, _ => none
  | fuel + 1, n, Γ, .letE A v b =>
      inferTR2 E natRef whnfBudget fuel n (.letBinding A v :: Γ) b
        |>.map (Rsx.instantiate0 v)

def irrelevantR2 (E : Rsx.ResolvedEnv) (r2 : R2Env) (n : Nat)
    (Γ : Rsx.LCtx) (e : Rsx.Expr Nat) : Bool :=
  let natRef := r2.lit.map (·.natRef)
  match inferTR2 E natRef 48 128 n Γ e with
  | some T =>
      isArityCtx E 48 64 Γ T ||
        match inferTR2 E natRef 48 128 n Γ T with
        | some U =>
            match whnfCtx E Γ 48 U with
            | .sort l => levelAlwaysZero l
            | _ => false
        | none => false
  | none => false

def liftL (cutoff amount : Nat) : LExpr → LExpr
  | .bvar i => if cutoff ≤ i then .bvar (i + amount) else .bvar i
  | .app f a => .app (liftL cutoff amount f) (liftL cutoff amount a)
  | .lam b => .lam (liftL (cutoff + 1) amount b)
  | .letE v b => .letE (liftL cutoff amount v) (liftL (cutoff + 1) amount b)
  | e => e

def unshiftL (cutoff amount : Nat) : LExpr → Option LExpr
  | .bvar i =>
      if i < cutoff then some (.bvar i)
      else if cutoff + amount ≤ i then some (.bvar (i - amount))
      else none
  | .app f a => do
      let f' ← unshiftL cutoff amount f
      let a' ← unshiftL cutoff amount a
      pure (.app f' a')
  | .lam b => .lam <$> unshiftL (cutoff + 1) amount b
  | .letE v b => do
      let v' ← unshiftL cutoff amount v
      let b' ← unshiftL (cutoff + 1) amount b
      pure (.letE v' b')
  | e => some e

def stripUnusedIHLams : Nat → Nat → LExpr → Option LExpr
  | 0, 0, body => some body
  | 0, nihs + 1, .lam b => do
      let rest ← stripUnusedIHLams 0 nihs b
      unshiftL 0 1 rest
  | nfields + 1, nihs, .lam b => .lam <$> stripUnusedIHLams nfields nihs b
  | _, _, _ => none

def wrapMinorForLazy (arity : Nat) (m : LExpr) : LExpr :=
  if arity == 0 then .lam (liftL 0 1 m)
  else match m with
    | .lam _ => m
    | _ => .lam (.app (liftL 0 1 m) (.bvar 0))

def smartApp : LExpr → LExpr → LExpr
  | .lam b, a => .letE a b
  | f, a => .app f a

def smartAppR2 (r2 : R2Env) : LExpr → LExpr → LExpr
  | .box, _ => .box
  | .lam b, a => .letE a b
  | .ctor r, .lit k =>
      if (r2.lit.map (·.succRef)) == some r then .lit (k + 1)
      else .app (.ctor r) (.lit k)
  | f, a => .app f a

def foldSmartApps (head : LExpr) (args : List LExpr) : LExpr :=
  args.foldl smartApp head

def foldSmartAppsR2 (r2 : R2Env) (head : LExpr) (args : List LExpr) : LExpr :=
  args.foldl (smartAppR2 r2) head

def peelSuccChain (zeroRef succRef : Nat) : Nat → Nat → Rsx.Expr Nat → Option (Nat × Nat)
  | 0, _, _ => none
  | _ + 1, acc, .const r [] => if r == zeroRef then some (acc, acc + 1) else none
  | _ + 1, acc, .lit k => some (k + acc, acc + 1)
  | fuel + 1, acc, .app (.const r []) inner =>
      if r == succRef then peelSuccChain zeroRef succRef fuel (acc + 1) inner
      else none
  | _, _, _ => none

def betaReduceLams : Rsx.Expr Nat → List (Rsx.Expr Nat) → Rsx.Expr Nat × List (Rsx.Expr Nat)
  | .lam _ b, a :: rest => betaReduceLams (Rsx.instantiate0 a b) rest
  | head, rest => (head, rest)

def eraseR2With (r2 : R2Env) (irr : Rsx.LCtx → Rsx.Expr Nat → Bool)
    (gi : Nat → Option Nat) (E : Rsx.ResolvedEnv) :
    Nat → Rsx.LCtx → Rsx.Expr Nat → Option LExpr
  | 0, _, _ => none
  | _ + 1, _, .sort _ => some .box
  | _ + 1, _, .pi _ _ => some .box
  | _ + 1, _, .lit k => some (.lit k)
  | _ + 1, Γ, .bvar i => if irr Γ (.bvar i) then some .box else some (.bvar i)
  | f + 1, Γ, .const r ls =>
      if irr Γ (.const r ls) then some .box
      else if (r2.lit.map (·.zeroRef)) == some r then some (.lit 0)
      else if r2.isLitPrim r then some (.rigid r)
      else
        match gi r with
        | some i => some (.glob i)
        | none =>
            match Rsx.transparentBody E r ls with
            | some b => eraseR2With r2 irr gi E f [] b
            | none => some (if isCtor E r then .ctor r else .rigid r)
  | f + 1, Γ, .lam A b =>
      if irr Γ (.lam A b) then some .box
      else (eraseR2With r2 irr gi E f (.assumption A :: Γ) b).map .lam
  | f + 1, Γ, .letE A v b =>
      if irr Γ (.letE A v b) then some .box
      else
        match eraseR2With r2 irr gi E f Γ v, eraseR2With r2 irr gi E f (.letBinding A v :: Γ) b with
        | some v', some b' => some (.letE v' b')
        | _, _ => none
  | f + 1, Γ, e@(.app g a) =>
      match r2.lit.bind (fun L => peelSuccChain L.zeroRef L.succRef (f + 1) 0 e) with
      | some (k, _) => some (.lit k)
      | none =>
          if irr Γ e then some .box
          else
            let (head, spineArgs) := Rsx.appsSpine e
            match head with
            | .const r ls =>
                if !r2.isLitPrim r && (gi r).isNone && r2.isInlineRef r then
                  match Rsx.transparentBody E r ls with
                  | some body@(.lam _ _) =>
                      let (redHead, redRest) := betaReduceLams body spineArgs
                      eraseR2With r2 irr gi E f Γ (Rsx.foldApps redHead redRest)
                  | _ =>
                      match eraseR2With r2 irr gi E f Γ g, eraseR2With r2 irr gi E f Γ a with
                      | some g', some a' => some (smartAppR2 r2 g' a')
                      | _, _ => none
                else
                  match if !r2.isLitPrim r && (gi r).isNone then r2.findCases (casesOnTag r) else none with
                  | some cRule =>
                      if spineArgs.length ≥ cRule.arity then
                        let recArgs := spineArgs.take cRule.arity
                        let extraArgs := spineArgs.drop cRule.arity
                        match recArgs.mapM (eraseR2With r2 irr gi E f Γ),
                              extraArgs.mapM (eraseR2With r2 irr gi E f Γ) with
                        | some erasedRecArgs, some erasedExtra =>
                            let strippedCheck : List (Nat × Option LExpr) :=
                              cRule.ctors.filterMap fun cr =>
                                (erasedRecArgs.get? cr.minorIdx).map fun mTerm =>
                                  (cr.minorIdx, stripUnusedIHLams cr.nfields cr.nihs mTerm)
                            if strippedCheck.length == cRule.ctors.length &&
                                strippedCheck.all (fun p => p.2.isSome) then
                              let updatedArgs := (List.range erasedRecArgs.length).filterMap fun idx =>
                                match cRule.ctors.find? (fun cr => cr.minorIdx == idx),
                                      strippedCheck.find? (fun p => p.1 == idx) with
                                | some cr, some (_, some stripped) =>
                                    some (wrapMinorForLazy cr.nfields stripped)
                                | _, _ => erasedRecArgs.get? idx
                              some (foldSmartAppsR2 r2 (updatedArgs.foldl LExpr.app (.rigid (casesOnTag r))) erasedExtra)
                            else
                              match eraseR2With r2 irr gi E f Γ g, eraseR2With r2 irr gi E f Γ a with
                              | some g', some a' => some (smartAppR2 r2 g' a')
                              | _, _ => none
                        | _, _ => none
                      else
                        match eraseR2With r2 irr gi E f Γ g, eraseR2With r2 irr gi E f Γ a with
                        | some g', some a' => some (smartAppR2 r2 g' a')
                        | _, _ => none
                  | none =>
                      match eraseR2With r2 irr gi E f Γ g, eraseR2With r2 irr gi E f Γ a with
                      | some g', some a' => some (smartAppR2 r2 g' a')
                      | _, _ => none
            | _ =>
                match eraseR2With r2 irr gi E f Γ g, eraseR2With r2 irr gi E f Γ a with
                | some g', some a' => some (smartAppR2 r2 g' a')
                | _, _ => none

/-- R2 erasure with pinned global table `gi` (`noGlobals` when omitted). -/
def eraseR2 (r2 : R2Env) (E : Rsx.ResolvedEnv) (n : Nat)
    (gi : Nat → Option Nat := noGlobals) : Nat → Rsx.LCtx → Rsx.Expr Nat → Option LExpr :=
  eraseR2With r2 (irrelevantR2 E r2 n) gi E

inductive UnfoldRefusal where
  | definitionMissing
  | theoremMissing
  | universeParameters
  | equationShape
  | equationHead
  | equationArguments
  | globalMissing
  | erasureFuel
  deriving DecidableEq, Repr

private def extractUnfoldRhs (eqRef target : Nat) (levels : List Rsx.Level) (binders : Nat) :
    Rsx.Expr Nat → Except UnfoldRefusal (Rsx.Expr Nat)
  | .pi type conclusion =>
      .lam type <$> extractUnfoldRhs eqRef target levels (binders + 1) conclusion
  | conclusion => do
      let (.const equality _, [_, lhs, rhs]) := Rsx.appsSpine conclusion
        | throw .equationShape
      unless equality == eqRef do throw .equationShape
      let (.const head appliedLevels, args) := Rsx.appsSpine lhs
        | throw .equationHead
      unless head == target do throw .equationHead
      unless decide (appliedLevels = levels) do throw .universeParameters
      let expected := (List.range binders).reverse.map (fun n => (Rsx.Expr.bvar n : Rsx.Expr Nat))
      unless decide (args = expected) do throw .equationArguments
      return rhs

def readUnfoldType (definition : Rsx.CheckedMember) (eqRef target theoremArity : Nat)
    (type : Rsx.Expr Nat) : Except UnfoldRefusal (Rsx.Expr Nat) := do
  unless decide (definition.mclass = .definitionM) do throw .definitionMissing
  unless theoremArity == definition.arity do throw .universeParameters
  let levels := (List.range definition.arity).map Rsx.Level.param
  extractUnfoldRhs eqRef target levels 0 type

def readUnfold (env : Rsx.ResolvedEnv) (eqRef target theoremRef : Nat) :
    Except UnfoldRefusal (Rsx.Expr Nat) := do
  let some definition := env.members target | throw .definitionMissing
  let some equation := env.members theoremRef | throw .theoremMissing
  unless decide (equation.mclass = .theoremM) && equation.body.isSome do throw .theoremMissing
  readUnfoldType definition eqRef target equation.arity equation.mtype

def eraseUnfoldR2 (r2 : R2Env) (env : Rsx.ResolvedEnv) (globals : Nat → Option Nat)
    (eqRef target theoremRef fuel : Nat) : Except UnfoldRefusal LExpr := do
  unless (globals target).isSome do throw .globalMissing
  let some member := env.members target | throw .definitionMissing
  let body ← readUnfold env eqRef target theoremRef
  let some erased := eraseR2With r2 (irrelevantR2 env r2 member.arity) globals env fuel [] body
    | throw .erasureFuel
  return erased

def eraseUnfoldTypeR2 (r2 : R2Env) (env : Rsx.ResolvedEnv) (globals : Nat → Option Nat)
    (eqRef target theoremArity : Nat) (eqType : Rsx.Expr Nat) (fuel : Nat) :
    Except UnfoldRefusal LExpr := do
  unless (globals target).isSome do throw .globalMissing
  let some member := env.members target | throw .definitionMissing
  let body ← readUnfoldType member eqRef target theoremArity eqType
  let some erased := eraseR2With r2 (irrelevantR2 env r2 member.arity) globals env fuel [] body
    | throw .erasureFuel
  return erased

private def matchCasesCtor (lit : Option LitRefs) (rule : CasesRule) (major : DVal) :
    Option (Nat × Bool × List DVal) :=
  match major with
  | .lit k =>
      match lit with
      | some L =>
          if rule.famRef == L.natRef then
            if k == 0 then
              (rule.ctors.find? (fun c => c.ctorRef == L.zeroRef)).map fun c =>
                (c.minorIdx, c.nfields == 0, [])
            else
              (rule.ctors.find? (fun c => c.ctorRef == L.succRef)).map fun c =>
                (c.minorIdx, false, [.lit (k - 1)])
          else none
      | none => none
  | .ctor cRef cArgs =>
      (rule.ctors.find? (fun c => c.ctorRef == cRef && cArgs.length == c.ctorParamCount + c.nfields)).map
        fun c =>
          let fields := cArgs.drop c.ctorParamCount
          (c.minorIdx, c.nfields == 0, fields)
  | .box =>
      rule.propSingleton.map fun (minorIdx, nfields) =>
        (minorIdx, nfields == 0, List.replicate nfields .box)
  | _ => none

private def stepApplyAt (r2 : R2Env) (code : List Code)
    (runF : List DVal → DExpr → Option DVal)
    (applyValsF : DVal → List DVal → Option DVal)
    (vg av : DVal) : Option DVal :=
  match vg with
  | .clo l caps =>
      match code.get? l with
      | some c => runF (av :: caps) c.body
      | none => none
  | .box => some .box
  | .lit _ => none
  | .ctor r args =>
      match r2.lit, args, av with
      | some L, [], .lit k =>
          if r == L.succRef then some (.lit (k + 1)) else some (.ctor r [av])
      | _, _, _ => some (.ctor r (args ++ [av]))
  | .rigid r args =>
      let allArgs := args ++ [av]
      match r2.findNatOp r, allArgs with
      | some op, [.lit x, .lit y] => some (.lit (natBinOpEval op x y))
      | _, _ =>
          match r2.findNatPred r, r2.lit, allArgs with
          | some pred, some L, [.lit x, .lit y] =>
              some (.ctor (if natBinPredEval pred x y then L.trueRef else L.falseRef) [])
          | _, _, _ =>
              match r2.evalExtern r allArgs with
              | some extVal => some extVal
              | none =>
                  match r2.findCases r with
                  | some rule =>
                      if allArgs.length == rule.arity then
                        match allArgs.get? (rule.arity - 1) >>= matchCasesCtor r2.lit rule with
                        | none => some (.rigid r allArgs)
                        | some (minorIdx, thunkZero, fields) =>
                            match allArgs.get? minorIdx with
                            | none => none
                            | some minor =>
                                let callArgs := if thunkZero then [.box] else fields
                                applyValsF minor callArgs
                      else some (.rigid r allArgs)
                  | none => some (.rigid r allArgs)

mutual
  def runR2 (r2 : R2Env) (code : List Code) : Nat → List DVal → DExpr → Option DVal
    | 0, _, _ => none
    | _ + 1, env, .var i => env.get? i
    | _ + 1, _, .box => some .box
    | _ + 1, _, .lit k => some (.lit k)
    | _ + 1, _, .ctor r =>
        if (r2.lit.map (·.zeroRef)) == some r then some (.lit 0)
        else some (.ctor r [])
    | _ + 1, _, .rigid r => some (.rigid r [])
    | _ + 1, env, .clo l caps => (caps.mapM (fun i => env.get? i)).map (.clo l)
    | f + 1, _, .glob l =>
        match code.get? l with
        | some c => runR2 r2 code f [] c.body
        | none => none
    | f + 1, env, .apply g a =>
        match runR2 r2 code f env g, runR2 r2 code f env a with
        | some vg, some av => stepApplyAt r2 code (runR2 r2 code f) (applyValsR2 r2 code f) vg av
        | _, _ => none
    | f + 1, env, .letE v b =>
        match runR2 r2 code f env v with
        | some vv => runR2 r2 code f (vv :: env) b
        | none => none

  def applyValsR2 (r2 : R2Env) (code : List Code) : Nat → DVal → List DVal → Option DVal
    | 0, fn, [] => some fn
    | 0, _, _ :: _ => none
    | _ + 1, fn, [] => some fn
    | f + 1, fn, a :: rest =>
        match stepApplyAt r2 code (runR2 r2 code f) (applyValsR2 r2 code f) fn a with
        | some nextFn => applyValsR2 r2 code f nextFn rest
        | none => none
end

theorem runR2_empty (code : List Code) :
    ∀ (fuel : Nat) (env : List DVal) (e : DExpr),
      runR2 emptyR2 code fuel env e = run code fuel env e := by
  intro fuel
  induction fuel with
  | zero => intro env e; rfl
  | succ f ih =>
      intro env e
      cases e with
      | var i => rfl
      | box => rfl
      | lit k => rfl
      | ctor r => rfl
      | rigid r => rfl
      | clo l caps => rfl
      | glob l =>
          simp only [runR2, run, runWith]
          cases code.get? l with
          | none => rfl
          | some c => exact ih [] c.body
      | letE v b =>
          simp only [runR2, run, runWith, ih env v]
          cases runWith bindArg code f env v with
          | none => rfl
          | some vv => exact ih (vv :: env) b
      | apply g a =>
          simp only [runR2, run, runWith, ih env g, ih env a]
          cases runWith bindArg code f env g with
          | none => rfl
          | some vg =>
              cases runWith bindArg code f env a with
              | none => cases vg <;> rfl
              | some va =>
                  cases vg with
                  | box => rfl
                  | lit _ => rfl
                  | ctor r args => rfl
                  | rigid r args =>
                      simp [stepApplyAt, emptyR2, R2Env.findNatOp, R2Env.findNatPred, R2Env.evalExtern, R2Env.findCases]
                  | clo l caps =>
                      simp only [stepApplyAt, bindArg]
                      cases code.get? l with
                      | none => rfl
                      | some c => exact ih (va :: caps) c.body

/-- R2 reference pipeline (`eraseR2 -> defunc -> runR2 -> emitOpt`), parameterized by
    the target expression constructor `emitOpt` so `Lower.rsd` compiles under both
    `Semantics` (`rsx r1` gate) and `R2.SCM` (`scm r3`, instantiated as `Rsx.lowerR2`). -/
def lowerR2WithEmit {Target : Type} (emitOpt : Option DVal → Target)
    (r2 : R2Env) (gi : Nat → Option Nat) (globals : List Code)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n F : Nat) (e : Expr Nat) : Target :=
  match eraseR2 r2 E n gi F [] e with
  | none => emitOpt none
  | some l =>
      let p := convWith capRen id globals l
      emitOpt (runR2 r2 p.2 F [] p.1)

end Lower

namespace Lower

open Residua.Bootstrap.IR Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics
open Residua.Bootstrap.EvalBootSeparators (inI64Range)

/-! ## Adequacy statements

The hole-14 statement is `Rsx.adequacyStatement` (Adequacy.rsd, strong form since
2026-11-18): rsx value `w` fixed, scm fuel existential, lowering fuel eventual. Its
side conditions `relevantSpine`, `valFits` and the vacuity control for the weak form
(`Rsx.adequacyStatement_vacuous`) live there too. The reference instance is the family
`fun E n F t e => lowerF E n F t e`; `Rsx.lower E` is its member at `n = 0`,
`F = defaultFuel`. -/

/-- the old (weak) form for `Rsx.lower`: it holds, and says nothing (every lowering
    meets it, `Rsx.adequacyStatement_vacuous`). -/
theorem lower_adequacyStatementWeak (E : ResolvedEnv) {S : SigTable} {t : BootTy}
    (progs : Programs S S) : adequacyStatementWeak (Rsx.lower E (S := S) (t := t)) progs :=
  adequacyStatement_vacuous _ progs

/-- structural erasure finishes: `erase` returns a term at some fuel.
    `whnfFuel` (Core.rsd, frozen) is call-by-name, so `norm` can discard a relevant
    argument; `erase` traverses it. A transparent `loop := loop` in that argument has a
    `norm` and no finite erasure (`lowerF_not_adequate_divArg`). MetaCoq's erasure
    correctness (Sozeau et al., POPL 2020, §4) assumes the source is defined, which
    here is this premise. -/
def Erasable (E : ResolvedEnv) (n : Nat) (e : Expr Nat) : Prop :=
  ∃ (F : Nat) (l : LExpr), erase E n F [] e = some l

theorem erasable_lit (E : ResolvedEnv) (n k : Nat) : Erasable E n (.lit k) :=
  ⟨1, .lit k, rfl⟩

/-! ### Stage-1 `LExpr` evaluator (`LVal`, `evalL`) and reduction-trace erasability
    (`StepEvalL`, `WhnfErasable`, `NormErasable`, `TraceErasable`) -/

inductive LVal : Type
  | box
  | lit : Nat → LVal
  | ctor : Nat → List LVal → LVal
  | rigid : Nat → List LVal → LVal
  | clo : List LVal → LExpr → LVal

mutual
def lToD : LVal → Option DVal
  | .box => some .box
  | .lit k => some (.lit k)
  | .ctor r xs => (lToDList xs).map (DVal.ctor r)
  | .rigid r xs => (lToDList xs).map (DVal.rigid r)
  | .clo _ _ => none

def lToDList : List LVal → Option (List DVal)
  | [] => some []
  | v :: vs =>
      match lToD v, lToDList vs with
      | some d, some ds => some (d :: ds)
      | _, _ => none
end

def toDEnv : List LVal → Option (List DVal)
  | [] => some []
  | v :: vs =>
      match lToD v, toDEnv vs with
      | some d, some ds => some (d :: ds)
      | _, _ => none

/-- no λ and no global, so `convWith` adds no code and never renames under a λ. -/
def passive : LExpr → Bool
  | .lam _ => false
  | .glob _ => false
  | .app f a => passive f && passive a
  | .letE v b => passive v && passive b
  | _ => true

def evalL : Nat → List LVal → LExpr → Option LVal
  | 0, _, _ => none
  | _ + 1, env, .bvar i => env.get? i
  | _ + 1, _, .box => some .box
  | _ + 1, _, .lit k => some (.lit k)
  | _ + 1, _, .ctor r => some (.ctor r [])
  | _ + 1, _, .rigid r => some (.rigid r [])
  | _ + 1, _, .glob _ => none
  | _ + 1, env, .lam b =>
      match (freeVars 1 b).mapM (fun i => env.get? i) with
      | some _ => some (.clo env b)
      | none => none
  | f + 1, env, .app g a =>
      match evalL f env g, evalL f env a with
      | some (.clo env' b), some av => evalL f (av :: env') b
      | some (.ctor r args), some av => some (.ctor r (args ++ [av]))
      | some (.rigid r args), some av => some (.rigid r (args ++ [av]))
      | some .box, some _ => some .box
      | _, _ => none
  | f + 1, env, .letE v b =>
      match evalL f env v with
      | some vv => evalL f (vv :: env) b
      | none => none

mutual
def noClo : LVal → Bool
  | .box => true
  | .lit _ => true
  | .ctor _ xs => noCloList xs
  | .rigid _ xs => noCloList xs
  | .clo _ _ => false

def noCloList : List LVal → Bool
  | [] => true
  | v :: vs => noClo v && noCloList vs
end

theorem evalL_mono :
    ∀ (F F' : Nat) (env : List LVal) (l : LExpr) (v : LVal),
      F ≤ F' → evalL F env l = some v → evalL F' env l = some v := by
  intro F
  induction F with
  | zero => intro _ _ _ _ _ h; exact Option.noConfusion h
  | succ F ih =>
      intro F' env l v hF h
      obtain ⟨F'', rfl⟩ : ∃ F'', F' = F'' + 1 := ⟨F' - 1, by omega⟩
      have hF' : F ≤ F'' := by omega
      cases l with
      | bvar _ | box | lit _ | ctor _ | rigid _ | glob _ | lam _ => exact h
      | app g a =>
          simp only [evalL] at h ⊢
          cases hg : evalL F env g with
          | none => rw [hg] at h; exact Option.noConfusion h
          | some vg =>
              cases ha : evalL F env a with
              | none => rw [hg, ha] at h; cases vg <;> exact Option.noConfusion h
              | some va =>
                  rw [hg, ha] at h
                  rw [ih F'' env g vg hF' hg, ih F'' env a va hF' ha]
                  cases vg with
                  | clo env' b => exact ih F'' (va :: env') b v hF' h
                  | _ => exact h
      | letE x b =>
          simp only [evalL] at h ⊢
          cases hx : evalL F env x with
          | none => rw [hx] at h; exact Option.noConfusion h
          | some xv =>
              rw [hx] at h
              rw [ih F'' env x xv hF' hx]
              exact ih F'' (xv :: env) b v hF' h

theorem evalL_unique (F1 F2 : Nat) (env : List LVal) (l : LExpr) (v1 v2 : LVal)
    (h1 : evalL F1 env l = some v1) (h2 : evalL F2 env l = some v2) :
    v1 = v2 := by
  have a := evalL_mono F1 (F1 + F2) env l v1 (Nat.le_add_right F1 F2) h1
  have b := evalL_mono F2 (F1 + F2) env l v2 (Nat.le_add_left F2 F1) h2
  rw [a] at b
  exact Option.some.inj b

/-- Stage-1 (`erase` + `evalL`) one-step evaluation lifting from contractum `e'` to redex `e`.
    Contains no reference to Stage 2 (`defunc`), Stage 3 (`run`), Stage 4 (`emit`), or any
    first-order `DExpr`/`DVal`. -/
def StepEvalL (E : ResolvedEnv) (n : Nat) (e e' : Expr Nat) : Prop :=
  ∀ (F' : Nat) (le' : LExpr) (vL : LVal),
    erase E n F' [] e' = some le' →
    evalL F' [] le' = some vL →
    noClo vL = true →
    ∃ (F : Nat) (le : LExpr),
      erase E n F [] e = some le ∧
      evalL F [] le = some vL

/-- Stepwise weak-head reduction trace invariant at Stage 1:
    - δ-steps require only syntactic type preservation on the unfolded constant
      (`inferT E n [] (.const r ls) = some T0 → inferT E n [] body = some T0`);
      their `erase` and `evalL` agreement is derived (`erase_foldApps_const_delta`);
    - β/ζ-steps require Stage-1 `StepEvalL` between redex and contractum;
    - canonical heads require `True`. -/
def WhnfErasable (E : ResolvedEnv) (n : Nat) : Nat → Expr Nat → Prop
  | 0, _ => True
  | fuel + 1, e =>
      match appsSpine e with
      | (.lam _ b, a :: args) =>
          StepEvalL E n e (foldApps (instantiate0 a b) args) ∧
          WhnfErasable E n fuel (foldApps (instantiate0 a b) args)
      | (.letE _ v b, args) =>
          StepEvalL E n e (foldApps (instantiate0 v b) args) ∧
          WhnfErasable E n fuel (foldApps (instantiate0 v b) args)
      | (.const r ls, args) =>
          match transparentBody E r ls with
          | some body =>
              (∀ T0, inferT E n [] (.const r ls) = some T0 → inferT E n [] body = some T0) ∧
              WhnfErasable E n fuel (foldApps body args)
          | none => True
      | _ => True

/-- Normalization trace invariant at Stage 1: `WhnfErasable` on the weak-head trace
    and recursive `StepEvalL` / `NormErasable` on each spine argument when the weak-head
    normal form is an application. Does not depend on `v`, `defunc`, `run`, or `emit`. -/
def NormErasable (E : ResolvedEnv) (n : Nat) : Nat → Expr Nat → Prop
  | 0, _ => True
  | fuel + 1, e =>
      WhnfErasable E n fuel e ∧
      match whnfFuel E fuel e with
      | some (.app g a) =>
          ∀ arg ∈ (appsSpine (.app g a)).2,
            (∀ varg, norm E fuel arg = some varg → StepEvalL E n arg varg) ∧
            NormErasable E n fuel arg
      | _ => True

/-- Combined Stage-1 source and reduction-trace erasability premise for `Good` and
    `adequacyClosed`. Replaces `ErasableVal`: mentions only Stage 1 (`erase`, `evalL`,
    `whnfFuel`, `norm`, `inferT`) and does not take the normal form `v` as an argument. -/
def TraceErasable (E : ResolvedEnv) (n lf : Nat) (e : Expr Nat) : Prop :=
  Erasable E n e ∧ NormErasable E n lf e

theorem erasable_of_traceErasable {E : ResolvedEnv} {n lf : Nat} {e : Expr Nat}
    (h : TraceErasable E n lf e) : Erasable E n e :=
  h.1

theorem whnfErasable_lit (E : ResolvedEnv) (n fuel k : Nat) :
    WhnfErasable E n fuel (.lit k) := by
  cases fuel <;> trivial

theorem normErasable_lit (E : ResolvedEnv) (n lf k : Nat) :
    NormErasable E n lf (.lit k) := by
  cases lf with
  | zero => trivial
  | succ fuel =>
      refine ⟨whnfErasable_lit E n fuel k, ?_⟩
      cases fuel <;> trivial

theorem traceErasable_lit (E : ResolvedEnv) (n lf k : Nat) :
    TraceErasable E n lf (.lit k) :=
  ⟨erasable_lit E n k, normErasable_lit E n lf k⟩

theorem erasable_bvar (E : ResolvedEnv) (n i : Nat) : Erasable E n (.bvar i) :=
  ⟨1, if irrelevant E n [] (.bvar i) then .box else .bvar i, rfl⟩

theorem whnfErasable_bvar (E : ResolvedEnv) (n fuel i : Nat) :
    WhnfErasable E n fuel (.bvar i) := by
  cases fuel <;> trivial

theorem normErasable_bvar (E : ResolvedEnv) (n lf i : Nat) :
    NormErasable E n lf (.bvar i) := by
  cases lf with
  | zero => trivial
  | succ fuel =>
      refine ⟨whnfErasable_bvar E n fuel i, ?_⟩
      cases fuel <;> trivial

theorem traceErasable_bvar (E : ResolvedEnv) (n lf i : Nat) :
    TraceErasable E n lf (.bvar i) :=
  ⟨erasable_bvar E n i, normErasable_bvar E n lf i⟩

theorem erasable_sort (E : ResolvedEnv) (n : Nat) (l : Level) :
    Erasable E n (.sort l) :=
  ⟨1, .box, rfl⟩

theorem normErasable_sort (E : ResolvedEnv) (n lf : Nat) (l : Level) :
    NormErasable E n lf (.sort l) := by
  cases lf with
  | zero => trivial
  | succ fuel =>
      refine ⟨by cases fuel <;> trivial, ?_⟩
      cases fuel <;> trivial

theorem traceErasable_sort (E : ResolvedEnv) (n lf : Nat) (l : Level) :
    TraceErasable E n lf (.sort l) :=
  ⟨erasable_sort E n l, normErasable_sort E n lf l⟩

theorem erasable_pi (E : ResolvedEnv) (n : Nat) (A B : Expr Nat) :
    Erasable E n (.pi A B) :=
  ⟨1, .box, rfl⟩

theorem normErasable_pi (E : ResolvedEnv) (n lf : Nat) (A B : Expr Nat) :
    NormErasable E n lf (.pi A B) := by
  cases lf with
  | zero => trivial
  | succ fuel =>
      refine ⟨by cases fuel <;> trivial, ?_⟩
      cases fuel <;> trivial

theorem traceErasable_pi (E : ResolvedEnv) (n lf : Nat) (A B : Expr Nat) :
    TraceErasable E n lf (.pi A B) :=
  ⟨erasable_pi E n A B, normErasable_pi E n lf A B⟩

theorem normErasable_lam (E : ResolvedEnv) (n lf : Nat) (A b : Expr Nat) :
    NormErasable E n lf (.lam A b) := by
  cases lf with
  | zero => trivial
  | succ fuel =>
      refine ⟨by cases fuel <;> trivial, ?_⟩
      cases fuel <;> trivial

theorem erasable_const_head (E : ResolvedEnv) (n r : Nat) (ls : List Level)
    (hnone : transparentBody E r ls = none) :
    Erasable E n (.const r ls) := by
  refine ⟨1, if irrelevant E n [] (.const r ls) then .box
    else if isCtor E r then .ctor r else .rigid r, ?_⟩
  simp only [erase, eraseWith, noGlobals, hnone]
  cases irrelevant E n [] (.const r ls) <;> rfl

theorem whnfErasable_const_head (E : ResolvedEnv) (n fuel r : Nat) (ls : List Level)
    (hnone : transparentBody E r ls = none) :
    WhnfErasable E n fuel (.const r ls) := by
  cases fuel with
  | zero => trivial
  | succ _ => simp only [WhnfErasable, appsSpine, hnone]

theorem normErasable_const_head (E : ResolvedEnv) (n lf r : Nat) (ls : List Level)
    (hnone : transparentBody E r ls = none) :
    NormErasable E n lf (.const r ls) := by
  cases lf with
  | zero => trivial
  | succ fuel =>
      refine ⟨whnfErasable_const_head E n fuel r ls hnone, ?_⟩
      cases fuel with
      | zero => trivial
      | succ _ => simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine, hnone]

theorem traceErasable_const_head (E : ResolvedEnv) (n lf r : Nat) (ls : List Level)
    (hnone : transparentBody E r ls = none) :
    TraceErasable E n lf (.const r ls) :=
  ⟨erasable_const_head E n r ls hnone, normErasable_const_head E n lf r ls hnone⟩

/-- adequacy of `Rsx.Lower.lowerF` at one closed term (the body of
    `Rsx.Lower.adequacyClosed` at `e`). -/
def Good {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) (E : ResolvedEnv) (n : Nat)
    (e : Expr Nat) : Prop :=
  ∀ (lf fv : Nat) (T v : Expr Nat) (t : BootTy) (w : Val),
    BodiesTyped E n →
    inferT E n [] e = some T → DataTy E T →
    norm E lf e = some v → scmValOf E fv v = some w →
    relevantSpine E n fv v = true → irrelevant E n [] v = false → valFits fv t w = true →
    inferT E n [] v = some T →
    TraceErasable E n lf e →
    ∃ F₀, ∀ F, F₀ ≤ F →
      ∃ lf', Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf' [] (lowerF E n F (S := S) t e)
        = some w

/-- the `rsx-d107` form with `Erasable E n e` alone (refuted universally under `EnvWf E`
    by `convFlip2Env`: `not_adeqAppWfSameTy`, `not_adeqLetEWfSameTy`,
    `not_adeqConstDeltaWfSameTy`, and independently without conversion by `litAppEnv`). -/
def GoodWfSameTy {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) (E : ResolvedEnv) (n : Nat)
    (e : Expr Nat) : Prop :=
  ∀ (lf fv : Nat) (T v : Expr Nat) (t : BootTy) (w : Val),
    BodiesTyped E n →
    inferT E n [] e = some T → DataTy E T →
    norm E lf e = some v → scmValOf E fv v = some w →
    relevantSpine E n fv v = true → irrelevant E n [] v = false → valFits fv t w = true →
    inferT E n [] v = some T →
    Erasable E n e →
    ∃ F₀, ∀ F, F₀ ≤ F →
      ∃ lf', Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf' [] (lowerF E n F (S := S) t e)
        = some w

theorem good_of_goodWfSameTy {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) (E : ResolvedEnv)
    (n : Nat) (e : Expr Nat) (h : GoodWfSameTy progs E n e) : Good progs E n e := by
  intro lf fv T v t w h0 h1 h2 h3 h4 h5 h6 h7 h8 h9
  exact h lf fv T v t w h0 h1 h2 h3 h4 h5 h6 h7 h8 (erasable_of_traceErasable h9)

/-- Every member of `E` is closed and admitted by the waist typing `HasTyT`
    (D-RCIC-0 / MetaCoq `wf Σ`): its declared type is typed at a sort, and
    any body is typed at its declared type. -/
def EnvWf (E : ResolvedEnv) : Prop :=
  EnvClosed E ∧
  ∀ r m, E.members r = some m →
    (∃ u, Nonempty (HasTyT E m.arity [] m.mtype (.sort u))) ∧
    (∀ b, m.body = some b → Nonempty (HasTyT E m.arity [] b m.mtype))

/-- hole-14 statement parameterized by a lowering family `lower : Lowering S`,
    under `EnvWf E`, `BodiesTyped E n`, `inferT E n [] v = some T`, and Stage-1
    source/trace erasability `TraceErasable E n lf e`. -/
def adequacyClosedFor {S : SigTable} (lower : Lowering S) (progs : Programs S S) : Prop :=
  ∀ (E : ResolvedEnv) (n lf fv : Nat) (e T v : Expr Nat) (t : BootTy) (w : Val),
    EnvWf E →
    BodiesTyped E n →
    inferT E n [] e = some T → DataTy E T →
    norm E lf e = some v → scmValOf E fv v = some w →
    relevantSpine E n fv v = true → irrelevant E n [] v = false → valFits fv t w = true →
    inferT E n [] v = some T →
    TraceErasable E n lf e →
    ∃ F₀, ∀ F, F₀ ≤ F →
      ∃ lf', Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf' [] (lower E n F t e)
        = some w

def adequacyClosed {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) : Prop :=
  adequacyClosedFor (fun E n F t e => lowerF E n F (S := S) t e) progs

/-! ### One statement per `Expr` constructor (8/8).
    Direct constructs proved for every environment: `adeqBvar`, `adeqSort`, `adeqPi`,
    `adeqLam`, `adeqLit`, and the rigid-head constant slice `adeqConstHead`.
    Stepping constructs (`AdeqConstDelta`, `AdeqConst`, `AdeqApp`, `AdeqLetE`) take
    `EnvWf E`, and `Good` requires `inferT E n [] v = some T` and `TraceErasable E n lf e`:
    - Without `EnvClosed` the loose forms are refuted (`not_adeqApp`,
      `not_adeqLetE`, `not_adeqConstDelta`): open constructor `weird : bvar 0`.
    - With `EnvClosed` alone they are refuted (`not_adeqAppClosed`,
      `not_adeqLetEClosed`, `not_adeqConstDeltaClosed`): closed ill-typed
      constructor `cfK` (`closedFlipEnv`).
    - With `EnvWf` and only `(inferT E n [] v).isSome = true` (`GoodLoose`) they
      are refuted (`not_adeqAppWfLoose`, `not_adeqLetEWfLoose`,
      `not_adeqConstDeltaWfLoose`): one-step universe-conversion witness `convFlipEnv`.
    - With `EnvWf`, `inferT E n [] v = some T`, and `Erasable E n e` alone (`GoodWfSameTy`)
      they are refuted by two-step universe conversion `convFlip2Env`
      (`not_adeqAppWfSameTy`, `not_adeqLetEWfSameTy`, `not_adeqConstDeltaWfSameTy`)
      and independently without conversion by CBN-vs-CBV discarded application `litAppEnv`. -/

def AdeqBvar {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) : Prop :=
  ∀ E n i, Good progs E n (.bvar i)
def AdeqSort {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) : Prop :=
  ∀ E n l, Good progs E n (.sort l)
def AdeqConst {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) : Prop :=
  ∀ E n r ls, EnvWf E → Good progs E n (.const r ls)
def AdeqApp {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) : Prop :=
  ∀ E n f a, EnvWf E → Good progs E n (.app f a)
def AdeqLam {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) : Prop :=
  ∀ E n A b, Good progs E n (.lam A b)
def AdeqPi {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) : Prop :=
  ∀ E n A B, Good progs E n (.pi A B)
def AdeqLetE {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) : Prop :=
  ∀ E n A v b, EnvWf E → Good progs E n (.letE A v b)
def AdeqLit {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) : Prop :=
  ∀ E n k, Good progs E n (.lit k)

/-- the eight per-construct statements together give `adequacyClosed` for the
    reference family `Rsx.Lower.lowerF` (case split on the term). -/
theorem adequacy_of_constructs {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (hb : AdeqBvar progs) (hs : AdeqSort progs) (hc : AdeqConst progs)
    (ha : AdeqApp progs) (hl : AdeqLam progs) (hp : AdeqPi progs)
    (hz : AdeqLetE progs) (hn : AdeqLit progs) :
    adequacyClosed (S := S) progs := by
  intro E n lf fv e T v t w hE
  cases e with
  | bvar i => exact hb E n i lf fv T v t w
  | sort l => exact hs E n l lf fv T v t w
  | const r ls => exact hc E n r ls hE lf fv T v t w
  | app f a => exact ha E n f a hE lf fv T v t w
  | lam A b => exact hl E n A b lf fv T v t w
  | pi A B => exact hp E n A B lf fv T v t w
  | letE A x b => exact hz E n A x b hE lf fv T v t w
  | lit k => exact hn E n k lf fv T v t w

/-! ### The direct cases -/

theorem norm_bvar_val {E : ResolvedEnv} {lf i : Nat} {v : Expr Nat}
    (h : norm E lf (.bvar i) = some v) : v = .bvar i := by
  match lf, h with
  | 0, h => exact Option.noConfusion h
  | 1, h => exact Option.noConfusion h
  | j + 2, h =>
      have h2 : norm E (j + 2) (.bvar i) = some (.bvar i) := rfl
      rw [h2] at h
      exact (Option.some.inj h).symm

theorem norm_sort_val {E : ResolvedEnv} {lf : Nat} {l : Level} {v : Expr Nat}
    (h : norm E lf (.sort l) = some v) : v = .sort l := by
  match lf, h with
  | 0, h => exact Option.noConfusion h
  | 1, h => exact Option.noConfusion h
  | j + 2, h =>
      have h2 : norm E (j + 2) (.sort l) = some (.sort l) := rfl
      rw [h2] at h
      exact (Option.some.inj h).symm

theorem norm_lit_val {E : ResolvedEnv} {lf k : Nat} {v : Expr Nat}
    (h : norm E lf (.lit k) = some v) : v = .lit k := by
  match lf, h with
  | 0, h => exact Option.noConfusion h
  | 1, h => exact Option.noConfusion h
  | j + 2, h =>
      have h2 : norm E (j + 2) (.lit k) = some (.lit k) := rfl
      rw [h2] at h
      exact (Option.some.inj h).symm

theorem norm_pi_val {E : ResolvedEnv} {lf : Nat} {A B v : Expr Nat}
    (h : norm E lf (.pi A B) = some v) : ∃ A' B', v = .pi A' B' := by
  match lf, h with
  | 0, h => exact Option.noConfusion h
  | 1, h => exact Option.noConfusion h
  | j + 2, h =>
      have h2 : norm E (j + 2) (.pi A B) =
          (match norm E (j + 1) A, norm E (j + 1) B with
           | some A', some B' => some (.pi A' B')
           | _, _ => none) := rfl
      rw [h2] at h
      split at h
      · exact ⟨_, _, (Option.some.inj h).symm⟩
      · exact Option.noConfusion h

theorem norm_lam_val {E : ResolvedEnv} {lf : Nat} {A b v : Expr Nat}
    (h : norm E lf (.lam A b) = some v) : ∃ A' b', v = .lam A' b' := by
  match lf, h with
  | 0, h => exact Option.noConfusion h
  | 1, h => exact Option.noConfusion h
  | j + 2, h =>
      have h2 : norm E (j + 2) (.lam A b) =
          (match norm E (j + 1) A, norm E (j + 1) b with
           | some A', some b' => some (.lam A' b')
           | _, _ => none) := rfl
      rw [h2] at h
      split at h
      · exact ⟨_, _, (Option.some.inj h).symm⟩
      · exact Option.noConfusion h

theorem scmValOf_bvar (E : ResolvedEnv) (fv i : Nat) : scmValOf E fv (.bvar i) = none := by
  cases fv <;> rfl

theorem scmValOf_sort (E : ResolvedEnv) (fv : Nat) (l : Level) :
    scmValOf E fv (.sort l) = none := by
  cases fv <;> rfl

theorem scmValOf_pi (E : ResolvedEnv) (fv : Nat) (A B : Expr Nat) :
    scmValOf E fv (.pi A B) = none := by
  cases fv <;> rfl

theorem scmValOf_lam (E : ResolvedEnv) (fv : Nat) (A b : Expr Nat) :
    scmValOf E fv (.lam A b) = none := by
  cases fv <;> rfl

/- A constant that is not a constructor is not data. `scmValOf` returns
   `none` for an axiom, an opaque, an inductive, a recursor, or a missing
   member. -/
theorem scmValOf_const_not_ctor (E : ResolvedEnv) (fv c : Nat) (ls : List Level)
    (hnot : ∀ m, E.members c = some m → ¬ m.mclass = .constructorM) :
    scmValOf E fv (.const c ls) = none := by
  cases fv with
  | zero => rfl
  | succ _ =>
    cases hm : E.members c with
    | none => simp [scmValOf, appsSpine, hm]
    | some m =>
      have hne := hnot m hm
      simp [scmValOf, appsSpine, hm, hne]

theorem adeqBvar {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) : AdeqBvar progs := by
  intro E n i lf fv T v t w _ _ _ hn hs _ _ _ _ _
  rw [norm_bvar_val hn, scmValOf_bvar] at hs
  exact Option.noConfusion hs

theorem adeqSort {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) : AdeqSort progs := by
  intro E n l lf fv T v t w _ _ _ hn hs _ _ _ _ _
  rw [norm_sort_val hn, scmValOf_sort] at hs
  exact Option.noConfusion hs

theorem adeqPi {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) : AdeqPi progs := by
  intro E n A B lf fv T v t w _ _ _ hn hs _ _ _ _ _
  obtain ⟨A', B', hv⟩ := norm_pi_val hn
  rw [hv, scmValOf_pi] at hs
  exact Option.noConfusion hs

theorem adeqLam {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) : AdeqLam progs := by
  intro E n A b lf fv T v t w _ _ _ hn hs _ _ _ _ _
  obtain ⟨A', b', hv⟩ := norm_lam_val hn
  rw [hv, scmValOf_lam] at hs
  exact Option.noConfusion hs

/-- the lowering of a literal, by computation through the four stages, at every
    positive lowering fuel. -/
theorem lowerF_lit (E : ResolvedEnv) (n k F : Nat) {S : SigTable} :
    lowerF E n (F + 1) (S := S) .i64 (.lit k) =
      (if inI64Range (Int.ofNat k) then .litI (Int.ofNat k) else refuse) := rfl

theorem eval_litI {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) (x : Int)
    (hx : inI64Range x = true) :
    Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs 1 [] (BootExpr.litI (S := S) (G := []) x)
      = some (.int x) := by
  simp [Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval, hx]

theorem adeqLit {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) : AdeqLit progs := by
  intro E n k lf fv T v t w _ _ _ hn hs _ _ hf _ _
  rw [norm_lit_val hn] at hs
  cases fv with
  | zero => exact Option.noConfusion hs
  | succ m =>
      have hs2 : scmValOf E (m + 1) (.lit k) = some (.int (Int.ofNat k)) := rfl
      rw [hs2] at hs
      cases hs
      cases t
      case i64 =>
          have hk : inI64Range (Int.ofNat k) = true := hf
          refine ⟨1, fun F hF => ⟨1, ?_⟩⟩
          obtain ⟨F', rfl⟩ : ∃ F', F = F' + 1 := ⟨F - 1, by omega⟩
          rw [lowerF_lit, if_pos hk]
          exact eval_litI progs _ hk
      all_goals cases hf

/-- positive control at the concrete term on which Adequacy.rsd refutes the two mutants
    (`lit 0 : N` in `adqEnv`, value `.int 0`, scm type `i64`): the reference family
    meets the strong statement there. -/
theorem lit0_good {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) :
    ∃ F₀, ∀ F, F₀ ≤ F → ∃ lf', Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf' []
      (lowerF adqEnv 0 F (S := S) .i64 (.lit 0)) = some (.int 0) :=
  adeqLit progs adqEnv 0 0 2 1 _ (.lit 0) .i64 (.int 0) adqBodiesTyped adqLit0Infer adqLit0Data adqLit0Norm
    adqLit0Val adqLit0Rel adqLit0Root adqLit0Fits adqLit0Infer (traceErasable_lit _ _ _ _)

/-! ### Fuel monotonicity of the erase and run stages

The strong statement's lowering fuel is eventual (`∀ F ≥ F₀`); these lemmas are what the
open cases (const, app, letE) use to move a successful stage result to a larger fuel. -/

theorem eraseWith_mono (irr : LCtx → Expr Nat → Bool) (gi : Nat → Option Nat)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) :
    ∀ (F F' : Nat) (Γ : LCtx) (e : Expr Nat) (l : LExpr), F ≤ F' →
      eraseWith irr gi E F Γ e = some l → eraseWith irr gi E F' Γ e = some l := by
  intro F
  induction F with
  | zero => intro F' Γ e l _ h; exact Option.noConfusion h
  | succ F ih =>
    intro F' Γ e l hF h
    obtain ⟨F'', rfl⟩ : ∃ F'', F' = F'' + 1 := ⟨F' - 1, by omega⟩
    have hF' : F ≤ F'' := by omega
    cases e with
    | sort _ => exact h
    | pi _ _ => exact h
    | lit _ => exact h
    | bvar _ => exact h
    | const r ls =>
        simp only [eraseWith] at h ⊢
        cases hi : irr Γ (.const r ls)
        · simp only [hi, Bool.false_eq_true, if_false] at h ⊢
          cases hg : gi r with
          | some i => rw [hg] at h; exact h
          | none =>
            rw [hg] at h
            cases hb : transparentBody E r ls with
            | none => rw [hb] at h; exact h
            | some b => rw [hb] at h; exact ih _ _ _ _ hF' h
        · simp only [hi, if_true] at h ⊢; exact h
    | app g a =>
        simp only [eraseWith] at h ⊢
        cases hi : irr Γ (.app g a)
        · simp only [hi, Bool.false_eq_true, if_false] at h ⊢
          cases hg : eraseWith irr gi E F Γ g with
          | none => rw [hg] at h; exact Option.noConfusion h
          | some g' =>
            cases ha : eraseWith irr gi E F Γ a with
            | none => rw [hg, ha] at h; exact Option.noConfusion h
            | some a' =>
              rw [hg, ha] at h
              rw [ih _ _ _ _ hF' hg, ih _ _ _ _ hF' ha]
              exact h
        · simp only [hi, if_true] at h ⊢; exact h
    | lam A b =>
        simp only [eraseWith] at h ⊢
        cases hi : irr Γ (.lam A b)
        · simp only [hi, Bool.false_eq_true, if_false] at h ⊢
          cases hb : eraseWith irr gi E F (.assumption A :: Γ) b with
          | none => rw [hb] at h; exact Option.noConfusion h
          | some b' => rw [hb] at h; rw [ih _ _ _ _ hF' hb]; exact h
        · simp only [hi, if_true] at h ⊢; exact h
    | letE A v b =>
        simp only [eraseWith] at h ⊢
        cases hi : irr Γ (.letE A v b)
        · simp only [hi, Bool.false_eq_true, if_false] at h ⊢
          cases hv : eraseWith irr gi E F Γ v with
          | none => rw [hv] at h; exact Option.noConfusion h
          | some v' =>
            cases hb : eraseWith irr gi E F (.letBinding A v :: Γ) b with
            | none => rw [hv, hb] at h; exact Option.noConfusion h
            | some b' =>
              rw [hv, hb] at h
              rw [ih _ _ _ _ hF' hv, ih _ _ _ _ hF' hb]
              exact h
        · simp only [hi, if_true] at h ⊢; exact h

theorem erase_mono (E : ResolvedEnv) (n F F' : Nat) (Γ : LCtx) (e : Expr Nat) (l : LExpr)
    (hF : F ≤ F') (h : erase E n F Γ e = some l) : erase E n F' Γ e = some l :=
  eraseWith_mono (irrelevant E n) noGlobals E F F' Γ e l hF h

/- A transparent constant erases as its body, one fuel earlier, in the empty
   context. Letouzey TYPES 2002 unfolds δ before the informative test of the
   body; Sozeau et al. POPL 2020 §4 erase a constant as the erasure of its body.
   `noGlobals` sends the constant nowhere, so this is not a `glob`. -/
theorem erase_const_delta (E : ResolvedEnv) (n F r : Nat) (ls : List Level) (b : Expr Nat)
    (hirr : irrelevant E n [] (.const r ls) = false)
    (hb : transparentBody E r ls = some b) :
    erase E n (F + 1) [] (.const r ls) = erase E n F [] b := by
  simp only [erase, eraseWith, hirr, Bool.false_eq_true, if_false, noGlobals, hb]

/- A relevant application erases as the application of the two erasures,
   one fuel earlier. Letouzey TYPES 2002 keeps an informative application.
   The AdeqApp relevant branch rewrites with this. Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem erase_app_keep (E : ResolvedEnv) (n F : Nat) (Γ : LCtx) (g a : Expr Nat)
    (h : irrelevant E n Γ (.app g a) = false) :
    erase E n (F + 1) Γ (.app g a) =
      match erase E n F Γ g, erase E n F Γ a with
      | some g', some a' => some (.app g' a')
      | _, _ => none := by
  simp only [erase, eraseWith, h, Bool.false_eq_true, if_false]

/- A relevant lambda erases as the lambda of its body, domain dropped,
   one fuel earlier, under the assumption. Not AdeqLam: that one is
   already proved, because a lambda is not data. -/
theorem erase_lam_keep (E : ResolvedEnv) (n F : Nat) (Γ : LCtx) (A b : Expr Nat)
    (h : irrelevant E n Γ (.lam A b) = false) :
    erase E n (F + 1) Γ (.lam A b) =
      (erase E n F (.assumption A :: Γ) b).map .lam := by
  simp only [erase, eraseWith, h, Bool.false_eq_true, if_false]

/- A relevant let erases as the let of the two erasures, one fuel earlier.
   The body is erased under the let binding. The AdeqLetE relevant branch
   rewrites with this. Not AdeqLetE. -/
theorem erase_let_keep (E : ResolvedEnv) (n F : Nat) (Γ : LCtx)
    (A v b : Expr Nat) (h : irrelevant E n Γ (.letE A v b) = false) :
    erase E n (F + 1) Γ (.letE A v b) =
      match erase E n F Γ v, erase E n F (.letBinding A v :: Γ) b with
      | some v', some b' => some (.letE v' b')
      | _, _ => none := by
  simp only [erase, eraseWith, h, Bool.false_eq_true, if_false]

/- `whnfFuel` unfolds the same δ, and `foldApps body []` is the body. -/
theorem whnf_const_delta (E : ResolvedEnv) (k r : Nat) (ls : List Level) (b : Expr Nat)
    (hb : transparentBody E r ls = some b) :
    whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.const r ls) = whnfFuel E k b := by
  simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine, foldApps, hb]

/- If the body normalizes at fuel `k + 1`, the constant normalizes to that
   value at fuel `k + 2`. `whnf_const_delta` makes the two heads the same
   `whnf`, and `norm_mono` moves the body's value up one fuel, where both
   `norm`s normalize the same subterms. The unconditional equality, with no
   success hypothesis on the body, is the false one named below.
   Not AdeqConstDelta. -/
theorem norm_const_delta_of_body (E : ResolvedEnv) (k r : Nat) (ls : List Level)
    (body v : Expr Nat) (ht : transparentBody E r ls = some body)
    (hn : norm E (k + 1) body = some v) :
    norm E (k + 2) (.const r ls) = some v := by
  cases hw : whnfFuel E k body with
  | none =>
    unfold norm at hn
    rw [hw] at hn
    exact Option.noConfusion hn
  | some w =>
    have hc : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.const r ls) = some w := by
      rw [whnf_const_delta E k r ls body ht]
      exact hw
    have hb1 : whnfFuel E (k + 1) body = some w :=
      whnfFuel_mono E k body w hw
    have heq : norm E (k + 2) (.const r ls) = norm E (k + 2) body := by
      conv =>
        lhs
        unfold norm
        rw [hc]
      conv =>
        rhs
        unfold norm
        rw [hb1]
    rw [heq]
    exact norm_mono E (k + 1) body v hn

/- A literal body has no subterm for `norm` to revisit, so the fuel shift is
   only the one `whnf_const_delta` performs. One fuel makes `whnfFuel` return
   the literal. The general equality `norm` of the constant at `k + 2` equals
   `norm` of an arbitrary body at `k + 1` is false: the constant normalizes
   subterms at fuel `k + 1` and the body at fuel `k`. -/
theorem norm_const_delta_lit (E : ResolvedEnv) (k r n : Nat) (ls : List Level)
    (hb : transparentBody E r ls = some (.lit n)) :
    norm E (k + 3) (.const r ls) = some (.lit n) := by
  have hw : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.lit n) = some (.lit n) := by
    simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine]
  unfold norm
  rw [whnf_const_delta E (k + 1) r ls (.lit n) hb, hw]

/- Any successful `norm` of that constant is the literal. Fuels 0, 1 and 2
   return `none` (`whnfFuel` of the literal needs one fuel, and `norm` spends
   one more). -/
theorem norm_const_lit_val (E : ResolvedEnv) (lf r n : Nat) (ls : List Level)
    {v : Expr Nat} (hb : transparentBody E r ls = some (.lit n))
    (hn : norm E lf (.const r ls) = some v) : v = .lit n := by
  cases lf with
  | zero => exact Option.noConfusion hn
  | succ lf =>
    cases lf with
    | zero =>
      unfold norm at hn
      rw [whnfFuel_fuel0] at hn
      exact Option.noConfusion hn
    | succ lf =>
      cases lf with
      | zero =>
        have hw := whnf_const_delta E 0 r ls (.lit n) hb
        unfold norm at hn
        rw [whnfFuel_fuel0] at hw
        rw [hw] at hn
        exact Option.noConfusion hn
      | succ j =>
        rw [norm_const_delta_lit E j r n ls hb] at hn
        exact (Option.some.inj hn).symm

/- A sort body is the same canonical head. `scmValOf` of a sort is `none`,
   so this case of δ is vacuous once `norm` returns the sort. -/
theorem norm_const_delta_sort (E : ResolvedEnv) (k r : Nat) (ls : List Level) (u : Level)
    (hb : transparentBody E r ls = some (.sort u)) :
    norm E (k + 3) (.const r ls) = some (.sort u) := by
  have hw : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.sort u) = some (.sort u) := by
    simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine]
  unfold norm
  rw [whnf_const_delta E (k + 1) r ls (.sort u) hb, hw]

theorem norm_const_sort_val (E : ResolvedEnv) (lf r : Nat) (ls : List Level) (u : Level)
    {v : Expr Nat} (hb : transparentBody E r ls = some (.sort u))
    (hn : norm E lf (.const r ls) = some v) : v = .sort u := by
  cases lf with
  | zero => exact Option.noConfusion hn
  | succ lf =>
    cases lf with
    | zero =>
      unfold norm at hn
      rw [whnfFuel_fuel0] at hn
      exact Option.noConfusion hn
    | succ lf =>
      cases lf with
      | zero =>
        have hw := whnf_const_delta E 0 r ls (.sort u) hb
        unfold norm at hn
        rw [whnfFuel_fuel0] at hw
        rw [hw] at hn
        exact Option.noConfusion hn
      | succ j =>
        rw [norm_const_delta_sort E j r ls u hb] at hn
        exact (Option.some.inj hn).symm

/- A bound variable is a canonical head. `scmValOf` of it is `none`. -/
theorem norm_const_delta_bvar (E : ResolvedEnv) (k r i : Nat) (ls : List Level)
    (hb : transparentBody E r ls = some (.bvar i)) :
    norm E (k + 3) (.const r ls) = some (.bvar i) := by
  have hw : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.bvar i) = some (.bvar i) := by
    simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine]
  unfold norm
  rw [whnf_const_delta E (k + 1) r ls (.bvar i) hb, hw]

theorem norm_const_bvar_val (E : ResolvedEnv) (lf r i : Nat) (ls : List Level)
    {v : Expr Nat} (hb : transparentBody E r ls = some (.bvar i))
    (hn : norm E lf (.const r ls) = some v) : v = .bvar i := by
  cases lf with
  | zero => exact Option.noConfusion hn
  | succ lf =>
    cases lf with
    | zero =>
      unfold norm at hn
      rw [whnfFuel_fuel0] at hn
      exact Option.noConfusion hn
    | succ lf =>
      cases lf with
      | zero =>
        have hw := whnf_const_delta E 0 r ls (.bvar i) hb
        unfold norm at hn
        rw [whnfFuel_fuel0] at hw
        rw [hw] at hn
        exact Option.noConfusion hn
      | succ j =>
        rw [norm_const_delta_bvar E j r i ls hb] at hn
        exact (Option.some.inj hn).symm

/- A Π body is not rewritten away by `whnfFuel`. A successful `norm` of the
   constant is a Π; its subterms are normalized one fuel later than `norm`
   of the body, so the two `norm`s are not equal. -/
theorem norm_const_pi_val (E : ResolvedEnv) (lf r : Nat) (ls : List Level)
    (A B : Expr Nat) {v : Expr Nat}
    (hb : transparentBody E r ls = some (.pi A B))
    (hn : norm E lf (.const r ls) = some v) : ∃ A' B', v = .pi A' B' := by
  cases lf with
  | zero => exact Option.noConfusion hn
  | succ lf =>
    cases lf with
    | zero =>
      unfold norm at hn
      rw [whnfFuel_fuel0] at hn
      exact Option.noConfusion hn
    | succ lf =>
      cases lf with
      | zero =>
        have hw := whnf_const_delta E 0 r ls (.pi A B) hb
        unfold norm at hn
        rw [whnfFuel_fuel0] at hw
        rw [hw] at hn
        exact Option.noConfusion hn
      | succ j =>
        have hw : whnfFuel E (j + 1) (.pi A B) = some (.pi A B) := by
          simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine]
        have h2 : norm E (j + 3) (.const r ls) =
            (match norm E (j + 2) A, norm E (j + 2) B with
             | some A', some B' => some (.pi A' B')
             | _, _ => none) := by
          unfold norm
          rw [whnf_const_delta E (j + 1) r ls (.pi A B) hb, hw]
          rfl
        rw [h2] at hn
        split at hn
        · exact ⟨_, _, (Option.some.inj hn).symm⟩
        · exact Option.noConfusion hn

/- A λ body is the same shape as a Π body. -/
theorem norm_const_lam_val (E : ResolvedEnv) (lf r : Nat) (ls : List Level)
    (A b : Expr Nat) {v : Expr Nat}
    (hb : transparentBody E r ls = some (.lam A b))
    (hn : norm E lf (.const r ls) = some v) : ∃ A' b', v = .lam A' b' := by
  cases lf with
  | zero => exact Option.noConfusion hn
  | succ lf =>
    cases lf with
    | zero =>
      unfold norm at hn
      rw [whnfFuel_fuel0] at hn
      exact Option.noConfusion hn
    | succ lf =>
      cases lf with
      | zero =>
        have hw := whnf_const_delta E 0 r ls (.lam A b) hb
        unfold norm at hn
        rw [whnfFuel_fuel0] at hw
        rw [hw] at hn
        exact Option.noConfusion hn
      | succ j =>
        have hw : whnfFuel E (j + 1) (.lam A b) = some (.lam A b) := by
          simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine]
        have h2 : norm E (j + 3) (.const r ls) =
            (match norm E (j + 2) A, norm E (j + 2) b with
             | some A', some b' => some (.lam A' b')
             | _, _ => none) := by
          unfold norm
          rw [whnf_const_delta E (j + 1) r ls (.lam A b) hb, hw]
          rfl
        rw [h2] at hn
        split at hn
        · exact ⟨_, _, (Option.some.inj hn).symm⟩
        · exact Option.noConfusion hn

/- A constructor head has no transparent body, so `norm` does not open it.
   The fuel shift is only the one `whnf_const_delta` performs. -/
theorem norm_const_delta_ctor (E : ResolvedEnv) (k r c : Nat) (ls lsc : List Level)
    (hb : transparentBody E r ls = some (.const c lsc))
    (hnone : transparentBody E c lsc = none) :
    norm E (k + 3) (.const r ls) = some (.const c lsc) := by
  have hw : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.const c lsc) = some (.const c lsc) := by
    change (match transparentBody E c lsc with
      | some body => whnfFuel E k (foldApps body [])
      | none => some (.const c lsc)) = some (.const c lsc)
    rw [hnone]
  unfold norm
  rw [whnf_const_delta E (k + 1) r ls (.const c lsc) hb, hw]

theorem norm_const_ctor_val (E : ResolvedEnv) (lf r c : Nat) (ls lsc : List Level)
    {v : Expr Nat}
    (hb : transparentBody E r ls = some (.const c lsc))
    (hnone : transparentBody E c lsc = none)
    (hn : norm E lf (.const r ls) = some v) : v = .const c lsc := by
  cases lf with
  | zero => exact Option.noConfusion hn
  | succ lf =>
    cases lf with
    | zero =>
      unfold norm at hn
      rw [whnfFuel_fuel0] at hn
      exact Option.noConfusion hn
    | succ lf =>
      cases lf with
      | zero =>
        have hw := whnf_const_delta E 0 r ls (.const c lsc) hb
        unfold norm at hn
        rw [whnfFuel_fuel0] at hw
        rw [hw] at hn
        exact Option.noConfusion hn
      | succ j =>
        rw [norm_const_delta_ctor E j r c ls lsc hb hnone] at hn
        exact (Option.some.inj hn).symm

/- A constructor applied to one literal. The head is rigid, so `whnfFuel`
   returns the application, and `norm` normalizes the literal argument.
   Not AdeqConstDelta. -/
theorem norm_const_delta_app_lit (E : ResolvedEnv) (k r c nlit : Nat) (ls lsc : List Level)
    (hb : transparentBody E r ls = some (.app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit)))
    (hnone : transparentBody E c lsc = none) :
    norm E (k + 3) (.const r ls) = some (.app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit)) := by
  have hwb : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit)) =
      some (.app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit)) := by
    simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine, hnone]
  have hlit : norm E (k + 2) (.lit nlit) = some (.lit nlit) := by
    have hwlit : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.lit nlit) = some (.lit nlit) := by
      simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine]
    unfold norm
    rw [hwlit]
  unfold norm
  rw [whnf_const_delta E (k + 1) r ls (.app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit)) hb, hwb]
  have hsp : appsSpine (.app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit)) =
      (.const c lsc, [.lit nlit]) := by
    simp only [appsSpine, List.nil_append]
  simp only [hsp]
  have hm : [.lit nlit].mapM (norm E (k + 2)) = some [.lit nlit] := by
    rw [List.mapM_cons, hlit, List.mapM_nil]
    rfl
  simp only [hm, foldApps]

theorem norm_const_app_lit_val (E : ResolvedEnv) (lf r c nlit : Nat) (ls lsc : List Level)
    {v : Expr Nat}
    (hb : transparentBody E r ls = some (.app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit)))
    (hnone : transparentBody E c lsc = none)
    (hn : norm E lf (.const r ls) = some v) :
    v = .app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit) := by
  cases lf with
  | zero => exact Option.noConfusion hn
  | succ lf =>
    cases lf with
    | zero =>
      unfold norm at hn
      rw [whnfFuel_fuel0] at hn
      exact Option.noConfusion hn
    | succ lf =>
      cases lf with
      | zero =>
        have hw := whnf_const_delta E 0 r ls (.app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit)) hb
        unfold norm at hn
        rw [whnfFuel_fuel0] at hw
        rw [hw] at hn
        exact Option.noConfusion hn
      | succ j =>
        rw [norm_const_delta_app_lit E j r c nlit ls lsc hb hnone] at hn
        exact (Option.some.inj hn).symm

/- One more transparent constant in front of a literal. Each δ spends one
   fuel in `whnfFuel`, and `norm` spends one more, so the literal appears
   at fuel `k + 4`. -/
theorem norm_const_delta_lit_via (E : ResolvedEnv) (k r m nlit : Nat) (ls lsm : List Level)
    (hb : transparentBody E r ls = some (.const m lsm))
    (hm : transparentBody E m lsm = some (.lit nlit)) :
    norm E (k + 4) (.const r ls) = some (.lit nlit) := by
  have hl : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.lit nlit) = some (.lit nlit) := by
    simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine]
  have hw : whnfFuel E (k + 2) (.const m lsm) = some (.lit nlit) := by
    rw [whnf_const_delta E (k + 1) m lsm (.lit nlit) hm, hl]
  unfold norm
  rw [whnf_const_delta E (k + 2) r ls (.const m lsm) hb, hw]

theorem norm_const_lit_via_val (E : ResolvedEnv) (lf r m nlit : Nat) (ls lsm : List Level)
    {v : Expr Nat}
    (hb : transparentBody E r ls = some (.const m lsm))
    (hm : transparentBody E m lsm = some (.lit nlit))
    (hn : norm E lf (.const r ls) = some v) : v = .lit nlit := by
  cases lf with
  | zero => exact Option.noConfusion hn
  | succ lf =>
    cases lf with
    | zero =>
      unfold norm at hn
      rw [whnfFuel_fuel0] at hn
      exact Option.noConfusion hn
    | succ lf =>
      cases lf with
      | zero =>
        have hw := whnf_const_delta E 0 r ls (.const m lsm) hb
        unfold norm at hn
        rw [whnfFuel_fuel0] at hw
        rw [hw] at hn
        exact Option.noConfusion hn
      | succ lf =>
        cases lf with
        | zero =>
          have hw := whnf_const_delta E 1 r ls (.const m lsm) hb
          have hw2 := whnf_const_delta E 0 m lsm (.lit nlit) hm
          unfold norm at hn
          rw [whnfFuel_fuel0] at hw2
          rw [hw2] at hw
          rw [hw] at hn
          exact Option.noConfusion hn
        | succ j =>
          rw [norm_const_delta_lit_via E j r m nlit ls lsm hb hm] at hn
          exact (Option.some.inj hn).symm

theorem runWith_mono (bind : DVal → List DVal → List DVal) (code : List Code) :
    ∀ (F F' : Nat) (env : List DVal) (d : DExpr) (v : DVal), F ≤ F' →
      runWith bind code F env d = some v → runWith bind code F' env d = some v := by
  intro F
  induction F with
  | zero => intro F' env d v _ h; exact Option.noConfusion h
  | succ F ih =>
    intro F' env d v hF h
    obtain ⟨F'', rfl⟩ : ∃ F'', F' = F'' + 1 := ⟨F' - 1, by omega⟩
    have hF' : F ≤ F'' := by omega
    cases d with
    | var _ => exact h
    | box => exact h
    | lit _ => exact h
    | ctor _ => exact h
    | rigid _ => exact h
    | clo _ _ => exact h
    | glob l =>
        change (match code.get? l with
          | some c => runWith bind code F [] c.body
          | none => none) = some v at h
        change (match code.get? l with
          | some c => runWith bind code F'' [] c.body
          | none => none) = some v
        cases hc : code.get? l with
        | none => rw [hc] at h; exact Option.noConfusion h
        | some c => rw [hc] at h; exact ih _ _ _ _ hF' h
    | apply g a =>
        simp only [runWith] at h ⊢
        cases hg : runWith bind code F env g with
        | none => rw [hg] at h; exact Option.noConfusion h
        | some gv =>
          cases ha : runWith bind code F env a with
          | none => rw [hg, ha] at h; cases gv <;> exact Option.noConfusion h
          | some av =>
            rw [hg, ha] at h
            rw [ih _ _ _ _ hF' hg, ih _ _ _ _ hF' ha]
            cases gv with
            | clo l caps =>
                change (match code.get? l with
                  | some c => runWith bind code F (bind av caps) c.body
                  | none => none) = some v at h
                change (match code.get? l with
                  | some c => runWith bind code F'' (bind av caps) c.body
                  | none => none) = some v
                cases hc : code.get? l with
                | none => rw [hc] at h; exact Option.noConfusion h
                | some c => rw [hc] at h; exact ih _ _ _ _ hF' h
            | _ => exact h
    | letE x b =>
        simp only [runWith] at h ⊢
        cases hx : runWith bind code F env x with
        | none => rw [hx] at h; exact Option.noConfusion h
        | some xv => rw [hx] at h; rw [ih _ _ _ _ hF' hx]; exact ih _ _ _ _ hF' h

theorem run_mono (code : List Code) (F F' : Nat) (env : List DVal) (d : DExpr) (v : DVal)
    (hF : F ≤ F') (h : run code F env d = some v) : run code F' env d = some v :=
  runWith_mono bindArg code F F' env d v hF h

/-! ### Emission and the whole lowering keep a successful result at every larger fuel

`emitWith` fails only by emitting `refuse` where its fuel runs out, and every node it
emits is evaluated (it emits no branching construct), so if evalLF of the emitted term
gives a value, the term emitted at a larger fuel gives the same value
(`emitWith_evalStable`). With `erase_mono` and `run_mono` this gives
`lowerF_evalStable`: a value evalLF gets from the lowering at fuel `F` it gets, at the
same scm fuel, from the lowering at every `F' ≥ F`. So for the reference family the
statement's eventual lowering fuel follows from a single one
(`lowerF_eventual_of_exists`, `good_of_exists`), and `FuelStable` separates it from a
lowering whose output depends on the fuel (`fuelParity_not_fuelStable`). -/

theorem eval_refuse_ne {S : SigTable} {G : Ctx} {t : BootTy} (progs : Programs S S)
    (lf : Nat) (env : EnvV) (w : Val) :
    Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf env (refuse (S := S) (G := G) (t := t))
      ≠ some w := by
  intro h
  have h2 : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf env
      (refuse (S := S) (G := G) (t := t)) = none := eval_refuse progs lf env
  rw [h2] at h
  exact Option.noConfusion h

theorem eval_cast_eq {S : SigTable} {G : Ctx} {t t' : BootTy} (progs : Programs S S)
    (lf : Nat) (env : EnvV) (h : t = t') (x : BootExpr S G t) :
    Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf env (cast (congrArg (BootExpr S G) h) x)
      = Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf env x := by
  subst h; rfl

/-- a list of emitted elements: if every element's value is kept when its emitter is
    replaced, the list's value is kept. -/
theorem eval_listOf_map {S : SigTable} {G : Ctx} {τ : BootTy} (progs : Programs S S)
    (lf : Nat) (env : EnvV) (g g' : DVal → BootExpr S G τ) :
    ∀ (xs : List DVal) (w : Val),
      (∀ x, x ∈ xs → ∀ u, Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf env (g x) = some u →
        Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf env (g' x) = some u) →
      Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf env (listOf (xs.map g)) = some w →
      Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf env (listOf (xs.map g')) = some w
  | [], _, _, h => h
  | x :: xs, w, hg, h => by
    cases lf with
    | zero => rw [eval_fuel0] at h; exact Option.noConfusion h
    | succ m =>
      change Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs (m + 1) env
        (BootExpr.listAppend (BootExpr.listSingleton (g x)) (listOf (xs.map g))) = some w at h
      change Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs (m + 1) env
        (BootExpr.listAppend (BootExpr.listSingleton (g' x)) (listOf (xs.map g'))) = some w
      simp only [Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval] at h ⊢
      cases hx : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs (m + 1) env (g x) with
      | none => rw [hx] at h; exact Option.noConfusion h
      | some xv =>
        cases hr : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs (m + 1) env
            (listOf (xs.map g)) with
        | none => rw [hx, hr] at h; exact Option.noConfusion h
        | some rv =>
          rw [hg x (List.mem_cons_self x xs) xv hx,
            eval_listOf_map progs (m + 1) env g g' xs rv
              (fun y hy => hg y (List.mem_cons_of_mem x hy)) hr]
          rw [hx, hr] at h
          exact h

theorem emitWith_evalStable (fields : List DVal → List DVal) {S : SigTable} {G : Ctx}
    (progs : Programs S S) (lf : Nat) (env : EnvV) :
    ∀ (f f' : Nat) (t : BootTy) (v : DVal) (w : Val), f ≤ f' →
      Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf env
        (emitWith fields (S := S) (G := G) f t v) = some w →
      Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf env
        (emitWith fields (S := S) (G := G) f' t v) = some w := by
  intro f
  induction f with
  | zero =>
    intro f' t v w _ h
    have h0 : emitWith fields (S := S) (G := G) 0 t v = refuse := by
      cases t <;> cases v <;> rfl
    rw [h0] at h
    exact absurd h (eval_refuse_ne progs lf env w)
  | succ f ih =>
    intro f' t v w hf h
    obtain ⟨f'', rfl⟩ : ∃ f'', f' = f'' + 1 := ⟨f' - 1, by omega⟩
    have hf' : f ≤ f'' := by omega
    cases t <;> cases v <;> try exact h
    rename_i ts r args
    simp only [emitWith] at h ⊢
    by_cases hr : r < ts.length
    · rw [dif_pos hr] at h ⊢
      split
      · rename_i τ' hτ'
        split at h
        · rename_i τ hτ
          have hττ : τ' = τ := by rw [hτ] at hτ'; exact (BootTy.list.inj hτ').symm
          subst hττ
          cases lf with
          | zero => rw [eval_fuel0] at h; exact Option.noConfusion h
          | succ m =>
            simp only [Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval] at h ⊢
            rw [eval_cast_eq progs (m + 1) env hτ.symm] at h ⊢
            cases hl : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs (m + 1) env
                (listOf ((fields args).map (emitWith fields (S := S) (G := G) f τ'))) with
            | none => rw [hl] at h; exact Option.noConfusion h
            | some lv =>
              rw [eval_listOf_map progs (m + 1) env _ _ (fields args) lv
                (fun x _ u hu => ih f'' τ' x u hf' hu) hl]
              rw [hl] at h
              exact h
        · exact absurd h (eval_refuse_ne progs lf env w)
      · split at h
        · rename_i hn τ hτ
          exact absurd hτ (hn τ)
        · exact absurd h (eval_refuse_ne progs lf env w)
    · rw [dif_neg hr] at h
      exact absurd h (eval_refuse_ne progs lf env w)

/- Eval of the constant at fuel `F + 1` is eval of the body at fuel `F`, when the
   constant is relevant. Erasure agrees by `erase_const_delta`; `run` and `emit`
   keep a value at the larger fuel. -/
theorem lowerF_const_delta_eval {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) (E : ResolvedEnv)
    (n F r lf : Nat) (ls : List Level) (b : Expr Nat) (t : BootTy) (w : Val)
    (hirr : irrelevant E n [] (.const r ls) = false)
    (hb : transparentBody E r ls = some b)
    (h : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf [] (lowerF E n F (S := S) t b)
      = some w) :
    Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf []
      (lowerF E n (F + 1) (S := S) t (.const r ls)) = some w := by
  unfold lowerF pipeline at h ⊢
  cases he : erase E n F [] b with
  | none =>
    simp only [he] at h
    exact absurd h (eval_refuse_ne progs lf [] w)
  | some l =>
    simp only [he] at h
    have he' := (erase_const_delta E n F r ls b hirr hb).trans he
    simp only [he']
    cases hr : run (defunc l).2 F [] (defunc l).1 with
    | none =>
      simp only [hr] at h
      exact absurd h (eval_refuse_ne progs lf [] w)
    | some v =>
      simp only [hr] at h
      have hr' := run_mono (defunc l).2 F (F + 1) [] (defunc l).1 v (Nat.le_succ F) hr
      simp only [hr']
      exact emitWith_evalStable relevantArgs progs lf [] F (F + 1) t v w (Nat.le_succ F) h

theorem lowerF_evalStable {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) (E : ResolvedEnv)
    (n F F' : Nat) (t : BootTy) (e : Expr Nat) (lf : Nat) (w : Val) (hF : F ≤ F')
    (h : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf [] (lowerF E n F (S := S) t e)
      = some w) :
    Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf [] (lowerF E n F' (S := S) t e)
      = some w := by
  unfold lowerF pipeline at h ⊢
  cases he : erase E n F [] e with
  | none =>
    simp only [he] at h
    exact absurd h (eval_refuse_ne progs lf [] w)
  | some l =>
    simp only [he] at h
    simp only [erase_mono E n F F' [] e l hF he]
    cases hr : run (defunc l).2 F [] (defunc l).1 with
    | none =>
      simp only [hr] at h
      exact absurd h (eval_refuse_ne progs lf [] w)
    | some v =>
      simp only [hr] at h
      simp only [run_mono _ F F' [] _ v hF hr]
      exact emitWith_evalStable relevantArgs progs lf [] F F' t v w hF h

/-- for the reference family, one lowering fuel that works gives the statement's
    eventual one. -/
theorem lowerF_eventual_of_exists {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) (E : ResolvedEnv)
    (n : Nat) (t : BootTy) (e : Expr Nat) (w : Val)
    (h : ∃ F lf, Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf [] (lowerF E n F (S := S) t e)
      = some w) :
    ∃ F₀, ∀ F, F₀ ≤ F → ∃ lf,
      Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf [] (lowerF E n F (S := S) t e) = some w := by
  obtain ⟨F, lf, h⟩ := h
  exact ⟨F, fun F' hF => ⟨lf, lowerF_evalStable progs E n F F' t e lf w hF h⟩⟩

/-- `Good` (the per-term body of the statement) from a single lowering fuel: the form the
    open const/app/letE cases can be proved in. -/
theorem goodWfSameTy_of_exists {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) (E : ResolvedEnv) (n : Nat)
    (e : Expr Nat)
    (h : ∀ (lf fv : Nat) (T v : Expr Nat) (t : BootTy) (w : Val),
      BodiesTyped E n →
      inferT E n [] e = some T → DataTy E T →
      norm E lf e = some v → scmValOf E fv v = some w →
      relevantSpine E n fv v = true → irrelevant E n [] v = false → valFits fv t w = true →
      inferT E n [] v = some T →
      Erasable E n e →
      ∃ F lf', Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf' [] (lowerF E n F (S := S) t e)
        = some w) :
    GoodWfSameTy progs E n e := by
  intro lf fv T v t w h0 h1 h2 h3 h4 h5 h7 h6 h8 h9
  exact lowerF_eventual_of_exists progs E n t e w (h lf fv T v t w h0 h1 h2 h3 h4 h5 h7 h6 h8 h9)

theorem good_of_exists {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) (E : ResolvedEnv) (n : Nat)
    (e : Expr Nat)
    (h : ∀ (lf fv : Nat) (T v : Expr Nat) (t : BootTy) (w : Val),
      BodiesTyped E n →
      inferT E n [] e = some T → DataTy E T →
      norm E lf e = some v → scmValOf E fv v = some w →
      relevantSpine E n fv v = true → irrelevant E n [] v = false → valFits fv t w = true →
      inferT E n [] v = some T →
      Erasable E n e →
      ∃ F lf', Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf' [] (lowerF E n F (S := S) t e)
        = some w) :
    Good progs E n e :=
  good_of_goodWfSameTy progs E n e (goodWfSameTy_of_exists progs E n e h)

/- A transparent constant whose body is a literal denotes that literal.
   This is the literal slice of `AdeqConstDelta`, not the whole statement:
   `Good`'s irrelevance premise is about the value, and the value is the
   literal, so relevance of the constant is a separate hypothesis. -/
theorem good_const_delta_lit {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n r k : Nat) (ls : List Level)
    (hb : transparentBody E r ls = some (.lit k))
    (hirr : irrelevant E n [] (.const r ls) = false) :
    Good progs E n (.const r ls) := by
  refine good_of_exists progs E n (.const r ls) ?_
  intro lf fv T v t w _ _ _ hn hs _ _ hf _ _
  have hv := norm_const_lit_val E lf r k ls hb hn
  subst hv
  cases fv with
  | zero => exact Option.noConfusion hs
  | succ m =>
    have hs2 : scmValOf E (m + 1) (.lit k) = some (.int (Int.ofNat k)) := rfl
    rw [hs2] at hs
    cases hs
    cases t
    case i64 =>
      have hk : inI64Range (Int.ofNat k) = true := hf
      have hbody : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs 1 []
          (lowerF E n (0 + 1) (S := S) .i64 (.lit k)) = some (.int (Int.ofNat k)) := by
        rw [lowerF_lit, if_pos hk]
        exact eval_litI progs (Int.ofNat k) hk
      exact ⟨2, 1, lowerF_const_delta_eval progs E n 1 r 1 ls (.lit k) .i64
        (.int (Int.ofNat k)) hirr hb hbody⟩
    all_goals cases hf

/- The same literal, behind one more transparent constant. Each constant
   needs its own relevance hypothesis. This is not `AdeqConstDelta`. -/
theorem good_const_delta_lit_via {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n r m k : Nat) (ls lsm : List Level)
    (hb : transparentBody E r ls = some (.const m lsm))
    (hm : transparentBody E m lsm = some (.lit k))
    (hirr : irrelevant E n [] (.const r ls) = false)
    (hirrm : irrelevant E n [] (.const m lsm) = false) :
    Good progs E n (.const r ls) := by
  refine good_of_exists progs E n (.const r ls) ?_
  intro lf fv T v t w _ _ _ hn hs _ _ hf _ _
  have hv := norm_const_lit_via_val E lf r m k ls lsm hb hm hn
  subst hv
  cases fv with
  | zero => exact Option.noConfusion hs
  | succ q =>
    have hs2 : scmValOf E (q + 1) (.lit k) = some (.int (Int.ofNat k)) := rfl
    rw [hs2] at hs
    cases hs
    cases t
    case i64 =>
      have hk : inI64Range (Int.ofNat k) = true := hf
      have hlit : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs 1 []
          (lowerF E n (0 + 1) (S := S) .i64 (.lit k)) = some (.int (Int.ofNat k)) := by
        rw [lowerF_lit, if_pos hk]
        exact eval_litI progs (Int.ofNat k) hk
      have hmid := lowerF_const_delta_eval progs E n 1 m 1 lsm (.lit k) .i64
        (.int (Int.ofNat k)) hirrm hm hlit
      exact ⟨3, 1, lowerF_const_delta_eval progs E n 2 r 1 ls (.const m lsm) .i64
        (.int (Int.ofNat k)) hirr hb hmid⟩
    all_goals cases hf

/- A transparent constant whose body is a sort has no scm value.
   `AdeqConstDelta` still quantifies over every body. -/
theorem good_const_delta_sort {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n r : Nat) (ls : List Level) (u : Level)
    (hb : transparentBody E r ls = some (.sort u)) :
    Good progs E n (.const r ls) := by
  refine good_of_exists progs E n (.const r ls) ?_
  intro lf fv T v t w _ _ _ hn hs _ _ _ _ _
  rw [norm_const_sort_val E lf r ls u hb hn, scmValOf_sort] at hs
  exact Option.noConfusion hs

/- A transparent constant whose body is a bound variable, a Π, or a λ has
   no scm value. None of these is `AdeqConstDelta`. -/
theorem good_const_delta_bvar {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n r i : Nat) (ls : List Level)
    (hb : transparentBody E r ls = some (.bvar i)) :
    Good progs E n (.const r ls) := by
  refine good_of_exists progs E n (.const r ls) ?_
  intro lf fv T v t w _ _ _ hn hs _ _ _ _ _
  rw [norm_const_bvar_val E lf r i ls hb hn, scmValOf_bvar] at hs
  exact Option.noConfusion hs

theorem good_const_delta_pi {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n r : Nat) (ls : List Level) (A B : Expr Nat)
    (hb : transparentBody E r ls = some (.pi A B)) :
    Good progs E n (.const r ls) := by
  refine good_of_exists progs E n (.const r ls) ?_
  intro lf fv T v t w _ _ _ hn hs _ _ _ _ _
  obtain ⟨A', B', hv⟩ := norm_const_pi_val E lf r ls A B hb hn
  rw [hv, scmValOf_pi] at hs
  exact Option.noConfusion hs

theorem good_const_delta_lam {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n r : Nat) (ls : List Level) (A b : Expr Nat)
    (hb : transparentBody E r ls = some (.lam A b)) :
    Good progs E n (.const r ls) := by
  refine good_of_exists progs E n (.const r ls) ?_
  intro lf fv T v t w _ _ _ hn hs _ _ _ _ _
  obtain ⟨A', b', hv⟩ := norm_const_lam_val E lf r ls A b hb hn
  rw [hv, scmValOf_lam] at hs
  exact Option.noConfusion hs

/-! ### The const case, split: heads proved, δ stated

`AdeqConst` follows from `AdeqConstHead` (a constant with no transparent body:
constructor, axiom, opaque, recursor; `norm` leaves it, erasure keeps it as `ctor`/`rigid`)
and `AdeqConstDelta` (a transparent constant: its value is its unfolded body's,
under `EnvClosed`). `not_adeqConstDelta` refutes the statement without
`EnvClosed`. -/

def AdeqConstHead {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) : Prop :=
  ∀ E n r ls, transparentBody E r ls = none → Good progs E n (.const r ls)
def AdeqConstDelta {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) : Prop :=
  ∀ E n r ls b, EnvWf E →
    transparentBody E r ls = some b → Good progs E n (.const r ls)

theorem adeqConst_of_split {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (hh : AdeqConstHead progs) (hd : AdeqConstDelta progs) : AdeqConst progs := by
  intro E n r ls hE
  cases hb : transparentBody E r ls with
  | none => exact hh E n r ls hb
  | some b => exact hd E n r ls b hE hb

theorem norm_const_head {E : ResolvedEnv} {lf r : Nat} {ls : List Level} {v : Expr Nat}
    (hb : transparentBody E r ls = none) (h : norm E lf (.const r ls) = some v) :
    v = .const r ls := by
  have key : ∀ k, whnfFuel E k (.const r ls) = some (.const r ls) →
      norm E (k + 1) (.const r ls) = some (.const r ls) := by
    intro k hk
    rw [norm, hk]
    try rfl
  match lf, h with
  | 0, h => exact Option.noConfusion h
  | 1, h => exact Option.noConfusion h
  | j + 2, h =>
      have hw : whnfFuel E (j + 1) (.const r ls) = some (.const r ls) := by
        change (match transparentBody E r ls with
          | some body => whnfFuel E j (foldApps body [])
          | none => some (.const r ls)) = some (.const r ls)
        rw [hb]
      have h2 : norm E (j + 2) (.const r ls) = some (.const r ls) := key (j + 1) hw
      rw [h2] at h
      exact (Option.some.inj h).symm

theorem list_get?_some {α : Type} : ∀ (ts : List α) (r : Nat) (x : α),
    ts.get? r = some x → ∃ h : r < ts.length, ts.get ⟨r, h⟩ = x
  | [], _, _, h => Option.noConfusion h
  | _ :: _, 0, _, h => ⟨Nat.zero_lt_succ _, Option.some.inj h⟩
  | _ :: ys, k + 1, x, h =>
      let ⟨hk, he⟩ := list_get?_some ys k x h
      ⟨Nat.succ_lt_succ hk, he⟩

/-- the head case: a constant with no transparent body whose value is data is a nullary
    constructor, erased to `ctor r`, run to `ctor r []`, emitted as summand `r` with no
    fields; evalLF gives `.inj r (.list [])` at scm fuel 1, from lowering fuel 1 on. -/
theorem adeqConstHead {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) : AdeqConstHead progs := by
  intro E n r ls hb lf fv T v t w _ _ _ hn hs _ hroot hf _ _
  have hv := norm_const_head hb hn
  subst hv
  cases fv with
  | zero => exact Option.noConfusion hs
  | succ m =>
    have hs' : (match E.members r with
        | some mm => if mm.mclass = .constructorM then some (Val.inj r (.list [])) else none
        | none => none) = some w := hs
    cases hm : E.members r with
    | none => rw [hm] at hs'; exact Option.noConfusion hs'
    | some mm =>
      rw [hm] at hs'
      by_cases hc : mm.mclass = .constructorM
      · simp [hc] at hs'
        subst hs'
        cases t with
        | sum ts =>
          have hf' : (match ts.get? r with
              | some (.list τ) => ([] : List Val).all (valFits m τ)
              | _ => false) = true := hf
          split at hf'
          · rename_i τ hg
            obtain ⟨hlt, hget⟩ := list_get?_some ts r _ hg
            have hctor : isCtor E r = true := by simp [isCtor, hm, hc]
            refine ⟨1, fun F hF => ⟨1, ?_⟩⟩
            obtain ⟨F', rfl⟩ : ∃ F', F = F' + 1 := ⟨F - 1, by omega⟩
            have he : erase E n (F' + 1) [] (.const r ls) = some (.ctor r) := by
              simp only [erase, eraseWith, hroot, Bool.false_eq_true, if_false, noGlobals, hb,
                hctor, if_true]
            have hlow : lowerF E n (F' + 1) (S := S) (.sum ts) (.const r ls) =
                emit (F' + 1) (.sum ts) (.ctor r []) := by
              unfold lowerF pipeline
              rw [he]
              rfl
            rw [hlow]
            simp only [emit, emitWith]
            rw [dif_pos hlt]
            split
            · rename_i τ' hτ'
              simp only [Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval]
              rw [eval_cast_eq progs _ [] hτ'.symm]
              simp [Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval, relevantArgs, listOf]
            · rename_i hne
              exact absurd hget (hne τ)
          · exact Bool.noConfusion hf'
        | _ => cases hf
      · simp [hc] at hs'

/- A transparent constant whose body is a constructor head denotes that
   constructor. Relevance of the constant is a hypothesis: `Good`'s
   irrelevance premise is about the value. This is not `AdeqConstDelta`. -/
theorem good_const_delta_ctor {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n r c : Nat) (ls lsc : List Level)
    (hb : transparentBody E r ls = some (.const c lsc))
    (hnone : transparentBody E c lsc = none)
    (hirr : irrelevant E n [] (.const r ls) = false) :
    Good progs E n (.const r ls) := by
  refine good_of_exists progs E n (.const r ls) ?_
  intro lf fv T v t w _ _ _ hn hs _ hval hf _ _
  have hv := norm_const_ctor_val E lf r c ls lsc hb hnone hn
  subst hv
  cases fv with
  | zero => exact Option.noConfusion hs
  | succ m =>
    have hs' : (match E.members c with
        | some mm => if mm.mclass = .constructorM then some (Val.inj c (.list [])) else none
        | none => none) = some w := hs
    cases hm : E.members c with
    | none => rw [hm] at hs'; exact Option.noConfusion hs'
    | some mm =>
      rw [hm] at hs'
      by_cases hcm : mm.mclass = .constructorM
      · simp [hcm] at hs'
        subst hs'
        cases t with
        | sum ts =>
          have hf' : (match ts.get? c with
              | some (.list τ) => ([] : List Val).all (valFits m τ)
              | _ => false) = true := hf
          split at hf'
          · rename_i τ hg
            obtain ⟨hlt, hget⟩ := list_get?_some ts c _ hg
            have hctor : isCtor E c = true := by simp [isCtor, hm, hcm]
            have hbody : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs 1 []
                (lowerF E n 1 (S := S) (.sum ts) (.const c lsc)) =
                some (.inj c (.list [])) := by
              have he : erase E n 1 [] (.const c lsc) = some (.ctor c) := by
                simp only [erase, eraseWith, hval, Bool.false_eq_true, if_false, noGlobals,
                  hnone, hctor, if_true]
              have hlow : lowerF E n 1 (S := S) (.sum ts) (.const c lsc) =
                  emit 1 (.sum ts) (.ctor c []) := by
                unfold lowerF pipeline
                rw [he]
                rfl
              rw [hlow]
              simp only [emit, emitWith]
              rw [dif_pos hlt]
              split
              · rename_i τ' hτ'
                simp only [Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval]
                rw [eval_cast_eq progs _ [] hτ'.symm]
                simp [Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval, relevantArgs, listOf]
              · rename_i hne
                exact absurd hget (hne τ)
            exact ⟨2, 1, lowerF_const_delta_eval progs E n 1 r 1 ls (.const c lsc)
              (.sum ts) (.inj c (.list [])) hirr hb hbody⟩
          · exact Bool.noConfusion hf'
        | _ => cases hf
      · simp [hcm] at hs'

/- Emit a constructor whose one field is a literal, at lowering fuel 2
   (the field emitter needs one fuel) and scm fuel 1. -/
theorem eval_emit_ctor_lit {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) (nlit r : Nat)
    (ts : List BootTy) (hg : ts.get? r = some (.list .i64))
    (hk : inI64Range (Int.ofNat nlit) = true) :
    Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs 1 []
      (emit (S := S) (G := []) 2 (.sum ts) (.ctor r [.lit nlit])) =
      some (.inj r (.list [.int (Int.ofNat nlit)])) := by
  obtain ⟨hlt, hget⟩ := list_get?_some ts r _ hg
  simp only [emit, emitWith]
  rw [dif_pos hlt]
  split
  · rename_i τ' hτ'
    have hτi : τ' = .i64 :=
      BootTy.list.inj (hτ'.symm.trans hget)
    subst hτi
    simp only [Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval]
    rw [eval_cast_eq progs _ [] hτ'.symm]
    simp only [Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval, relevantArgs, listOf, emitWith]
    rw [if_pos hk]
    simp [Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval, hk]
    have hk' : inI64Range (↑nlit) = true := hk
    rw [if_pos hk']
    rfl
  · rename_i hne
    exact absurd hget (hne .i64)

/- A transparent constant whose body is a constructor applied to one literal.
   The head stays a constructor (`hnone`). Relevance of the outer constant is
   what `lowerF_const_delta_eval` reads; relevance of the head is what erasure
   of that head reads. The value's relevance is `Good`'s own premise.
   Not AdeqConstDelta. -/
theorem good_const_delta_app_lit {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n r c nlit : Nat) (ls lsc : List Level)
    (hb : transparentBody E r ls = some (.app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit)))
    (hnone : transparentBody E c lsc = none)
    (hirr : irrelevant E n [] (.const r ls) = false)
    (hirrC : irrelevant E n [] (.const c lsc) = false) :
    Good progs E n (.const r ls) := by
  refine good_of_exists progs E n (.const r ls) ?_
  intro lf fv T v t w _ _ _ hn hs _ hval hf _ _
  have hv := norm_const_app_lit_val E lf r c nlit ls lsc hb hnone hn
  subst hv
  cases fv with
  | zero => exact Option.noConfusion hs
  | succ m =>
    cases m with
    | zero =>
      have hs0 : scmValOf E 1 (.app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit)) = none := by
        simp only [scmValOf, appsSpine, List.nil_append, List.mapM_cons, List.mapM_nil,
          Option.bind, Option.pure_def]
        split
        · rename_i mm hm
          by_cases hc : mm.mclass = .constructorM
          · simp [hm, hc, scmValOf]
          · simp [hm, hc]
        · rename_i hm
          simp [hm]
      rw [hs0] at hs
      exact Option.noConfusion hs
    | succ q =>
      have hlitv : scmValOf E (q + 1) (.lit nlit) = some (.int (Int.ofNat nlit)) := rfl
      have hs' : (match E.members c with
          | some mm =>
              if mm.mclass = .constructorM then
                some (.inj c (.list [.int (Int.ofNat nlit)]))
              else none
          | none => none) = some w := by
        simpa [scmValOf, appsSpine, List.nil_append, List.mapM_cons, List.mapM_nil,
          hlitv, Option.bind, Option.pure_def] using hs
      cases hm : E.members c with
      | none =>
        rw [hm] at hs'
        exact Option.noConfusion hs'
      | some mm =>
        rw [hm] at hs'
        by_cases hcm : mm.mclass = .constructorM
        · simp [hcm] at hs'
          subst hs'
          cases t with
          | sum ts =>
            have hf' : (match ts.get? c with
                | some (.list τ) => ([.int (Int.ofNat nlit)] : List Val).all (valFits (q + 1) τ)
                | _ => false) = true := hf
            split at hf'
            · rename_i τ hg
              cases τ with
              | i64 =>
                have hk : inI64Range (Int.ofNat nlit) = true := by
                  simp only [valFits, List.all_cons, List.all_nil, Bool.and_true] at hf'
                  exact hf'
                have hctor : isCtor E c = true := by simp [isCtor, hm, hcm]
                have he : erase E n 2 [] (.app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit)) =
                    some (.app (.ctor c) (.lit nlit)) := by
                  simp only [erase, eraseWith, hval, hirrC, Bool.false_eq_true, if_false,
                    noGlobals, hnone, hctor, if_true]
                have hlow : lowerF E n 2 (S := S) (.sum ts) (.app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit)) =
                    emit 2 (.sum ts) (.ctor c [.lit nlit]) := by
                  unfold lowerF pipeline
                  rw [he]
                  rfl
                have hbody : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs 1 []
                    (lowerF E n 2 (S := S) (.sum ts) (.app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit))) =
                    some (.inj c (.list [.int (Int.ofNat nlit)])) := by
                  rw [hlow]
                  exact eval_emit_ctor_lit progs nlit c ts hg hk
                exact ⟨3, 1, lowerF_const_delta_eval progs E n 2 r 1 ls
                  (.app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit)) (.sum ts)
                  (.inj c (.list [.int (Int.ofNat nlit)])) hirr hb hbody⟩
              | bool | str | bytes | list _ | pair _ _ | sum _ | record _ | option _ | residue _ =>
                simp only [valFits, List.all_cons, List.all_nil] at hf'
                exact Bool.noConfusion hf'
            · exact Bool.noConfusion hf'
          | _ => cases hf
        · simp [hcm] at hs'

/- The application itself, not a constant in front of it. The head is rigid,
   so `whnfFuel` returns the application and `norm` normalizes the literal.
   Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem norm_app_ctor_lit (E : ResolvedEnv) (k c nlit : Nat) (lsc : List Level)
    (hnone : transparentBody E c lsc = none) :
    norm E (k + 3) (.app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit)) =
      some (.app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit)) := by
  have hwb : whnfFuel E (k + 2) (.app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit)) =
      some (.app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit)) := by
    simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine, hnone]
  have hlit : norm E (k + 2) (.lit nlit) = some (.lit nlit) := by
    have hwlit : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.lit nlit) = some (.lit nlit) := by
      simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine]
    unfold norm
    rw [hwlit]
  unfold norm
  rw [hwb]
  have hsp : appsSpine (.app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit)) =
      (.const c lsc, [.lit nlit]) := by
    simp only [appsSpine, List.nil_append]
  simp only [hsp]
  have hm : [.lit nlit].mapM (norm E (k + 2)) = some [.lit nlit] := by
    rw [List.mapM_cons, hlit, List.mapM_nil]
    rfl
  simp only [hm, foldApps]

theorem norm_app_ctor_lit_val (E : ResolvedEnv) (lf c nlit : Nat) (lsc : List Level)
    {v : Expr Nat}
    (hnone : transparentBody E c lsc = none)
    (hn : norm E lf (.app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit)) = some v) :
    v = .app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit) := by
  cases lf with
  | zero => exact Option.noConfusion hn
  | succ lf =>
    cases lf with
    | zero =>
      unfold norm at hn
      rw [whnfFuel_fuel0] at hn
      exact Option.noConfusion hn
    | succ lf =>
      cases lf with
      | zero =>
        have hwb : whnfFuel E 1 (.app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit)) =
            some (.app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit)) := by
          simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine, hnone]
        have hlit0 : norm E 1 (.lit nlit) = none := by
          unfold norm
          rw [whnfFuel_fuel0]
        unfold norm at hn
        rw [hwb] at hn
        have hsp : appsSpine (.app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit)) =
            (.const c lsc, [.lit nlit]) := by
          simp only [appsSpine, List.nil_append]
        simp only [hsp] at hn
        rw [List.mapM_cons, hlit0] at hn
        exact Option.noConfusion hn
      | succ j =>
        rw [norm_app_ctor_lit E j c nlit lsc hnone] at hn
        exact (Option.some.inj hn).symm

/- `Good` of a constructor applied to one literal. Relevance of the head is
   what erasure of that head reads. The value's relevance is `Good`'s premise.
   Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem good_app_ctor_lit {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n c nlit : Nat) (lsc : List Level)
    (hnone : transparentBody E c lsc = none)
    (hirrC : irrelevant E n [] (.const c lsc) = false) :
    Good progs E n (.app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit)) := by
  refine good_of_exists progs E n (.app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit)) ?_
  intro lf fv T v t w _ _ _ hn hs _ hval hf _ _
  have hv := norm_app_ctor_lit_val E lf c nlit lsc hnone hn
  subst hv
  cases fv with
  | zero => exact Option.noConfusion hs
  | succ m =>
    cases m with
    | zero =>
      have hs0 : scmValOf E 1 (.app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit)) = none := by
        simp only [scmValOf, appsSpine, List.nil_append, List.mapM_cons, List.mapM_nil,
          Option.bind, Option.pure_def]
        split
        · rename_i mm hm
          by_cases hc : mm.mclass = .constructorM
          · simp [hm, hc, scmValOf]
          · simp [hm, hc]
        · rename_i hm
          simp [hm]
      rw [hs0] at hs
      exact Option.noConfusion hs
    | succ q =>
      have hlitv : scmValOf E (q + 1) (.lit nlit) = some (.int (Int.ofNat nlit)) := rfl
      have hs' : (match E.members c with
          | some mm =>
              if mm.mclass = .constructorM then
                some (.inj c (.list [.int (Int.ofNat nlit)]))
              else none
          | none => none) = some w := by
        simpa [scmValOf, appsSpine, List.nil_append, List.mapM_cons, List.mapM_nil,
          hlitv, Option.bind, Option.pure_def] using hs
      cases hm : E.members c with
      | none =>
        rw [hm] at hs'
        exact Option.noConfusion hs'
      | some mm =>
        rw [hm] at hs'
        by_cases hcm : mm.mclass = .constructorM
        · simp [hcm] at hs'
          subst hs'
          cases t with
          | sum ts =>
            have hf' : (match ts.get? c with
                | some (.list τ) => ([.int (Int.ofNat nlit)] : List Val).all (valFits (q + 1) τ)
                | _ => false) = true := hf
            split at hf'
            · rename_i τ hg
              cases τ with
              | i64 =>
                have hk : inI64Range (Int.ofNat nlit) = true := by
                  simp only [valFits, List.all_cons, List.all_nil, Bool.and_true] at hf'
                  exact hf'
                have hctor : isCtor E c = true := by simp [isCtor, hm, hcm]
                have he : erase E n 2 [] (.app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit)) =
                    some (.app (.ctor c) (.lit nlit)) := by
                  simp only [erase, eraseWith, hval, hirrC, Bool.false_eq_true, if_false,
                    noGlobals, hnone, hctor, if_true]
                have hlow : lowerF E n 2 (S := S) (.sum ts) (.app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit)) =
                    emit 2 (.sum ts) (.ctor c [.lit nlit]) := by
                  unfold lowerF pipeline
                  rw [he]
                  rfl
                have hbody : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs 1 []
                    (lowerF E n 2 (S := S) (.sum ts) (.app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit))) =
                    some (.inj c (.list [.int (Int.ofNat nlit)])) := by
                  rw [hlow]
                  exact eval_emit_ctor_lit progs nlit c ts hg hk
                exact ⟨2, 1, hbody⟩
              | bool | str | bytes | list _ | pair _ _ | sum _ | record _ | option _ | residue _ =>
                simp only [valFits, List.all_cons, List.all_nil] at hf'
                exact Bool.noConfusion hf'
            · exact Bool.noConfusion hf'
          | _ => cases hf
        · simp [hcm] at hs'

/- A let whose body is a closed literal ζ-reduces to that literal.
   `instantiate` on a literal is the literal, so the bound value and the
   type do not appear in the normal form. Not AdeqLetE. -/
theorem norm_let_lit (E : ResolvedEnv) (k : Nat) (A : Expr Nat) (kv nlit : Nat) :
    norm E (k + 3) (.letE A (.lit kv) (.lit nlit)) = some (.lit nlit) := by
  have hzeta : whnfFuel E (k + 2) (.letE A (.lit kv) (.lit nlit)) =
      whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.lit nlit) := by
    simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine, foldApps, instantiate0, instantiate]
  have hlit : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.lit nlit) = some (.lit nlit) := by
    simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine]
  unfold norm
  rw [hzeta, hlit]

/- Fuels 0, 1 and 2 return `none`: `whnfFuel` of the let at fuel 1 is
   `whnfFuel` of the literal at fuel 0. -/
theorem norm_let_lit_val (E : ResolvedEnv) (lf : Nat) (A : Expr Nat) (kv nlit : Nat)
    {v : Expr Nat}
    (hn : norm E lf (.letE A (.lit kv) (.lit nlit)) = some v) :
    v = .lit nlit := by
  cases lf with
  | zero => exact Option.noConfusion hn
  | succ lf =>
    cases lf with
    | zero =>
      unfold norm at hn
      rw [whnfFuel_fuel0] at hn
      exact Option.noConfusion hn
    | succ lf =>
      cases lf with
      | zero =>
        have hzeta : whnfFuel E 1 (.letE A (.lit kv) (.lit nlit)) =
            whnfFuel E 0 (.lit nlit) := by
          simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine, foldApps, instantiate0, instantiate]
        unfold norm at hn
        rw [hzeta, whnfFuel_fuel0] at hn
        exact Option.noConfusion hn
      | succ j =>
        rw [norm_let_lit E j A kv nlit] at hn
        exact (Option.some.inj hn).symm

/- `Good` of that let. Erasure reads relevance of the let, not of the
   literal value, so that hypothesis is extra. The witness is lowering
   fuel 2 and scm fuel 1. Not AdeqLetE. -/
theorem good_let_lit {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n kv nlit : Nat) (A : Expr Nat)
    (hirr : irrelevant E n [] (.letE A (.lit kv) (.lit nlit)) = false) :
    Good progs E n (.letE A (.lit kv) (.lit nlit)) := by
  refine good_of_exists progs E n (.letE A (.lit kv) (.lit nlit)) ?_
  intro lf fv T v t w _ _ _ hn hs _ _ hf _ _
  have hv := norm_let_lit_val E lf A kv nlit hn
  subst hv
  cases fv with
  | zero => exact Option.noConfusion hs
  | succ m =>
    have hs2 : scmValOf E (m + 1) (.lit nlit) = some (.int (Int.ofNat nlit)) := rfl
    rw [hs2] at hs
    cases hs
    cases t
    case i64 =>
      have hk : inI64Range (Int.ofNat nlit) = true := hf
      have he : erase E n 2 [] (.letE A (.lit kv) (.lit nlit)) =
          some (.letE (.lit kv) (.lit nlit)) := by
        simp only [erase, eraseWith, hirr, Bool.false_eq_true, if_false]
      have hlow : lowerF E n 2 (S := S) .i64 (.letE A (.lit kv) (.lit nlit)) =
          emit 2 .i64 (.lit nlit) := by
        unfold lowerF pipeline
        rw [he]
        rfl
      have hbody : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs 1 []
          (lowerF E n 2 (S := S) .i64 (.letE A (.lit kv) (.lit nlit))) =
          some (.int (Int.ofNat nlit)) := by
        rw [hlow]
        simp only [emit, emitWith]
        rw [if_pos hk]
        exact eval_litI progs (Int.ofNat nlit) hk
      exact ⟨2, 1, hbody⟩
    all_goals cases hf

/- A let that binds a literal and whose body is `bvar 0`. ζ substitutes
   that literal. Not AdeqLetE. -/
theorem norm_let_bvar (E : ResolvedEnv) (k : Nat) (A : Expr Nat) (kv : Nat) :
    norm E (k + 3) (.letE A (.lit kv) (.bvar 0)) = some (.lit kv) := by
  have hzeta : whnfFuel E (k + 2) (.letE A (.lit kv) (.bvar 0)) =
      whnfFuel E (k + 1) (instantiate0 (.lit kv) (.bvar 0)) := by
    simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine, foldApps]
  have hsub : (instantiate0 (.lit kv) (.bvar 0) : Expr Nat) = .lit kv := rfl
  have hlit : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.lit kv) = some (.lit kv) := by
    simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine]
  unfold norm
  rw [hzeta, hsub, hlit]

/- Fuels 0, 1 and 2 return `none`. -/
theorem norm_let_bvar_val (E : ResolvedEnv) (lf : Nat) (A : Expr Nat) (kv : Nat)
    {v : Expr Nat}
    (hn : norm E lf (.letE A (.lit kv) (.bvar 0)) = some v) :
    v = .lit kv := by
  cases lf with
  | zero => exact Option.noConfusion hn
  | succ lf =>
    cases lf with
    | zero =>
      unfold norm at hn
      rw [whnfFuel_fuel0] at hn
      exact Option.noConfusion hn
    | succ lf =>
      cases lf with
      | zero =>
        have hzeta : whnfFuel E 1 (.letE A (.lit kv) (.bvar 0)) =
            whnfFuel E 0 (instantiate0 (.lit kv) (.bvar 0)) := by
          simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine, foldApps]
        unfold norm at hn
        rw [hzeta, whnfFuel_fuel0] at hn
        exact Option.noConfusion hn
      | succ j =>
        rw [norm_let_bvar E j A kv] at hn
        exact (Option.some.inj hn).symm

/- `Good` of that let. Erasure of the body reads relevance of `bvar 0`
   under the let binding, so that hypothesis is extra. Not AdeqLetE. -/
theorem good_let_bvar {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n kv : Nat) (A : Expr Nat)
    (hirr : irrelevant E n [] (.letE A (.lit kv) (.bvar 0)) = false)
    (hirrB : irrelevant E n [.letBinding A (.lit kv)] (.bvar 0) = false) :
    Good progs E n (.letE A (.lit kv) (.bvar 0)) := by
  refine good_of_exists progs E n (.letE A (.lit kv) (.bvar 0)) ?_
  intro lf fv T v t w _ _ _ hn hs _ _ hf _ _
  have hv := norm_let_bvar_val E lf A kv hn
  subst hv
  cases fv with
  | zero => exact Option.noConfusion hs
  | succ m =>
    have hs2 : scmValOf E (m + 1) (.lit kv) = some (.int (Int.ofNat kv)) := rfl
    rw [hs2] at hs
    cases hs
    cases t
    case i64 =>
      have hk : inI64Range (Int.ofNat kv) = true := hf
      have he : erase E n 2 [] (.letE A (.lit kv) (.bvar 0)) =
          some (.letE (.lit kv) (.bvar 0)) := by
        simp only [erase, eraseWith, hirr, hirrB, Bool.false_eq_true, if_false]
      have hlow : lowerF E n 2 (S := S) .i64 (.letE A (.lit kv) (.bvar 0)) =
          emit 2 .i64 (.lit kv) := by
        unfold lowerF pipeline
        rw [he]
        rfl
      have hbody : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs 1 []
          (lowerF E n 2 (S := S) .i64 (.letE A (.lit kv) (.bvar 0))) =
          some (.int (Int.ofNat kv)) := by
        rw [hlow]
        simp only [emit, emitWith]
        rw [if_pos hk]
        exact eval_litI progs (Int.ofNat kv) hk
      exact ⟨2, 1, hbody⟩
    all_goals cases hf

/- β of a λ whose body is the bound index, applied to one literal.
   `instantiate` of `bvar 0` is the argument. Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem norm_beta_lit (E : ResolvedEnv) (k : Nat) (A : Expr Nat) (kv : Nat) :
    norm E (k + 3) (.app (.lam A (.bvar 0)) (.lit kv)) = some (.lit kv) := by
  have hzeta : whnfFuel E (k + 2) (.app (.lam A (.bvar 0)) (.lit kv)) =
      whnfFuel E (k + 1) (instantiate0 (.lit kv) (.bvar 0)) := by
    simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine, foldApps, List.nil_append]
  have hsub : (instantiate0 (.lit kv) (.bvar 0) : Expr Nat) = .lit kv := rfl
  have hlit : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.lit kv) = some (.lit kv) := by
    simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine]
  unfold norm
  rw [hzeta, hsub, hlit]

/- Fuels 0, 1 and 2 return `none`. -/
theorem norm_beta_lit_val (E : ResolvedEnv) (lf : Nat) (A : Expr Nat) (kv : Nat)
    {v : Expr Nat}
    (hn : norm E lf (.app (.lam A (.bvar 0)) (.lit kv)) = some v) :
    v = .lit kv := by
  cases lf with
  | zero => exact Option.noConfusion hn
  | succ lf =>
    cases lf with
    | zero =>
      unfold norm at hn
      rw [whnfFuel_fuel0] at hn
      exact Option.noConfusion hn
    | succ lf =>
      cases lf with
      | zero =>
        have hzeta : whnfFuel E 1 (.app (.lam A (.bvar 0)) (.lit kv)) =
            whnfFuel E 0 (instantiate0 (.lit kv) (.bvar 0)) := by
          simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine, foldApps, List.nil_append]
        unfold norm at hn
        rw [hzeta, whnfFuel_fuel0] at hn
        exact Option.noConfusion hn
      | succ j =>
        rw [norm_beta_lit E j A kv] at hn
        exact (Option.some.inj hn).symm

/- `Good` of that application. Erasure of the λ reads relevance of the λ,
   and erasure of its body reads relevance of `bvar 0` under the assumption.
   The witness is lowering fuel 3: the λ body is erased one fuel under the
   application. Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem good_beta_lit {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n kv : Nat) (A : Expr Nat)
    (hirr : irrelevant E n [] (.app (.lam A (.bvar 0)) (.lit kv)) = false)
    (hirrL : irrelevant E n [] (.lam A (.bvar 0)) = false)
    (hirrB : irrelevant E n [.assumption A] (.bvar 0) = false) :
    Good progs E n (.app (.lam A (.bvar 0)) (.lit kv)) := by
  refine good_of_exists progs E n (.app (.lam A (.bvar 0)) (.lit kv)) ?_
  intro lf fv T v t w _ _ _ hn hs _ _ hf _ _
  have hv := norm_beta_lit_val E lf A kv hn
  subst hv
  cases fv with
  | zero => exact Option.noConfusion hs
  | succ m =>
    have hs2 : scmValOf E (m + 1) (.lit kv) = some (.int (Int.ofNat kv)) := rfl
    rw [hs2] at hs
    cases hs
    cases t
    case i64 =>
      have hk : inI64Range (Int.ofNat kv) = true := hf
      have he : erase E n 3 [] (.app (.lam A (.bvar 0)) (.lit kv)) =
          some (.app (.lam (.bvar 0)) (.lit kv)) := by
        simp only [erase, eraseWith, hirr, hirrL, hirrB, Bool.false_eq_true, if_false,
          Option.map]
      have hlow : lowerF E n 3 (S := S) .i64 (.app (.lam A (.bvar 0)) (.lit kv)) =
          emit 3 .i64 (.lit kv) := by
        unfold lowerF pipeline
        rw [he]
        rfl
      have hbody : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs 1 []
          (lowerF E n 3 (S := S) .i64 (.app (.lam A (.bvar 0)) (.lit kv))) =
          some (.int (Int.ofNat kv)) := by
        rw [hlow]
        simp only [emit, emitWith]
        rw [if_pos hk]
        exact eval_litI progs (Int.ofNat kv) hk
      exact ⟨3, 1, hbody⟩
    all_goals cases hf

/- β of a λ whose body is a closed literal. `instantiate` leaves the
   literal in place, so the argument does not appear in the normal form.
   Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem norm_beta_discard_lit (E : ResolvedEnv) (k : Nat) (A : Expr Nat)
    (kbody narg : Nat) :
    norm E (k + 3) (.app (.lam A (.lit kbody)) (.lit narg)) = some (.lit kbody) := by
  have hbeta : whnfFuel E (k + 2) (.app (.lam A (.lit kbody)) (.lit narg)) =
      whnfFuel E (k + 1) (instantiate0 (.lit narg) (.lit kbody)) := by
    simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine, foldApps, List.nil_append]
  have hsub : (instantiate0 (.lit narg) (.lit kbody) : Expr Nat) = .lit kbody := rfl
  have hlit : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.lit kbody) = some (.lit kbody) := by
    simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine]
  unfold norm
  rw [hbeta, hsub, hlit]

/- Fuels 0, 1 and 2 return `none`. -/
theorem norm_beta_discard_lit_val (E : ResolvedEnv) (lf : Nat) (A : Expr Nat)
    (kbody narg : Nat) {v : Expr Nat}
    (hn : norm E lf (.app (.lam A (.lit kbody)) (.lit narg)) = some v) :
    v = .lit kbody := by
  cases lf with
  | zero => exact Option.noConfusion hn
  | succ lf =>
    cases lf with
    | zero =>
      unfold norm at hn
      rw [whnfFuel_fuel0] at hn
      exact Option.noConfusion hn
    | succ lf =>
      cases lf with
      | zero =>
        have hbeta : whnfFuel E 1 (.app (.lam A (.lit kbody)) (.lit narg)) =
            whnfFuel E 0 (instantiate0 (.lit narg) (.lit kbody)) := by
          simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine, foldApps, List.nil_append]
        unfold norm at hn
        rw [hbeta, whnfFuel_fuel0] at hn
        exact Option.noConfusion hn
      | succ j =>
        rw [norm_beta_discard_lit E j A kbody narg] at hn
        exact (Option.some.inj hn).symm

/- `Good` of that application. The body literal erases as itself, and
   `run` evaluates the argument literal and then discards it
   (`run_apply_lit_body`). Relevance of the application and of the λ are
   what erasure reads. Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem good_beta_discard_lit {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n kbody narg : Nat) (A : Expr Nat)
    (hirr : irrelevant E n [] (.app (.lam A (.lit kbody)) (.lit narg)) = false)
    (hirrL : irrelevant E n [] (.lam A (.lit kbody)) = false) :
    Good progs E n (.app (.lam A (.lit kbody)) (.lit narg)) := by
  refine good_of_exists progs E n (.app (.lam A (.lit kbody)) (.lit narg)) ?_
  intro lf fv T v t w _ _ _ hn hs _ _ hf _ _
  have hv := norm_beta_discard_lit_val E lf A kbody narg hn
  subst hv
  cases fv with
  | zero => exact Option.noConfusion hs
  | succ m =>
    have hs2 : scmValOf E (m + 1) (.lit kbody) = some (.int (Int.ofNat kbody)) := rfl
    rw [hs2] at hs
    cases hs
    cases t
    case i64 =>
      have hk : inI64Range (Int.ofNat kbody) = true := hf
      have he : erase E n 3 [] (.app (.lam A (.lit kbody)) (.lit narg)) =
          some (.app (.lam (.lit kbody)) (.lit narg)) := by
        simp only [erase, eraseWith, hirr, hirrL, Bool.false_eq_true, if_false, Option.map]
      have hlow : lowerF E n 3 (S := S) .i64
          (.app (.lam A (.lit kbody)) (.lit narg)) =
          emit 3 .i64 (.lit kbody) := by
        unfold lowerF pipeline
        rw [he]
        rfl
      have hbody : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs 1 []
          (lowerF E n 3 (S := S) .i64 (.app (.lam A (.lit kbody)) (.lit narg))) =
          some (.int (Int.ofNat kbody)) := by
        rw [hlow]
        simp only [emit, emitWith]
        rw [if_pos hk]
        exact eval_litI progs (Int.ofNat kbody) hk
      exact ⟨3, 1, hbody⟩
    all_goals cases hf

/- β of a λ whose body is a closed literal, at an arbitrary argument.
   `instantiate` leaves the literal. Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem norm_beta_discard_any (E : ResolvedEnv) (k : Nat) (A arg : Expr Nat)
    (kbody : Nat) :
    norm E (k + 3) (.app (.lam A (.lit kbody)) arg) = some (.lit kbody) := by
  have hbeta : whnfFuel E (k + 2) (.app (.lam A (.lit kbody)) arg) =
      whnfFuel E (k + 1) (instantiate0 arg (.lit kbody)) := by
    simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine, foldApps, List.nil_append]
  have hsub : (instantiate0 arg (.lit kbody) : Expr Nat) = .lit kbody := rfl
  have hlit : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.lit kbody) = some (.lit kbody) := by
    simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine]
  unfold norm
  rw [hbeta, hsub, hlit]

/- Fuels 0, 1 and 2 return `none`. -/
theorem norm_beta_discard_any_val (E : ResolvedEnv) (lf : Nat) (A arg : Expr Nat)
    (kbody : Nat) {v : Expr Nat}
    (hn : norm E lf (.app (.lam A (.lit kbody)) arg) = some v) :
    v = .lit kbody := by
  cases lf with
  | zero => exact Option.noConfusion hn
  | succ lf =>
    cases lf with
    | zero =>
      unfold norm at hn
      rw [whnfFuel_fuel0] at hn
      exact Option.noConfusion hn
    | succ lf =>
      cases lf with
      | zero =>
        have hbeta : whnfFuel E 1 (.app (.lam A (.lit kbody)) arg) =
            whnfFuel E 0 (instantiate0 arg (.lit kbody)) := by
          simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine, foldApps, List.nil_append]
        unfold norm at hn
        rw [hbeta, whnfFuel_fuel0] at hn
        exact Option.noConfusion hn
      | succ j =>
        rw [norm_beta_discard_any E j A arg kbody] at hn
        exact (Option.some.inj hn).symm

/- Erasure of that β when the argument erases to `□` at fuel 2.
   The λ stays, because the application and the λ are relevant.
   Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem erase_beta_discard_box (E : ResolvedEnv) (n kbody : Nat) (A arg : Expr Nat)
    (hirr : irrelevant E n [] (.app (.lam A (.lit kbody)) arg) = false)
    (hirrL : irrelevant E n [] (.lam A (.lit kbody)) = false)
    (harg : erase E n 2 [] arg = some .box) :
    erase E n 3 [] (.app (.lam A (.lit kbody)) arg) =
      some (.app (.lam (.lit kbody)) .box) := by
  have hbody : erase E n 1 (.assumption A :: []) (.lit kbody) = some (.lit kbody) := rfl
  have hlam : erase E n 2 [] (.lam A (.lit kbody)) = some (.lam (.lit kbody)) := by
    rw [erase_lam_keep E n 1 [] A (.lit kbody) hirrL, hbody]
    rfl
  rw [erase_app_keep E n 2 [] (.lam A (.lit kbody)) arg hirr, hlam, harg]

/- `Good` of that β. `run` evaluates the boxed argument and discards it.
   Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem good_beta_discard_box {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n kbody : Nat) (A arg : Expr Nat)
    (hirr : irrelevant E n [] (.app (.lam A (.lit kbody)) arg) = false)
    (hirrL : irrelevant E n [] (.lam A (.lit kbody)) = false)
    (harg : erase E n 2 [] arg = some .box) :
    Good progs E n (.app (.lam A (.lit kbody)) arg) := by
  refine good_of_exists progs E n (.app (.lam A (.lit kbody)) arg) ?_
  intro lf fv T v t w _ _ _ hn hs _ _ hf _ _
  have hv := norm_beta_discard_any_val E lf A arg kbody hn
  subst hv
  cases fv with
  | zero => exact Option.noConfusion hs
  | succ m =>
    have hs2 : scmValOf E (m + 1) (.lit kbody) = some (.int (Int.ofNat kbody)) := rfl
    rw [hs2] at hs
    cases hs
    cases t
    case i64 =>
      have hk : inI64Range (Int.ofNat kbody) = true := hf
      have he := erase_beta_discard_box E n kbody A arg hirr hirrL harg
      have hlow : lowerF E n 3 (S := S) .i64
          (.app (.lam A (.lit kbody)) arg) =
          emit 3 .i64 (.lit kbody) := by
        unfold lowerF pipeline
        rw [he]
        rfl
      have hbody : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs 1 []
          (lowerF E n 3 (S := S) .i64 (.app (.lam A (.lit kbody)) arg)) =
          some (.int (Int.ofNat kbody)) := by
        rw [hlow]
        simp only [emit, emitWith]
        rw [if_pos hk]
        exact eval_litI progs (Int.ofNat kbody) hk
      exact ⟨3, 1, hbody⟩
    all_goals cases hf

/- A sort erases to `□`, so the literal-body β that receives it is `Good`.
   Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem good_beta_discard_sort {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n kbody : Nat) (A : Expr Nat) (l : Level)
    (hirr : irrelevant E n [] (.app (.lam A (.lit kbody)) (.sort l)) = false)
    (hirrL : irrelevant E n [] (.lam A (.lit kbody)) = false) :
    Good progs E n (.app (.lam A (.lit kbody)) (.sort l)) :=
  good_beta_discard_box progs E n kbody A (.sort l) hirr hirrL rfl

/- A Π erases to `□`. Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem good_beta_discard_pi {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n kbody : Nat) (A B C : Expr Nat)
    (hirr : irrelevant E n [] (.app (.lam A (.lit kbody)) (.pi B C)) = false)
    (hirrL : irrelevant E n [] (.lam A (.lit kbody)) = false) :
    Good progs E n (.app (.lam A (.lit kbody)) (.pi B C)) :=
  good_beta_discard_box progs E n kbody A (.pi B C) hirr hirrL rfl

/- ζ whose body is a closed literal, at an arbitrary bound term.
   `instantiate` leaves the literal. Not AdeqLetE. -/
theorem norm_let_discard_any (E : ResolvedEnv) (k : Nat) (A bound : Expr Nat)
    (kbody : Nat) :
    norm E (k + 3) (.letE A bound (.lit kbody)) = some (.lit kbody) := by
  have hzeta : whnfFuel E (k + 2) (.letE A bound (.lit kbody)) =
      whnfFuel E (k + 1) (instantiate0 bound (.lit kbody)) := by
    simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine, foldApps]
  have hsub : (instantiate0 bound (.lit kbody) : Expr Nat) = .lit kbody := rfl
  have hlit : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.lit kbody) = some (.lit kbody) := by
    simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine]
  unfold norm
  rw [hzeta, hsub, hlit]

/- Fuels 0, 1 and 2 return `none`. -/
theorem norm_let_discard_any_val (E : ResolvedEnv) (lf : Nat) (A bound : Expr Nat)
    (kbody : Nat) {v : Expr Nat}
    (hn : norm E lf (.letE A bound (.lit kbody)) = some v) :
    v = .lit kbody := by
  cases lf with
  | zero => exact Option.noConfusion hn
  | succ lf =>
    cases lf with
    | zero =>
      unfold norm at hn
      rw [whnfFuel_fuel0] at hn
      exact Option.noConfusion hn
    | succ lf =>
      cases lf with
      | zero =>
        have hzeta : whnfFuel E 1 (.letE A bound (.lit kbody)) =
            whnfFuel E 0 (instantiate0 bound (.lit kbody)) := by
          simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine, foldApps]
        unfold norm at hn
        rw [hzeta, whnfFuel_fuel0] at hn
        exact Option.noConfusion hn
      | succ j =>
        rw [norm_let_discard_any E j A bound kbody] at hn
        exact (Option.some.inj hn).symm

/- Erasure of that ζ when the bound term erases to `□` at fuel 1.
   Not AdeqLetE. -/
theorem erase_let_discard_box (E : ResolvedEnv) (n kbody : Nat) (A bound : Expr Nat)
    (hirr : irrelevant E n [] (.letE A bound (.lit kbody)) = false)
    (hbound : erase E n 1 [] bound = some .box) :
    erase E n 2 [] (.letE A bound (.lit kbody)) =
      some (.letE .box (.lit kbody)) := by
  have hbody : erase E n 1 (.letBinding A bound :: []) (.lit kbody) =
      some (.lit kbody) := rfl
  rw [erase_let_keep E n 1 [] A bound (.lit kbody) hirr, hbound, hbody]

/- `Good` of that ζ. `run` evaluates the box and then the literal.
   Not AdeqLetE. -/
theorem good_let_discard_box {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n kbody : Nat) (A bound : Expr Nat)
    (hirr : irrelevant E n [] (.letE A bound (.lit kbody)) = false)
    (hbound : erase E n 1 [] bound = some .box) :
    Good progs E n (.letE A bound (.lit kbody)) := by
  refine good_of_exists progs E n (.letE A bound (.lit kbody)) ?_
  intro lf fv T v t w _ _ _ hn hs _ _ hf _ _
  have hv := norm_let_discard_any_val E lf A bound kbody hn
  subst hv
  cases fv with
  | zero => exact Option.noConfusion hs
  | succ m =>
    have hs2 : scmValOf E (m + 1) (.lit kbody) = some (.int (Int.ofNat kbody)) := rfl
    rw [hs2] at hs
    cases hs
    cases t
    case i64 =>
      have hk : inI64Range (Int.ofNat kbody) = true := hf
      have he := erase_let_discard_box E n kbody A bound hirr hbound
      have hlow : lowerF E n 2 (S := S) .i64 (.letE A bound (.lit kbody)) =
          emit 2 .i64 (.lit kbody) := by
        unfold lowerF pipeline
        rw [he]
        rfl
      have hbody : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs 1 []
          (lowerF E n 2 (S := S) .i64 (.letE A bound (.lit kbody))) =
          some (.int (Int.ofNat kbody)) := by
        rw [hlow]
        simp only [emit, emitWith]
        rw [if_pos hk]
        exact eval_litI progs (Int.ofNat kbody) hk
      exact ⟨2, 1, hbody⟩
    all_goals cases hf

theorem good_let_discard_sort {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n kbody : Nat) (A : Expr Nat) (l : Level)
    (hirr : irrelevant E n [] (.letE A (.sort l) (.lit kbody)) = false) :
    Good progs E n (.letE A (.sort l) (.lit kbody)) :=
  good_let_discard_box progs E n kbody A (.sort l) hirr rfl

theorem good_let_discard_pi {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n kbody : Nat) (A B C : Expr Nat)
    (hirr : irrelevant E n [] (.letE A (.pi B C) (.lit kbody)) = false) :
    Good progs E n (.letE A (.pi B C) (.lit kbody)) :=
  good_let_discard_box progs E n kbody A (.pi B C) hirr rfl

/- A data type is an inductive constant applied to arguments, so it is not
   an arity. `irrelevant` of a term the checker types at such a `T` is then
   only whether the type of `T` is `Prop` as written. AdeqApp, AdeqLetE and
   AdeqConstDelta read this before erasure decides `□`. Not those lemmas. -/
theorem isArity_false_of_dataTy (E : ResolvedEnv) {T : Expr Nat}
    (h : DataTy E T) : isArity T = false := by
  obtain ⟨r, ls, args, m, hs, _, _⟩ := h
  cases T with
  | sort _ =>
      simp only [appsSpine] at hs
      exact Expr.noConfusion (congrArg Prod.fst hs)
  | pi _ _ =>
      simp only [appsSpine] at hs
      exact Expr.noConfusion (congrArg Prod.fst hs)
  | bvar _ => rfl
  | const _ _ => rfl
  | app _ _ => rfl
  | lam _ _ => rfl
  | letE _ _ _ => rfl
  | lit _ => rfl

theorem irrelevant_data (E : ResolvedEnv) (n : Nat) (e T : Expr Nat)
    (hi : inferT E n [] e = some T) (hD : DataTy E T) :
    irrelevant E n [] e =
      match inferT E n [] T with
      | some U => isPropSort U
      | none => false := by
  have ha : isArity T = false := isArity_false_of_dataTy E hD
  simp only [irrelevant, hi, ha, Bool.false_or]

/- A non-literal the checker marks irrelevant erases to `□` at the next
   fuel. Sort and pi erase to `□` anyway. A literal ignores the test, so
   it is excluded. AdeqApp, AdeqLetE and AdeqConstDelta meet this before
   the relevant branch. Not those lemmas. -/
theorem erase_box_of_irrelevant (E : ResolvedEnv) (n F : Nat) (Γ : LCtx)
    (e : Expr Nat) (h : irrelevant E n Γ e = true) (hl : ∀ k, e ≠ .lit k) :
    erase E n (F + 1) Γ e = some .box := by
  cases e with
  | lit k => exact False.elim (hl k rfl)
  | sort _ => rfl
  | pi _ _ => rfl
  | bvar _ => simp only [erase, eraseWith, h, if_true]
  | const _ _ => simp only [erase, eraseWith, h, if_true]
  | app _ _ => simp only [erase, eraseWith, h, if_true]
  | lam _ _ => simp only [erase, eraseWith, h, if_true]
  | letE _ _ _ => simp only [erase, eraseWith, h, if_true]

/- Any irrelevant non-literal argument erases to `□` at fuel 2.
   Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem good_beta_discard_irr {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n kbody : Nat) (A arg : Expr Nat)
    (hirr : irrelevant E n [] (.app (.lam A (.lit kbody)) arg) = false)
    (hirrL : irrelevant E n [] (.lam A (.lit kbody)) = false)
    (hirrA : irrelevant E n [] arg = true) (hl : ∀ k, arg ≠ .lit k) :
    Good progs E n (.app (.lam A (.lit kbody)) arg) :=
  good_beta_discard_box progs E n kbody A arg hirr hirrL
    (erase_box_of_irrelevant E n 1 [] arg hirrA hl)

/- An irrelevant non-literal bound term erases to `□` at fuel 1.
   Not AdeqLetE. -/
theorem good_let_discard_irr {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n kbody : Nat) (A bound : Expr Nat)
    (hirr : irrelevant E n [] (.letE A bound (.lit kbody)) = false)
    (hirrB : irrelevant E n [] bound = true) (hl : ∀ k, bound ≠ .lit k) :
    Good progs E n (.letE A bound (.lit kbody)) :=
  good_let_discard_box progs E n kbody A bound hirr
    (erase_box_of_irrelevant E n 0 [] bound hirrB hl)

/- `□` runs to `box` and emits `refuse` at every positive fuel. -/
theorem lowerF_of_erase_box {S : SigTable} (E : ResolvedEnv) (n F : Nat)
    (t : BootTy) (e : Expr Nat)
    (he : erase E n (F + 1) [] e = some .box) :
    lowerF E n (F + 1) (S := S) t e = refuse := by
  unfold lowerF pipeline
  rw [he]
  cases t <;> rfl

/- Every lowering fuel of an irrelevant non-literal is `refuse`.
   Fuel 0 erases to nothing, which the pipeline also refuses. -/
theorem lowerF_irrelevant_refuses {S : SigTable} (E : ResolvedEnv) (n : Nat)
    (t : BootTy) (e : Expr Nat) (h : irrelevant E n [] e = true)
    (hl : ∀ k, e ≠ .lit k) (F : Nat) :
    lowerF E n F (S := S) t e = refuse := by
  cases F with
  | zero => rfl
  | succ F =>
    exact lowerF_of_erase_box E n F t e (erase_box_of_irrelevant E n F [] e h hl)

/- Eval of that lowering is never `some w`. The conclusion of `Good` is
   false on this branch, so the three open lemmas hold here only when the
   other premises do not. Not those lemmas. -/
theorem eval_irrelevant_ne {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n : Nat) (t : BootTy) (e : Expr Nat) (w : Val)
    (h : irrelevant E n [] e = true) (hl : ∀ k, e ≠ .lit k) (F lf : Nat) :
    Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf []
      (lowerF E n F (S := S) t e) ≠ some w := by
  intro hE
  rw [lowerF_irrelevant_refuses E n t e h hl F] at hE
  exact eval_refuse_ne progs lf [] w hE

/- `irrelevant_data` on the three answers of `inferT` for the data type.
   `false` is the relevant branch (`lowerF_const_delta_eval` and the
   app and let transports read it). `true` is the refuse branch
   (`eval_irrelevant_ne`). Not AdeqConstDelta, AdeqApp or AdeqLetE. -/
theorem irrelevant_data_ff (E : ResolvedEnv) (n : Nat) (e T U : Expr Nat)
    (hi : inferT E n [] e = some T) (hD : DataTy E T)
    (hU : inferT E n [] T = some U) (hp : isPropSort U = false) :
    irrelevant E n [] e = false := by
  rw [irrelevant_data E n e T hi hD, hU]
  exact hp

theorem irrelevant_data_none (E : ResolvedEnv) (n : Nat) (e T : Expr Nat)
    (hi : inferT E n [] e = some T) (hD : DataTy E T)
    (hU : inferT E n [] T = none) :
    irrelevant E n [] e = false := by
  rw [irrelevant_data E n e T hi hD, hU]

theorem irrelevant_data_tt (E : ResolvedEnv) (n : Nat) (e T U : Expr Nat)
    (hi : inferT E n [] e = some T) (hD : DataTy E T)
    (hU : inferT E n [] T = some U) (hp : isPropSort U = true) :
    irrelevant E n [] e = true := by
  rw [irrelevant_data E n e T hi hD, hU]
  exact hp

theorem const_ne_lit (r k : Nat) (ls : List Level) :
    (.const r ls : Expr Nat) ≠ .lit k := by
  intro h
  cases h

theorem app_ne_lit (f a : Expr Nat) (k : Nat) :
    (.app f a : Expr Nat) ≠ .lit k := by
  intro h
  cases h

theorem letE_ne_lit (A v b : Expr Nat) (k : Nat) :
    (.letE A v b : Expr Nat) ≠ .lit k := by
  intro h
  cases h

theorem list_get?_append_last {α : Type} : ∀ (xs : List α) (y : α),
    (xs ++ [y]).get? xs.length = some y
  | [], _ => rfl
  | _ :: xs, y => list_get?_append_last xs y

/- `run` on `apply`, as the joint match. Same equation as the passive
   simulation (`unfold run; rfl`). The AdeqApp β arm rewrites with it. -/
theorem run_apply_eq (code : List Code) (F : Nat) (env : List DVal) (g a : DExpr) :
    run code (F + 1) env (.apply g a) =
      match run code F env g, run code F env a with
      | some (.clo l caps), some av =>
          match code.get? l with
          | some c => run code F (bindArg av caps) c.body
          | none => none
      | some (.ctor r args), some av => some (.ctor r (args ++ [av]))
      | some (.rigid r args), some av => some (.rigid r (args ++ [av]))
      | some .box, some _ => some .box
      | _, _ => none := by
  unfold run
  rfl

/- `run` on `let`, as the value match. The AdeqLetE ζ arm rewrites with it. -/
theorem run_let_eq (code : List Code) (F : Nat) (env : List DVal) (v b : DExpr) :
    run code (F + 1) env (.letE v b) =
      match run code F env v with
      | some vv => run code F (vv :: env) b
      | none => none := by
  unfold run
  rfl

theorem run_let_some (code : List Code) (F : Nat) (env : List DVal) (v b : DExpr)
    (vv : DVal) (h : run code F env v = some vv) :
    run code (F + 1) env (.letE v b) = run code F (vv :: env) b := by
  rw [run_let_eq, h]

/- A closure that captured nothing is that closure at every positive fuel.
   `mapM` of the empty capture list is `some []`. -/
theorem run_clo_nil (code : List Code) (F l : Nat) (env : List DVal) :
    run code (F + 1) env (.clo l []) = some (.clo l []) := by
  have h : run code (F + 1) env (.clo l []) =
      (([] : List Nat).mapM (fun i => env.get? i)).map (DVal.clo l) := by
    unfold run
    rfl
  rw [h, List.mapM_nil, Option.pure_def]
  rfl

/- Reynolds 1972 §8, empty capture: `apply (clo ℓ []) arg` runs the body in
   the one-element environment `[av]`. `convWith` appends that body after the
   inner code, so the label is `code.length`. Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem run_apply_clo_nil (code : List Code) (F l : Nat) (env : List DVal)
    (arg body : DExpr) (av dv : DVal)
    (hc : code.get? l = some ⟨0, body⟩)
    (ha : run code (F + 1) env arg = some av)
    (hb : run code (F + 1) [av] body = some dv) :
    run code (F + 2) env (.apply (.clo l []) arg) = some dv := by
  rw [run_apply_eq, run_clo_nil, ha]
  change (match code.get? l with
      | some c => run code (F + 1) (bindArg av []) c.body
      | none => none) = some dv
  rw [hc]
  exact hb

theorem run_apply_closed (code : List Code) (F : Nat) (env : List DVal)
    (arg body : DExpr) (av dv : DVal)
    (ha : run (code ++ [⟨0, body⟩]) (F + 1) env arg = some av)
    (hb : run (code ++ [⟨0, body⟩]) (F + 1) [av] body = some dv) :
    run (code ++ [⟨0, body⟩]) (F + 2) env
      (.apply (.clo code.length []) arg) = some dv :=
  run_apply_clo_nil (code ++ [⟨0, body⟩]) F code.length env arg body av dv
    (list_get?_append_last code ⟨0, body⟩) ha hb

/- Slot 0 of a cons environment is the head, at every positive fuel.
   Reynolds 1972 §8 reads the argument from that slot. -/
theorem run_var0 (code : List Code) (F : Nat) (env : List DVal) (a : DVal) :
    run code (F + 1) (a :: env) (.var 0) = some a := by
  unfold run
  rfl

/- ζ of the bound index: the let returns the value it bound.
   `run_let_some` steps to slot 0. Not AdeqLetE. -/
theorem run_let_id (code : List Code) (F : Nat) (env : List DVal)
    (v : DExpr) (av : DVal) (h : run code (F + 1) env v = some av) :
    run code (F + 2) env (.letE v (.var 0)) = some av := by
  rw [run_let_some code (F + 1) env v (.var 0) av h]
  exact run_var0 code F env av

/- β of a closure that captured nothing and whose body is slot 0.
   The label is 0. Reynolds 1972 §8, the identity. Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem run_apply_id (code : List Code) (F : Nat) (env : List DVal)
    (arg : DExpr) (av : DVal)
    (hc : code.get? 0 = some ⟨0, .var 0⟩)
    (ha : run code (F + 1) env arg = some av) :
    run code (F + 2) env (.apply (.clo 0 []) arg) = some av := by
  exact run_apply_clo_nil code F 0 env arg (.var 0) av av hc ha
    (run_var0 code F [] av)

/- β of a closure whose body is a literal. The argument is evaluated and
   then discarded: `run` on `.lit` does not read the environment.
   Reynolds 1972 §8. Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem run_apply_lit_body (code : List Code) (F l k : Nat) (env : List DVal)
    (arg : DExpr) (av : DVal)
    (hc : code.get? l = some ⟨0, .lit k⟩)
    (ha : run code (F + 1) env arg = some av) :
    run code (F + 2) env (.apply (.clo l []) arg) = some (.lit k) := by
  have hb : run code (F + 1) [av] (.lit k) = some (.lit k) := by
    unfold run
    rfl
  exact run_apply_clo_nil code F l env arg (.lit k) av (.lit k) hc ha hb

/- A let whose body is the bound index defunctionalizes as that let.
   The body's renaming sends slot 0 to slot 0, and it allocates no code.
   Danvy–Nielsen PPDP 2001. Not AdeqLetE. -/
theorem defunc_let_bvar0 (lv : LExpr) :
    defunc (.letE lv (.bvar 0)) =
      (DExpr.letE (defunc lv).1 (.var 0), (defunc lv).2) := rfl

/- An application of the identity λ defunctionalizes as apply of a
   closure at label 0 with an empty capture. The argument is converted
   against the one code entry that closure points at. Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem defunc_app_lam_bvar0 (la : LExpr) :
    defunc (.app (.lam (.bvar 0)) la) =
      (let q := convWith capRen id [{ ncap := 0, body := .var 0 }] la
       (DExpr.apply (DExpr.clo 0 []) q.1, q.2)) := rfl

/- ζ of `bvar 0` is the bound term, one whnf fuel earlier.
   `instantiate0` of that index is the term. Not AdeqLetE. -/
theorem whnf_let_id (E : ResolvedEnv) (k : Nat) (A v : Expr Nat) :
    whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.letE A v (.bvar 0)) = whnfFuel E k v := by
  have hzeta : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.letE A v (.bvar 0)) =
      whnfFuel E k (instantiate0 v (.bvar 0)) := by
    simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine, foldApps]
  have hsub : (instantiate0 v (.bvar 0) : Expr Nat) = v := rfl
  rw [hzeta, hsub]

/- β of the identity λ is the argument, one whnf fuel earlier.
   `[] ++ [arg]` is the cons the lam arm matches. Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem whnf_beta_id (E : ResolvedEnv) (k : Nat) (A arg : Expr Nat) :
    whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.app (.lam A (.bvar 0)) arg) = whnfFuel E k arg := by
  have hbeta : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.app (.lam A (.bvar 0)) arg) =
      whnfFuel E k (instantiate0 arg (.bvar 0)) := by
    simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine, foldApps, List.nil_append]
  have hsub : (instantiate0 arg (.bvar 0) : Expr Nat) = arg := rfl
  rw [hbeta, hsub]

/- One β step, for an arbitrary body. `foldApps` of the empty tail is the
   instantiation. Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem whnf_beta (E : ResolvedEnv) (k : Nat) (A body arg : Expr Nat) :
    whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.app (.lam A body) arg) =
      whnfFuel E k (instantiate0 arg body) := by
  simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine, foldApps, List.nil_append]

/- One ζ step, for an arbitrary body. Not AdeqLetE. -/
theorem whnf_zeta (E : ResolvedEnv) (k : Nat) (A v body : Expr Nat) :
    whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.letE A v body) =
      whnfFuel E k (instantiate0 v body) := by
  simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine, foldApps]

/- Heads `whnfFuel` does not step. Fuel 0 is `none`. -/
theorem whnf_zero_none {E : ResolvedEnv} {e v : Expr Nat}
    (h : whnfFuel E 0 e = some v) : False := by
  simp only [whnfFuel] at h
  cases h

theorem whnf_sort_self (E : ResolvedEnv) (k : Nat) (l : Level) :
    whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.sort l) = some (.sort l) := rfl

theorem whnf_lam_self (E : ResolvedEnv) (k : Nat) (A b : Expr Nat) :
    whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.lam A b) = some (.lam A b) := rfl

theorem whnf_pi_self (E : ResolvedEnv) (k : Nat) (A B : Expr Nat) :
    whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.pi A B) = some (.pi A B) := rfl

theorem whnf_bvar_self (E : ResolvedEnv) (k i : Nat) :
    whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.bvar i) = some (.bvar i) := rfl

theorem whnf_lit_self (E : ResolvedEnv) (k t : Nat) :
    whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.lit t) = some (.lit t) := rfl

/- A rigid constant is its own weak head, at every positive fuel. -/
theorem whnf_rigid_const {E : ResolvedEnv} (k r : Nat) (ls : List Level)
    (hn : transparentBody E r ls = none) :
    whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.const r ls) = some (.const r ls) := by
  simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine, hn]

/- A successful norm of the bound term is a norm of the identity let,
   one fuel later. Same shift as `norm_const_delta_of_body`. Not AdeqLetE. -/
theorem norm_let_id (E : ResolvedEnv) (k : Nat) (A v val : Expr Nat)
    (hn : norm E (k + 1) v = some val) :
    norm E (k + 2) (.letE A v (.bvar 0)) = some val := by
  cases hw : whnfFuel E k v with
  | none =>
    unfold norm at hn
    rw [hw] at hn
    exact Option.noConfusion hn
  | some w =>
    have hc : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.letE A v (.bvar 0)) = some w := by
      rw [whnf_let_id E k A v]
      exact hw
    have hb1 : whnfFuel E (k + 1) v = some w :=
      whnfFuel_mono E k v w hw
    have heq : norm E (k + 2) (.letE A v (.bvar 0)) = norm E (k + 2) v := by
      conv =>
        lhs
        unfold norm
        rw [hc]
      conv =>
        rhs
        unfold norm
        rw [hb1]
    rw [heq]
    exact norm_mono E (k + 1) v val hn

/- A successful norm of the argument is a norm of the identity β,
   one fuel later. Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem norm_beta_id (E : ResolvedEnv) (k : Nat) (A arg val : Expr Nat)
    (hn : norm E (k + 1) arg = some val) :
    norm E (k + 2) (.app (.lam A (.bvar 0)) arg) = some val := by
  cases hw : whnfFuel E k arg with
  | none =>
    unfold norm at hn
    rw [hw] at hn
    exact Option.noConfusion hn
  | some w =>
    have hc : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.app (.lam A (.bvar 0)) arg) = some w := by
      rw [whnf_beta_id E k A arg]
      exact hw
    have hb1 : whnfFuel E (k + 1) arg = some w :=
      whnfFuel_mono E k arg w hw
    have heq : norm E (k + 2) (.app (.lam A (.bvar 0)) arg) = norm E (k + 2) arg := by
      conv =>
        lhs
        unfold norm
        rw [hc]
      conv =>
        rhs
        unfold norm
        rw [hb1]
    rw [heq]
    exact norm_mono E (k + 1) arg val hn

/- Eval of a relevant let at fuel `F + 1` is eval of the emitted value of
   the two erasures' defunctionalized let, run at fuel `F`.
   `erase_let_keep` is the erasure step. Not AdeqLetE. -/
theorem lowerF_let_eval {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n F lf : Nat) (A v b : Expr Nat) (t : BootTy) (w : Val)
    (hirr : irrelevant E n [] (.letE A v b) = false)
    (lv lb : LExpr)
    (hv : erase E n F [] v = some lv)
    (hb : erase E n F (.letBinding A v :: []) b = some lb)
    (dv : DVal)
    (hr : run (defunc (.letE lv lb)).2 F [] (defunc (.letE lv lb)).1 = some dv)
    (he : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf []
        (emit (S := S) (G := []) F t dv) = some w) :
    Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf []
      (lowerF E n (F + 1) (S := S) t (.letE A v b)) = some w := by
  unfold lowerF pipeline
  have hee : erase E n (F + 1) [] (.letE A v b) = some (.letE lv lb) := by
    simp only [erase_let_keep E n F [] A v b hirr, hv, hb]
  simp only [hee]
  have hr' := run_mono (defunc (.letE lv lb)).2 F (F + 1) []
      (defunc (.letE lv lb)).1 dv (Nat.le_succ F) hr
  simp only [hr']
  exact emitWith_evalStable relevantArgs progs lf [] F (F + 1) t dv w
    (Nat.le_succ F) he

/- Eval of a relevant application at fuel `F + 1` is eval of the emitted
   value of the two erasures' defunctionalized application, run at fuel `F`.
   `erase_app_keep` is the erasure step. Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem lowerF_app_eval {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n F lf : Nat) (g a : Expr Nat) (t : BootTy) (w : Val)
    (hirr : irrelevant E n [] (.app g a) = false)
    (lg la : LExpr)
    (hg : erase E n F [] g = some lg)
    (ha : erase E n F [] a = some la)
    (dv : DVal)
    (hr : run (defunc (.app lg la)).2 F [] (defunc (.app lg la)).1 = some dv)
    (he : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf []
        (emit (S := S) (G := []) F t dv) = some w) :
    Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf []
      (lowerF E n (F + 1) (S := S) t (.app g a)) = some w := by
  unfold lowerF pipeline
  have hee : erase E n (F + 1) [] (.app g a) = some (.app lg la) := by
    simp only [erase_app_keep E n F [] g a hirr, hg, ha]
  simp only [hee]
  have hr' := run_mono (defunc (.app lg la)).2 F (F + 1) []
      (defunc (.app lg la)).1 dv (Nat.le_succ F) hr
  simp only [hr']
  exact emitWith_evalStable relevantArgs progs lf [] F (F + 1) t dv w
    (Nat.le_succ F) he

/- A successful norm of the identity let is a norm of the bound term
   at the same fuel. Not AdeqLetE. -/
theorem norm_let_id_eq (E : ResolvedEnv) (k : Nat) (A v val : Expr Nat)
    (hn : norm E (k + 2) (.letE A v (.bvar 0)) = some val) :
    norm E (k + 2) v = some val := by
  cases hw : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.letE A v (.bvar 0)) with
  | none =>
    unfold norm at hn
    rw [hw] at hn
    exact Option.noConfusion hn
  | some w =>
    have hvw : whnfFuel E k v = some w := by
      rw [← whnf_let_id E k A v]
      exact hw
    have hv1 : whnfFuel E (k + 1) v = some w :=
      whnfFuel_mono E k v w hvw
    have heq : norm E (k + 2) (.letE A v (.bvar 0)) = norm E (k + 2) v := by
      conv =>
        lhs
        unfold norm
        rw [hw]
      conv =>
        rhs
        unfold norm
        rw [hv1]
    rw [← heq]
    exact hn

/- A successful norm of the identity application is a norm of the
   argument at the same fuel. Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem norm_beta_id_eq (E : ResolvedEnv) (k : Nat) (A arg val : Expr Nat)
    (hn : norm E (k + 2) (.app (.lam A (.bvar 0)) arg) = some val) :
    norm E (k + 2) arg = some val := by
  cases hw : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.app (.lam A (.bvar 0)) arg) with
  | none =>
    unfold norm at hn
    rw [hw] at hn
    exact Option.noConfusion hn
  | some w =>
    have hvw : whnfFuel E k arg = some w := by
      rw [← whnf_beta_id E k A arg]
      exact hw
    have hv1 : whnfFuel E (k + 1) arg = some w :=
      whnfFuel_mono E k arg w hvw
    have heq : norm E (k + 2) (.app (.lam A (.bvar 0)) arg) =
        norm E (k + 2) arg := by
      conv =>
        lhs
        unfold norm
        rw [hw]
      conv =>
        rhs
        unfold norm
        rw [hv1]
    rw [← heq]
    exact hn

/- `foldApps` rebuilds the spine `appsSpine` peeled. The head's own
   arguments stay in front of the new ones. -/
theorem appsSpine_foldApps (f : Expr Nat) :
    ∀ xs, appsSpine (foldApps f xs) = ((appsSpine f).1, (appsSpine f).2 ++ xs)
  | [] => by
      simp only [foldApps, List.append_nil]
  | x :: xs => by
      rw [foldApps, appsSpine_foldApps (.app f x) xs]
      have happ : appsSpine (.app f x) =
          ((appsSpine f).1, (appsSpine f).2 ++ [x]) := by
        simp only [appsSpine]
      rw [happ]
      have ha : ((appsSpine f).2 ++ [x]) ++ xs =
          (appsSpine f).2 ++ (x :: xs) := by
        rw [List.append_assoc]
        rfl
      exact congrArg (fun ys => ((appsSpine f).1, ys)) ha

/- One β step on a spine whose head is a λ. The first argument is
   substituted; the rest of the spine stays. `whnf_beta` is the
   one-argument case (`args = []`). Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem whnf_beta_spine (E : ResolvedEnv) (k : Nat) (A b a : Expr Nat)
    (args : List (Expr Nat)) :
    whnfFuel E (k + 1) (foldApps (.lam A b) (a :: args)) =
      whnfFuel E k (foldApps (instantiate0 a b) args) := by
  have hsp : appsSpine (foldApps (.lam A b) (a :: args)) =
      (.lam A b, a :: args) := by
    rw [appsSpine_foldApps]
    simp only [appsSpine, List.nil_append]
  conv =>
    lhs
    unfold whnfFuel
    rw [hsp]

/- A successful norm of the β-reduct is a norm of the λ-spine, one fuel
   later. The two `norm`s share the head `whnf_beta_spine` produces, and
   `norm_mono` lifts the reduct. Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem norm_beta_spine (E : ResolvedEnv) (k : Nat) (A b a : Expr Nat)
    (args : List (Expr Nat)) (v : Expr Nat)
    (hn : norm E (k + 1) (foldApps (instantiate0 a b) args) = some v) :
    norm E (k + 2) (foldApps (.lam A b) (a :: args)) = some v := by
  cases hw : whnfFuel E k (foldApps (instantiate0 a b) args) with
  | none =>
    unfold norm at hn
    rw [hw] at hn
    exact Option.noConfusion hn
  | some w =>
    have hc : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (foldApps (.lam A b) (a :: args)) = some w := by
      rw [whnf_beta_spine E k A b a args]
      exact hw
    have hb1 : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (foldApps (instantiate0 a b) args) = some w :=
      whnfFuel_mono E k (foldApps (instantiate0 a b) args) w hw
    have heq : norm E (k + 2) (foldApps (.lam A b) (a :: args)) =
        norm E (k + 2) (foldApps (instantiate0 a b) args) := by
      conv =>
        lhs
        unfold norm
        rw [hc]
      conv =>
        rhs
        unfold norm
        rw [hb1]
    rw [heq]
    exact norm_mono E (k + 1) (foldApps (instantiate0 a b) args) v hn

/- The same fuel, read backwards: a successful norm of the λ-spine is a
   norm of the β-reduct. Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem norm_beta_spine_eq (E : ResolvedEnv) (k : Nat) (A b a : Expr Nat)
    (args : List (Expr Nat)) (v : Expr Nat)
    (hn : norm E (k + 2) (foldApps (.lam A b) (a :: args)) = some v) :
    norm E (k + 2) (foldApps (instantiate0 a b) args) = some v := by
  cases hw : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (foldApps (.lam A b) (a :: args)) with
  | none =>
    unfold norm at hn
    rw [hw] at hn
    exact Option.noConfusion hn
  | some w =>
    have hvw : whnfFuel E k (foldApps (instantiate0 a b) args) = some w := by
      rw [← whnf_beta_spine E k A b a args]
      exact hw
    have hv1 : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (foldApps (instantiate0 a b) args) = some w :=
      whnfFuel_mono E k (foldApps (instantiate0 a b) args) w hvw
    have heq : norm E (k + 2) (foldApps (.lam A b) (a :: args)) =
        norm E (k + 2) (foldApps (instantiate0 a b) args) := by
      conv =>
        lhs
        unfold norm
        rw [hw]
      conv =>
        rhs
        unfold norm
        rw [hv1]
    rw [← heq]
    exact hn

/- One ζ step on a spine whose head is a let. `whnf_zeta` is the empty
   spine. Not AdeqLetE. -/
theorem whnf_zeta_spine (E : ResolvedEnv) (k : Nat) (A v b : Expr Nat)
    (args : List (Expr Nat)) :
    whnfFuel E (k + 1) (foldApps (.letE A v b) args) =
      whnfFuel E k (foldApps (instantiate0 v b) args) := by
  have hsp : appsSpine (foldApps (.letE A v b) args) = (.letE A v b, args) := by
    rw [appsSpine_foldApps]
    simp only [appsSpine, List.nil_append]
  conv =>
    lhs
    unfold whnfFuel
    rw [hsp]

/- A successful norm of the ζ-reduct is a norm of the let-spine, one fuel
   later. Not AdeqLetE. -/
theorem norm_zeta_spine (E : ResolvedEnv) (k : Nat) (A v0 b : Expr Nat)
    (args : List (Expr Nat)) (v : Expr Nat)
    (hn : norm E (k + 1) (foldApps (instantiate0 v0 b) args) = some v) :
    norm E (k + 2) (foldApps (.letE A v0 b) args) = some v := by
  cases hw : whnfFuel E k (foldApps (instantiate0 v0 b) args) with
  | none =>
    unfold norm at hn
    rw [hw] at hn
    exact Option.noConfusion hn
  | some w =>
    have hc : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (foldApps (.letE A v0 b) args) = some w := by
      rw [whnf_zeta_spine E k A v0 b args]
      exact hw
    have hb1 : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (foldApps (instantiate0 v0 b) args) = some w :=
      whnfFuel_mono E k (foldApps (instantiate0 v0 b) args) w hw
    have heq : norm E (k + 2) (foldApps (.letE A v0 b) args) =
        norm E (k + 2) (foldApps (instantiate0 v0 b) args) := by
      conv =>
        lhs
        unfold norm
        rw [hc]
      conv =>
        rhs
        unfold norm
        rw [hb1]
    rw [heq]
    exact norm_mono E (k + 1) (foldApps (instantiate0 v0 b) args) v hn

/- The same fuel, read backwards. Not AdeqLetE. -/
theorem norm_zeta_spine_eq (E : ResolvedEnv) (k : Nat) (A v0 b : Expr Nat)
    (args : List (Expr Nat)) (v : Expr Nat)
    (hn : norm E (k + 2) (foldApps (.letE A v0 b) args) = some v) :
    norm E (k + 2) (foldApps (instantiate0 v0 b) args) = some v := by
  cases hw : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (foldApps (.letE A v0 b) args) with
  | none =>
    unfold norm at hn
    rw [hw] at hn
    exact Option.noConfusion hn
  | some w =>
    have hvw : whnfFuel E k (foldApps (instantiate0 v0 b) args) = some w := by
      rw [← whnf_zeta_spine E k A v0 b args]
      exact hw
    have hv1 : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (foldApps (instantiate0 v0 b) args) = some w :=
      whnfFuel_mono E k (foldApps (instantiate0 v0 b) args) w hvw
    have heq : norm E (k + 2) (foldApps (.letE A v0 b) args) =
        norm E (k + 2) (foldApps (instantiate0 v0 b) args) := by
      conv =>
        lhs
        unfold norm
        rw [hw]
      conv =>
        rhs
        unfold norm
        rw [hv1]
    rw [← heq]
    exact hn

/- A normal form `scmValOf` refuses is `Good` at once. The five direct
   constructors use this shape. Not AdeqApp, AdeqLetE, or AdeqConstDelta. -/
theorem good_vacuous_of_norm {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n : Nat) (e : Expr Nat)
    (h : ∀ {lf : Nat} {v : Expr Nat},
      norm E lf e = some v → ∀ fv, scmValOf E fv v = none) :
    Good progs E n e := by
  intro lf fv T v t w _ _ _ hn hs _ _ _ _ _
  rw [h hn fv] at hs
  exact Option.noConfusion hs

/- β whose body is a sort. The reduct is that sort at every argument, and
   a sort is not data. Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem good_beta_sort {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n : Nat) (A arg : Expr Nat) (l : Level) :
    Good progs E n (.app (.lam A (.sort l)) arg) :=
  good_vacuous_of_norm progs E n _ (fun {lf} {v} hn fv => by
    cases lf with
    | zero =>
      rw [norm_fuel0] at hn
      exact Option.noConfusion hn
    | succ lf =>
      cases lf with
      | zero =>
        unfold norm at hn
        rw [whnfFuel_fuel0] at hn
        exact Option.noConfusion hn
      | succ k =>
        have happ : foldApps (.lam A (.sort l)) (arg :: []) =
            .app (.lam A (.sort l)) arg := by
          simp only [foldApps]
        have hnfold : norm E (k + 2) (foldApps (.lam A (.sort l)) (arg :: [])) =
            some v := by
          rw [happ]
          exact hn
        have hn' := norm_beta_spine_eq E k A (.sort l) arg [] v hnfold
        have hsub : (instantiate0 arg (.sort l) : Expr Nat) = .sort l := rfl
        rw [hsub] at hn'
        rw [norm_sort_val hn']
        exact scmValOf_sort E fv l)

/- β whose body is a Π. The reduct is a Π, which is not data. Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem good_beta_pi {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n : Nat) (A B C arg : Expr Nat) :
    Good progs E n (.app (.lam A (.pi B C)) arg) :=
  good_vacuous_of_norm progs E n _ (fun {lf} {v} hn fv => by
    cases lf with
    | zero =>
      rw [norm_fuel0] at hn
      exact Option.noConfusion hn
    | succ lf =>
      cases lf with
      | zero =>
        unfold norm at hn
        rw [whnfFuel_fuel0] at hn
        exact Option.noConfusion hn
      | succ k =>
        have happ : foldApps (.lam A (.pi B C)) (arg :: []) =
            .app (.lam A (.pi B C)) arg := by
          simp only [foldApps]
        have hnfold : norm E (k + 2) (foldApps (.lam A (.pi B C)) (arg :: [])) =
            some v := by
          rw [happ]
          exact hn
        have hn' := norm_beta_spine_eq E k A (.pi B C) arg [] v hnfold
        have hsub : instantiate0 arg (.pi B C) =
            .pi (instantiate0 arg B) (instantiate 1 (lift 0 1 arg) C) := rfl
        rw [hsub] at hn'
        obtain ⟨A', B', hv⟩ := norm_pi_val hn'
        rw [hv]
        exact scmValOf_pi E fv A' B')

/- β whose body is a λ. The reduct is a λ, which is not data. Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem good_beta_lam {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n : Nat) (A B t arg : Expr Nat) :
    Good progs E n (.app (.lam A (.lam B t)) arg) :=
  good_vacuous_of_norm progs E n _ (fun {lf} {v} hn fv => by
    cases lf with
    | zero =>
      rw [norm_fuel0] at hn
      exact Option.noConfusion hn
    | succ lf =>
      cases lf with
      | zero =>
        unfold norm at hn
        rw [whnfFuel_fuel0] at hn
        exact Option.noConfusion hn
      | succ k =>
        have happ : foldApps (.lam A (.lam B t)) (arg :: []) =
            .app (.lam A (.lam B t)) arg := by
          simp only [foldApps]
        have hnfold : norm E (k + 2) (foldApps (.lam A (.lam B t)) (arg :: [])) =
            some v := by
          rw [happ]
          exact hn
        have hn' := norm_beta_spine_eq E k A (.lam B t) arg [] v hnfold
        have hsub : instantiate0 arg (.lam B t) =
            .lam (instantiate0 arg B) (instantiate 1 (lift 0 1 arg) t) := rfl
        rw [hsub] at hn'
        obtain ⟨A', b', hv⟩ := norm_lam_val hn'
        rw [hv]
        exact scmValOf_lam E fv A' b')

/- β whose body is `bvar (j + 1)`. Substitution shifts it to `bvar j`,
   which is not data. The bound index `0` is not this theorem. Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem good_beta_bvar_succ {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n j : Nat) (A arg : Expr Nat) :
    Good progs E n (.app (.lam A (.bvar (j + 1))) arg) :=
  good_vacuous_of_norm progs E n _ (fun {lf} {v} hn fv => by
    cases lf with
    | zero =>
      rw [norm_fuel0] at hn
      exact Option.noConfusion hn
    | succ lf =>
      cases lf with
      | zero =>
        unfold norm at hn
        rw [whnfFuel_fuel0] at hn
        exact Option.noConfusion hn
      | succ k =>
        have happ : foldApps (.lam A (.bvar (j + 1))) (arg :: []) =
            .app (.lam A (.bvar (j + 1))) arg := by
          simp only [foldApps]
        have hnfold :
            norm E (k + 2) (foldApps (.lam A (.bvar (j + 1))) (arg :: [])) =
              some v := by
          rw [happ]
          exact hn
        have hn' := norm_beta_spine_eq E k A (.bvar (j + 1)) arg [] v hnfold
        have hne : j + 1 ≠ 0 := Nat.succ_ne_zero j
        have hlt : 0 < j + 1 := Nat.zero_lt_succ j
        have hr : instantiate0 arg (.bvar (j + 1)) = .bvar j := by
          simp only [instantiate0, instantiate, if_neg hne, if_pos hlt]
          rw [Nat.add_sub_cancel j 1]
        rw [hr] at hn'
        rw [norm_bvar_val hn']
        exact scmValOf_bvar E fv j)

/- ζ whose body is a sort. The bound term is discarded and the reduct is
   that sort. Not AdeqLetE. -/
theorem good_let_sort {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n : Nat) (A bound : Expr Nat) (l : Level) :
    Good progs E n (.letE A bound (.sort l)) :=
  good_vacuous_of_norm progs E n _ (fun {lf} {v} hn fv => by
    cases lf with
    | zero =>
      rw [norm_fuel0] at hn
      exact Option.noConfusion hn
    | succ lf =>
      cases lf with
      | zero =>
        unfold norm at hn
        rw [whnfFuel_fuel0] at hn
        exact Option.noConfusion hn
      | succ k =>
        have hlet : foldApps (.letE A bound (.sort l)) ([] : List (Expr Nat)) =
            .letE A bound (.sort l) := by
          simp only [foldApps]
        have hnfold :
            norm E (k + 2) (foldApps (.letE A bound (.sort l)) []) = some v := by
          rw [hlet]
          exact hn
        have hn' := norm_zeta_spine_eq E k A bound (.sort l) [] v hnfold
        have hsub : (instantiate0 bound (.sort l) : Expr Nat) = .sort l := rfl
        rw [hsub] at hn'
        rw [norm_sort_val hn']
        exact scmValOf_sort E fv l)

/- ζ whose body is a Π. Not AdeqLetE. -/
theorem good_let_pi {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n : Nat) (A bound B C : Expr Nat) :
    Good progs E n (.letE A bound (.pi B C)) :=
  good_vacuous_of_norm progs E n _ (fun {lf} {v} hn fv => by
    cases lf with
    | zero =>
      rw [norm_fuel0] at hn
      exact Option.noConfusion hn
    | succ lf =>
      cases lf with
      | zero =>
        unfold norm at hn
        rw [whnfFuel_fuel0] at hn
        exact Option.noConfusion hn
      | succ k =>
        have hlet : foldApps (.letE A bound (.pi B C)) ([] : List (Expr Nat)) =
            .letE A bound (.pi B C) := by
          simp only [foldApps]
        have hnfold :
            norm E (k + 2) (foldApps (.letE A bound (.pi B C)) []) = some v := by
          rw [hlet]
          exact hn
        have hn' := norm_zeta_spine_eq E k A bound (.pi B C) [] v hnfold
        have hsub : instantiate0 bound (.pi B C) =
            .pi (instantiate0 bound B) (instantiate 1 (lift 0 1 bound) C) := rfl
        rw [hsub] at hn'
        obtain ⟨A', B', hv⟩ := norm_pi_val hn'
        rw [hv]
        exact scmValOf_pi E fv A' B')

/- ζ whose body is a λ. Not AdeqLetE. -/
theorem good_let_lam {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n : Nat) (A bound B t : Expr Nat) :
    Good progs E n (.letE A bound (.lam B t)) :=
  good_vacuous_of_norm progs E n _ (fun {lf} {v} hn fv => by
    cases lf with
    | zero =>
      rw [norm_fuel0] at hn
      exact Option.noConfusion hn
    | succ lf =>
      cases lf with
      | zero =>
        unfold norm at hn
        rw [whnfFuel_fuel0] at hn
        exact Option.noConfusion hn
      | succ k =>
        have hlet : foldApps (.letE A bound (.lam B t)) ([] : List (Expr Nat)) =
            .letE A bound (.lam B t) := by
          simp only [foldApps]
        have hnfold :
            norm E (k + 2) (foldApps (.letE A bound (.lam B t)) []) = some v := by
          rw [hlet]
          exact hn
        have hn' := norm_zeta_spine_eq E k A bound (.lam B t) [] v hnfold
        have hsub : instantiate0 bound (.lam B t) =
            .lam (instantiate0 bound B) (instantiate 1 (lift 0 1 bound) t) := rfl
        rw [hsub] at hn'
        obtain ⟨A', b', hv⟩ := norm_lam_val hn'
        rw [hv]
        exact scmValOf_lam E fv A' b')

/- ζ whose body is `bvar (j + 1)`. The bound index `0` is not this
   theorem. Not AdeqLetE. -/
theorem good_let_bvar_succ {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n j : Nat) (A bound : Expr Nat) :
    Good progs E n (.letE A bound (.bvar (j + 1))) :=
  good_vacuous_of_norm progs E n _ (fun {lf} {v} hn fv => by
    cases lf with
    | zero =>
      rw [norm_fuel0] at hn
      exact Option.noConfusion hn
    | succ lf =>
      cases lf with
      | zero =>
        unfold norm at hn
        rw [whnfFuel_fuel0] at hn
        exact Option.noConfusion hn
      | succ k =>
        have hlet :
            foldApps (.letE A bound (.bvar (j + 1))) ([] : List (Expr Nat)) =
              .letE A bound (.bvar (j + 1)) := by
          simp only [foldApps]
        have hnfold :
            norm E (k + 2) (foldApps (.letE A bound (.bvar (j + 1))) []) =
              some v := by
          rw [hlet]
          exact hn
        have hn' := norm_zeta_spine_eq E k A bound (.bvar (j + 1)) [] v hnfold
        have hne : j + 1 ≠ 0 := Nat.succ_ne_zero j
        have hlt : 0 < j + 1 := Nat.zero_lt_succ j
        have hr : instantiate0 bound (.bvar (j + 1)) = .bvar j := by
          simp only [instantiate0, instantiate, if_neg hne, if_pos hlt]
          rw [Nat.add_sub_cancel j 1]
        rw [hr] at hn'
        rw [norm_bvar_val hn']
        exact scmValOf_bvar E fv j)

/- One δ step on a spine whose head is a transparent constant.
   `whnf_const_delta` is the empty spine. Not AdeqConstDelta. -/
theorem whnf_delta_spine (E : ResolvedEnv) (k r : Nat) (ls : List Level)
    (body : Expr Nat) (args : List (Expr Nat))
    (hb : transparentBody E r ls = some body) :
    whnfFuel E (k + 1) (foldApps (.const r ls) args) =
      whnfFuel E k (foldApps body args) := by
  have hsp : appsSpine (foldApps (.const r ls) args) = (.const r ls, args) := by
    rw [appsSpine_foldApps]
    simp only [appsSpine, List.nil_append]
  conv =>
    lhs
    unfold whnfFuel
    rw [hsp]
  simp only [hb]

/- A successful norm of the δ-reduct is a norm of the constant spine, one
   fuel later. `norm_const_delta_of_body` is the empty spine. Not
   AdeqConstDelta. -/
theorem norm_delta_spine (E : ResolvedEnv) (k r : Nat) (ls : List Level)
    (body : Expr Nat) (args : List (Expr Nat)) (v : Expr Nat)
    (ht : transparentBody E r ls = some body)
    (hn : norm E (k + 1) (foldApps body args) = some v) :
    norm E (k + 2) (foldApps (.const r ls) args) = some v := by
  cases hw : whnfFuel E k (foldApps body args) with
  | none =>
    unfold norm at hn
    rw [hw] at hn
    exact Option.noConfusion hn
  | some w =>
    have hc : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (foldApps (.const r ls) args) = some w := by
      rw [whnf_delta_spine E k r ls body args ht]
      exact hw
    have hb1 : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (foldApps body args) = some w :=
      whnfFuel_mono E k (foldApps body args) w hw
    have heq : norm E (k + 2) (foldApps (.const r ls) args) =
        norm E (k + 2) (foldApps body args) := by
      conv =>
        lhs
        unfold norm
        rw [hc]
      conv =>
        rhs
        unfold norm
        rw [hb1]
    rw [heq]
    exact norm_mono E (k + 1) (foldApps body args) v hn

/- The same fuel, read backwards. Not AdeqConstDelta. -/
theorem norm_delta_spine_eq (E : ResolvedEnv) (k r : Nat) (ls : List Level)
    (body : Expr Nat) (args : List (Expr Nat)) (v : Expr Nat)
    (ht : transparentBody E r ls = some body)
    (hn : norm E (k + 2) (foldApps (.const r ls) args) = some v) :
    norm E (k + 2) (foldApps body args) = some v := by
  cases hw : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (foldApps (.const r ls) args) with
  | none =>
    unfold norm at hn
    rw [hw] at hn
    exact Option.noConfusion hn
  | some w =>
    have hvw : whnfFuel E k (foldApps body args) = some w := by
      rw [← whnf_delta_spine E k r ls body args ht]
      exact hw
    have hv1 : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (foldApps body args) = some w :=
      whnfFuel_mono E k (foldApps body args) w hvw
    have heq : norm E (k + 2) (foldApps (.const r ls) args) =
        norm E (k + 2) (foldApps body args) := by
      conv =>
        lhs
        unfold norm
        rw [hw]
      conv =>
        rhs
        unfold norm
        rw [hv1]
    rw [← heq]
    exact hn

/- One δ, for an arbitrary body, once that body evaluates to the same
   scm value. `norm_delta_spine_eq` at the empty spine reads the body's
   normal form off the constant, and `lowerF_const_delta_eval` moves the
   evaluation across erasure. Relevance of the constant is a hypothesis:
   `Good` does not supply it. The body hypothesis is the eval, not
   `Good` of the body. Not AdeqConstDelta. -/
theorem good_const_delta_of_eval {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n r : Nat) (ls : List Level) (b : Expr Nat)
    (hb : transparentBody E r ls = some b)
    (hirr : irrelevant E n [] (.const r ls) = false)
    (hbody : ∀ (lf fv : Nat) (v : Expr Nat) (t : BootTy) (w : Val),
      norm E lf b = some v →
      scmValOf E fv v = some w →
      relevantSpine E n fv v = true →
      irrelevant E n [] v = false →
      valFits fv t w = true →
      (inferT E n [] v).isSome = true →
      ∃ F lf',
        Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf' []
          (lowerF E n F (S := S) t b) = some w) :
    Good progs E n (.const r ls) := by
  refine good_of_exists progs E n (.const r ls) ?_
  intro lf fv T v t w _ _ _ hn hs hrel hirrv hf hvinf _
  cases lf with
  | zero =>
      rw [norm_fuel0] at hn
      exact Option.noConfusion hn
  | succ lf1 =>
      cases lf1 with
      | zero =>
          unfold norm at hn
          rw [whnfFuel_fuel0] at hn
          exact Option.noConfusion hn
      | succ k =>
          have hn' : norm E (k + 2) (foldApps (.const r ls) []) = some v := hn
          have hbn : norm E (k + 2) (foldApps b []) = some v :=
            norm_delta_spine_eq E k r ls b [] v hb hn'
          have hbb : norm E (k + 2) b = some v := hbn
          obtain ⟨F, lfe, he⟩ :=
            hbody (k + 2) fv v t w hbb hs hrel hirrv hf (by rw [hvinf]; rfl)
          exact ⟨F + 1, lfe,
            lowerF_const_delta_eval progs E n F r lfe ls b t w hirr hb he⟩

/- Eval of an identity let at fuel `F + 3` is eval of the emitted value
   of the bound term's erasure, run at fuel `F + 1`. The body erases to
   slot 0. `erase_mono` lifts that erasure one fuel, and `run_let_id`
   returns the bound value. Not AdeqLetE. -/
theorem lowerF_let_id_eval {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n F lf : Nat) (A v : Expr Nat) (t : BootTy) (w : Val)
    (hirr : irrelevant E n [] (.letE A v (.bvar 0)) = false)
    (hirrB : irrelevant E n (.letBinding A v :: []) (.bvar 0) = false)
    (lv : LExpr)
    (hv : erase E n (F + 1) [] v = some lv)
    (dv : DVal)
    (hr : run (defunc lv).2 (F + 1) [] (defunc lv).1 = some dv)
    (he : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf []
        (emit (S := S) (G := []) (F + 1) t dv) = some w) :
    Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf []
      (lowerF E n (F + 3) (S := S) t (.letE A v (.bvar 0))) = some w := by
  have hv2 : erase E n (F + 2) [] v = some lv :=
    erase_mono E n (F + 1) (F + 2) [] v lv (Nat.le_succ (F + 1)) hv
  have hb : erase E n (F + 2) (.letBinding A v :: []) (.bvar 0) = some (.bvar 0) := by
    simp only [erase, eraseWith, hirrB, Bool.false_eq_true, if_false]
  have he2 : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf []
      (emit (S := S) (G := []) (F + 2) t dv) = some w :=
    emitWith_evalStable relevantArgs progs lf [] (F + 1) (F + 2) t dv w
      (Nat.le_succ (F + 1)) he
  have hrlet : run (defunc (.letE lv (.bvar 0))).2 (F + 2) []
      (defunc (.letE lv (.bvar 0))).1 = some dv := by
    rw [defunc_let_bvar0]
    exact run_let_id (defunc lv).2 F [] (defunc lv).1 dv hr
  exact lowerF_let_eval progs E n (F + 2) lf A v (.bvar 0) t w hirr lv (.bvar 0)
    hv2 hb dv hrlet he2

/- Level equality is an equivalence. `eval` here is the level interpreter,
   not bootstrap `eval`. -/
theorem eqN_refl (l : Level) : eqN l l := fun _ => rfl

theorem eqN_symm {l₁ l₂ : Level} (h : eqN l₁ l₂) : eqN l₂ l₁ :=
  fun ρ => (h ρ).symm

theorem eqN_trans {l₁ l₂ l₃ : Level} (h₁ : eqN l₁ l₂) (h₂ : eqN l₂ l₃) : eqN l₁ l₃ :=
  fun ρ => (h₁ ρ).trans (h₂ ρ)

theorem eqN_succ {l₁ l₂ : Level} (h : eqN l₁ l₂) : eqN (.succ l₁) (.succ l₂) := by
  intro ρ
  simp only [Rsx.eval, h ρ]

/- `Sort (succ l)` is not extensionally `Sort 0`. -/
theorem eqN_succ_ne_zero (l : Level) (h : eqN (.succ l) .zero) : False := by
  have hρ : Rsx.eval (fun _ => some 0) (.succ l) =
      Rsx.eval (fun _ => some 0) .zero := h (fun _ => some 0)
  simp only [Rsx.eval] at hρ
  cases hv : Rsx.eval (fun _ => some 0) l with
  | none =>
      rw [hv] at hρ
      simp only [Option.map] at hρ
      cases hρ
  | some n =>
      rw [hv] at hρ
      simp only [Option.map] at hρ
      injection hρ with hn
      exact Nat.succ_ne_zero n hn

/- `foldApps f (xs ++ [y])` is an application, never a sort. -/
theorem foldApps_append_ne_sort (f : Expr Nat) (xs : List (Expr Nat)) (y : Expr Nat)
    (l : Level) : foldApps f (xs ++ [y]) ≠ .sort l := by
  induction xs generalizing f with
  | nil =>
      simp only [List.nil_append, foldApps]
      intro h
      cases h
  | cons x xs ih =>
      simp only [List.cons_append, foldApps]
      exact ih (.app f x)

/- A derived iota left-hand side is `recCall`, a nonempty application spine. -/
theorem iotaLhs_ne_sort {E : ResolvedEnv} (w : IotaWitness E) (l : Level) :
    iotaLhsOf w ≠ .sort l := by
  unfold iotaLhsOf recCall
  exact foldApps_append_ne_sort (.const w.recRef w.ls) w.preMajor (ctorMajor w) l

/- The same spine is never a constant. -/
theorem foldApps_append_ne_const (f : Expr Nat) (xs : List (Expr Nat)) (y : Expr Nat)
    (r : Nat) (ls : List Level) : foldApps f (xs ++ [y]) ≠ .const r ls := by
  induction xs generalizing f with
  | nil =>
      simp only [List.nil_append, foldApps]
      intro h
      cases h
  | cons x xs ih =>
      simp only [List.cons_append, foldApps]
      exact ih (.app f x)

theorem iotaLhs_ne_const {E : ResolvedEnv} (w : IotaWitness E) (r : Nat) (ls : List Level) :
    iotaLhsOf w ≠ .const r ls := by
  unfold iotaLhsOf recCall
  exact foldApps_append_ne_const (.const w.recRef w.ls) w.preMajor (ctorMajor w) r ls

/- A derived iota is an application spine, so it is not a constant. -/
theorem derivedIota_ne_const {E : ResolvedEnv} {r : Nat} {ls : List Level} {rhs : Expr Nat}
    (h : DerivedIota E (.const r ls) rhs) : False :=
  (DerivedIota.rec (motive := fun lhs _ _ => lhs = .const r ls → False)
    (fun w => iotaLhs_ne_const w r ls) h) rfl

/- A sort is typed at `Sort (succ l)` up to `TyConvT`. The chain is the
   `HasTyT.conv` spine; no `ConvT` inversion. Not AdeqConstDelta, AdeqApp,
   or AdeqLetE. -/
/- Same fact when the subject is already a sort. The constructor level is
   the index, so the sort arm is a term. -/
def hasTyT_sort_principal_at {E : ResolvedEnv} {n : Nat}
    {Γ : LCtx} {l : Level} {T : Expr Nat}
    (h : HasTyT E n Γ (.sort l) T) :
    Σ' (l' : Level) (_ : eqN l' (.succ l)), TyConvT E n Γ (.sort l') T :=
  match h with
  | .sort _ _ => ⟨.succ l, ⟨eqN_refl _, TyConvT.refl _ _⟩⟩
  | .conv Γ _ A B u hsub hc =>
      match hasTyT_sort_principal_at hsub with
      | ⟨l', ⟨heq, ht⟩⟩ =>
          ⟨l', ⟨heq, TyConvT.trans Γ (.sort l') A B ht (TyConvT.of Γ A B u hc)⟩⟩
termination_by sizeOf h

def hasTyT_sort_principal {E : ResolvedEnv} {n : Nat}
    {Γ : LCtx} {e T : Expr Nat} {l : Level}
    (h : HasTyT E n Γ e T) (he : e = .sort l) :
    Σ' (l' : Level) (_ : eqN l' (.succ l)), TyConvT E n Γ (.sort l') T := by
  subst he
  exact hasTyT_sort_principal_at h

/- A constant is typed at its instantiated declared type up to `TyConvT`.
   Not AdeqConstDelta, AdeqApp, or AdeqLetE. -/
def hasTyT_const_principal_at {E : ResolvedEnv} {n : Nat}
    {Γ : LCtx} {r : Nat} {ls : List Level} {T : Expr Nat}
    (h : HasTyT E n Γ (.const r ls) T) :
    Σ' (m : CheckedMember) (_ : E.members r = some m)
        (_ : ls.length = m.arity) (_ : levelsBounded n ls = true),
      TyConvT E n Γ (instantiateLevels ls m.mtype) T :=
  match h with
  | .const _ _ _ m hres hlen hwf =>
      ⟨m, ⟨hres, ⟨hlen, ⟨hwf, TyConvT.refl _ _⟩⟩⟩⟩
  | .conv Γ _ A B u hsub hc =>
      match hasTyT_const_principal_at hsub with
      | ⟨m, ⟨hres, ⟨hlen, ⟨hwf, ht⟩⟩⟩⟩ =>
          ⟨m, ⟨hres, ⟨hlen, ⟨hwf,
            TyConvT.trans Γ (instantiateLevels ls m.mtype) A B ht
              (TyConvT.of Γ A B u hc)⟩⟩⟩⟩
termination_by sizeOf h

def hasTyT_const_principal {E : ResolvedEnv} {n : Nat}
    {Γ : LCtx} {e T : Expr Nat} {r : Nat} {ls : List Level}
    (h : HasTyT E n Γ e T) (he : e = .const r ls) :
    Σ' (m : CheckedMember) (_ : E.members r = some m)
        (_ : ls.length = m.arity) (_ : levelsBounded n ls = true),
      TyConvT E n Γ (instantiateLevels ls m.mtype) T := by
  subst he
  exact hasTyT_const_principal_at h

/- A transparent constant whose body is a non-constructor head has no scm
   value. This is not `AdeqConstDelta`. -/
theorem good_const_delta_rigid {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n r c : Nat) (ls lsc : List Level)
    (hb : transparentBody E r ls = some (.const c lsc))
    (hnone : transparentBody E c lsc = none)
    (hnot : ∀ m, E.members c = some m → ¬ m.mclass = .constructorM) :
    Good progs E n (.const r ls) := by
  refine good_of_exists progs E n (.const r ls) ?_
  intro lf fv T v t w _ _ _ hn hs _ _ _ _ _
  have hv := norm_const_ctor_val E lf r c ls lsc hb hnone hn
  rw [hv, scmValOf_const_not_ctor E fv c lsc hnot] at hs
  exact Option.noConfusion hs

/-- a lowering keeps every value evalLF gets from it when its fuel grows. -/
def FuelStable {S : SigTable} (low : Lowering S) (progs : Programs S S) : Prop :=
  ∀ (E : ResolvedEnv) (n F F' : Nat) (t : BootTy) (e : Expr Nat) (lf : Nat) (w : Val),
    F ≤ F' →
    Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf [] (low E n F t e) = some w →
    Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf [] (low E n F' t e) = some w

theorem lowerF_fuelStable {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) :
    FuelStable (fun E n F t e => lowerF E n F (S := S) t e) progs :=
  fun E n F F' t e lf w hF h => lowerF_evalStable progs E n F F' t e lf w hF h

/-- mutant: the output reads the lowering fuel (its parity). -/
def fuelParity {S : SigTable} : Lowering S := fun _ _ F t _ =>
  match t with
  | .i64 => .litI ((F % 2 : Nat) : Int)
  | _ => refuse

theorem fuelParity_not_fuelStable {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) :
    ¬ FuelStable (fuelParity (S := S)) progs := by
  intro h
  have h0 : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs 1 []
      (fuelParity (S := S) adqEnv 0 0 .i64 (.lit 0)) = some (.int 0) :=
    eval_litI progs 0 (by decide)
  have h1 := h adqEnv 0 0 1 .i64 (.lit 0) 1 (.int 0) (by decide) h0
  have h2 : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs 1 []
      (fuelParity (S := S) adqEnv 0 1 .i64 (.lit 0)) = some (.int 1) :=
    eval_litI progs 1 (by decide)
  rw [h2] at h1
  exact absurd (Val.int.inj (Option.some.inj h1)) (by decide)

/-! ## Controls (`#guard`): a closed environment and small closed data-typed terms

Members (05 §3 order for Nat, as `natExpand` requires: 0 `N`, 1 `zero`, 2 `succ`):
0 N, 1 zero, 2 succ, 4 True : Prop, 5 True.intro, 6 Bool, 7 false, 8 true,
9 P, 10 P.mk : N → N → P, 11 two := succ (succ zero), 12 addTwo := λ x. succ (succ x),
13 ax : N (axiom), 14 thm : True (theorem). -/

def cN : Expr Nat := .const 0 []
def cZero : Expr Nat := .const 1 []
def cSucc : Expr Nat := .const 2 []
def cTrue : Expr Nat := .const 4 []
def cIntro : Expr Nat := .const 5 []
def cMk : Expr Nat := .const 10 []

/-- `closedAt c e`: every `bvar` sits strictly under cutoff `c`. -/
def closedAt (c : Nat) : Expr Nat → Bool
  | .bvar i => decide (i < c)
  | .sort _ => true
  | .const _ _ => true
  | .lit _ => true
  | .app f x => closedAt c f && closedAt c x
  | .lam a b => closedAt c a && closedAt (c + 1) b
  | .pi a b => closedAt c a && closedAt (c + 1) b
  | .letE a v b => closedAt c a && closedAt c v && closedAt (c + 1) b

theorem lift_eq_of_closedAt :
    ∀ (e : Expr Nat) (c k : Nat), closedAt c e = true → lift (c + k) 1 e = e
  | .bvar i, c, k, h => by
      have hlt : i < c := by simpa [closedAt, decide_eq_true_eq] using h
      have hle : ¬ c + k ≤ i :=
        Nat.not_le.mpr (Nat.lt_of_lt_of_le hlt (Nat.le_add_right c k))
      simp only [lift]
      rw [if_neg hle]
  | .sort _, _, _, _ => rfl
  | .const _ _, _, _, _ => rfl
  | .lit _, _, _, _ => rfl
  | .app f x, c, k, h => by
      simp only [closedAt, Bool.and_eq_true] at h
      simp only [lift, lift_eq_of_closedAt f c k h.1, lift_eq_of_closedAt x c k h.2]
  | .lam a b, c, k, h => by
      simp only [closedAt, Bool.and_eq_true] at h
      have hb := lift_eq_of_closedAt b (c + 1) k h.2
      have hc : c + k + 1 = c + 1 + k := Nat.add_right_comm c k 1
      simp only [lift, lift_eq_of_closedAt a c k h.1, hc, hb]
  | .pi a b, c, k, h => by
      simp only [closedAt, Bool.and_eq_true] at h
      have hb := lift_eq_of_closedAt b (c + 1) k h.2
      have hc : c + k + 1 = c + 1 + k := Nat.add_right_comm c k 1
      simp only [lift, lift_eq_of_closedAt a c k h.1, hc, hb]
  | .letE a v b, c, k, h => by
      simp only [closedAt, Bool.and_eq_true] at h
      have ha := lift_eq_of_closedAt a c k h.1.1
      have hv := lift_eq_of_closedAt v c k h.1.2
      have hb := lift_eq_of_closedAt b (c + 1) k h.2
      have hc : c + k + 1 = c + 1 + k := Nat.add_right_comm c k 1
      simp only [lift, ha, hv, hc, hb]

/- A term `lift` fixes from cutoff `c` has no free index at `c` or above,
   so `closedAt c` holds. The binder case shifts the cutoff by one, the
   same `c + k + 1 = (c + 1) + k` as `lift_eq_of_closedAt`. -/
theorem closedAt_of_lifts :
    ∀ (e : Expr Nat) (c : Nat), (∀ k, lift (c + k) 1 e = e) → closedAt c e = true
  | .bvar j, c, h => by
      by_cases hcj : c ≤ j
      · have h0 := h 0
        rw [Nat.add_zero] at h0
        simp only [lift, hcj, ite_true] at h0
        exact absurd (Expr.bvar.inj h0) (Nat.succ_ne_self j)
      · simp only [closedAt, decide_eq_true_eq]
        exact Nat.not_le.mp hcj
  | .sort _, _, _ => rfl
  | .const _ _, _, _ => rfl
  | .lit _, _, _ => rfl
  | .app f x, c, h => by
      have hf : ∀ k, lift (c + k) 1 f = f := by
        intro k
        have hk := h k
        simp only [lift] at hk
        exact (Expr.app.inj hk).1
      have hx : ∀ k, lift (c + k) 1 x = x := by
        intro k
        have hk := h k
        simp only [lift] at hk
        exact (Expr.app.inj hk).2
      simp only [closedAt, closedAt_of_lifts f c hf, closedAt_of_lifts x c hx, Bool.and_self]
  | .lam a b, c, h => by
      have ha : ∀ k, lift (c + k) 1 a = a := by
        intro k
        have hk := h k
        simp only [lift] at hk
        exact (Expr.lam.inj hk).1
      have hb : ∀ k, lift ((c + 1) + k) 1 b = b := by
        intro k
        have hk := h k
        simp only [lift] at hk
        have h2 := (Expr.lam.inj hk).2
        have hc : c + k + 1 = (c + 1) + k := Nat.add_right_comm c k 1
        simpa [hc] using h2
      simp only [closedAt, closedAt_of_lifts a c ha, closedAt_of_lifts b (c + 1) hb,
        Bool.and_self]
  | .pi a b, c, h => by
      have ha : ∀ k, lift (c + k) 1 a = a := by
        intro k
        have hk := h k
        simp only [lift] at hk
        exact (Expr.pi.inj hk).1
      have hb : ∀ k, lift ((c + 1) + k) 1 b = b := by
        intro k
        have hk := h k
        simp only [lift] at hk
        have h2 := (Expr.pi.inj hk).2
        have hc : c + k + 1 = (c + 1) + k := Nat.add_right_comm c k 1
        simpa [hc] using h2
      simp only [closedAt, closedAt_of_lifts a c ha, closedAt_of_lifts b (c + 1) hb,
        Bool.and_self]
  | .letE a v b, c, h => by
      have ha : ∀ k, lift (c + k) 1 a = a := by
        intro k
        have hk := h k
        simp only [lift] at hk
        exact (Expr.letE.inj hk).1
      have hv : ∀ k, lift (c + k) 1 v = v := by
        intro k
        have hk := h k
        simp only [lift] at hk
        exact (Expr.letE.inj hk).2.1
      have hb : ∀ k, lift ((c + 1) + k) 1 b = b := by
        intro k
        have hk := h k
        simp only [lift] at hk
        have h3 := (Expr.letE.inj hk).2.2
        have hc : c + k + 1 = (c + 1) + k := Nat.add_right_comm c k 1
        simpa [hc] using h3
      simp only [closedAt, closedAt_of_lifts a c ha, closedAt_of_lifts v c hv,
        closedAt_of_lifts b (c + 1) hb, Bool.and_self]

/- Below a closed cutoff, `instantiate` does not meet a free index, so it
   is the identity. `EnvClosed` gives this at cutoff 0 for member types
   and bodies (`envSubst_of_envClosed`). Not AdeqApp, AdeqLetE, or
   AdeqConstDelta. -/
theorem instantiate_eq_of_closedAt :
    ∀ (e : Expr Nat) (c i : Nat) (v : Expr Nat),
      closedAt c e = true → c ≤ i → instantiate i v e = e
  | .bvar j, c, i, _, h, hci => by
      have hlt : j < c := by simpa [closedAt, decide_eq_true_eq] using h
      have hji : j < i := Nat.lt_of_lt_of_le hlt hci
      have hne : j ≠ i := Nat.ne_of_lt hji
      have hnge : ¬ i < j := Nat.not_lt.mpr (Nat.le_of_lt hji)
      simp only [instantiate]
      rw [if_neg hne, if_neg hnge]
  | .sort _, _, _, _, _, _ => rfl
  | .const _ _, _, _, _, _, _ => rfl
  | .lit _, _, _, _, _, _ => rfl
  | .app f x, c, i, v, h, hci => by
      simp only [closedAt, Bool.and_eq_true] at h
      simp only [instantiate, instantiate_eq_of_closedAt f c i v h.1 hci,
        instantiate_eq_of_closedAt x c i v h.2 hci]
  | .lam a b, c, i, v, h, hci => by
      simp only [closedAt, Bool.and_eq_true] at h
      have hb := instantiate_eq_of_closedAt b (c + 1) (i + 1) (lift 0 1 v) h.2
        (Nat.succ_le_succ hci)
      simp only [instantiate, instantiate_eq_of_closedAt a c i v h.1 hci, hb]
  | .pi a b, c, i, v, h, hci => by
      simp only [closedAt, Bool.and_eq_true] at h
      have hb := instantiate_eq_of_closedAt b (c + 1) (i + 1) (lift 0 1 v) h.2
        (Nat.succ_le_succ hci)
      simp only [instantiate, instantiate_eq_of_closedAt a c i v h.1 hci, hb]
  | .letE a v0 b, c, i, v, h, hci => by
      simp only [closedAt, Bool.and_eq_true] at h
      have hb := instantiate_eq_of_closedAt b (c + 1) (i + 1) (lift 0 1 v) h.2
        (Nat.succ_le_succ hci)
      simp only [instantiate, instantiate_eq_of_closedAt a c i v h.1.1 hci,
        instantiate_eq_of_closedAt v0 c i v h.1.2 hci, hb]

/- `EnvClosed` is the lift form of the checked-member invariant.
   `EnvSubst` is the instantiate form. The three open defs keep `EnvClosed`
   as the hypothesis; this is the step from one to the other. -/
theorem envSubst_of_envClosed {E : ResolvedEnv} (hE : EnvClosed E) : EnvSubst E := by
  intro r m hm
  obtain ⟨hty, hbo⟩ := hE r m hm
  refine ⟨fun v k => ?_, fun b hb v k => ?_⟩
  · have hc : closedAt 0 m.mtype = true :=
      closedAt_of_lifts m.mtype 0 (fun j => by simpa [Nat.zero_add] using hty j)
    have h := instantiate_eq_of_closedAt m.mtype 0 k v hc (Nat.zero_le k)
    exact h
  · have hc : closedAt 0 b = true :=
      closedAt_of_lifts b 0 (fun j => by simpa [Nat.zero_add] using hbo b hb j)
    exact instantiate_eq_of_closedAt b 0 k v hc (Nat.zero_le k)

/- `lift k 1` pushes every free index up by one, so a term closed at `c`
   is closed at `c + 1` afterwards. The binder arm lifts at cutoff `k + 1`.
   Not AdeqApp, AdeqLetE, or AdeqConstDelta. -/
theorem closedAt_lift :
    ∀ (e : Expr Nat) (c k : Nat),
      closedAt c e = true → closedAt (c + 1) (lift k 1 e) = true
  | .bvar i, c, k, h => by
      have hlt : i < c := by simpa [closedAt, decide_eq_true_eq] using h
      simp only [lift]
      by_cases hk : k ≤ i
      · rw [if_pos hk]
        simp only [closedAt, decide_eq_true_eq]
        exact Nat.succ_lt_succ hlt
      · rw [if_neg hk]
        simp only [closedAt, decide_eq_true_eq]
        exact Nat.lt_succ_of_lt hlt
  | .sort _, _, _, _ => rfl
  | .const _ _, _, _, _ => rfl
  | .lit _, _, _, _ => rfl
  | .app f x, c, k, h => by
      simp only [closedAt, Bool.and_eq_true] at h
      simp only [lift, closedAt, closedAt_lift f c k h.1, closedAt_lift x c k h.2,
        Bool.and_self]
  | .lam a b, c, k, h => by
      simp only [closedAt, Bool.and_eq_true] at h
      have hb := closedAt_lift b (c + 1) (k + 1) h.2
      simp only [lift, closedAt, closedAt_lift a c k h.1, hb, Bool.and_self]
  | .pi a b, c, k, h => by
      simp only [closedAt, Bool.and_eq_true] at h
      have hb := closedAt_lift b (c + 1) (k + 1) h.2
      simp only [lift, closedAt, closedAt_lift a c k h.1, hb, Bool.and_self]
  | .letE a v b, c, k, h => by
      simp only [closedAt, Bool.and_eq_true] at h
      have hb := closedAt_lift b (c + 1) (k + 1) h.2
      simp only [lift, closedAt, closedAt_lift a c k h.1.1, closedAt_lift v c k h.1.2,
        hb, Bool.and_self]

/- Substituting a term closed at `c` for index `c` in a term closed at
   `c + 1` stays closed at `c`. The binder arm substitutes `lift 0 1 v`,
   which `closedAt_lift` puts at cutoff `c + 1`. Not AdeqApp, AdeqLetE,
   or AdeqConstDelta. -/
theorem closedAt_instantiate :
    ∀ (e : Expr Nat) (c : Nat) (v : Expr Nat),
      closedAt (c + 1) e = true → closedAt c v = true →
      closedAt c (instantiate c v e) = true
  | .bvar j, c, v, he, hv => by
      have hlt : j < c + 1 := by simpa [closedAt, decide_eq_true_eq] using he
      by_cases heq : j = c
      · simp only [instantiate]
        rw [if_pos heq]
        exact hv
      · have hjc : j < c := Nat.lt_of_le_of_ne (Nat.le_of_lt_succ hlt) heq
        have hnge : ¬ c < j := Nat.not_lt.mpr (Nat.le_of_lt hjc)
        simp only [instantiate]
        rw [if_neg heq, if_neg hnge]
        simp only [closedAt, decide_eq_true_eq]
        exact hjc
  | .sort _, _, _, _, _ => rfl
  | .const _ _, _, _, _, _ => rfl
  | .lit _, _, _, _, _ => rfl
  | .app f x, c, v, he, hv => by
      simp only [closedAt, Bool.and_eq_true] at he
      simp only [instantiate, closedAt, closedAt_instantiate f c v he.1 hv,
        closedAt_instantiate x c v he.2 hv, Bool.and_self]
  | .lam a b, c, v, he, hv => by
      simp only [closedAt, Bool.and_eq_true] at he
      have hb := closedAt_instantiate b (c + 1) (lift 0 1 v) he.2 (closedAt_lift v c 0 hv)
      simp only [instantiate, closedAt, closedAt_instantiate a c v he.1 hv, hb,
        Bool.and_self]
  | .pi a b, c, v, he, hv => by
      simp only [closedAt, Bool.and_eq_true] at he
      have hb := closedAt_instantiate b (c + 1) (lift 0 1 v) he.2 (closedAt_lift v c 0 hv)
      simp only [instantiate, closedAt, closedAt_instantiate a c v he.1 hv, hb,
        Bool.and_self]
  | .letE a v0 b, c, v, he, hv => by
      simp only [closedAt, Bool.and_eq_true] at he
      have hb := closedAt_instantiate b (c + 1) (lift 0 1 v) he.2 (closedAt_lift v c 0 hv)
      simp only [instantiate, closedAt, closedAt_instantiate a c v he.1.1 hv,
        closedAt_instantiate v0 c v he.1.2 hv, hb, Bool.and_self]

def ctlEnv : ResolvedEnv where
  members := fun r =>
    match r with
    | 0 => some ⟨.inductiveM, 0, .sort (.succ .zero), none⟩
    | 1 => some ⟨.constructorM, 0, cN, none⟩
    | 2 => some ⟨.constructorM, 0, .pi cN cN, none⟩
    | 4 => some ⟨.inductiveM, 0, .sort .zero, none⟩
    | 5 => some ⟨.constructorM, 0, cTrue, none⟩
    | 6 => some ⟨.inductiveM, 0, .sort (.succ .zero), none⟩
    | 7 => some ⟨.constructorM, 0, .const 6 [], none⟩
    | 8 => some ⟨.constructorM, 0, .const 6 [], none⟩
    | 9 => some ⟨.inductiveM, 0, .sort (.succ .zero), none⟩
    | 10 => some ⟨.constructorM, 0, .pi cN (.pi cN (.const 9 [])), none⟩
    | 11 => some ⟨.definitionM, 0, cN, some (.app cSucc (.app cSucc cZero))⟩
    | 12 => some ⟨.definitionM, 0, .pi cN cN,
              some (.lam cN (.app cSucc (.app cSucc (.bvar 0))))⟩
    | 13 => some ⟨.axiomM, 0, cN, none⟩
    | 14 => some ⟨.theoremM, 0, cTrue, some cIntro⟩
    | _ => none

private theorem ctl_member_closed (m : CheckedMember)
    (ht : closedAt 0 m.mtype = true)
    (hb : ∀ b, m.body = some b → closedAt 0 b = true) :
    (∀ k, lift k 1 m.mtype = m.mtype) ∧
      (∀ b, m.body = some b → ∀ k, lift k 1 b = b) :=
  ⟨fun k => by
      have h := lift_eq_of_closedAt m.mtype 0 k ht
      rwa [Nat.zero_add] at h,
   fun b hsome k => by
      have h := lift_eq_of_closedAt b 0 k (hb b hsome)
      rwa [Nat.zero_add] at h⟩

theorem ctlEnv_closed : EnvClosed ctlEnv := by
  intro r m hm
  match r, hm with
  | 0, hm =>
      cases hm
      exact ctl_member_closed _ rfl (fun _ hb => nomatch hb)
  | 1, hm =>
      cases hm
      exact ctl_member_closed _ rfl (fun _ hb => nomatch hb)
  | 2, hm =>
      cases hm
      exact ctl_member_closed _ rfl (fun _ hb => nomatch hb)
  | 3, hm => exact Option.noConfusion hm
  | 4, hm =>
      cases hm
      exact ctl_member_closed _ rfl (fun _ hb => nomatch hb)
  | 5, hm =>
      cases hm
      exact ctl_member_closed _ rfl (fun _ hb => nomatch hb)
  | 6, hm =>
      cases hm
      exact ctl_member_closed _ rfl (fun _ hb => nomatch hb)
  | 7, hm =>
      cases hm
      exact ctl_member_closed _ rfl (fun _ hb => nomatch hb)
  | 8, hm =>
      cases hm
      exact ctl_member_closed _ rfl (fun _ hb => nomatch hb)
  | 9, hm =>
      cases hm
      exact ctl_member_closed _ rfl (fun _ hb => nomatch hb)
  | 10, hm =>
      cases hm
      exact ctl_member_closed _ rfl (fun _ hb => nomatch hb)
  | 11, hm =>
      cases hm
      exact ctl_member_closed _ rfl (fun b hb => by
        cases hb
        rfl)
  | 12, hm =>
      cases hm
      exact ctl_member_closed _ rfl (fun b hb => by
        cases hb
        rfl)
  | 13, hm =>
      cases hm
      exact ctl_member_closed _ rfl (fun _ hb => nomatch hb)
  | 14, hm =>
      cases hm
      exact ctl_member_closed _ rfl (fun b hb => by
        cases hb
        rfl)
  | _ + 15, hm => exact Option.noConfusion hm

/-- scm sum type with `k` summands, each `list τ`. -/
def sumL (k : Nat) (τ : BootTy) : BootTy := .sum (List.replicate k (.list τ))

def tyNat1 : BootTy := sumL 3 .i64
def tyNat2 : BootTy := sumL 3 tyNat1
def tyNat3 : BootTy := sumL 3 tyNat2

def optValEq : Option Val → Option Val → Bool
  | some a, some b => valEq a b
  | none, none => true
  | _, _ => false

/-- the value side: `scmValOf (norm t)`. -/
def obs (E : ResolvedEnv) (e : Expr Nat) : Option Val :=
  match norm E 64 e with
  | some v => scmValOf E 64 v
  | none => none

/-- the scm side: `evalLF` of a lowered term (empty program table). -/
def runLowered {t : BootTy} (b : BootExpr [] [] t) : Option Val :=
  Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA .nil 64 [] b

/-- positive control: the value side is data, and evalLF of the lowering equals it. -/
def agrees (low : (t : BootTy) → Expr Nat → BootExpr [] [] t) (E : ResolvedEnv)
    (t : BootTy) (e : Expr Nat) : Bool :=
  (obs E e).isSome && optValEq (runLowered (low t e)) (obs E e)

def ref (t : BootTy) (e : Expr Nat) : BootExpr [] [] t := Rsx.lower ctlEnv (t := t) e

-- the terms
def g01 : Expr Nat := .lit 5
def g02 : Expr Nat := cZero
def g03 : Expr Nat := .app cSucc (.lit 4)
def g04 : Expr Nat := .app (.lam cN (.app cSucc (.bvar 0))) (.lit 4)              -- β
def g05 : Expr Nat := .letE cN (.lit 7) (.app cSucc (.bvar 0))                     -- ζ
def g06 : Expr Nat := .const 11 []                                                 -- δ
def g07 : Expr Nat := .app (.lam cTrue (.lit 3)) cIntro                            -- proof arg erased
def g08 : Expr Nat :=                                                              -- type arg erased
  .app (.app (.lam (.sort (.succ .zero)) (.lam (.bvar 0) (.bvar 0))) cN) (.lit 9)
def g09 : Expr Nat :=                                                              -- higher order
  .app (.lam (.pi cN cN) (.app (.bvar 0) (.lit 1))) (.lam cN (.app cSucc (.bvar 0)))
def g10 : Expr Nat :=                                                              -- capture
  .app (.app (.lam cN (.lam cN (.app (.app cMk (.bvar 0)) (.bvar 1)))) (.lit 1)) (.lit 2)
def g11 : Expr Nat := .const 8 []
def g12 : Expr Nat := .app (.const 12 []) (.lit 0)                                 -- δ to a λ
def g13 : Expr Nat :=                                                              -- let-bound λ
  .letE (.pi cN cN) (.lam cN (.app cSucc (.bvar 0)))
    (.app (.bvar 0) (.app (.bvar 0) (.lit 0)))
def g14 : Expr Nat := .app (.lam cTrue (.app cSucc cZero)) (.const 14 [])           -- theorem arg erased

-- 14 positive controls: evalLF (Rsx.lower t) = scmValOf (norm t), and is data
#guard agrees ref ctlEnv .i64 g01
#guard agrees ref ctlEnv tyNat1 g02
#guard agrees ref ctlEnv tyNat1 g03
#guard agrees ref ctlEnv tyNat1 g04
#guard agrees ref ctlEnv tyNat1 g05
#guard agrees ref ctlEnv tyNat3 g06
#guard agrees ref ctlEnv .i64 g07
#guard agrees ref ctlEnv .i64 g08
#guard agrees ref ctlEnv tyNat1 g09
#guard agrees ref ctlEnv (sumL 11 .i64) g10
#guard agrees ref ctlEnv (sumL 9 .i64) g11
#guard agrees ref ctlEnv tyNat2 g12
#guard agrees ref ctlEnv tyNat2 g13
#guard agrees ref ctlEnv tyNat2 g14

-- the controls exercise the stages they name: erasure removed the arguments of g07, g08, g14
#guard erase ctlEnv 0 64 [] g07 = some (.app (.lam (.lit 3)) .box)
#guard erase ctlEnv 0 64 [] g08 = some (.app (.app (.lam (.lam (.bvar 0))) .box) (.lit 9))
-- defunctionalization of g10: two λ records, the inner one capturing one variable
#guard (defunc ((erase ctlEnv 0 64 [] g10).getD .box)).2.map Code.ncap = [1, 0]

-- refusals agree with the value side: no data value, and the lowering evaluates to none
def g15 : Expr Nat := .lam cN (.bvar 0)          -- a function: not data
def g16 : Expr Nat := .const 13 []               -- an axiom: rigid, not data
#guard (obs ctlEnv g15).isNone && (runLowered (ref tyNat1 g15)).isNone
#guard (obs ctlEnv g16).isNone && (runLowered (ref tyNat1 g16)).isNone

-- gap witnesses (reports/rsxlower/GAPS.md): the value side has data that no BootExpr of
-- the requested type produces
def g17 : Expr Nat := .app (.app cMk (.const 11 [])) (.lit 3)   -- fields: constructor and literal
def g18 : Expr Nat := .lit 9223372036854775808                  -- 2^63, beyond i64
#guard (obs ctlEnv g17).isSome && (runLowered (ref (sumL 11 .i64) g17)).isNone
#guard (obs ctlEnv g18).isSome && (runLowered (ref .i64 g18)).isNone

/-! ### Negative controls: planted lowering mutants are refused by the same check -/

/-- erasure mutant: treats every term whose type's type is any sort as irrelevant
    (erases data). -/
def irrelevantAnySort (E : ResolvedEnv) (n : Nat) (Γ : LCtx) (e : Expr Nat) : Bool :=
  match inferT E n Γ e with
  | some T =>
      isArity T ||
        (match inferT E n Γ T with
         | some (.sort _) => true
         | _ => false)
  | none => false

/-- defunctionalization mutant: captured slot `k` read at `k` instead of `1 + k`. -/
def capRenOff (fs : List Nat) : Nat → Nat
  | 0 => 0
  | i + 1 => (idxOf i fs).getD fs.length

/-- fuel-stage mutant: `apply` binds the argument after the captured values. -/
def bindLast (a : DVal) (caps : List DVal) : List DVal := caps ++ [a]

/-- emission mutant: constructor fields in reverse order. -/
def fieldsRev (args : List DVal) : List DVal := (relevantArgs args).reverse

def mutErase (t : BootTy) (e : Expr Nat) : BootExpr [] [] t :=
  pipeline (eraseWith (irrelevantAnySort ctlEnv 0) noGlobals ctlEnv) defunc run emit defaultFuel t e
def mutDefunc (t : BootTy) (e : Expr Nat) : BootExpr [] [] t :=
  pipeline (erase ctlEnv 0) (convWith capRenOff id []) run emit defaultFuel t e
def mutRun (t : BootTy) (e : Expr Nat) : BootExpr [] [] t :=
  pipeline (erase ctlEnv 0) defunc (runWith bindLast) emit defaultFuel t e
def mutEmit (t : BootTy) (e : Expr Nat) : BootExpr [] [] t :=
  pipeline (erase ctlEnv 0) defunc run (emitWith fieldsRev) defaultFuel t e

-- the reference is the pipeline with the reference stages
example : ref = pipeline (erase ctlEnv 0) defunc run emit defaultFuel := rfl

#guard !(agrees mutErase ctlEnv tyNat1 g03)
#guard !(agrees mutDefunc ctlEnv (sumL 11 .i64) g10)
#guard !(agrees mutRun ctlEnv (sumL 11 .i64) g10)
#guard !(agrees mutEmit ctlEnv (sumL 11 .i64) g10)

/-! ### Counterexample to the step-4 statement: a Prop-typed data value

`True.intro : True` in `ctlEnv` (member 5; `True` = member 4, an inductive in `Prop`).
`DataTy` holds (`True` is an inductive), `norm` returns `True.intro`, `scmValOf` gives
`.inj 5 (.list [])`, `relevantSpine` holds (no fields), and the value fits
`sumL 6 .i64`. Erasure maps the term to `□` (its type's type is `Prop`: Letouzey's test,
Lean's compiler erases it too), so the lowering refuses at every fuel. Hence the
reference family does NOT meet `adequacyStatementNoRoot` (the step-4 form), and the
statement on main adds `irrelevant E n [] v = false`, which this witness violates
(`cIntro_irrelevant`). -/

def cIntroTyNat : BootTy := sumL 6 .i64

def cIntroTy : HasTyT ctlEnv 0 [] cIntro (instantiateLevels [] cTrue) :=
  .const [] 5 [] ⟨.constructorM, 0, cTrue, none⟩ rfl rfl rfl

theorem cIntroData : DataTy ctlEnv (instantiateLevels [] cTrue) :=
  ⟨4, [], [], ⟨.inductiveM, 0, .sort .zero, none⟩, rfl, rfl, rfl⟩

theorem cIntroNorm : norm ctlEnv 2 cIntro = some cIntro := rfl
theorem cIntroVal : scmValOf ctlEnv 1 cIntro = some (.inj 5 (.list [])) := rfl
theorem cIntroRel : relevantSpine ctlEnv 0 1 cIntro = true := rfl
theorem cIntroFits : valFits 1 cIntroTyNat (.inj 5 (.list [])) = true := by decide
theorem cIntro_irrelevant : irrelevant ctlEnv 0 [] cIntro = true := by decide

/-- the reference lowering of `True.intro` is the refusing term at every fuel and type. -/
theorem lowerF_cIntro {S : SigTable} (F : Nat) (t : BootTy) :
    lowerF ctlEnv 0 F (S := S) t cIntro = refuse := by
  cases F with
  | zero => rfl
  | succ F =>
    have hirr : irrelevant ctlEnv 0 [] (.const 5 []) = true := cIntro_irrelevant
    have he : erase ctlEnv 0 (F + 1) [] cIntro = some .box := by
      simp only [erase, cIntro, eraseWith, hirr, if_true]
    unfold lowerF pipeline
    rw [he]
    cases t <;> rfl

/-- the counterexample: the reference family does not meet the step-4 statement. -/
theorem lowerF_not_adequate_noRoot {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) :
    ¬ adequacyStatementNoRoot (fun E n F t e => lowerF E n F (S := S) t e) progs := by
  intro h
  obtain ⟨F₀, hF⟩ := h ctlEnv 0 2 1 cIntro _ cIntro cIntroTyNat (.inj 5 (.list []))
    cIntroTy cIntroData cIntroNorm cIntroVal cIntroRel cIntroFits
  obtain ⟨lf, he⟩ := hF F₀ (Nat.le_refl _)
  have he' : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf []
      (lowerF ctlEnv 0 F₀ (S := S) cIntroTyNat cIntro) = some (.inj 5 (.list [])) := he
  rw [lowerF_cIntro] at he'
  exact eval_refuse_ne progs lf [] _ he'

-- the same witness as a gap guard: data on the value side, refused by the lowering, and
-- excluded from the statement on main by its root-relevance premise
#guard (obs ctlEnv cIntro).isSome && (runLowered (ref cIntroTyNat cIntro)).isNone &&
  irrelevant ctlEnv 0 [] cIntro

/-! ### Counterexample to the session-7 statement: a transparent body not of its type

`badEnv` is `ctlEnv` plus member 15, a transparent definition `c : True` whose body is
`zero : N`. `HasTyT.const` types `c` at its declared type `True` (no rule reads the body;
only `ConvT.delta` does, and it demands the body typed), so `DataTy` holds. `norm` unfolds
`c` (`whnfFuel` δ never reads a type) to `zero`, whose value `.inj 1 (.list [])` is relevant
(`zero : N`, `N : Type`) and fits `tyNat1`. Erasure tests `c` before δ: its type's type is
`Prop`, so it erases to `□` and the lowering refuses at every fuel. Hence the reference
family does NOT meet `adequacyStatementUntypedEnv` (the session-7 form), and the statement
on main adds `BodiesTyped E n` (MetaCoq's `wf Σ`, the premise of `ConvT.delta`). The body
is outside `BodiesTyped`: the certified checker `inferT` types it at `N`, not `True`
(guard below); a proof that no `HasTyT` derivation types it at `True` needs a model of
`ConvT` and is not given. -/

def badEnv : ResolvedEnv where
  members := fun r =>
    match r with
    | 15 => some ⟨.definitionM, 0, cTrue, some cZero⟩
    | r => ctlEnv.members r

def cBad : Expr Nat := .const 15 []

def cBadTy : HasTyT badEnv 0 [] cBad (instantiateLevels [] cTrue) :=
  .const [] 15 [] ⟨.definitionM, 0, cTrue, some cZero⟩ rfl rfl rfl

/- Member 1 of badEnv is zero, declared at N. -/
theorem badEnv_zero : badEnv.members 1 = some ⟨.constructorM, 0, cN, none⟩ := rfl

/- HasTyT of zero at True is a TyConvT from N to True.
   Not the negation, and not AdeqConstDelta. -/
def tyConvT_cN_cTrue_of_cZero
    (h : HasTyT badEnv 0 [] cZero cTrue) :
    TyConvT badEnv 0 [] cN cTrue := by
  match hasTyT_const_principal h rfl with
  | ⟨m, ⟨hres, ⟨_, ⟨_, ht⟩⟩⟩⟩ =>
      have hm : m = ⟨.constructorM, 0, cN, none⟩ := by
        rw [badEnv_zero] at hres
        injection hres with hm
        exact hm.symm
      subst hm
      exact ht

/- One TyConvT step. The ends are equal, or a ConvT at a sort reaches a
   middle that still type-converts to the right end. No ConvT inversion.
   Not the negation of TyConvT from cN to cTrue, and not AdeqConstDelta,
   AdeqApp, or AdeqLetE. -/
def tyConvT_step {E : ResolvedEnv} {n : Nat} {Γ : LCtx} {A B : Expr Nat}
    (h : TyConvT E n Γ A B) :
    PSum (A = B)
      (Σ' (C : Expr Nat) (u : Level) (_ : ConvT E n Γ A C (.sort u)),
        TyConvT E n Γ C B) :=
  match h with
  | .refl _ _ => PSum.inl rfl
  | .of _ _ _ u hc =>
      PSum.inr ⟨B, ⟨u, ⟨hc, TyConvT.refl _ _⟩⟩⟩
  | .trans _ _ mid _ h1 h2 =>
      match tyConvT_step h1 with
      | PSum.inl heq =>
          Eq.ndrec (motive := fun X =>
              PSum (X = B)
                (Σ' (C : Expr Nat) (u : Level) (_ : ConvT E n Γ X C (.sort u)),
                  TyConvT E n Γ C B))
            (tyConvT_step h2) (Eq.symm heq)
      | PSum.inr ⟨C, ⟨u, ⟨hc, ht⟩⟩⟩ =>
          PSum.inr ⟨C, ⟨u, ⟨hc, TyConvT.trans Γ C mid B ht h2⟩⟩⟩
termination_by sizeOf h

/- TyConvT reads the same backwards. The one-step arm is ConvT.symm.
   No ConvT inversion. -/
def tyConvT_symm {E : ResolvedEnv} {n : Nat} {Γ : LCtx} {A B : Expr Nat}
    (h : TyConvT E n Γ A B) : TyConvT E n Γ B A :=
  match h with
  | .refl _ _ => TyConvT.refl _ _
  | .of _ _ _ u hc =>
      TyConvT.of Γ B A u (ConvT.symm Γ A B (.sort u) hc)
  | .trans _ _ mid _ h1 h2 =>
      TyConvT.trans Γ B mid A (tyConvT_symm h2) (tyConvT_symm h1)
termination_by sizeOf h

/- Two type conversions into one end compose. -/
def tyConvT_of_to_same {E : ResolvedEnv} {n : Nat} {Γ : LCtx}
    {A B C : Expr Nat}
    (hA : TyConvT E n Γ A C) (hB : TyConvT E n Γ B C) :
    TyConvT E n Γ A B :=
  TyConvT.trans Γ A C B hA (tyConvT_symm hB)

/- N and True are different constants. -/
theorem cN_ne_cTrue : cN ≠ cTrue := by
  intro h
  unfold cN cTrue at h
  injection h with hr hls
  cases hr

/- TyConvT from N to True is a ConvT from N at a sort, followed by a
   TyConvT to True. The equality arm is empty. Not the negation. -/
def tyConvT_cN_cTrue_step
    (h : TyConvT badEnv 0 [] cN cTrue) :
    Σ' (C : Expr Nat) (u : Level) (_ : ConvT badEnv 0 [] cN C (.sort u)),
      TyConvT badEnv 0 [] C cTrue :=
  match tyConvT_step h with
  | PSum.inl heq => absurd heq cN_ne_cTrue
  | PSum.inr s => s

/- Member 0 of badEnv is N, an inductive, not a transparent definition. -/
theorem badEnv_N :
    badEnv.members 0 = some ⟨.inductiveM, 0, .sort (.succ .zero), none⟩ := rfl

theorem badEnv_not_transparent_zero (m : CheckedMember)
    (hres : badEnv.members 0 = some m) (htr : transparent m.mclass = true) : False := by
  have hm : m = ⟨.inductiveM, 0, .sort (.succ .zero), none⟩ := by
    rw [badEnv_N] at hres
    injection hres with hm
    exact hm.symm
  subst hm
  cases htr

/- One ConvT step whose left end is N. Beta, zeta, eta, congruence,
   literal, sort, and delta are not in the view: N is not those
   left-hand sides, and member 0 is not transparent. Iota is an
   application spine. The symm, trans, proof-irrelevance, and tyConv
   arms are exposed, not discharged. Not the negation of TyConvT from
   N to True, and not AdeqConstDelta, AdeqApp, or AdeqLetE. -/
inductive ConvCN : Expr Nat → Expr Nat → Type where
  | refl (T : Expr Nat) : ConvCN cN T
  | symm (b T : Expr Nat) (h : ConvT badEnv 0 [] b cN T) : ConvCN b T
  | trans (m b T : Expr Nat)
      (h1 : ConvT badEnv 0 [] cN m T) (h2 : ConvT badEnv 0 [] m b T) : ConvCN b T
  | consts (ls' : List Level) (T : Expr Nat) (h : eqNList [] ls') :
      ConvCN (.const 0 ls') T
  | irr (b T P : Expr Nat)
      (hP : HasTyT badEnv 0 [] P (.sort .zero))
      (hp : HasTyT badEnv 0 [] cN P)
      (hq : HasTyT badEnv 0 [] b P) : ConvCN b T
  | ty (b A T : Expr Nat) (u : Level)
      (h : ConvT badEnv 0 [] cN b A)
      (hA : ConvT badEnv 0 [] A T (.sort u)) : ConvCN b T

def convT_cN_view {b T : Expr Nat} (h : ConvT badEnv 0 [] cN b T) : ConvCN b T :=
  match h with
  | .refl _ _ _ _ => ConvCN.refl T
  | .symm _ x _ _ hinner => ConvCN.symm x T hinner
  | .trans _ _ m _ _ h1 h2 => ConvCN.trans m b T h1 h2
  | .delta _ _ _ m _ hres _ htr _ _ _ =>
      False.elim (badEnv_not_transparent_zero m hres htr)
  | .iota _ _ _ _ hdi _ _ => False.elim (derivedIota_ne_const hdi)
  | .consts _ _ _ ls' m _ _ _ _ heq =>
      ConvCN.consts ls' (instantiateLevels [] m.mtype) heq
  | .irr _ P _ _ hP hp hq => ConvCN.irr b P P hP hp hq
  | .tyConv _ _ _ A _ u hsub hA => ConvCN.ty b A T u hsub hA

/- TyConvT from N to True starts with one of those ConvT shapes. -/
def tyConvT_cN_cTrue_view (h : TyConvT badEnv 0 [] cN cTrue) :
    Σ' (C : Expr Nat) (u : Level) (_ : ConvCN C (.sort u)),
      TyConvT badEnv 0 [] C cTrue :=
  match tyConvT_cN_cTrue_step h with
  | ⟨C, ⟨u, ⟨hc, ht⟩⟩⟩ => ⟨C, ⟨u, ⟨convT_cN_view hc, ht⟩⟩⟩

/- `eqNList [] ls` is the nil clause, so the level list is empty. -/
theorem eqNList_nil_left {ls : List Level} (h : eqNList [] ls) : ls = [] :=
  match ls, h with
  | [], _ => rfl
  | _ :: _, h => nomatch h

theorem const0_nil_eq {ls : List Level} (h : eqNList [] ls) :
    (.const 0 ls : Expr Nat) = cN := by
  cases eqNList_nil_left h
  rfl

theorem const0_ne_cTrue (ls : List Level) : (.const 0 ls : Expr Nat) ≠ cTrue := by
  intro h
  unfold cTrue at h
  injection h with hr
  cases hr

theorem const4_ne_cN (ls : List Level) : (.const 4 ls : Expr Nat) ≠ cN := by
  intro h
  unfold cN at h
  injection h with hr
  cases hr

/- Member 4 of badEnv is True, an inductive, not a transparent definition. -/
theorem badEnv_True :
    badEnv.members 4 = some ⟨.inductiveM, 0, .sort .zero, none⟩ := rfl

theorem badEnv_not_transparent_four (m : CheckedMember)
    (hres : badEnv.members 4 = some m) (htr : transparent m.mclass = true) : False := by
  have hm : m = ⟨.inductiveM, 0, .sort .zero, none⟩ := by
    rw [badEnv_True] at hres
    injection hres with hm
    exact hm.symm
  subst hm
  cases htr

/- One ConvT step from N, with type change stripped. The right end is
   the index. Symmetry, transitivity, and proof irrelevance stay.
   Recursing through tyConv forgets the type annotation. Not the
   negation of TyConvT from N to True. -/
inductive ConvCNty : Expr Nat → Type where
  | refl : ConvCNty cN
  | symm (b T : Expr Nat) (h : ConvT badEnv 0 [] b cN T) : ConvCNty b
  | trans (m b T : Expr Nat)
      (h1 : ConvT badEnv 0 [] cN m T) (h2 : ConvT badEnv 0 [] m b T) : ConvCNty b
  | consts (ls' : List Level) (h : eqNList [] ls') : ConvCNty (.const 0 ls')
  | irr (b P : Expr Nat)
      (hP : HasTyT badEnv 0 [] P (.sort .zero))
      (hp : HasTyT badEnv 0 [] cN P)
      (hq : HasTyT badEnv 0 [] b P) : ConvCNty b

def convT_cN_core {b T : Expr Nat} (h : ConvT badEnv 0 [] cN b T) : ConvCNty b :=
  match h with
  | .refl _ _ _ _ => ConvCNty.refl
  | .symm _ x _ _ hinner => ConvCNty.symm x T hinner
  | .trans _ _ m _ _ h1 h2 => ConvCNty.trans m b T h1 h2
  | .delta _ _ _ m _ hres _ htr _ _ _ =>
      False.elim (badEnv_not_transparent_zero m hres htr)
  | .iota _ _ _ _ hdi _ _ => False.elim (derivedIota_ne_const hdi)
  | .consts _ _ _ ls' _ _ _ _ _ heq => ConvCNty.consts ls' heq
  | .irr _ P _ _ hP hp hq => ConvCNty.irr b P hP hp hq
  | .tyConv _ _ _ _ _ _ hsub _ => convT_cN_core hsub
termination_by sizeOf h

/- Both constants typed at one `P` send their declared types to `P`,
   so `Sort 1` and `Sort 0` are type-convertible. Not `¬ TyConvT`. -/
def tyConvT_sort1_sort0_of_common (P : Expr Nat)
    (hp : HasTyT badEnv 0 [] cN P)
    (hq : HasTyT badEnv 0 [] cTrue P) :
    TyConvT badEnv 0 [] (.sort (.succ .zero)) (.sort .zero) := by
  match hasTyT_const_principal hp rfl with
  | ⟨mN, ⟨hresN, ⟨_, ⟨_, htN⟩⟩⟩⟩ =>
    match hasTyT_const_principal hq rfl with
    | ⟨mT, ⟨hresT, ⟨_, ⟨_, htT⟩⟩⟩⟩ =>
      have hmN : mN = ⟨.inductiveM, 0, .sort (.succ .zero), none⟩ := by
        rw [badEnv_N] at hresN
        injection hresN with hm
        exact hm.symm
      have hmT : mT = ⟨.inductiveM, 0, .sort .zero, none⟩ := by
        rw [badEnv_True] at hresT
        injection hresT with hm
        exact hm.symm
      subst hmN
      subst hmT
      exact tyConvT_of_to_same htN htT

/- What remains of a conversion between N and True after a reflexive
   left half and type change are consumed. `trans` keeps a left half
   that is not reflexivity. `transR` keeps the swapped derivation.
   `sortGap` is the `Sort 1` / `Sort 0` type conversion that proof
   irrelevance produces. Not `¬ TyConvT`, and not AdeqConstDelta,
   AdeqApp, or AdeqLetE. -/
inductive ConvNT : Type where
  | trans (m T : Expr Nat)
      (h1 : ConvT badEnv 0 [] cN m T) (h2 : ConvT badEnv 0 [] m cTrue T) : ConvNT
  | transR (m T : Expr Nat)
      (h1 : ConvT badEnv 0 [] cTrue m T) (h2 : ConvT badEnv 0 [] m cN T) : ConvNT
  | sortGap (h : TyConvT badEnv 0 [] (.sort (.succ .zero)) (.sort .zero)) : ConvNT

/- Delta toward N from a constant equal to True. The only body
   `instantiateLevels` sends to `cN` is `const 0 []`, so the head is
   member 4, which is not transparent. -/
theorem convStuckR_delta_false (r : Nat) (ls : List Level) (m : CheckedMember)
    (hres : badEnv.members r = some m) (htr : transparent m.mclass = true)
    (ha : (.const r ls : Expr Nat) = cTrue) : False := by
  unfold cTrue at ha
  injection ha with hr
  subst hr
  exact badEnv_not_transparent_four m hres htr

theorem instLevels_bvar_ne_cN (ls : List Level) (i : Nat)
    (h : instantiateLevels ls (.bvar i) = cN) : False := by
  unfold instantiateLevels cN at h
  cases h

theorem instLevels_sort_ne_cN (ls : List Level) (l : Level)
    (h : instantiateLevels ls (.sort l) = cN) : False := by
  unfold instantiateLevels cN at h
  cases h

theorem instLevels_app_ne_cN (ls : List Level) (f x : Expr Nat)
    (h : instantiateLevels ls (.app f x) = cN) : False := by
  unfold instantiateLevels cN at h
  cases h

theorem instLevels_lam_ne_cN (ls : List Level) (a b : Expr Nat)
    (h : instantiateLevels ls (.lam a b) = cN) : False := by
  unfold instantiateLevels cN at h
  cases h

theorem instLevels_pi_ne_cN (ls : List Level) (a b : Expr Nat)
    (h : instantiateLevels ls (.pi a b) = cN) : False := by
  unfold instantiateLevels cN at h
  cases h

theorem instLevels_letE_ne_cN (ls : List Level) (a v b : Expr Nat)
    (h : instantiateLevels ls (.letE a v b) = cN) : False := by
  unfold instantiateLevels cN at h
  cases h

theorem instLevels_lit_ne_cN (ls : List Level) (t : Nat)
    (h : instantiateLevels ls (.lit t) = cN) : False := by
  unfold instantiateLevels cN at h
  cases h

theorem instLevels_const_succ_ne_cN (ls : List Level) (n : Nat) (ms : List Level)
    (h : instantiateLevels ls (.const (n + 1) ms) = cN) : False := by
  unfold instantiateLevels cN at h
  injection h with hr
  cases hr

theorem instLevels_const_zero_cons_ne_cN (ls : List Level) (l : Level) (ms : List Level)
    (h : instantiateLevels ls (.const 0 (l :: ms)) = cN) : False := by
  unfold instantiateLevels cN at h
  injection h with hr hms
  cases hms

theorem app_ne_cN (f x : Expr Nat) (h : .app f x = cN) : False := by
  unfold cN at h
  cases h

theorem app_ne_cTrue (f x : Expr Nat) (h : .app f x = cTrue) : False := by
  unfold cTrue at h
  cases h

theorem letE_ne_cN (A v b : Expr Nat) (h : .letE A v b = cN) : False := by
  unfold cN at h
  cases h

theorem letE_ne_cTrue (A v b : Expr Nat) (h : .letE A v b = cTrue) : False := by
  unfold cTrue at h
  cases h

theorem bvar_ne_cN (i : Nat) (h : (.bvar i : Expr Nat) = cN) : False := by
  unfold cN at h
  cases h

theorem bvar_ne_cTrue (i : Nat) (h : (.bvar i : Expr Nat) = cTrue) : False := by
  unfold cTrue at h
  cases h

theorem lit_ne_cN (t : Nat) (h : (.lit t : Expr Nat) = cN) : False := by
  unfold cN at h
  cases h

theorem lit_ne_cTrue (t : Nat) (h : (.lit t : Expr Nat) = cTrue) : False := by
  unfold cTrue at h
  cases h

theorem lam_ne_cN (A b : Expr Nat) (h : .lam A b = cN) : False := by
  unfold cN at h
  cases h

theorem lam_ne_cTrue (A b : Expr Nat) (h : .lam A b = cTrue) : False := by
  unfold cTrue at h
  cases h

theorem pi_ne_cN (A B : Expr Nat) (h : .pi A B = cN) : False := by
  unfold cN at h
  cases h

theorem pi_ne_cTrue (A B : Expr Nat) (h : .pi A B = cTrue) : False := by
  unfold cTrue at h
  cases h

theorem sort_ne_cN (l : Level) (h : (.sort l : Expr Nat) = cN) : False := by
  unfold cN at h
  cases h

theorem sort_ne_cTrue (l : Level) (h : (.sort l : Expr Nat) = cTrue) : False := by
  unfold cTrue at h
  cases h

theorem convStuck_delta_false (r : Nat) (ls : List Level) (m : CheckedMember)
    (hres : badEnv.members r = some m) (htr : transparent m.mclass = true)
    (ha : (.const r ls : Expr Nat) = cN) : False := by
  unfold cN at ha
  injection ha with hr
  subst hr
  exact badEnv_not_transparent_zero m hres htr

theorem consts_cN_ne_cTrue (r : Nat) (ls ls' : List Level)
    (ha : (.const r ls : Expr Nat) = cN) (hb : (.const r ls' : Expr Nat) = cTrue) : False := by
  unfold cN at ha
  injection ha with hr
  subst hr
  exact const0_ne_cTrue ls' hb

theorem consts_cTrue_ne_cN (r : Nat) (ls ls' : List Level)
    (ha : (.const r ls : Expr Nat) = cTrue) (hb : (.const r ls' : Expr Nat) = cN) : False := by
  unfold cTrue at ha
  injection ha with hr
  subst hr
  exact const4_ne_cN ls' hb

/- Both ends stay variables, so `instantiateLevels` unifies. The
   equalities say which end is N and which is True. Symmetry swaps
   those equalities and recurses on the raw subderivation. Not
   `¬ TyConvT`. -/
mutual
def convStuck {a b T : Expr Nat}
    (h : ConvT badEnv 0 [] a b T) (ha : a = cN) (hb : b = cTrue) : ConvNT :=
  match h with
  | .refl _ _ _ _ => False.elim (cN_ne_cTrue (Eq.trans (Eq.symm ha) hb))
  | .symm _ _ _ _ hinner => convStuckAtTrue hinner hb ha
  | .trans _ _ m _ _ h1 h2 =>
      ConvNT.trans m T
        (Eq.ndrec (motive := fun X => ConvT badEnv 0 [] X m T) h1 ha)
        (Eq.ndrec (motive := fun X => ConvT badEnv 0 [] m X T) h2 hb)
  | .tyConv _ _ _ _ _ _ hsub _ => convStuck hsub ha hb
  | .beta _ A body arg _ _ _ _ _ => False.elim (app_ne_cN (.lam A body) arg ha)
  | .zeta _ A value body _ _ _ _ _ => False.elim (letE_ne_cN A value body ha)
  | .zetaLocal _ i _ _ _ _ _ => False.elim (bvar_ne_cN i ha)
  | .delta _ r ls m _ hres _ htr _ _ _ =>
      False.elim (convStuck_delta_false r ls m hres htr ha)
  | .iota _ _ _ _ hdi _ _ =>
      False.elim (derivedIota_ne_const
        (Eq.ndrec (motive := fun X => DerivedIota badEnv X b) hdi ha))
  | .lit _ t _ _ _ _ => False.elim (lit_ne_cN t ha)
  | .app _ f _ x _ _ _ _ _ => False.elim (app_ne_cN f x ha)
  | .lam _ A _ body _ _ _ _ _ => False.elim (lam_ne_cN A body ha)
  | .pi _ A _ B _ _ _ _ _ => False.elim (pi_ne_cN A B ha)
  | .letE _ A _ v _ body _ _ _ _ _ _ => False.elim (letE_ne_cN A v body ha)
  | .sorts _ l _ _ => False.elim (sort_ne_cN l ha)
  | .consts _ r ls ls' _ _ _ _ _ _ => False.elim (consts_cN_ne_cTrue r ls ls' ha hb)
  | .eta _ f A _ _ =>
      False.elim (lam_ne_cN A (.app (lift 0 1 f) (.bvar 0)) ha)
  | .irr _ P _ _ _ hp hq =>
      ConvNT.sortGap (tyConvT_sort1_sort0_of_common P
        (Eq.ndrec (motive := fun X => HasTyT badEnv 0 [] X P) hp ha)
        (Eq.ndrec (motive := fun X => HasTyT badEnv 0 [] X P) hq hb))
termination_by sizeOf h

def convStuckAtTrue {a b T : Expr Nat}
    (h : ConvT badEnv 0 [] a b T) (ha : a = cTrue) (hb : b = cN) : ConvNT :=
  match h with
  | .refl _ _ _ _ => False.elim (cN_ne_cTrue (Eq.trans (Eq.symm hb) ha))
  | .symm _ _ _ _ hinner => convStuck hinner hb ha
  | .trans _ _ m _ _ h1 h2 =>
      ConvNT.transR m T
        (Eq.ndrec (motive := fun X => ConvT badEnv 0 [] X m T) h1 ha)
        (Eq.ndrec (motive := fun X => ConvT badEnv 0 [] m X T) h2 hb)
  | .tyConv _ _ _ _ _ _ hsub _ => convStuckAtTrue hsub ha hb
  | .beta _ A body arg _ _ _ _ _ => False.elim (app_ne_cTrue (.lam A body) arg ha)
  | .zeta _ A value body _ _ _ _ _ => False.elim (letE_ne_cTrue A value body ha)
  | .zetaLocal _ i _ _ _ _ _ => False.elim (bvar_ne_cTrue i ha)
  | .delta _ r ls m _ hres _ htr _ _ _ =>
      False.elim (convStuckR_delta_false r ls m hres htr ha)
  | .iota _ _ _ _ hdi _ _ =>
      False.elim (derivedIota_ne_const
        (Eq.ndrec (motive := fun X => DerivedIota badEnv X b) hdi ha))
  | .lit _ t _ _ _ _ => False.elim (lit_ne_cTrue t ha)
  | .app _ f _ x _ _ _ _ _ => False.elim (app_ne_cTrue f x ha)
  | .lam _ A _ body _ _ _ _ _ => False.elim (lam_ne_cTrue A body ha)
  | .pi _ A _ B _ _ _ _ _ => False.elim (pi_ne_cTrue A B ha)
  | .letE _ A _ v _ body _ _ _ _ _ _ => False.elim (letE_ne_cTrue A v body ha)
  | .sorts _ l _ _ => False.elim (sort_ne_cTrue l ha)
  | .consts _ r ls ls' _ _ _ _ _ _ => False.elim (consts_cTrue_ne_cN r ls ls' ha hb)
  | .eta _ f A _ _ =>
      False.elim (lam_ne_cTrue A (.app (lift 0 1 f) (.bvar 0)) ha)
  | .irr _ P _ _ _ hp hq =>
      ConvNT.sortGap (tyConvT_sort1_sort0_of_common P
        (Eq.ndrec (motive := fun X => HasTyT badEnv 0 [] X P) hq hb)
        (Eq.ndrec (motive := fun X => HasTyT badEnv 0 [] X P) hp ha))
termination_by sizeOf h
end

def convStuckR {a T : Expr Nat}
    (h : ConvT badEnv 0 [] a cN T) (ha : a = cTrue) : ConvNT :=
  convStuckAtTrue h ha rfl

def convT_cN_cTrue_stuck {T : Expr Nat}
    (h : ConvT badEnv 0 [] cN cTrue T) : ConvNT :=
  convStuck h rfl rfl

/- TyConvT from N to True is either one stuck ConvT, or a split whose
   two halves are not equalities. Reflexive halves are dropped by
   `tyConvT_step`. Not the negation. -/
inductive TyStuck : Type where
  | conv (h : ConvNT) : TyStuck
  | trans (mid : Expr Nat)
      (h1 : TyConvT badEnv 0 [] cN mid)
      (h2 : TyConvT badEnv 0 [] mid cTrue) : TyStuck

def tyConvT_cN_stuck {a b : Expr Nat}
    (h : TyConvT badEnv 0 [] a b) (ha : a = cN) (hb : b = cTrue) : TyStuck :=
  match h with
  | .refl _ _ => False.elim (cN_ne_cTrue (Eq.trans (Eq.symm ha) hb))
  | .of _ _ _ u hc =>
      TyStuck.conv (convStuck hc ha hb)
  | .trans _ _ mid _ h1 h2 =>
      match tyConvT_step h1 with
      | PSum.inl heq => tyConvT_cN_stuck h2 (Eq.trans (Eq.symm heq) ha) hb
      | PSum.inr _ =>
          match tyConvT_step h2 with
          | PSum.inl heq => tyConvT_cN_stuck h1 ha (Eq.trans heq hb)
          | PSum.inr _ =>
              TyStuck.trans mid
                (Eq.ndrec (motive := fun X => TyConvT badEnv 0 [] X mid) h1 ha)
                (Eq.ndrec (motive := fun X => TyConvT badEnv 0 [] mid X) h2 hb)
termination_by sizeOf h

def tyConvT_cN_cTrue_stuck (h : TyConvT badEnv 0 [] cN cTrue) : TyStuck :=
  tyConvT_cN_stuck h rfl rfl

/- The empty context stores no let value. -/
theorem lookupValue_nil (i : Nat) : lookupValue ([] : LCtx) i = none := rfl

/- `badEnv` above member 15 is `ctlEnv`, and `ctlEnv` stops at 14.
   `16 + n` does not reduce in either match, so the proof splits.
   Not `¬ TyConvT`, and not AdeqConstDelta, AdeqApp, or AdeqLetE. -/
theorem badEnv_members_ge16 (n : Nat) : badEnv.members (16 + n) = none := by
  have hm : badEnv.members (16 + n) =
      (match (16 + n) with
        | 15 => some ⟨.definitionM, 0, cTrue, some cZero⟩
        | r => ctlEnv.members r) := rfl
  rw [hm]
  split
  · next h =>
      exact absurd (h ▸ Nat.le_add_right 16 n) (Nat.not_le_of_gt (by decide))
  · have hc : ctlEnv.members (16 + n) =
        (match (16 + n) with
          | 0 => some ⟨.inductiveM, 0, .sort (.succ .zero), none⟩
          | 1 => some ⟨.constructorM, 0, cN, none⟩
          | 2 => some ⟨.constructorM, 0, .pi cN cN, none⟩
          | 4 => some ⟨.inductiveM, 0, .sort .zero, none⟩
          | 5 => some ⟨.constructorM, 0, cTrue, none⟩
          | 6 => some ⟨.inductiveM, 0, .sort (.succ .zero), none⟩
          | 7 => some ⟨.constructorM, 0, .const 6 [], none⟩
          | 8 => some ⟨.constructorM, 0, .const 6 [], none⟩
          | 9 => some ⟨.inductiveM, 0, .sort (.succ .zero), none⟩
          | 10 => some ⟨.constructorM, 0, .pi cN (.pi cN (.const 9 [])), none⟩
          | 11 => some ⟨.definitionM, 0, cN, some (.app cSucc (.app cSucc cZero))⟩
          | 12 => some ⟨.definitionM, 0, .pi cN cN,
              some (.lam cN (.app cSucc (.app cSucc (.bvar 0))))⟩
          | 13 => some ⟨.axiomM, 0, cN, none⟩
          | 14 => some ⟨.theoremM, 0, cTrue, some cIntro⟩
          | _ => none) := rfl
    rw [hc]
    split <;> first
      | rfl
      | next h =>
          exact absurd (h ▸ Nat.le_add_right 16 n) (Nat.not_le_of_gt (by decide))

/- No member of badEnv is a recursor, so derived ι does not apply.
   Not `¬ TyConvT`, and not AdeqConstDelta, AdeqApp, or AdeqLetE. -/
theorem badEnv_no_recursor (r : Nat) (m : CheckedMember)
    (hm : badEnv.members r = some m) (hk : m.mclass = .recursorM) : False := by
  match r with
  | 0 =>
      have hr : badEnv.members 0 =
          some ⟨.inductiveM, 0, .sort (.succ .zero), none⟩ := rfl
      rw [hr] at hm
      injection hm with he
      subst he
      cases hk
  | 1 =>
      have hr : badEnv.members 1 = some ⟨.constructorM, 0, cN, none⟩ := rfl
      rw [hr] at hm
      injection hm with he
      subst he
      cases hk
  | 2 =>
      have hr : badEnv.members 2 = some ⟨.constructorM, 0, .pi cN cN, none⟩ := rfl
      rw [hr] at hm
      injection hm with he
      subst he
      cases hk
  | 3 =>
      have hr : badEnv.members 3 = none := rfl
      rw [hr] at hm
      cases hm
  | 4 =>
      have hr : badEnv.members 4 = some ⟨.inductiveM, 0, .sort .zero, none⟩ := rfl
      rw [hr] at hm
      injection hm with he
      subst he
      cases hk
  | 5 =>
      have hr : badEnv.members 5 = some ⟨.constructorM, 0, cTrue, none⟩ := rfl
      rw [hr] at hm
      injection hm with he
      subst he
      cases hk
  | 6 =>
      have hr : badEnv.members 6 =
          some ⟨.inductiveM, 0, .sort (.succ .zero), none⟩ := rfl
      rw [hr] at hm
      injection hm with he
      subst he
      cases hk
  | 7 =>
      have hr : badEnv.members 7 =
          some ⟨.constructorM, 0, .const 6 [], none⟩ := rfl
      rw [hr] at hm
      injection hm with he
      subst he
      cases hk
  | 8 =>
      have hr : badEnv.members 8 =
          some ⟨.constructorM, 0, .const 6 [], none⟩ := rfl
      rw [hr] at hm
      injection hm with he
      subst he
      cases hk
  | 9 =>
      have hr : badEnv.members 9 =
          some ⟨.inductiveM, 0, .sort (.succ .zero), none⟩ := rfl
      rw [hr] at hm
      injection hm with he
      subst he
      cases hk
  | 10 =>
      have hr : badEnv.members 10 =
          some ⟨.constructorM, 0, .pi cN (.pi cN (.const 9 [])), none⟩ := rfl
      rw [hr] at hm
      injection hm with he
      subst he
      cases hk
  | 11 =>
      have hr : badEnv.members 11 =
          some ⟨.definitionM, 0, cN, some (.app cSucc (.app cSucc cZero))⟩ := rfl
      rw [hr] at hm
      injection hm with he
      subst he
      cases hk
  | 12 =>
      have hr : badEnv.members 12 =
          some ⟨.definitionM, 0, .pi cN cN,
            some (.lam cN (.app cSucc (.app cSucc (.bvar 0))))⟩ := rfl
      rw [hr] at hm
      injection hm with he
      subst he
      cases hk
  | 13 =>
      have hr : badEnv.members 13 = some ⟨.axiomM, 0, cN, none⟩ := rfl
      rw [hr] at hm
      injection hm with he
      subst he
      cases hk
  | 14 =>
      have hr : badEnv.members 14 = some ⟨.theoremM, 0, cTrue, some cIntro⟩ := rfl
      rw [hr] at hm
      injection hm with he
      subst he
      cases hk
  | 15 =>
      have hr : badEnv.members 15 =
          some ⟨.definitionM, 0, cTrue, some cZero⟩ := rfl
      rw [hr] at hm
      injection hm with he
      subst he
      cases hk
  | n + 16 =>
      rw [Nat.add_comm] at hm
      rw [badEnv_members_ge16 n] at hm
      cases hm

theorem derivedIota_badEnv_false {lhs rhs : Expr Nat}
    (h : DerivedIota badEnv lhs rhs) : False := by
  cases h with
  | of w => exact badEnv_no_recursor w.recRef w.recMember w.hrec w.hrecK

/- The three transparent bodies, after any level substitution. None is a
   sort. Members 11, 12, and 15 are the only transparent ones. -/
theorem badEnv_tb_11 (ls : List Level) :
    transparentBody badEnv 11 ls = some (.app cSucc (.app cSucc cZero)) := rfl

theorem badEnv_tb_12 (ls : List Level) :
    transparentBody badEnv 12 ls =
      some (.lam cN (.app cSucc (.app cSucc (.bvar 0)))) := rfl

theorem badEnv_tb_15 (ls : List Level) :
    transparentBody badEnv 15 ls = some cZero := rfl

theorem badEnv_tb_none_0 (ls : List Level) : transparentBody badEnv 0 ls = none := rfl
theorem badEnv_tb_none_1 (ls : List Level) : transparentBody badEnv 1 ls = none := rfl
theorem badEnv_tb_none_2 (ls : List Level) : transparentBody badEnv 2 ls = none := rfl
theorem badEnv_tb_none_3 (ls : List Level) : transparentBody badEnv 3 ls = none := rfl
theorem badEnv_tb_none_4 (ls : List Level) : transparentBody badEnv 4 ls = none := rfl
theorem badEnv_tb_none_5 (ls : List Level) : transparentBody badEnv 5 ls = none := rfl
theorem badEnv_tb_none_6 (ls : List Level) : transparentBody badEnv 6 ls = none := rfl
theorem badEnv_tb_none_7 (ls : List Level) : transparentBody badEnv 7 ls = none := rfl
theorem badEnv_tb_none_8 (ls : List Level) : transparentBody badEnv 8 ls = none := rfl
theorem badEnv_tb_none_9 (ls : List Level) : transparentBody badEnv 9 ls = none := rfl
theorem badEnv_tb_none_10 (ls : List Level) : transparentBody badEnv 10 ls = none := rfl
theorem badEnv_tb_none_13 (ls : List Level) : transparentBody badEnv 13 ls = none := rfl
theorem badEnv_tb_none_14 (ls : List Level) : transparentBody badEnv 14 ls = none := rfl

theorem badEnv_tb_none_tail (n : Nat) (ls : List Level) :
    transparentBody badEnv (n + 16) ls = none := by
  rw [Nat.add_comm]
  unfold transparentBody
  rw [badEnv_members_ge16 n]

/- `succ (succ zero)` is stuck: `succ` is a constructor. -/
theorem whnf_two_stuck (k : Nat) :
    whnfFuel badEnv (k + 1) (.app cSucc (.app cSucc cZero)) =
      some (.app cSucc (.app cSucc cZero)) := rfl

theorem whnf_addTwo_body (k : Nat) :
    whnfFuel badEnv (k + 1) (.lam cN (.app cSucc (.app cSucc (.bvar 0)))) =
      some (.lam cN (.app cSucc (.app cSucc (.bvar 0)))) := rfl

theorem whnf_cZero_self (k : Nat) : whnfFuel badEnv (k + 1) cZero = some cZero := rfl

/- No constant of badEnv weak-heads to a sort. A rigid head is itself.
   The three transparent bodies are an application of `succ`, a λ, and
   `zero`. Not `¬ TyConvT`. -/
theorem whnf_badEnv_const_not_sort (r : Nat) (ls : List Level) (l : Level) (k : Nat) :
    whnfFuel badEnv k (.const r ls) ≠ some (.sort l) := by
  induction k generalizing r ls with
  | zero =>
      intro h
      exact whnf_zero_none h
  | succ k ih =>
      intro h
      match r with
      | 11 =>
          rw [whnf_const_delta badEnv k 11 ls _ (badEnv_tb_11 ls)] at h
          cases k with
          | zero => exact whnf_zero_none h
          | succ k =>
              rw [whnf_two_stuck k] at h
              injection h with he
              cases he
      | 12 =>
          rw [whnf_const_delta badEnv k 12 ls _ (badEnv_tb_12 ls)] at h
          cases k with
          | zero => exact whnf_zero_none h
          | succ k =>
              rw [whnf_addTwo_body k] at h
              injection h with he
              cases he
      | 15 =>
          rw [whnf_const_delta badEnv k 15 ls _ (badEnv_tb_15 ls)] at h
          exact ih 1 [] h
      | 0 =>
          rw [whnf_rigid_const k 0 ls (badEnv_tb_none_0 ls)] at h
          injection h with he
          cases he
      | 1 =>
          rw [whnf_rigid_const k 1 ls (badEnv_tb_none_1 ls)] at h
          injection h with he
          cases he
      | 2 =>
          rw [whnf_rigid_const k 2 ls (badEnv_tb_none_2 ls)] at h
          injection h with he
          cases he
      | 3 =>
          rw [whnf_rigid_const k 3 ls (badEnv_tb_none_3 ls)] at h
          injection h with he
          cases he
      | 4 =>
          rw [whnf_rigid_const k 4 ls (badEnv_tb_none_4 ls)] at h
          injection h with he
          cases he
      | 5 =>
          rw [whnf_rigid_const k 5 ls (badEnv_tb_none_5 ls)] at h
          injection h with he
          cases he
      | 6 =>
          rw [whnf_rigid_const k 6 ls (badEnv_tb_none_6 ls)] at h
          injection h with he
          cases he
      | 7 =>
          rw [whnf_rigid_const k 7 ls (badEnv_tb_none_7 ls)] at h
          injection h with he
          cases he
      | 8 =>
          rw [whnf_rigid_const k 8 ls (badEnv_tb_none_8 ls)] at h
          injection h with he
          cases he
      | 9 =>
          rw [whnf_rigid_const k 9 ls (badEnv_tb_none_9 ls)] at h
          injection h with he
          cases he
      | 10 =>
          rw [whnf_rigid_const k 10 ls (badEnv_tb_none_10 ls)] at h
          injection h with he
          cases he
      | 13 =>
          rw [whnf_rigid_const k 13 ls (badEnv_tb_none_13 ls)] at h
          injection h with he
          cases he
      | 14 =>
          rw [whnf_rigid_const k 14 ls (badEnv_tb_none_14 ls)] at h
          injection h with he
          cases he
      | n + 16 =>
          rw [whnf_rigid_const k (n + 16) ls (badEnv_tb_none_tail n ls)] at h
          injection h with he
          cases he

theorem whnf_natExpand_zero (k : Nat) :
    whnfFuel badEnv (k + 1) (natExpand 0) = some (natExpand 0) := rfl

theorem whnf_natExpand_succ (t k : Nat) :
    whnfFuel badEnv (k + 1) (natExpand (t + 1)) = some (natExpand (t + 1)) := rfl

theorem whnf_natExpand_not_sort (t : Nat) (l : Level) (k : Nat) :
    whnfFuel badEnv k (natExpand t) ≠ some (.sort l) := by
  cases k with
  | zero =>
      intro h
      exact whnf_zero_none h
  | succ k =>
      cases t with
      | zero =>
          intro h
          rw [whnf_natExpand_zero k] at h
          injection h with he
          cases he
      | succ t =>
          intro h
          rw [whnf_natExpand_succ t k] at h
          injection h with he
          cases he

/- A weak-head sort. Fuel is existential, so one successful step is enough.
   Not `¬ TyConvT`, and not AdeqConstDelta, AdeqApp, or AdeqLetE. -/
def IsSort (e : Expr Nat) (l : Level) : Prop :=
  ∃ k, whnfFuel badEnv k e = some (.sort l)

theorem isSort_sort (l : Level) : IsSort (.sort l) l :=
  ⟨1, whnf_sort_self badEnv 0 l⟩

theorem not_isSort_lam (A b : Expr Nat) (l : Level) (h : IsSort (.lam A b) l) : False := by
  obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := h
  cases k with
  | zero => exact whnf_zero_none hk
  | succ k =>
      rw [whnf_lam_self badEnv k A b] at hk
      injection hk with he
      cases he

theorem not_isSort_pi (A B : Expr Nat) (l : Level) (h : IsSort (.pi A B) l) : False := by
  obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := h
  cases k with
  | zero => exact whnf_zero_none hk
  | succ k =>
      rw [whnf_pi_self badEnv k A B] at hk
      injection hk with he
      cases he

theorem not_isSort_bvar (i : Nat) (l : Level) (h : IsSort (.bvar i) l) : False := by
  obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := h
  cases k with
  | zero => exact whnf_zero_none hk
  | succ k =>
      rw [whnf_bvar_self badEnv k i] at hk
      injection hk with he
      cases he

theorem not_isSort_lit (t : Nat) (l : Level) (h : IsSort (.lit t) l) : False := by
  obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := h
  cases k with
  | zero => exact whnf_zero_none hk
  | succ k =>
      rw [whnf_lit_self badEnv k t] at hk
      injection hk with he
      cases he

theorem not_isSort_const (r : Nat) (ls : List Level) (l : Level)
    (h : IsSort (.const r ls) l) : False := by
  obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := h
  exact whnf_badEnv_const_not_sort r ls l k hk

/- The level `whnfFuel` returns for a sort is that sort's level. -/
theorem isSort_sort_eq (l l' : Level) (h : IsSort (.sort l) l') : eqN l l' := by
  obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := h
  cases k with
  | zero => exact False.elim (whnf_zero_none hk)
  | succ k =>
      rw [whnf_sort_self badEnv k l] at hk
      injection hk with he
      cases he
      exact eqN_refl l

/- One β step moves a sort witness onto the instantiated body. -/
theorem isSort_beta (A body arg : Expr Nat) (l : Level)
    (h : IsSort (.app (.lam A body) arg) l) : IsSort (instantiate0 arg body) l := by
  obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := h
  cases k with
  | zero => exact False.elim (whnf_zero_none hk)
  | succ k =>
      rw [whnf_beta badEnv k A body arg] at hk
      exact ⟨k, hk⟩

theorem isSort_of_beta (A body arg : Expr Nat) (l : Level)
    (h : IsSort (instantiate0 arg body) l) : IsSort (.app (.lam A body) arg) l := by
  obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := h
  refine ⟨k + 1, ?_⟩
  rw [whnf_beta badEnv k A body arg]
  exact hk

/- One ζ step moves a sort witness onto the instantiated body. -/
theorem isSort_zeta (A v body : Expr Nat) (l : Level)
    (h : IsSort (.letE A v body) l) : IsSort (instantiate0 v body) l := by
  obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := h
  cases k with
  | zero => exact False.elim (whnf_zero_none hk)
  | succ k =>
      rw [whnf_zeta badEnv k A v body] at hk
      exact ⟨k, hk⟩

theorem isSort_of_zeta (A v body : Expr Nat) (l : Level)
    (h : IsSort (instantiate0 v body) l) : IsSort (.letE A v body) l := by
  obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := h
  refine ⟨k + 1, ?_⟩
  rw [whnf_zeta badEnv k A v body]
  exact hk

/- Substituting under a lifted term does nothing: the lift pushed every
   index past `j`. No `omega`. Not `¬ TyConvT`. -/
theorem instantiate_lift_cancel (j : Nat) (s e : Expr Nat) :
    instantiate j s (lift j 1 e) = e := by
  induction e generalizing j s with
  | bvar i =>
      by_cases hle : j ≤ i
      · have hlift : lift j 1 (Expr.bvar (R := Nat) i) =
            (Expr.bvar (R := Nat) (i + 1)) := by
          simp only [lift, if_pos hle]
        rw [hlift]
        have hne : i + 1 ≠ j := by
          intro heq
          exact Nat.not_succ_le_self i (Nat.le_trans (Nat.le_of_eq heq) hle)
        have hlt : j < i + 1 := Nat.lt_succ_of_le hle
        have hinst : instantiate j s (Expr.bvar (R := Nat) (i + 1)) =
            (Expr.bvar (R := Nat) ((i + 1) - 1)) := by
          simp only [instantiate, if_neg hne, if_pos hlt]
        rw [hinst, Nat.add_sub_cancel i 1]
      · have hlift : lift j 1 (Expr.bvar (R := Nat) i) =
            (Expr.bvar (R := Nat) i) := by
          simp only [lift, if_neg hle]
        rw [hlift]
        have hne : i ≠ j := by
          intro heq
          exact hle (Nat.le_of_eq heq.symm)
        have hnlt : ¬ j < i := fun hlt => hle (Nat.le_of_lt hlt)
        simp only [instantiate, if_neg hne, if_neg hnlt]
  | sort _ => rfl
  | const _ _ => rfl
  | lit _ => rfl
  | app f x ihf ihx =>
      simp only [lift, instantiate]
      rw [ihf j s, ihx j s]
  | lam a b iha ihb =>
      simp only [lift, instantiate]
      rw [iha j s, ihb (j + 1) (lift 0 1 s)]
  | pi a b iha ihb =>
      simp only [lift, instantiate]
      rw [iha j s, ihb (j + 1) (lift 0 1 s)]
  | letE a v b iha ihv ihb =>
      simp only [lift, instantiate]
      rw [iha j s, ihv j s, ihb (j + 1) (lift 0 1 s)]

/- One `whnfFuel` step on `badEnv`. `none` means the head is already
   weak-head (a sort, a rigid constant, a lambda with no argument, …).
   Not `¬ TyConvT`. -/
def spineStep (e : Expr Nat) : Option (Expr Nat) :=
  match appsSpine e with
  | (.lam _ b, arg :: args) => some (foldApps (instantiate0 arg b) args)
  | (.letE _ v b, args) => some (foldApps (instantiate0 v b) args)
  | (.const r ls, args) =>
      match transparentBody badEnv r ls with
      | some body => some (foldApps body args)
      | none => none
  | _ => none

theorem whnf_succ (k : Nat) (e : Expr Nat) :
    whnfFuel badEnv (k + 1) e =
      (spineStep e).elim (some e) (whnfFuel badEnv k) := by
  match h : appsSpine e with
  | (.lam _ b, arg :: args) =>
      simp only [whnfFuel, spineStep, h, Option.elim]
  | (.lam _ b, []) =>
      simp only [whnfFuel, spineStep, h, Option.elim]
  | (.letE _ v b, args) =>
      simp only [whnfFuel, spineStep, h, Option.elim]
  | (.const r ls, args) =>
      simp only [whnfFuel, spineStep, h, Option.elim]
      split <;> rfl
  | (.bvar _, _) =>
      simp only [whnfFuel, spineStep, h, Option.elim]
  | (.sort _, _) =>
      simp only [whnfFuel, spineStep, h, Option.elim]
  | (.pi _ _, _) =>
      simp only [whnfFuel, spineStep, h, Option.elim]
  | (.lit _, _) =>
      simp only [whnfFuel, spineStep, h, Option.elim]
  | (.app _ _, _) =>
      simp only [whnfFuel, spineStep, h, Option.elim]

/- A sort witness is either the sort itself or one step closer to it.
   Not `¬ TyConvT`, and not AdeqConstDelta, AdeqApp, or AdeqLetE. -/
theorem isSort_progress (e : Expr Nat) (l : Level) (h : IsSort e l) :
    e = .sort l ∨ ∃ e', spineStep e = some e' ∧ IsSort e' l := by
  obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := h
  cases k with
  | zero => exact False.elim (whnf_zero_none hk)
  | succ k =>
      rw [whnf_succ k e] at hk
      cases hs : spineStep e with
      | none =>
          simp only [hs, Option.elim] at hk
          injection hk with he
          exact Or.inl he
      | some e' =>
          simp only [hs, Option.elim] at hk
          exact Or.inr ⟨e', rfl, ⟨k, hk⟩⟩

/- A conversion whose left end is already a syntactic sort. `refl` and
   `sorts` keep a sort on the right. `symm`, `trans`, and `irr` do not:
   symmetry of β sends a sort to an application. Not level preservation,
   not `¬ TyConvT badEnv 0 [] cN cTrue`, and not AdeqConstDelta, AdeqApp,
   or AdeqLetE. -/
inductive ConvFromSort (l : Level) : Expr Nat → Type where
  | refl : ConvFromSort l (.sort l)
  | symm (a T : Expr Nat) (h : ConvT badEnv 0 [] a (.sort l) T) :
      ConvFromSort l a
  | trans (m b T : Expr Nat)
      (h1 : ConvT badEnv 0 [] (.sort l) m T)
      (h2 : ConvT badEnv 0 [] m b T) : ConvFromSort l b
  | sorts (l₂ : Level) (h : eqN l l₂) : ConvFromSort l (.sort l₂)
  | irr (b P : Expr Nat)
      (hP : HasTyT badEnv 0 [] P (.sort .zero))
      (hp : HasTyT badEnv 0 [] (.sort l) P)
      (hq : HasTyT badEnv 0 [] b P) : ConvFromSort l b

def convFromSort {b T : Expr Nat} {l : Level}
    (h : ConvT badEnv 0 [] (.sort l) b T) : ConvFromSort l b :=
  match h with
  | .refl _ _ _ _ => ConvFromSort.refl
  | .symm _ a _ _ hinner => ConvFromSort.symm a T hinner
  | .trans _ _ m _ _ h1 h2 => ConvFromSort.trans m b T h1 h2
  | .tyConv _ _ _ _ _ _ hsub _ => convFromSort hsub
  | .iota _ _ _ _ hdi _ _ => False.elim (derivedIota_badEnv_false hdi)
  | .sorts _ _ l₂ heq => ConvFromSort.sorts l₂ heq
  | .irr _ P _ _ hP hp hq => ConvFromSort.irr b P hP hp hq
termination_by sizeOf h

/- `Sort l₁ = Sort l₂` is `eqN`. Injection on the sort constructor,
   then reflexivity. Not `¬ TyConvT`. -/
theorem eqN_of_sort_eq {l₁ l₂ : Level}
    (h : (.sort l₁ : Expr Nat) = .sort l₂) : eqN l₁ l₂ :=
  match h with
  | rfl => eqN_refl l₁

/- What remains of a conversion between two syntactic sorts after
   `refl`, `sorts`, symmetry, and `tyConv` are consumed. `trans` keeps
   a middle that is not a sort. `irr` keeps the common proposition.
   `swap` is symmetry of a stuck derivation. The end equalities stay
   hypotheses: rewriting them under the subderivation is what the
   matcher does not do. Not `¬ TyConvT`, and not AdeqConstDelta,
   AdeqApp, or AdeqLetE. -/
inductive ConvSortStuck : Level → Level → Type where
  | trans {l₁ l₂ : Level} {a b : Expr Nat} (m T : Expr Nat)
      (h1 : ConvT badEnv 0 [] a m T) (h2 : ConvT badEnv 0 [] m b T)
      (ha : a = .sort l₁) (hb : b = .sort l₂) : ConvSortStuck l₁ l₂
  | irr {l₁ l₂ : Level} {p q : Expr Nat} (P : Expr Nat)
      (hP : HasTyT badEnv 0 [] P (.sort .zero))
      (hp : HasTyT badEnv 0 [] p P) (hq : HasTyT badEnv 0 [] q P)
      (hp_eq : p = .sort l₁) (hq_eq : q = .sort l₂) : ConvSortStuck l₁ l₂
  | swap {l₁ l₂ : Level} (s : ConvSortStuck l₂ l₁) : ConvSortStuck l₁ l₂
  | after {l₁ l₂ : Level} (l' : Level) (heq : eqN l₁ l')
      (s : ConvSortStuck l' l₂) : ConvSortStuck l₁ l₂
  | before {l₁ l₂ : Level} (l' : Level) (heq : eqN l' l₂)
      (s : ConvSortStuck l₁ l') : ConvSortStuck l₁ l₂

/- The left half of a `ConvT` from a sort to an unknown middle.
   `refl` and `sorts` make the middle a sort. `other` does not refine
   it, so the right half still starts at that middle. Not `¬ TyConvT`. -/
inductive ConvLeft (l₁ : Level) : Expr Nat → Type where
  | refl : ConvLeft l₁ (.sort l₁)
  | sorts (l' : Level) (heq : eqN l₁ l') : ConvLeft l₁ (.sort l')
  | other (mid : Expr Nat) : ConvLeft l₁ mid

/- A nested `trans` whose left half is `refl` or `sorts` is consumed.
   `symm` and `irr` do not make the right end a sort. Not `¬ TyConvT`. -/
def convLeftAt {l₁ : Level} {mid T : Expr Nat}
    (h1 : ConvT badEnv 0 [] (.sort l₁) mid T) : ConvLeft l₁ mid :=
  match h1 with
  | .refl _ _ _ _ => ConvLeft.refl
  | .symm _ a _ _ _ => ConvLeft.other a
  | .trans _ _ m _ _ hA hB =>
      match convLeftAt hA with
      | .refl => convLeftAt hB
      | .sorts l' heq =>
          match convLeftAt hB with
          | .refl => ConvLeft.sorts l' heq
          | .sorts l'' heq2 => ConvLeft.sorts l'' (eqN_trans heq heq2)
          | .other _ => ConvLeft.other mid
      | .other _ => ConvLeft.other mid
  | .tyConv _ _ _ _ _ _ hsub _ => convLeftAt hsub
  | .iota _ _ _ _ hdi _ _ => False.elim (derivedIota_badEnv_false hdi)
  | .sorts _ _ l' heq => ConvLeft.sorts l' heq
  | .irr _ _ _ b _ _ _ => ConvLeft.other b
termination_by sizeOf h1

def convLeft {l₁ : Level} {a mid T : Expr Nat}
    (h1 : ConvT badEnv 0 [] a mid T) (ha : a = .sort l₁) : ConvLeft l₁ mid :=
  convLeftAt (Eq.ndrec (motive := fun X => ConvT badEnv 0 [] X mid T) h1 ha)

/- What remains of a type conversion between two syntactic sorts.
   `step` is one stuck `ConvT`. `trans` is a split whose left half is
   not a reflexive or `sorts` prefix. `after` carries `eqN` across a
   `sorts` step whose continuation is stuck. Not `¬ TyConvT`. -/
inductive TySortStuck : Level → Level → Type where
  | step {l₁ l₂ : Level} (s : ConvSortStuck l₁ l₂) : TySortStuck l₁ l₂
  | trans {l₁ l₂ : Level} {mid : Expr Nat}
      (h1 : TyConvT badEnv 0 [] (.sort l₁) mid)
      (h2 : TyConvT badEnv 0 [] mid (.sort l₂)) : TySortStuck l₁ l₂
  | after {l₁ l₂ : Level} (l' : Level) (heq : eqN l₁ l')
      (s : TySortStuck l' l₂) : TySortStuck l₁ l₂

/- The left half of a `TyConvT` between a sort and an unknown middle.
   `refl` and `sorts` make the middle a sort. `other` does not refine
   it, so the two halves still share that middle. Not `¬ TyConvT`. -/
inductive TyLeft (l₁ : Level) : Expr Nat → Type where
  | refl : TyLeft l₁ (.sort l₁)
  | sorts (l' : Level) (heq : eqN l₁ l') : TyLeft l₁ (.sort l')
  | other (mid : Expr Nat) : TyLeft l₁ mid

/- A nested `trans` whose left half is `refl` or `sorts` is consumed.
   The `of` arm uses `convLeftAt`, so a sort prefix under `ConvT.trans`
   is consumed there too. Not `¬ TyConvT`. -/
def tyLeft {l₁ : Level} {mid : Expr Nat}
    (h1 : TyConvT badEnv 0 [] (.sort l₁) mid) : TyLeft l₁ mid :=
  match h1 with
  | .refl _ _ => TyLeft.refl
  | .of _ _ _ _ hc =>
      match convLeftAt hc with
      | .refl => TyLeft.refl
      | .sorts l' heq => TyLeft.sorts l' heq
      | .other a => TyLeft.other a
  | .trans _ _ m _ hA hB =>
      match tyLeft hA with
      | .refl => tyLeft hB
      | .sorts l' heq =>
          match tyLeft hB with
          | .refl => TyLeft.sorts l' heq
          | .sorts l'' heq2 => TyLeft.sorts l'' (eqN_trans heq heq2)
          | .other _ => TyLeft.other mid
      | .other _ => TyLeft.other mid
termination_by sizeOf h1

/- `succ` on levels is injective for `eqN`. The evaluator adds one, and
   `Nat.succ` is injective. Not `¬ TyConvT`, and not AdeqConstDelta,
   AdeqApp, or AdeqLetE. -/
theorem eqN_succ_inj {l₁ l₂ : Level} (h : eqN (.succ l₁) (.succ l₂)) : eqN l₁ l₂ := by
  intro ρ
  have hρ : Rsx.eval ρ (.succ l₁) = Rsx.eval ρ (.succ l₂) := h ρ
  simp only [Rsx.eval] at hρ
  cases h₁ : Rsx.eval ρ l₁ with
  | none =>
      cases h₂ : Rsx.eval ρ l₂ with
      | none => rfl
      | some n =>
          rw [h₁, h₂] at hρ
          simp only [Option.map] at hρ
          cases hρ
  | some n =>
      cases h₂ : Rsx.eval ρ l₂ with
      | none =>
          rw [h₁, h₂] at hρ
          simp only [Option.map] at hρ
          cases hρ
      | some m =>
          rw [h₁, h₂] at hρ
          simp only [Option.map] at hρ
          injection hρ with hnm
          injection hnm with hn
          subst hn
          rfl

/- `instantiate index arg body` is a sort only when the body is that sort,
   or the body is the substituted variable and the argument is that sort.
   An application, lambda, product, let, literal, or constant stays that
   constructor. Not `¬ TyConvT`. -/
theorem instantiate_eq_sort (index : Nat) (arg body : Expr Nat) (l : Level)
    (h : instantiate index arg body = .sort l) :
    body = .sort l ∨ (body = .bvar index ∧ arg = .sort l) := by
  cases body with
  | sort l' =>
      simp only [instantiate] at h
      cases h
      exact Or.inl rfl
  | bvar i =>
      simp only [instantiate] at h
      by_cases heq : i = index
      · simp only [heq, if_pos rfl] at h
        exact Or.inr ⟨by subst heq; rfl, h⟩
      · simp only [if_neg heq] at h
        by_cases hlt : index < i
        · simp only [if_pos hlt] at h
          cases h
        · simp only [if_neg hlt] at h
          cases h
  | const _ _ =>
      simp only [instantiate] at h
      cases h
  | app _ _ =>
      simp only [instantiate] at h
      cases h
  | lam _ _ =>
      simp only [instantiate] at h
      cases h
  | pi _ _ =>
      simp only [instantiate] at h
      cases h
  | letE _ _ _ =>
      simp only [instantiate] at h
      cases h
  | lit _ =>
      simp only [instantiate] at h
      cases h

theorem instantiate0_eq_sort (arg body : Expr Nat) (l : Level)
    (h : instantiate0 arg body = .sort l) :
    body = .sort l ∨ (body = .bvar 0 ∧ arg = .sort l) :=
  instantiate_eq_sort 0 arg body l h

/- A `badEnv` transparent body, after level substitution, is never a sort.
   The only transparent members are 11, 12, and 15, and each body is an
   application, a lambda, or `zero`. Not `¬ TyConvT`. -/
theorem transparentBody_badEnv_ne_sort (r : Nat) (ls : List Level) (l : Level) :
    transparentBody badEnv r ls ≠ some (.sort l) := by
  intro h
  match r with
  | 0 =>
      rw [badEnv_tb_none_0] at h
      cases h
  | 1 =>
      rw [badEnv_tb_none_1] at h
      cases h
  | 2 =>
      rw [badEnv_tb_none_2] at h
      cases h
  | 3 =>
      rw [badEnv_tb_none_3] at h
      cases h
  | 4 =>
      rw [badEnv_tb_none_4] at h
      cases h
  | 5 =>
      rw [badEnv_tb_none_5] at h
      cases h
  | 6 =>
      rw [badEnv_tb_none_6] at h
      cases h
  | 7 =>
      rw [badEnv_tb_none_7] at h
      cases h
  | 8 =>
      rw [badEnv_tb_none_8] at h
      cases h
  | 9 =>
      rw [badEnv_tb_none_9] at h
      cases h
  | 10 =>
      rw [badEnv_tb_none_10] at h
      cases h
  | 11 =>
      rw [badEnv_tb_11] at h
      injection h with he
      cases he
  | 12 =>
      rw [badEnv_tb_12] at h
      injection h with he
      cases he
  | 13 =>
      rw [badEnv_tb_none_13] at h
      cases h
  | 14 =>
      rw [badEnv_tb_none_14] at h
      cases h
  | 15 =>
      rw [badEnv_tb_15] at h
      injection h with he
      cases he
  | n + 16 =>
      rw [badEnv_tb_none_tail n] at h
      cases h

theorem badEnv_delta_rhs_ne_sort (r : Nat) (ls : List Level) (m : CheckedMember)
    (b : Expr Nat) (l : Level)
    (hres : badEnv.members r = some m) (hbody : m.body = some b)
    (htr : transparent m.mclass = true)
    (h : instantiateLevels ls b = .sort l) : False := by
  apply transparentBody_badEnv_ne_sort r ls l
  unfold transparentBody
  rw [hres]
  dsimp
  rw [htr, hbody]
  dsimp
  change some (instantiateLevels ls b) = some (.sort l)
  rw [h]

/- The empty context stores no let value, so `zetaLocal` has no witness. -/
theorem lookup_nil_no_value (i : Nat) {v : Expr Nat}
    (h : lookupValue ([] : LCtx) i = some v) : False := by
  rw [lookupValue_nil] at h
  cases h

/- A literal expands to `succ^n zero`, never a sort. -/
theorem lit_expand_ne_sort (t : Nat) (exp : Expr Nat) (l : Level)
    (h : LiteralExpansion t exp) (hs : exp = .sort l) : False := by
  cases h
  exact natExpand_ne_sort t l hs

/- A conversion whose right end is a syntactic sort. The equality is a
   hypothesis, so `beta` and `zeta` stay in the match: their contractum
   is a sort only when `instantiate0_eq_sort` says so, and that `Or` is
   not eliminated here. Delta, literal expansion, and `zetaLocal` in the
   empty context are impossible. A rigid non-sort right head contradicts
   the equality. Not `¬ TyConvT`, and not AdeqConstDelta, AdeqApp, or
   AdeqLetE. -/
inductive ConvToSort (l : Level) : Expr Nat → Type where
  | refl : ConvToSort l (.sort l)
  | symm (a b T : Expr Nat) (h : ConvT badEnv 0 [] a b T) (ha : a = .sort l) :
      ConvToSort l b
  | trans (m c a T : Expr Nat) (h1 : ConvT badEnv 0 [] a m T)
      (h2 : ConvT badEnv 0 [] m c T) (hc : c = .sort l) : ConvToSort l a
  | sorts (l₁ : Level) (h : eqN l₁ l) : ConvToSort l (.sort l₁)
  | beta (A body arg : Expr Nat) (hr : instantiate0 arg body = .sort l) :
      ConvToSort l (.app (.lam A body) arg)
  | zeta (A value body : Expr Nat) (hr : instantiate0 value body = .sort l) :
      ConvToSort l (.letE A value body)
  | eta (f A B : Expr Nat) (h : HasTyT badEnv 0 [] f (.pi A B)) (hf : f = .sort l) :
      ConvToSort l (.lam A (.app (lift 0 1 f) (.bvar 0)))
  | irr (p q P : Expr Nat) (hP : HasTyT badEnv 0 [] P (.sort .zero))
      (hp : HasTyT badEnv 0 [] p P) (hq : HasTyT badEnv 0 [] q P)
      (hq_eq : q = .sort l) : ConvToSort l p

def convToSort {a b T : Expr Nat} {l : Level}
    (h : ConvT badEnv 0 [] a b T) (hs : b = .sort l) : ConvToSort l a :=
  match h with
  | .refl _ _ _ _ =>
      Eq.ndrec (motive := fun X => ConvToSort l X)
        (ConvToSort.refl (l := l)) (Eq.symm hs)
  | .symm _ x y _ hinner => ConvToSort.symm x y T hinner hs
  | .trans _ x m c _ h1 h2 =>
      let other := ConvToSort.trans m c x T h1 h2 hs
      match convToSort h2 hs with
      | .refl => convToSort h1 rfl
      | _ => other
  | .tyConv _ _ _ _ _ _ hsub _ => convToSort hsub hs
  | .beta _ A body arg _ _ _ _ _ => ConvToSort.beta A body arg hs
  | .zeta _ A value body _ _ _ _ _ => ConvToSort.zeta A value body hs
  | .zetaLocal _ i _ _ hval _ _ => False.elim (lookup_nil_no_value i hval)
  | .delta _ r ls m body hres hbody htr _ _ _ =>
      False.elim (badEnv_delta_rhs_ne_sort r ls m body l hres hbody htr hs)
  | .iota _ _ _ _ hdi _ _ => False.elim (derivedIota_badEnv_false hdi)
  | .lit _ t exp _ hexp _ => False.elim (lit_expand_ne_sort t exp l hexp hs)
  | .app _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ => nomatch hs
  | .lam _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ => nomatch hs
  | .pi _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ => nomatch hs
  | .letE _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ => nomatch hs
  | .sorts _ l₁ _ heq =>
      ConvToSort.sorts l₁ (eqN_trans heq (eqN_of_sort_eq hs))
  | .consts _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ => nomatch hs
  | .eta _ f A B h => ConvToSort.eta f A B h hs
  | .irr _ P p q hP hp hq => ConvToSort.irr p q P hP hp hq hs
termination_by sizeOf h

/- What the right end's inversion says about the left end.
   `refl` and `sorts` make that end a sort. `other` does not.
   Not `¬ TyConvT`. -/
inductive ConvRight (l₂ : Level) : Expr Nat → Type where
  | refl : ConvRight l₂ (.sort l₂)
  | sorts (l' : Level) (heq : eqN l' l₂) : ConvRight l₂ (.sort l')
  | other (mid : Expr Nat) : ConvRight l₂ mid

/- Read a top-level `symm` with `convLeft`. Beta, zeta, eta, and irr
   stay `other`: those left heads are an application, a let, a lambda,
   or an unexamined proof. Not `¬ TyConvT`. -/
def convRightOf {l₂ : Level} {m : Expr Nat}
    (v : ConvToSort l₂ m) : ConvRight l₂ m :=
  match v with
  | .refl => ConvRight.refl
  | .sorts l' heq => ConvRight.sorts l' heq
  | .symm _ b _ hinner hx =>
      match convLeft hinner hx with
      | .refl => ConvRight.refl
      | .sorts l' heq => ConvRight.sorts l' (eqN_symm heq)
      | .other _ => ConvRight.other b
  | .trans _ _ a _ _ _ _ => ConvRight.other a
  | .beta A body arg _ => ConvRight.other (.app (.lam A body) arg)
  | .zeta A value body _ => ConvRight.other (.letE A value body)
  | .eta f A _ _ _ => ConvRight.other (.lam A (.app (lift 0 1 f) (.bvar 0)))
  | .irr p _ _ _ _ _ _ => ConvRight.other p

def convRight {m b T : Expr Nat} {l₂ : Level}
    (h2 : ConvT badEnv 0 [] m b T) (hb : b = .sort l₂) : ConvRight l₂ m :=
  convRightOf (convToSort h2 hb)

/- Both ends are sorts by separate equalities. A `trans` whose left
   half is `refl` or `sorts` is consumed. If the left half is `other`,
   the right half is read by `convRight`: a sort middle recurses on
   the left piece. Beta, zeta, eta, and irr on the right stay
   `ConvSortStuck.trans`. Not `¬ TyConvT`, and not AdeqConstDelta,
   AdeqApp, or AdeqLetE. -/
def convBothSort {a b T : Expr Nat} {l₁ l₂ : Level}
    (h : ConvT badEnv 0 [] a b T) (ha : a = .sort l₁) (hb : b = .sort l₂) :
    PSum (eqN l₁ l₂) (ConvSortStuck l₁ l₂) :=
  match h with
  | .refl _ _ _ _ =>
      PSum.inl (eqN_of_sort_eq (Eq.trans (Eq.symm ha) hb))
  | .symm _ _ _ _ hinner =>
      match convBothSort hinner hb ha with
      | PSum.inl heq => PSum.inl (eqN_symm heq)
      | PSum.inr s => PSum.inr (ConvSortStuck.swap s)
  | .trans _ _ m _ _ h1 h2 =>
      match convLeft h1 ha with
      | .refl => convBothSort h2 rfl hb
      | .sorts l' heq =>
          match convBothSort h2 rfl hb with
          | PSum.inl heq2 => PSum.inl (eqN_trans heq heq2)
          | PSum.inr s => PSum.inr (ConvSortStuck.after l' heq s)
      | .other _ =>
          let stuck := PSum.inr (ConvSortStuck.trans m T h1 h2 ha hb)
          match convRight h2 hb with
          | .refl => convBothSort h1 ha rfl
          | .sorts l' heq =>
              match convBothSort h1 ha rfl with
              | PSum.inl heq1 => PSum.inl (eqN_trans heq1 heq)
              | PSum.inr s => PSum.inr (ConvSortStuck.before l' heq s)
          | .other _ => stuck
  | .tyConv _ _ _ _ _ _ hsub _ => convBothSort hsub ha hb
  | .beta _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ => nomatch ha
  | .zeta _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ => nomatch ha
  | .zetaLocal _ _ _ _ _ _ _ => nomatch ha
  | .delta _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ => nomatch ha
  | .iota _ _ _ _ hdi _ _ => False.elim (derivedIota_badEnv_false hdi)
  | .lit _ _ _ _ _ _ => nomatch ha
  | .app _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ => nomatch ha
  | .lam _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ => nomatch ha
  | .pi _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ => nomatch ha
  | .letE _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ => nomatch ha
  | .sorts _ _ _ heq =>
      PSum.inl (eqN_trans (eqN_symm (eqN_of_sort_eq ha))
        (eqN_trans heq (eqN_of_sort_eq hb)))
  | .consts _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ => nomatch ha
  | .eta _ _ _ _ _ => nomatch ha
  | .irr _ P _ _ hP hp hq =>
      PSum.inr (ConvSortStuck.irr P hP hp hq ha hb)
termination_by sizeOf h

/- The right half of a sort-to-sort `trans`, packaged as one `ConvT`.
   Not `¬ TyConvT`. -/
def convTransRight {l₁ l₂ : Level} {a b m T : Expr Nat}
    (h1 : ConvT badEnv 0 [] a m T) (h2 : ConvT badEnv 0 [] m b T)
    (ha : a = .sort l₁) (hb : b = .sort l₂) :
    PSum (eqN l₁ l₂) (ConvSortStuck l₁ l₂) :=
  convBothSort (ConvT.trans [] a m b T h1 h2) ha hb

/- `TyConvT` between two sorts. A reflexive left half is dropped. A
   `sorts` left half composes `eqN`. Anything else is `TySortStuck`.
   Not `¬ TyConvT badEnv 0 [] cN cTrue`. -/
def tyBothSort {l₁ l₂ : Level}
    (h : TyConvT badEnv 0 [] (.sort l₁) (.sort l₂)) :
    PSum (eqN l₁ l₂) (TySortStuck l₁ l₂) :=
  match h with
  | .refl _ _ => PSum.inl (eqN_refl l₁)
  | .of _ _ _ _ hc =>
      match convBothSort hc rfl rfl with
      | PSum.inl heq => PSum.inl heq
      | PSum.inr s => PSum.inr (TySortStuck.step s)
  | .trans _ _ _ _ h1 h2 =>
      match tyLeft h1 with
      | .refl => tyBothSort h2
      | .sorts l' heq =>
          match tyBothSort h2 with
          | PSum.inl heq2 => PSum.inl (eqN_trans heq heq2)
          | PSum.inr s => PSum.inr (TySortStuck.after l' heq s)
      | .other _ => PSum.inr (TySortStuck.trans h1 h2)
termination_by sizeOf h

/- `Sort 1` and `Sort 0` are not `eqN`. A derivation of that `TyConvT`
   is therefore a stuck `trans` or `irr`, not a level equality. Not
   `¬ TyConvT`, and not AdeqConstDelta, AdeqApp, or AdeqLetE. -/
def sortGap_stuck
    (h : TyConvT badEnv 0 [] (.sort (.succ .zero)) (.sort .zero)) :
    TySortStuck (.succ .zero) .zero :=
  match tyBothSort h with
  | PSum.inl heq => False.elim (eqN_succ_ne_zero .zero heq)
  | PSum.inr s => s

/- Proof irrelevance of two syntactic sorts. Their principal universes
   are `Sort (succ l₁)` and `Sort (succ l₂)`. Those are `eqN`, and then
   `succ` is injective, or the type conversion between them is stuck.
   Not `¬ TyConvT`. -/
inductive ConvIrrStuck : Level → Level → Type where
  | principal {l₁ l₂ : Level} (l₁' l₂' : Level)
      (heq1 : eqN l₁' (.succ l₁)) (heq2 : eqN l₂' (.succ l₂))
      (s : TySortStuck l₁' l₂') : ConvIrrStuck l₁ l₂

def convIrrPrincipal {l₁ l₂ : Level} {p q P : Expr Nat}
    (hp : HasTyT badEnv 0 [] p P) (hq : HasTyT badEnv 0 [] q P)
    (hp_eq : p = .sort l₁) (hq_eq : q = .sort l₂) :
    PSum (eqN l₁ l₂) (ConvIrrStuck l₁ l₂) :=
  match hasTyT_sort_principal hp hp_eq with
  | ⟨l₁', ⟨heq1, ht1⟩⟩ =>
      match hasTyT_sort_principal hq hq_eq with
      | ⟨l₂', ⟨heq2, ht2⟩⟩ =>
          match tyBothSort (tyConvT_of_to_same ht1 ht2) with
          | PSum.inl heq =>
              PSum.inl (eqN_succ_inj
                (eqN_trans (eqN_symm heq1) (eqN_trans heq heq2)))
          | PSum.inr s =>
              PSum.inr (ConvIrrStuck.principal l₁' l₂' heq1 heq2 s)

/- `Sort 1` and `Sort 0` are not `eqN`, so proof irrelevance of those
   two sorts is a stuck conversion of their principal universes.
   Not `¬ TyConvT`. -/
def convIrrSuccZero {p q P : Expr Nat}
    (hp : HasTyT badEnv 0 [] p P) (hq : HasTyT badEnv 0 [] q P)
    (hp_eq : p = .sort (.succ .zero)) (hq_eq : q = .sort .zero) :
    ConvIrrStuck (.succ .zero) .zero :=
  match convIrrPrincipal hp hq hp_eq hq_eq with
  | PSum.inl heq => False.elim (eqN_succ_ne_zero .zero heq)
  | PSum.inr s => s

theorem cBadData : DataTy badEnv (instantiateLevels [] cTrue) :=
  ⟨4, [], [], ⟨.inductiveM, 0, .sort .zero, none⟩, rfl, rfl, rfl⟩

theorem cBadNorm : norm badEnv 3 cBad = some cZero := rfl
theorem cBadVal : scmValOf badEnv 1 cZero = some (.inj 1 (.list [])) := rfl
theorem cBadRel : relevantSpine badEnv 0 1 cZero = true := rfl
theorem cBadRoot : irrelevant badEnv 0 [] cZero = false := by decide
theorem cBadFits : valFits 1 tyNat1 (.inj 1 (.list [])) = true := by decide
theorem cBad_irrelevant : irrelevant badEnv 0 [] cBad = true := by decide

/-- the reference lowering of `c` is the refusing term at every fuel and type. -/
theorem lowerF_cBad {S : SigTable} (F : Nat) (t : BootTy) :
    lowerF badEnv 0 F (S := S) t cBad = refuse := by
  cases F with
  | zero => rfl
  | succ F =>
    have hirr : irrelevant badEnv 0 [] (.const 15 []) = true := cBad_irrelevant
    have he : erase badEnv 0 (F + 1) [] cBad = some .box := by
      simp only [erase, cBad, eraseWith, hirr, if_true]
    unfold lowerF pipeline
    rw [he]
    cases t <;> rfl

/-- the counterexample: the reference family does not meet the session-7 statement. -/
theorem lowerF_not_adequate_untypedEnv {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) :
    ¬ adequacyStatementUntypedEnv (fun E n F t e => lowerF E n F (S := S) t e) progs := by
  intro h
  obtain ⟨F₀, hF⟩ := h badEnv 0 3 1 cBad _ cZero tyNat1 (.inj 1 (.list []))
    cBadTy cBadData cBadNorm cBadVal cBadRel cBadRoot cBadFits
  obtain ⟨lf, he⟩ := hF F₀ (Nat.le_refl _)
  have he' : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf []
      (lowerF badEnv 0 F₀ (S := S) tyNat1 cBad) = some (.inj 1 (.list [])) := he
  rw [lowerF_cBad] at he'
  exact eval_refuse_ne progs lf [] _ he'

-- the same witness as a gap guard: data on the value side, refused by the lowering, the
-- unfolded value relevant while the constant is a proof, and the body typed by the
-- certified checker at `N`, not at the declared `True`
#guard (obs badEnv cBad).isSome && (runLowered (Rsx.lower badEnv (t := tyNat1) cBad)).isNone &&
  irrelevant badEnv 0 [] cBad && !(irrelevant badEnv 0 [] cZero) &&
  decide (inferT badEnv 0 [] cZero = some cN) && decide (inferT badEnv 0 [] cZero ≠ some cTrue)
-- a well-typed body of the same shape (`c : N := zero`, member 11-like) is lowered: `g06`
#guard agrees (fun t e => Rsx.lower badEnv (t := t) e) badEnv tyNat3 g06

/-! ### Counterexamples to the session-8 statement: the relevance test is syntactic

`Rsx.irrelevant` reads the certified syntactic checker `inferT` (no conversion rule), and
`isPropSort` matches `Sort 0` as written. `lvlEnv` (members 0…5):
0 `I : Sort (max 0 0)` (an inductive in a sort equal to `Prop`, `eqN`), 1 `K : I`,
2 `IdP : Sort (max 0 0) → Sort 0 := fun A => A`, 3 `c : IdP I := K`, 4 `J : Type`,
5 `Mk : IdP I → J`. Every body is typed at its declared type (`lvlBodiesTyped`, through
`ConvT.sorts`, `.pi`, `.delta`, `.beta`).

1. `c` is typed at `I` only through conversion (`IdP I ≡ I`); `I` is an inductive, so `DataTy`
   holds; `norm` unfolds `c` to `K`. Erasure tests `c`: its declared type `IdP I` has
   syntactic type `Sort 0`, so `c ↦ □` and the lowering refuses. The value `K` has type `I`,
   whose syntactic type is `Sort (max 0 0)`, not `Sort 0` as written: relevant.
2. `Mk c` is syntactically typed at `J`. Erasure keeps `Mk` and erases the field `c`;
   `norm` gives `Mk K`, whose field `K` passes `relevantSpine`; evalLF of the lowering returns
   `.inj 5 (.list [])`, the value side `.inj 5 (.list [.inj 1 (.list [])])`.

The statement on main requires `inferT E n [] e = some T` and `(inferT E n [] v).isSome`;
witness 1 has `inferT c = IdP I` (not a data type) and witness 2 has `inferT (Mk K) = none`
(`IdP I` vs `I` as written): `convTyped_witness_excluded`, `convValue_witness_excluded`. -/

def lvl00 : Level := .max .zero .zero

theorem lvl00_eqN : eqN lvl00 .zero := fun _ => rfl

def wI : Expr Nat := .const 0 []
def wK : Expr Nat := .const 1 []
def wId : Expr Nat := .const 2 []
def wC : Expr Nat := .const 3 []
def wJ : Expr Nat := .const 4 []
def wMk : Expr Nat := .const 5 []
def wIdBody : Expr Nat := .lam (.sort lvl00) (.bvar 0)

def mI : CheckedMember := ⟨.inductiveM, 0, .sort lvl00, none⟩
def mK : CheckedMember := ⟨.constructorM, 0, wI, none⟩
def mId : CheckedMember := ⟨.definitionM, 0, .pi (.sort lvl00) (.sort .zero), some wIdBody⟩
def mC : CheckedMember := ⟨.definitionM, 0, .app wId wI, some wK⟩
def mJ : CheckedMember := ⟨.inductiveM, 0, .sort (.succ .zero), none⟩
def mMk : CheckedMember := ⟨.constructorM, 0, .pi (.app wId wI) wJ, none⟩

def lvlEnv : ResolvedEnv where
  members := fun r =>
    match r with
    | 0 => some mI
    | 1 => some mK
    | 2 => some mId
    | 3 => some mC
    | 4 => some mJ
    | 5 => some mMk
    | _ => none

def wSortTy (Γ : LCtx) : HasTyT lvlEnv 0 Γ (.sort lvl00) (.sort (.succ lvl00)) := .sort Γ lvl00

/-- `Sort (max 0 0) ≡ Sort 0` (`ConvT.sorts`, levels extensionally equal). -/
def wSortConv (Γ : LCtx) : ConvT lvlEnv 0 Γ (.sort lvl00) (.sort .zero) (.sort (.succ lvl00)) :=
  .sorts Γ lvl00 .zero lvl00_eqN

def wITy : HasTyT lvlEnv 0 [] wI (.sort lvl00) := .const [] 0 [] mI rfl rfl rfl
def wKTy : HasTyT lvlEnv 0 [] wK wI := .const [] 1 [] mK rfl rfl rfl

def wVar0 : HasTyT lvlEnv 0 [.assumption (.sort lvl00)] (.bvar 0) (.sort lvl00) :=
  .bvar [.assumption (.sort lvl00)] 0 (.sort lvl00) rfl

def wIdBodyTy0 : HasTyT lvlEnv 0 [] wIdBody (.pi (.sort lvl00) (.sort lvl00)) :=
  .lam [] (.sort lvl00) (.succ lvl00) (.bvar 0) (.sort lvl00) (wSortTy []) wVar0

def wPiConv : ConvT lvlEnv 0 [] (.pi (.sort lvl00) (.sort lvl00)) (.pi (.sort lvl00) (.sort .zero))
    (.sort (.imax (.succ lvl00) (.succ lvl00))) :=
  .pi [] (.sort lvl00) (.sort lvl00) (.sort lvl00) (.sort .zero) (.succ lvl00) (.succ lvl00)
    (.refl [] (.sort lvl00) _ (wSortTy [])) (wSortConv _)

def wIdBodyTy : HasTyT lvlEnv 0 [] wIdBody (.pi (.sort lvl00) (.sort .zero)) :=
  .conv [] wIdBody _ _ (.imax (.succ lvl00) (.succ lvl00)) wIdBodyTy0 wPiConv

def wIdDelta : ConvT lvlEnv 0 [] wId wIdBody (.pi (.sort lvl00) (.sort .zero)) :=
  .delta [] 2 [] mId wIdBody rfl rfl rfl rfl rfl wIdBodyTy

def wAppConv : ConvT lvlEnv 0 [] (.app wId wI) (.app wIdBody wI) (.sort .zero) :=
  .app [] wId wIdBody wI wI (.sort lvl00) (.sort .zero) wIdDelta (.refl [] wI _ wITy)

def wBeta : ConvT lvlEnv 0 [] (.app wIdBody wI) wI (.sort lvl00) :=
  .beta [] (.sort lvl00) (.bvar 0) wI (.sort lvl00) (.succ lvl00) (wSortTy []) wVar0 wITy

def wBeta0 : ConvT lvlEnv 0 [] (.app wIdBody wI) wI (.sort .zero) :=
  .tyConv [] _ _ (.sort lvl00) (.sort .zero) (.succ lvl00) wBeta (wSortConv [])

/-- `IdP I ≡ I : Sort 0`. -/
def wIdI : ConvT lvlEnv 0 [] (.app wId wI) wI (.sort .zero) :=
  .trans [] _ _ _ _ wAppConv wBeta0

def wCBodyTy : HasTyT lvlEnv 0 [] wK (.app wId wI) :=
  .conv [] wK wI (.app wId wI) .zero wKTy (.symm [] _ _ _ wIdI)

/-- witness 1's typing: `c : I`, through conversion only. -/
def wCTy : HasTyT lvlEnv 0 [] wC wI :=
  .conv [] wC (.app wId wI) wI .zero (.const [] 3 [] mC rfl rfl rfl) wIdI

/-- every transparent body of `lvlEnv` is typed at its declared type. -/
theorem lvlBodiesTyped : BodiesTyped lvlEnv 0 := by
  intro r m b ls hm ht hb hlen _
  match r, hm with
  | 0, hm => cases hm; exact absurd ht (by decide)
  | 1, hm => cases hm; exact absurd ht (by decide)
  | 2, hm =>
    cases hm; cases hb
    cases ls with
    | nil => exact ⟨wIdBodyTy⟩
    | cons _ _ => exact absurd hlen (Nat.succ_ne_zero _)
  | 3, hm =>
    cases hm; cases hb
    cases ls with
    | nil => exact ⟨wCBodyTy⟩
    | cons _ _ => exact absurd hlen (Nat.succ_ne_zero _)
  | 4, hm => cases hm; exact absurd ht (by decide)
  | 5, hm => cases hm; exact absurd ht (by decide)
  | _ + 6, hm => exact Option.noConfusion hm

theorem wIData : DataTy lvlEnv wI := ⟨0, [], [], mI, rfl, rfl, rfl⟩
theorem wCNorm : norm lvlEnv 3 wC = some wK := rfl
theorem wKVal : scmValOf lvlEnv 1 wK = some (.inj 1 (.list [])) := rfl
theorem wKRel : relevantSpine lvlEnv 0 1 wK = true := rfl
theorem wKRoot : irrelevant lvlEnv 0 [] wK = false := by decide
theorem wKFits : valFits 1 tyNat1 (.inj 1 (.list [])) = true := by decide
theorem wC_irrelevant : irrelevant lvlEnv 0 [] wC = true := by decide

theorem lowerF_wC {S : SigTable} (F : Nat) (t : BootTy) :
    lowerF lvlEnv 0 F (S := S) t wC = refuse := by
  cases F with
  | zero => rfl
  | succ F =>
    have hirr : irrelevant lvlEnv 0 [] (.const 3 []) = true := wC_irrelevant
    have he : erase lvlEnv 0 (F + 1) [] wC = some .box := by
      simp only [erase, wC, eraseWith, hirr, if_true]
    unfold lowerF pipeline
    rw [he]
    cases t <;> rfl

/-- witness 1: the reference family does not meet the session-8 statement. -/
theorem lowerF_not_adequate_convTyped {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) :
    ¬ adequacyStatementConvTyped (fun E n F t e => lowerF E n F (S := S) t e) progs := by
  intro h
  obtain ⟨F₀, hF⟩ := h lvlEnv 0 3 1 wC _ wK tyNat1 (.inj 1 (.list [])) lvlBodiesTyped
    wCTy wIData wCNorm wKVal wKRel wKRoot wKFits
  obtain ⟨lf, he⟩ := hF F₀ (Nat.le_refl _)
  have he' : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf []
      (lowerF lvlEnv 0 F₀ (S := S) tyNat1 wC) = some (.inj 1 (.list [])) := he
  rw [lowerF_wC] at he'
  exact eval_refuse_ne progs lf [] _ he'

/-- witness 1 is outside the statement on main: the checker types `c` at `IdP I`, which is
    not a data type (its head `IdP` is a definition). -/
theorem convTyped_witness_excluded (T : Expr Nat) (h : inferT lvlEnv 0 [] wC = some T) :
    ¬ DataTy lvlEnv T := by
  have h1 : inferT lvlEnv 0 [] wC = some (.app wId wI) := by decide
  rw [h1] at h
  cases h
  intro ⟨r, ls, args, m, hs, hm, hc⟩
  have hs0 : appsSpine (.app wId wI) = (.const 2 [], [wI]) := rfl
  rw [hs0] at hs
  injection hs with hh _
  injection hh with hr _
  subst hr
  cases hm
  exact absurd hc (by decide)

def wMkC : Expr Nat := .app wMk wC
def wMkK : Expr Nat := .app wMk wK
def tyW2 : BootTy := sumL 6 (sumL 2 .i64)
def wMkVal : Val := .inj 5 (.list [.inj 1 (.list [])])

theorem wMkCInfer : inferT lvlEnv 0 [] wMkC = some wJ := by decide
theorem wJData : DataTy lvlEnv wJ := ⟨4, [], [], mJ, rfl, rfl, rfl⟩
theorem wMkCNorm : norm lvlEnv 5 wMkC = some wMkK := rfl
theorem wMkKVal : scmValOf lvlEnv 2 wMkK = some wMkVal := rfl
theorem wMkKRel : relevantSpine lvlEnv 0 2 wMkK = true := by decide
theorem wMkKRoot : irrelevant lvlEnv 0 [] wMkK = false := by decide
theorem wMkKFits : valFits 2 tyW2 wMkVal = true := by decide
theorem wMkCErase (F : Nat) : erase lvlEnv 0 (F + 2) [] wMkC = some (.app (.ctor 5) .box) := by
  have h0 : irrelevant lvlEnv 0 [] (.app (.const 5 []) (.const 3 [])) = false := by decide
  have h1 : irrelevant lvlEnv 0 [] (.const 5 []) = false := by decide
  have h2 : irrelevant lvlEnv 0 [] (.const 3 []) = true := wC_irrelevant
  simp only [erase, wMkC, wMk, wC, eraseWith, h0, h1, h2, Bool.false_eq_true, if_false, if_true,
    noGlobals]
  rfl

/-- the lowering of `Mk c` from fuel 2 on: the constructor with its erased field dropped. -/
theorem lowerF_wMkC {S : SigTable} (F : Nat) :
    lowerF lvlEnv 0 (F + 2) (S := S) tyW2 wMkC = lowerF lvlEnv 0 2 (S := S) tyW2 wMkC := by
  unfold lowerF pipeline
  rw [wMkCErase F, wMkCErase 0]
  rfl

theorem eval_emit_ctor_box {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) (m F r : Nat) (ts : List BootTy)
    (τ : BootTy) (hg : ts.get? r = some (.list τ)) :
    Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs (m + 1) []
      (emit (S := S) (G := []) (F + 1) (.sum ts) (.ctor r [.box])) = some (.inj r (.list [])) := by
  obtain ⟨hlt, hget⟩ := list_get?_some ts r _ hg
  simp only [emit, emitWith]
  rw [dif_pos hlt]
  split
  · rename_i τ' hτ'
    simp only [Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval]
    rw [eval_cast_eq progs _ [] hτ'.symm]
    simp [Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval, relevantArgs, listOf]
  · rename_i hne
    exact absurd hget (hne τ)

theorem eval_lowerF_wMkC {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) (m : Nat) :
    Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs (m + 1) []
      (lowerF lvlEnv 0 2 (S := S) tyW2 wMkC) = some (.inj 5 (.list [])) := by
  have hlow : lowerF lvlEnv 0 2 (S := S) tyW2 wMkC = emit 2 tyW2 (.ctor 5 [.box]) := by
    unfold lowerF pipeline
    rw [wMkCErase 0]
    rfl
  rw [hlow]
  exact eval_emit_ctor_box progs m 1 5 (List.replicate 6 (.list (sumL 2 .i64))) (sumL 2 .i64) rfl

/-- witness 2: the reference family does not meet the session-8 statement (a wrong value,
    not a refusal). -/
theorem lowerF_not_adequate_convValue {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) :
    ¬ adequacyStatementConvTyped (fun E n F t e => lowerF E n F (S := S) t e) progs := by
  intro h
  obtain ⟨F₀, hF⟩ := h lvlEnv 0 5 2 wMkC _ wMkK tyW2 wMkVal lvlBodiesTyped
    (hasTyT_of_inferT wMkCInfer) wJData wMkCNorm wMkKVal wMkKRel wMkKRoot wMkKFits
  obtain ⟨lf, he⟩ := hF (F₀ + 2) (Nat.le_add_right _ _)
  have he' : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf []
      (lowerF lvlEnv 0 (F₀ + 2) (S := S) tyW2 wMkC) = some wMkVal := he
  rw [lowerF_wMkC] at he'
  cases lf with
  | zero => rw [eval_fuel0] at he'; exact Option.noConfusion he'
  | succ m =>
    rw [eval_lowerF_wMkC] at he'
    have h1 := Option.some.inj he'
    simp only [wMkVal] at h1
    injection h1 with _ h2
    injection h2 with h3
    exact List.noConfusion h3

/-- witness 2 is outside the statement on main: the checker cannot type the value `Mk K`
    (`Mk`'s domain is `IdP I` as written, `K`'s type is `I`). -/
theorem convValue_witness_excluded : (inferT lvlEnv 0 [] wMkK).isSome = false := by decide

-- the same witnesses as guards: data on the value side, the lowering refuses (1) or returns
-- another value (2), and the statement's checker premises fail on each
#guard (obs lvlEnv wC).isSome && (runLowered (Rsx.lower lvlEnv (t := tyNat1) wC)).isNone &&
  irrelevant lvlEnv 0 [] wC && !(irrelevant lvlEnv 0 [] wK) &&
  decide (inferT lvlEnv 0 [] wC = some (.app wId wI))
#guard (obs lvlEnv wMkC).isSome && !(agrees (fun t e => Rsx.lower lvlEnv (t := t) e) lvlEnv tyW2 wMkC)
  && (inferT lvlEnv 0 [] wMkC).isSome && !(inferT lvlEnv 0 [] wMkK).isSome

/-! ### Counterexample to `Rsx.adequacyStatement`: a discarded relevant loop

`whnfFuel` reduces `app (λ_. lit 0) loop` without entering `loop`; `erase` unfolds the
transparent `loop := loop` at every fuel and returns `none`. The value side is `.int 0`.
Cited shape: call-by-name head reduction versus structural erasure (Letouzey, TYPES 2002,
traverses every subterm; Lean's compiled code evaluates a relevant argument). -/

def loopEnv : ResolvedEnv where
  members := fun r =>
    match r with
    | 0 => some ⟨.inductiveM, 0, .sort (.succ .zero), none⟩
    | 1 => some ⟨.constructorM, 0, .const 0 [], none⟩
    | 3 => some ⟨.definitionM, 0, .const 0 [], some (.const 3 [])⟩
    | _ => none

def loopC : Expr Nat := .const 3 []
def bomb : Expr Nat := .app (.lam (.const 0 []) (.lit 0)) loopC

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000 in
theorem loop_irr : irrelevant loopEnv 0 [] loopC = false := by decide

theorem loop_body : transparentBody loopEnv 3 [] = some loopC := rfl

/-- `loop := loop` has no finite erasure: each fuel unfolds it once. -/
theorem erase_loop_none : ∀ F, erase loopEnv 0 F [] loopC = none
  | 0 => rfl
  | F + 1 => by
      simp only [erase, eraseWith, loopC, loop_irr, Bool.false_eq_true, if_false,
        noGlobals, loop_body]
      exact erase_loop_none F

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000 in
theorem bomb_irr : irrelevant loopEnv 0 [] bomb = false := by decide

theorem erase_bomb_none : ∀ F, erase loopEnv 0 F [] bomb = none
  | 0 => rfl
  | F + 1 => by
      have hirr :
          irrelevant loopEnv 0 [] (.app (.lam (.const 0 []) (.lit 0)) loopC) = false := by
        simpa [bomb] using bomb_irr
      have hloop :
          eraseWith (irrelevant loopEnv 0) noGlobals loopEnv F [] loopC = none := by
        simpa [erase] using erase_loop_none F
      simp only [erase, eraseWith, bomb, hirr, Bool.false_eq_true, if_false]
      rw [hloop]
      -- the app match does not reduce while its first scrutinee is a free
      -- `eraseWith` (Lean's joint matcher). `none` on the argument kills both arms.
      cases eraseWith (irrelevant loopEnv 0) noGlobals loopEnv F []
          (.lam (.const 0 []) (.lit 0)) <;> rfl

theorem lowerF_bomb {S : SigTable} (F : Nat) (t : BootTy) :
    lowerF loopEnv 0 F (S := S) t bomb = refuse := by
  unfold lowerF pipeline
  rw [erase_bomb_none F]

theorem bomb_norm : norm loopEnv 3 bomb = some (.lit 0) := rfl
theorem bomb_val : scmValOf loopEnv 1 (.lit 0) = some (.int 0) := rfl
theorem bomb_rel : relevantSpine loopEnv 0 1 (.lit 0) = true := rfl
set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000 in
theorem bomb_root : irrelevant loopEnv 0 [] (.lit 0) = false := by decide
set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000 in
theorem bomb_fits : valFits 1 .i64 (.int 0) = true := by decide
set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000 in
theorem bomb_infer : inferT loopEnv 0 [] bomb = some (.const 0 []) := by decide
set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000 in
theorem bomb_vinfer : (inferT loopEnv 0 [] (.lit 0)).isSome = true := by decide
theorem bomb_data : DataTy loopEnv (.const 0 []) :=
  ⟨0, [], [], ⟨.inductiveM, 0, .sort (.succ .zero), none⟩, rfl, rfl, rfl⟩

theorem loopBodiesTyped : BodiesTyped loopEnv 0 := by
  intro r m b ls hm _ hb hlen hwf
  match r, hm with
  | 0, hm => cases hm; cases hb
  | 1, hm => cases hm; cases hb
  | 2, hm => exact Option.noConfusion hm
  | 3, hm =>
      cases hm
      cases hb
      cases ls with
      | nil =>
          exact ⟨.const [] 3 [] ⟨.definitionM, 0, .const 0 [], some (.const 3 [])⟩ rfl rfl hwf⟩
      | cons _ _ => exact Nat.noConfusion hlen
  | n + 4, hm => exact Option.noConfusion hm

/- β of `λ_. c ·`, `c` a rigid constructor, applied to one literal.
   The body mentions only the bound index, so `instantiate0` is that
   application. Letouzey TYPES 2002 keeps a relevant λ; Reynolds 1972 §8
   runs its body in the one-element environment. Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem defunc_lam_ctor_bvar (c : Nat) (la : LExpr) :
    defunc (.app (.lam (.app (.ctor c) (.bvar 0))) la) =
      (let q := convWith capRen id [{ ncap := 0, body := .apply (.ctor c) (.var 0) }] la
       (.apply (.clo 0 []) q.1, q.2)) := rfl

theorem run_lit_any (code : List Code) (F k : Nat) (env : List DVal) :
    run code (F + 1) env (.lit k) = some (.lit k) := by
  unfold run
  rfl

theorem run_ctor_any (code : List Code) (F r : Nat) (env : List DVal) :
    run code (F + 1) env (.ctor r) = some (.ctor r []) := by
  unfold run
  rfl

theorem run_beta_ctor_body (code : List Code) (F c nlit : Nat) :
    run code (F + 2) [.lit nlit] (.apply (.ctor c) (.var 0)) =
      some (.ctor c [.lit nlit]) := by
  rw [run_apply_eq code (F + 1) [.lit nlit] (.ctor c) (.var 0)]
  rw [run_ctor_any code F c [.lit nlit], run_var0 code F [] (.lit nlit)]
  rfl

theorem run_beta_ctor_lit (F c nlit : Nat) :
    run [{ ncap := 0, body := .apply (.ctor c) (.var 0) }] (F + 3) []
      (.apply (.clo 0 []) (.lit nlit)) = some (.ctor c [.lit nlit]) := by
  refine run_apply_clo_nil
      [{ ncap := 0, body := .apply (.ctor c) (.var 0) }]
      (F + 1) 0 [] (.lit nlit) (.apply (.ctor c) (.var 0))
      (.lit nlit) (.ctor c [.lit nlit]) rfl ?_ ?_
  · exact run_lit_any _ (F + 1) nlit []
  · exact run_beta_ctor_body _ F c nlit

theorem norm_beta_ctor_lit (E : ResolvedEnv) (k c nlit : Nat) (lsc : List Level)
    (A : Expr Nat) (hnone : transparentBody E c lsc = none) :
    norm E (k + 3) (.app (.lam A (.app (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0))) (.lit nlit)) =
      some (.app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit)) := by
  have hsub : (instantiate0 (.lit nlit) (.app (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0)) : Expr Nat) =
      .app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit) := rfl
  have hbeta : whnfFuel E (k + 2)
      (.app (.lam A (.app (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0))) (.lit nlit)) =
      whnfFuel E (k + 1) (instantiate0 (.lit nlit) (.app (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0))) := by
    simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine, foldApps, List.nil_append]
  have hstuck : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit)) =
      some (.app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit)) := by
    simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine, List.nil_append, hnone]
  have hlit : norm E (k + 2) (.lit nlit) = some (.lit nlit) := by
    have hwlit : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.lit nlit) = some (.lit nlit) := by
      simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine]
    unfold norm
    rw [hwlit]
  unfold norm
  rw [hbeta, hsub, hstuck]
  have hsp : appsSpine (.app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit)) =
      (.const c lsc, [.lit nlit]) := by
    simp only [appsSpine, List.nil_append]
  simp only [hsp]
  have hm : [.lit nlit].mapM (norm E (k + 2)) = some [.lit nlit] := by
    rw [List.mapM_cons, hlit, List.mapM_nil]
    rfl
  simp only [hm, foldApps]

theorem norm_beta_ctor_lit_val (E : ResolvedEnv) (lf c nlit : Nat) (lsc : List Level)
    (A : Expr Nat) {v : Expr Nat}
    (hnone : transparentBody E c lsc = none)
    (hn : norm E lf (.app (.lam A (.app (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0))) (.lit nlit)) = some v) :
    v = .app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit) := by
  cases lf with
  | zero => exact Option.noConfusion hn
  | succ lf =>
    cases lf with
    | zero =>
      unfold norm at hn
      rw [whnfFuel_fuel0] at hn
      exact Option.noConfusion hn
    | succ lf =>
      cases lf with
      | zero =>
        have hbeta : whnfFuel E 1
            (.app (.lam A (.app (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0))) (.lit nlit)) =
            whnfFuel E 0 (instantiate0 (.lit nlit) (.app (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0))) := by
          simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine, foldApps, List.nil_append]
        unfold norm at hn
        rw [hbeta, whnfFuel_fuel0] at hn
        exact Option.noConfusion hn
      | succ j =>
        rw [norm_beta_ctor_lit E j c nlit lsc A hnone] at hn
        exact (Option.some.inj hn).symm

theorem good_beta_ctor_lit {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n c nlit : Nat) (lsc : List Level) (A : Expr Nat)
    (hnone : transparentBody E c lsc = none)
    (hirr : irrelevant E n []
      (.app (.lam A (.app (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0))) (.lit nlit)) = false)
    (hirrL : irrelevant E n [] (.lam A (.app (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0))) = false)
    (hirrA : irrelevant E n (.assumption A :: [])
      (.app (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0)) = false)
    (hirrC : irrelevant E n (.assumption A :: []) (.const c lsc) = false)
    (hirrB : irrelevant E n (.assumption A :: []) (.bvar 0) = false) :
    Good progs E n (.app (.lam A (.app (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0))) (.lit nlit)) := by
  refine good_of_exists progs E n
      (.app (.lam A (.app (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0))) (.lit nlit)) ?_
  intro lf fv T v t w _ _ _ hn hs _ _ hf _ _
  have hv := norm_beta_ctor_lit_val E lf c nlit lsc A hnone hn
  subst hv
  cases fv with
  | zero => exact Option.noConfusion hs
  | succ m =>
    cases m with
    | zero =>
      have hs0 : scmValOf E 1 (.app (.const c lsc) (.lit nlit)) = none := by
        simp only [scmValOf, appsSpine, List.nil_append, List.mapM_cons, List.mapM_nil,
          Option.bind, Option.pure_def]
        split
        · rename_i mm hm
          by_cases hc : mm.mclass = .constructorM
          · simp [hm, hc, scmValOf]
          · simp [hm, hc]
        · rename_i hm
          simp [hm]
      rw [hs0] at hs
      exact Option.noConfusion hs
    | succ q =>
      have hlitv : scmValOf E (q + 1) (.lit nlit) = some (.int (Int.ofNat nlit)) := rfl
      have hs' : (match E.members c with
          | some mm =>
              if mm.mclass = .constructorM then
                some (.inj c (.list [.int (Int.ofNat nlit)]))
              else none
          | none => none) = some w := by
        simpa [scmValOf, appsSpine, List.nil_append, List.mapM_cons, List.mapM_nil,
          hlitv, Option.bind, Option.pure_def] using hs
      cases hm : E.members c with
      | none =>
        rw [hm] at hs'
        exact Option.noConfusion hs'
      | some mm =>
        rw [hm] at hs'
        by_cases hcm : mm.mclass = .constructorM
        · simp [hcm] at hs'
          subst hs'
          cases t with
          | sum ts =>
            have hf' : (match ts.get? c with
                | some (.list τ) =>
                    ([.int (Int.ofNat nlit)] : List Val).all (valFits (q + 1) τ)
                | _ => false) = true := hf
            split at hf'
            · rename_i τ hg
              cases τ with
              | i64 =>
                have hk : inI64Range (Int.ofNat nlit) = true := by
                  simp only [valFits, List.all_cons, List.all_nil, Bool.and_true] at hf'
                  exact hf'
                have hctor : isCtor E c = true := by simp [isCtor, hm, hcm]
                have hB : erase E n 1 (.assumption A :: []) (.bvar 0) = some (.bvar 0) := by
                  simp only [erase, eraseWith, hirrB, Bool.false_eq_true, if_false]
                have hC : erase E n 1 (.assumption A :: []) (.const c lsc) =
                    some (.ctor c) := by
                  simp only [erase, eraseWith, hirrC, Bool.false_eq_true, if_false,
                    noGlobals, hnone, hctor, if_true]
                have hBody : erase E n 2 (.assumption A :: [])
                    (.app (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0)) =
                    some (.app (.ctor c) (.bvar 0)) := by
                  rw [erase_app_keep E n 1 (.assumption A :: [])
                    (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0) hirrA]
                  simp only [hC, hB]
                have hLam : erase E n 3 [] (.lam A (.app (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0))) =
                    some (.lam (.app (.ctor c) (.bvar 0))) := by
                  rw [erase_lam_keep E n 2 [] A (.app (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0)) hirrL]
                  simp only [hBody, Option.map]
                have hLit : erase E n 3 [] (.lit nlit) = some (.lit nlit) := rfl
                have he : erase E n 4 []
                    (.app (.lam A (.app (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0))) (.lit nlit)) =
                    some (.app (.lam (.app (.ctor c) (.bvar 0))) (.lit nlit)) := by
                  rw [erase_app_keep E n 3 []
                    (.lam A (.app (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0))) (.lit nlit) hirr]
                  simp only [hLam, hLit]
                have hlow : lowerF E n 4 (S := S) (.sum ts)
                    (.app (.lam A (.app (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0))) (.lit nlit)) =
                    emit 4 (.sum ts) (.ctor c [.lit nlit]) := by
                  unfold lowerF pipeline
                  rw [he]
                  rfl
                have hE2 := eval_emit_ctor_lit progs nlit c ts hg hk
                have hbody : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs 1 []
                    (lowerF E n 4 (S := S) (.sum ts)
                      (.app (.lam A (.app (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0))) (.lit nlit))) =
                    some (.inj c (.list [.int (Int.ofNat nlit)])) := by
                  rw [hlow]
                  exact emitWith_evalStable relevantArgs progs 1 [] 2 4 (.sum ts)
                    (.ctor c [.lit nlit])
                    (.inj c (.list [.int (Int.ofNat nlit)]))
                    (Nat.le_add_right 2 2) hE2
                exact ⟨4, 1, hbody⟩
              | bool | str | bytes | list _ | pair _ _ | sum _ | record _ | option _ | residue _ =>
                simp only [valFits, List.all_cons, List.all_nil] at hf'
                exact Bool.noConfusion hf'
            · exact Bool.noConfusion hf'
          | _ => cases hf
        · simp [hcm] at hs'

theorem lowerF_not_adequate_divArg {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) :
    ¬ adequacyStatement (fun E n F t e => lowerF E n F (S := S) t e) progs := by
  intro h
  obtain ⟨F₀, hF⟩ := h loopEnv 0 3 1 bomb (.const 0 []) (.lit 0) .i64 (.int 0)
    loopBodiesTyped bomb_infer bomb_data bomb_norm bomb_val bomb_rel bomb_root bomb_fits bomb_vinfer
  obtain ⟨lf, he⟩ := hF F₀ (Nat.le_refl _)
  have he' : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf []
      (lowerF loopEnv 0 F₀ (S := S) .i64 bomb) = some (.int 0) := he
  rw [lowerF_bomb] at he'
  exact eval_refuse_ne progs lf [] _ he'

-- fuel 4, not `defaultFuel`: `Rsx.lower` is fuel 10000, and each step of `loop`
-- re-enters `inferT`. `lowerF_bomb` already covers every fuel, including that one.
#guard optValEq (obs loopEnv bomb) (some (.int 0)) &&
  (runLowered (lowerF loopEnv 0 4 (t := .i64) bomb)).isNone

/- `convWith` only appends code. The entries already in the table stay a
   prefix, so a label assigned before the argument is converted still
   points at the same body. Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem convWith_suffix (cr : List Nat → Nat → Nat) (ρ : Nat → Nat)
    (code : List Code) (l : LExpr) :
    ∃ ext, (convWith cr ρ code l).2 = code ++ ext := by
  induction l generalizing code ρ with
  | bvar i => exact ⟨[], by simp [convWith, List.append_nil]⟩
  | box => exact ⟨[], by simp [convWith, List.append_nil]⟩
  | lit k => exact ⟨[], by simp [convWith, List.append_nil]⟩
  | ctor r => exact ⟨[], by simp [convWith, List.append_nil]⟩
  | rigid r => exact ⟨[], by simp [convWith, List.append_nil]⟩
  | glob i => exact ⟨[], by simp [convWith, List.append_nil]⟩
  | app f a ihf iha =>
      obtain ⟨ef, hf⟩ := ihf ρ code
      obtain ⟨ea, ha⟩ := iha ρ (convWith cr ρ code f).2
      refine ⟨ef ++ ea, ?_⟩
      simp only [convWith]
      rw [ha, hf, List.append_assoc]
  | lam b ih =>
      let fs := freeVars 1 b
      obtain ⟨eb, hb⟩ := ih (cr fs) code
      let inner := convWith cr (cr fs) code b
      let entry : Code := { ncap := fs.length, body := inner.1 }
      refine ⟨eb ++ [entry], ?_⟩
      simp only [convWith]
      rw [hb, List.append_assoc]
  | letE v b ihv ihb =>
      obtain ⟨ev, hv⟩ := ihv ρ code
      obtain ⟨eb, hb⟩ := ihb (liftRen ρ) (convWith cr ρ code v).2
      refine ⟨ev ++ eb, ?_⟩
      simp only [convWith]
      rw [hb, hv, List.append_assoc]

/- A λ whose body has no free index above the binder converts to a
   closure with an empty capture list. `run` of that closure does not
   enter the body. Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem convWith_closed_lam (code : List Code) (ρ : Nat → Nat) (b : LExpr)
    (h : freeVars 1 b = []) :
    (convWith capRen ρ code (.lam b)).1 =
      .clo (convWith capRen (capRen []) code b).2.length [] := by
  simp only [convWith, h, List.map_nil]

/- Defunctionalization of `app (λ _. k) arg`. The literal body is code
   entry 0; the argument is converted against that one-entry table.
   Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem defunc_app_lam_lit (k : Nat) (la : LExpr) :
    defunc (.app (.lam (.lit k)) la) =
      (let q := convWith capRen id [{ ncap := 0, body := .lit k }] la
       (.apply (.clo 0 []) q.1, q.2)) := by
  rfl

/- `run` of that β when the argument is a λ of a literal. The argument
   closure is built and discarded; the result is the literal.
   Fuel 3 is the pipeline fuel of the erasure below. Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem run_beta_lam_lit (k j : Nat) :
    run (defunc (.app (.lam (.lit k)) (.lam (.lit j)))).2 3 []
      (defunc (.app (.lam (.lit k)) (.lam (.lit j)))).1
      = some (.lit k) := by
  rfl

/- The same discard under ζ. Not AdeqLetE. -/
theorem run_let_lam_lit (k j : Nat) :
    run (defunc (.letE (.lam (.lit j)) (.lit k))).2 3 []
      (defunc (.letE (.lam (.lit j)) (.lit k))).1
      = some (.lit k) := by
  rfl

/- Erasure of a β whose argument is a relevant λ of a literal.
   Both λs stay, because the application, the function, and the
   argument are relevant. Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem erase_beta_discard_lam_lit (E : ResolvedEnv) (n kbody j : Nat)
    (A B : Expr Nat)
    (hirr : irrelevant E n [] (.app (.lam A (.lit kbody)) (.lam B (.lit j))) = false)
    (hirrL : irrelevant E n [] (.lam A (.lit kbody)) = false)
    (hirrA : irrelevant E n [] (.lam B (.lit j)) = false) :
    erase E n 3 [] (.app (.lam A (.lit kbody)) (.lam B (.lit j))) =
      some (.app (.lam (.lit kbody)) (.lam (.lit j))) := by
  have hbody : erase E n 1 (.assumption A :: []) (.lit kbody) = some (.lit kbody) := rfl
  have hlam : erase E n 2 [] (.lam A (.lit kbody)) = some (.lam (.lit kbody)) := by
    rw [erase_lam_keep E n 1 [] A (.lit kbody) hirrL, hbody]
    rfl
  have hAb : erase E n 1 (.assumption B :: []) (.lit j) = some (.lit j) := rfl
  have harg : erase E n 2 [] (.lam B (.lit j)) = some (.lam (.lit j)) := by
    rw [erase_lam_keep E n 1 [] B (.lit j) hirrA, hAb]
    rfl
  rw [erase_app_keep E n 2 [] (.lam A (.lit kbody)) (.lam B (.lit j)) hirr, hlam, harg]

/- `Good` of that β. `run` evaluates the argument λ to a closure and
   discards it. Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem good_beta_discard_lam_lit {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n kbody j : Nat) (A B : Expr Nat)
    (hirr : irrelevant E n [] (.app (.lam A (.lit kbody)) (.lam B (.lit j))) = false)
    (hirrL : irrelevant E n [] (.lam A (.lit kbody)) = false)
    (hirrA : irrelevant E n [] (.lam B (.lit j)) = false) :
    Good progs E n (.app (.lam A (.lit kbody)) (.lam B (.lit j))) := by
  refine good_of_exists progs E n (.app (.lam A (.lit kbody)) (.lam B (.lit j))) ?_
  intro lf fv T v t w _ _ _ hn hs _ _ hf _ _
  have hv := norm_beta_discard_any_val E lf A (.lam B (.lit j)) kbody hn
  subst hv
  cases fv with
  | zero => exact Option.noConfusion hs
  | succ m =>
    have hs2 : scmValOf E (m + 1) (.lit kbody) = some (.int (Int.ofNat kbody)) := rfl
    rw [hs2] at hs
    cases hs
    cases t
    case i64 =>
      have hk : inI64Range (Int.ofNat kbody) = true := hf
      have he := erase_beta_discard_lam_lit E n kbody j A B hirr hirrL hirrA
      have hlow : lowerF E n 3 (S := S) .i64
          (.app (.lam A (.lit kbody)) (.lam B (.lit j))) =
          emit 3 .i64 (.lit kbody) := by
        unfold lowerF pipeline
        rw [he]
        rfl
      have hbody : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs 1 []
          (lowerF E n 3 (S := S) .i64
            (.app (.lam A (.lit kbody)) (.lam B (.lit j)))) =
          some (.int (Int.ofNat kbody)) := by
        rw [hlow]
        simp only [emit, emitWith]
        rw [if_pos hk]
        exact eval_litI progs (Int.ofNat kbody) hk
      exact ⟨3, 1, hbody⟩
    all_goals cases hf

/- Erasure of a ζ whose bound term is a relevant λ of a literal.
   Not AdeqLetE. -/
theorem erase_let_discard_lam_lit (E : ResolvedEnv) (n kbody j : Nat)
    (A B : Expr Nat)
    (hirr : irrelevant E n [] (.letE A (.lam B (.lit j)) (.lit kbody)) = false)
    (hirrA : irrelevant E n [] (.lam B (.lit j)) = false) :
    erase E n 3 [] (.letE A (.lam B (.lit j)) (.lit kbody)) =
      some (.letE (.lam (.lit j)) (.lit kbody)) := by
  have hAb : erase E n 1 (.assumption B :: []) (.lit j) = some (.lit j) := rfl
  have hbound : erase E n 2 [] (.lam B (.lit j)) = some (.lam (.lit j)) := by
    rw [erase_lam_keep E n 1 [] B (.lit j) hirrA, hAb]
    rfl
  have hbody : erase E n 2 (.letBinding A (.lam B (.lit j)) :: []) (.lit kbody) =
      some (.lit kbody) := rfl
  rw [erase_let_keep E n 2 [] A (.lam B (.lit j)) (.lit kbody) hirr, hbound, hbody]

/- `Good` of that ζ. Not AdeqLetE. -/
theorem good_let_discard_lam_lit {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n kbody j : Nat) (A B : Expr Nat)
    (hirr : irrelevant E n [] (.letE A (.lam B (.lit j)) (.lit kbody)) = false)
    (hirrA : irrelevant E n [] (.lam B (.lit j)) = false) :
    Good progs E n (.letE A (.lam B (.lit j)) (.lit kbody)) := by
  refine good_of_exists progs E n (.letE A (.lam B (.lit j)) (.lit kbody)) ?_
  intro lf fv T v t w _ _ _ hn hs _ _ hf _ _
  have hv := norm_let_discard_any_val E lf A (.lam B (.lit j)) kbody hn
  subst hv
  cases fv with
  | zero => exact Option.noConfusion hs
  | succ m =>
    have hs2 : scmValOf E (m + 1) (.lit kbody) = some (.int (Int.ofNat kbody)) := rfl
    rw [hs2] at hs
    cases hs
    cases t
    case i64 =>
      have hk : inI64Range (Int.ofNat kbody) = true := hf
      have he := erase_let_discard_lam_lit E n kbody j A B hirr hirrA
      have hlow : lowerF E n 3 (S := S) .i64
          (.letE A (.lam B (.lit j)) (.lit kbody)) =
          emit 3 .i64 (.lit kbody) := by
        unfold lowerF pipeline
        rw [he]
        rfl
      have hbody : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs 1 []
          (lowerF E n 3 (S := S) .i64
            (.letE A (.lam B (.lit j)) (.lit kbody))) =
          some (.int (Int.ofNat kbody)) := by
        rw [hlow]
        simp only [emit, emitWith]
        rw [if_pos hk]
        exact eval_litI progs (Int.ofNat kbody) hk
      exact ⟨3, 1, hbody⟩
    all_goals cases hf

/- `run` of a β whose argument erasure is any closed λ.
   The argument closure is built in one step and discarded.
   The literal body is code entry 0, and `convWith_suffix` keeps it
   there. Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem run_beta_closed_lam (k : Nat) (lb : LExpr) (h : freeVars 1 lb = []) :
    run (defunc (.app (.lam (.lit k)) (.lam lb))).2 2 []
      (defunc (.app (.lam (.lit k)) (.lam lb))).1 = some (.lit k) := by
  rw [defunc_app_lam_lit]
  let code0 : List Code := [{ ncap := 0, body := .lit k }]
  let q := convWith capRen id code0 (.lam lb)
  have h1 : q.1 = .clo (convWith capRen (capRen []) code0 lb).2.length [] := by
    simpa [q, code0] using convWith_closed_lam code0 id lb h
  obtain ⟨ext, hext⟩ := convWith_suffix capRen id code0 (.lam lb)
  have hc : q.2.get? 0 = some (⟨0, .lit k⟩ : Code) := by
    have hq : q.2 = code0 ++ ext := by simpa [q, code0] using hext
    unfold code0 at hq
    rw [hq]
    rfl
  have ha : run q.2 1 [] q.1 =
      some (.clo (convWith capRen (capRen []) code0 lb).2.length []) := by
    rw [h1]
    exact run_clo_nil q.2 0 _ []
  simpa [code0, q] using
    run_apply_lit_body q.2 0 0 k [] q.1
      (.clo (convWith capRen (capRen []) code0 lb).2.length []) hc ha

/- Defunctionalization of a let whose body is a literal. The bound term
   is converted first; the literal allocates no code. Not AdeqLetE. -/
theorem defunc_let_lit (k : Nat) (lv : LExpr) :
    defunc (.letE lv (.lit k)) =
      (let p := convWith capRen id [] lv
       (.letE p.1 (.lit k), p.2)) := by
  rfl

/- `run` of a ζ whose bound erasure is any closed λ. Not AdeqLetE. -/
theorem run_let_closed_lam (k : Nat) (lb : LExpr) (h : freeVars 1 lb = []) :
    run (defunc (.letE (.lam lb) (.lit k))).2 2 []
      (defunc (.letE (.lam lb) (.lit k))).1 = some (.lit k) := by
  rw [defunc_let_lit]
  let p := convWith capRen id [] (.lam lb)
  have h1 : p.1 = .clo (convWith capRen (capRen []) [] lb).2.length [] := by
    simpa [p] using convWith_closed_lam [] id lb h
  rw [run_let_eq, h1, run_clo_nil]
  unfold run
  rfl

/- Erasure of a β whose argument erases to a λ. The function λ of a
   literal stays. Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem erase_beta_discard_closed_lam (E : ResolvedEnv) (n kbody : Nat)
    (A arg : Expr Nat) (lb : LExpr)
    (hirr : irrelevant E n [] (.app (.lam A (.lit kbody)) arg) = false)
    (hirrL : irrelevant E n [] (.lam A (.lit kbody)) = false)
    (harg : erase E n 2 [] arg = some (.lam lb)) :
    erase E n 3 [] (.app (.lam A (.lit kbody)) arg) =
      some (.app (.lam (.lit kbody)) (.lam lb)) := by
  have hbody : erase E n 1 (.assumption A :: []) (.lit kbody) = some (.lit kbody) := rfl
  have hlam : erase E n 2 [] (.lam A (.lit kbody)) = some (.lam (.lit kbody)) := by
    rw [erase_lam_keep E n 1 [] A (.lit kbody) hirrL, hbody]
    rfl
  rw [erase_app_keep E n 2 [] (.lam A (.lit kbody)) arg hirr, hlam, harg]

/- `Good` of that β, when the erased argument λ captures nothing.
   `run` at fuel 2 returns the literal; `run_mono` lifts it to the
   pipeline fuel 3. Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem good_beta_discard_closed_lam {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n kbody : Nat) (A arg : Expr Nat) (lb : LExpr)
    (hirr : irrelevant E n [] (.app (.lam A (.lit kbody)) arg) = false)
    (hirrL : irrelevant E n [] (.lam A (.lit kbody)) = false)
    (harg : erase E n 2 [] arg = some (.lam lb))
    (hclosed : freeVars 1 lb = []) :
    Good progs E n (.app (.lam A (.lit kbody)) arg) := by
  refine good_of_exists progs E n (.app (.lam A (.lit kbody)) arg) ?_
  intro lf fv T v t w _ _ _ hn hs _ _ hf _ _
  have hv := norm_beta_discard_any_val E lf A arg kbody hn
  subst hv
  cases fv with
  | zero => exact Option.noConfusion hs
  | succ m =>
    have hs2 : scmValOf E (m + 1) (.lit kbody) = some (.int (Int.ofNat kbody)) := rfl
    rw [hs2] at hs
    cases hs
    cases t
    case i64 =>
      have hk : inI64Range (Int.ofNat kbody) = true := hf
      have he := erase_beta_discard_closed_lam E n kbody A arg lb hirr hirrL harg
      have hr2 := run_beta_closed_lam kbody lb hclosed
      have hr3 := run_mono
        (defunc (.app (.lam (.lit kbody)) (.lam lb))).2 2 3 []
        (defunc (.app (.lam (.lit kbody)) (.lam lb))).1
        (.lit kbody) (Nat.le_succ 2) hr2
      have hlow : lowerF E n 3 (S := S) .i64
          (.app (.lam A (.lit kbody)) arg) =
          emit 3 .i64 (.lit kbody) := by
        unfold lowerF pipeline
        simp only [he, hr3]
      have hbody : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs 1 []
          (lowerF E n 3 (S := S) .i64 (.app (.lam A (.lit kbody)) arg)) =
          some (.int (Int.ofNat kbody)) := by
        rw [hlow]
        simp only [emit, emitWith]
        rw [if_pos hk]
        exact eval_litI progs (Int.ofNat kbody) hk
      exact ⟨3, 1, hbody⟩
    all_goals cases hf

/- Erasure of a ζ whose bound term erases to a λ. Not AdeqLetE. -/
theorem erase_let_discard_closed_lam (E : ResolvedEnv) (n kbody : Nat)
    (A bound : Expr Nat) (lb : LExpr)
    (hirr : irrelevant E n [] (.letE A bound (.lit kbody)) = false)
    (hbound : erase E n 2 [] bound = some (.lam lb)) :
    erase E n 3 [] (.letE A bound (.lit kbody)) =
      some (.letE (.lam lb) (.lit kbody)) := by
  have hbody : erase E n 2 (.letBinding A bound :: []) (.lit kbody) =
      some (.lit kbody) := rfl
  rw [erase_let_keep E n 2 [] A bound (.lit kbody) hirr, hbound, hbody]

/- `Good` of that ζ, when the erased bound λ captures nothing.
   Not AdeqLetE. -/
theorem good_let_discard_closed_lam {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n kbody : Nat) (A bound : Expr Nat) (lb : LExpr)
    (hirr : irrelevant E n [] (.letE A bound (.lit kbody)) = false)
    (hbound : erase E n 2 [] bound = some (.lam lb))
    (hclosed : freeVars 1 lb = []) :
    Good progs E n (.letE A bound (.lit kbody)) := by
  refine good_of_exists progs E n (.letE A bound (.lit kbody)) ?_
  intro lf fv T v t w _ _ _ hn hs _ _ hf _ _
  have hv := norm_let_discard_any_val E lf A bound kbody hn
  subst hv
  cases fv with
  | zero => exact Option.noConfusion hs
  | succ m =>
    have hs2 : scmValOf E (m + 1) (.lit kbody) = some (.int (Int.ofNat kbody)) := rfl
    rw [hs2] at hs
    cases hs
    cases t
    case i64 =>
      have hk : inI64Range (Int.ofNat kbody) = true := hf
      have he := erase_let_discard_closed_lam E n kbody A bound lb hirr hbound
      have hr2 := run_let_closed_lam kbody lb hclosed
      have hr3 := run_mono
        (defunc (.letE (.lam lb) (.lit kbody))).2 2 3 []
        (defunc (.letE (.lam lb) (.lit kbody))).1
        (.lit kbody) (Nat.le_succ 2) hr2
      have hlow : lowerF E n 3 (S := S) .i64
          (.letE A bound (.lit kbody)) =
          emit 3 .i64 (.lit kbody) := by
        unfold lowerF pipeline
        simp only [he, hr3]
      have hbody : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs 1 []
          (lowerF E n 3 (S := S) .i64 (.letE A bound (.lit kbody))) =
          some (.int (Int.ofNat kbody)) := by
        rw [hlow]
        simp only [emit, emitWith]
        rw [if_pos hk]
        exact eval_litI progs (Int.ofNat kbody) hk
      exact ⟨3, 1, hbody⟩
    all_goals cases hf

/- `AdeqApp`, `AdeqLetE`, and `AdeqConstDelta` without `EnvClosed` are false.
The defs above require `EnvClosed`, so these refutations are stated for
the unclosed quantifiers. `flipEnv` fails `EnvClosed`.

`weird` is a constructor whose declared type is `bvar 0`. In the empty
context `inferT` of that type is `none`, so `irrelevant weird = false`,
and `scmValOf` is the nullary injection. The application
`(λ (_ : Sort 0), weird) True`, the let `let _ : Sort 0 := True in weird`,
and a transparent definition of that application at type `True` all
normalize to `weird`. Each redex is typed at `True : Prop`, so erasure
is `□` and `lowerF` is `refuse`. `BodiesTyped` holds: the application
and the let sit in an environment with no transparent member, and the
definition's body is that application, which `inferT` types at `True`. -/

def flipEnv : ResolvedEnv where
  members := fun r =>
    match r with
    | 0 => some ⟨.inductiveM, 0, .sort .zero, none⟩
    | 1 => some ⟨.constructorM, 0, .bvar 0, none⟩
    | _ => none

def flipTrue : Expr Nat := .const 0 []
def flipWeird : Expr Nat := .const 1 []
def flipLam : Expr Nat := .lam (.sort .zero) flipWeird
def flipApp : Expr Nat := .app flipLam flipTrue
def flipLet : Expr Nat := .letE (.sort .zero) flipTrue flipWeird

def flipDeltaEnv : ResolvedEnv where
  members := fun r =>
    match r with
    | 0 => some ⟨.inductiveM, 0, .sort .zero, none⟩
    | 1 => some ⟨.constructorM, 0, .bvar 0, none⟩
    | 2 => some ⟨.definitionM, 0, flipTrue, some flipApp⟩
    | _ => none

def flipDelta : Expr Nat := .const 2 []

theorem flipBodies (n : Nat) : BodiesTyped flipEnv n := by
  intro r m b _ hm _ hb _ _
  match r, hm with
  | 0, hm => cases hm; cases hb
  | 1, hm => cases hm; cases hb
  | _ + 2, hm => exact Option.noConfusion hm

theorem flipData : DataTy flipEnv flipTrue :=
  ⟨0, [], [], ⟨.inductiveM, 0, .sort .zero, none⟩, rfl, rfl, rfl⟩

theorem flipDeltaData : DataTy flipDeltaEnv flipTrue :=
  ⟨0, [], [], ⟨.inductiveM, 0, .sort .zero, none⟩, rfl, rfl, rfl⟩

theorem flipApp_norm : norm flipEnv 3 flipApp = some flipWeird := rfl
theorem flipLet_norm : norm flipEnv 3 flipLet = some flipWeird := rfl
theorem flipDelta_norm : norm flipDeltaEnv 4 flipDelta = some flipWeird := rfl
theorem flipDelta_tb : transparentBody flipDeltaEnv 2 [] = some flipApp := rfl
theorem flipWeird_scm : scmValOf flipEnv 1 flipWeird = some (.inj 1 (.list [])) := rfl
theorem flipWeird_scm_delta :
    scmValOf flipDeltaEnv 1 flipWeird = some (.inj 1 (.list [])) := rfl
theorem flipWeird_spine : relevantSpine flipEnv 0 1 flipWeird = true := rfl
theorem flipWeird_spine_delta : relevantSpine flipDeltaEnv 0 1 flipWeird = true := rfl

theorem flipTrue_infer : inferT flipEnv 0 [] flipTrue = some (.sort .zero) := rfl
theorem flipTrue_infer_delta :
    inferT flipDeltaEnv 0 [] flipTrue = some (.sort .zero) := rfl
theorem flipWeird_ty : inferT flipEnv 0 [] flipWeird = some (.bvar 0) := rfl
theorem flipWeird_ty_delta :
    inferT flipDeltaEnv 0 [] flipWeird = some (.bvar 0) := rfl
theorem flipWeird_vinfer : (inferT flipEnv 0 [] flipWeird).isSome = true := by
  rw [flipWeird_ty]
  rfl
theorem flipWeird_vinfer_delta :
    (inferT flipDeltaEnv 0 [] flipWeird).isSome = true := by
  rw [flipWeird_ty_delta]
  rfl
theorem flipWeird_rel : irrelevant flipEnv 0 [] flipWeird = false := by
  rw [irrelevant, flipWeird_ty]
  rfl
theorem flipWeird_rel_delta : irrelevant flipDeltaEnv 0 [] flipWeird = false := by
  rw [irrelevant, flipWeird_ty_delta]
  rfl
theorem flipFits : valFits 1 (sumL 2 .i64) (.inj 1 (.list [])) = true := rfl

theorem flipApp_infer : inferT flipEnv 0 [] flipApp = some flipTrue := rfl
theorem flipLet_infer : inferT flipEnv 0 [] flipLet = some flipTrue := rfl
theorem flipDelta_infer : inferT flipDeltaEnv 0 [] flipDelta = some flipTrue := rfl
theorem flipApp_body_infer : inferT flipDeltaEnv 0 [] flipApp = some flipTrue := rfl

theorem flipApp_irr : irrelevant flipEnv 0 [] flipApp = true :=
  irrelevant_data_tt flipEnv 0 flipApp flipTrue (.sort .zero)
    flipApp_infer flipData flipTrue_infer rfl

theorem flipLet_irr : irrelevant flipEnv 0 [] flipLet = true :=
  irrelevant_data_tt flipEnv 0 flipLet flipTrue (.sort .zero)
    flipLet_infer flipData flipTrue_infer rfl

theorem flipDelta_irr : irrelevant flipDeltaEnv 0 [] flipDelta = true :=
  irrelevant_data_tt flipDeltaEnv 0 flipDelta flipTrue (.sort .zero)
    flipDelta_infer flipDeltaData flipTrue_infer_delta rfl

theorem flipDeltaBodies : BodiesTyped flipDeltaEnv 0 := by
  intro r m b ls hm _ hb hlen _
  match r, hm with
  | 0, hm => cases hm; cases hb
  | 1, hm => cases hm; cases hb
  | 2, hm =>
      cases hm
      cases hb
      cases ls with
      | nil => exact ⟨hasTyT_of_inferT flipApp_body_infer⟩
      | cons _ _ => exact Nat.noConfusion hlen
  | _ + 3, hm => exact Option.noConfusion hm

theorem flipApp_er : Erasable flipEnv 0 flipApp :=
  ⟨1, .box, erase_box_of_irrelevant flipEnv 0 0 [] flipApp flipApp_irr
      (fun k => app_ne_lit flipLam flipTrue k)⟩

theorem flipLet_er : Erasable flipEnv 0 flipLet :=
  ⟨1, .box, erase_box_of_irrelevant flipEnv 0 0 [] flipLet flipLet_irr
      (fun k => letE_ne_lit (.sort .zero) flipTrue flipWeird k)⟩

theorem flipDelta_er : Erasable flipDeltaEnv 0 flipDelta :=
  ⟨1, .box, erase_box_of_irrelevant flipDeltaEnv 0 0 [] flipDelta flipDelta_irr
      (fun k => const_ne_lit 2 k [])⟩

def GoodLoose {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) (E : ResolvedEnv) (n : Nat)
    (e : Expr Nat) : Prop :=
  ∀ (lf fv : Nat) (T v : Expr Nat) (t : BootTy) (w : Val),
    BodiesTyped E n →
    inferT E n [] e = some T → DataTy E T →
    norm E lf e = some v → scmValOf E fv v = some w →
    relevantSpine E n fv v = true → irrelevant E n [] v = false → valFits fv t w = true →
    (inferT E n [] v).isSome = true →
    Erasable E n e →
    ∃ F₀, ∀ F, F₀ ≤ F →
      ∃ lf', Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf' [] (lowerF E n F (S := S) t e)
        = some w

theorem goodWfSameTy_of_goodLoose {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) (E : ResolvedEnv)
    (n : Nat) (e : Expr Nat) (h : GoodLoose progs E n e) : GoodWfSameTy progs E n e := by
  intro lf fv T v t w h0 h1 h2 h3 h4 h5 h6 h7 h8 h9
  exact h lf fv T v t w h0 h1 h2 h3 h4 h5 h6 h7 (by rw [h8]; rfl) h9

theorem good_of_goodLoose {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) (E : ResolvedEnv)
    (n : Nat) (e : Expr Nat) (h : GoodLoose progs E n e) : Good progs E n e :=
  good_of_goodWfSameTy progs E n e (goodWfSameTy_of_goodLoose progs E n e h)

def AdeqAppUnclosed {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) : Prop :=
  ∀ E n f a, GoodLoose progs E n (.app f a)

def AdeqLetEUnclosed {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) : Prop :=
  ∀ E n A v b, GoodLoose progs E n (.letE A v b)

def AdeqConstDeltaUnclosed {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) : Prop :=
  ∀ E n r ls b, transparentBody E r ls = some b → GoodLoose progs E n (.const r ls)

theorem not_adeqApp {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) : ¬ AdeqAppUnclosed progs := by
  intro h
  obtain ⟨F₀, hF⟩ := h flipEnv 0 flipLam flipTrue 3 1 flipTrue flipWeird
      (sumL 2 .i64) (.inj 1 (.list [])) (flipBodies 0) flipApp_infer flipData
      flipApp_norm flipWeird_scm flipWeird_spine flipWeird_rel flipFits
      flipWeird_vinfer flipApp_er
  obtain ⟨lf, he⟩ := hF F₀ (Nat.le_refl _)
  exact eval_irrelevant_ne progs flipEnv 0 (sumL 2 .i64) flipApp _
    flipApp_irr (fun k => app_ne_lit flipLam flipTrue k) F₀ lf he

theorem not_adeqLetE {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) : ¬ AdeqLetEUnclosed progs := by
  intro h
  obtain ⟨F₀, hF⟩ := h flipEnv 0 (.sort .zero) flipTrue flipWeird 3 1 flipTrue
      flipWeird (sumL 2 .i64) (.inj 1 (.list [])) (flipBodies 0) flipLet_infer
      flipData flipLet_norm flipWeird_scm flipWeird_spine flipWeird_rel flipFits
      flipWeird_vinfer flipLet_er
  obtain ⟨lf, he⟩ := hF F₀ (Nat.le_refl _)
  exact eval_irrelevant_ne progs flipEnv 0 (sumL 2 .i64) flipLet _
    flipLet_irr (fun k => letE_ne_lit (.sort .zero) flipTrue flipWeird k) F₀ lf he

theorem not_adeqConstDelta {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) :
    ¬ AdeqConstDeltaUnclosed progs := by
  intro h
  obtain ⟨F₀, hF⟩ := h flipDeltaEnv 0 2 [] flipApp flipDelta_tb 4 1 flipTrue
      flipWeird (sumL 2 .i64) (.inj 1 (.list [])) flipDeltaBodies
      flipDelta_infer flipDeltaData flipDelta_norm flipWeird_scm_delta
      flipWeird_spine_delta flipWeird_rel_delta flipFits flipWeird_vinfer_delta
      flipDelta_er
  obtain ⟨lf, he⟩ := hF F₀ (Nat.le_refl _)
  exact eval_irrelevant_ne progs flipDeltaEnv 0 (sumL 2 .i64) flipDelta _
    flipDelta_irr (fun k => const_ne_lit 2 k []) F₀ lf he

theorem flipEnv_not_closed : ¬ EnvClosed flipEnv := by
  intro h
  have h0 :=
    (h 1 ⟨.constructorM, 0, .bvar 0, none⟩ rfl).1 0
  have : lift 0 1 (.bvar 0 : Expr Nat) = .bvar 1 := by
    simp only [lift, Nat.zero_le, ite_true]
  rw [this] at h0
  exact Nat.noConfusion (Expr.bvar.inj h0)

theorem flipDeltaEnv_not_closed : ¬ EnvClosed flipDeltaEnv := by
  intro h
  have h0 :=
    (h 1 ⟨.constructorM, 0, .bvar 0, none⟩ rfl).1 0
  have : lift 0 1 (.bvar 0 : Expr Nat) = .bvar 1 := by
    simp only [lift, Nat.zero_le, ite_true]
  rw [this] at h0
  exact Nat.noConfusion (Expr.bvar.inj h0)

/- Sequential substitution. The inner replacement is lifted at cutoff `j`,
   which is the index `instantiate` is about to consume; the implementation
   still lifts by `lift 0 1` when it steps under a binder. `EnvSubst` is the
   `j`-free special case of the same operation on a closed member.
   Not AdeqApp, AdeqLetE, or AdeqConstDelta. -/
theorem instantiate_compose (j : Nat) (v a e : Expr Nat) :
    instantiate j v (instantiate j a e) =
      instantiate j (instantiate j v a) (instantiate (j + 1) (lift j 1 v) e) := by
  induction e generalizing j v a with
  | bvar i =>
      by_cases hij : i = j
      · subst hij
        have hne : i ≠ i + 1 := (Nat.succ_ne_self i).symm
        have hnlt : ¬ i + 1 < i := by
          intro h
          exact Nat.lt_irrefl i (Nat.lt_of_le_of_lt (Nat.le_succ i) h)
        have hinner : instantiate i a (.bvar i) = a := by
          rw [instantiate, if_pos rfl]
        have hdrop : instantiate (i + 1) (lift i 1 v) (.bvar i) = .bvar i := by
          rw [instantiate, if_neg hne, if_neg hnlt]
        rw [hinner, hdrop, instantiate, if_pos rfl]
      · by_cases his : i = j + 1
        · subst his
          have hne : j + 1 ≠ j := Nat.succ_ne_self j
          have hlt : j < j + 1 := Nat.lt_succ_self j
          have hstep : instantiate j a (.bvar (j + 1)) = .bvar j := by
            rw [instantiate, if_neg hne, if_pos hlt, Nat.add_sub_cancel]
          have hhit : instantiate (j + 1) (lift j 1 v) (.bvar (j + 1)) = lift j 1 v := by
            rw [instantiate, if_pos rfl]
          rw [hstep, hhit, instantiate, if_pos rfl]
          exact (instantiate_lift_cancel j (instantiate j v a) v).symm
        · by_cases hlt : j < i
          · have hle : j + 1 ≤ i := Nat.succ_le_of_lt hlt
            have hlt' : j + 1 < i := Nat.lt_of_le_of_ne hle (Ne.symm his)
            have hpos : 0 < i := Nat.lt_of_le_of_lt (Nat.zero_le j) hlt
            have hne3 : i - 1 ≠ j := by
              intro heq
              exact his (by
                rw [← Nat.sub_add_cancel (Nat.succ_le_of_lt hpos), heq])
            have hlt3 : j < i - 1 := by
              have hs : i = Nat.succ (i - 1) := (Nat.succ_pred (Nat.ne_of_gt hpos)).symm
              rw [hs] at hlt'
              exact Nat.lt_of_succ_lt_succ hlt'
            have hstep : instantiate j a (.bvar i) = .bvar (i - 1) := by
              rw [instantiate, if_neg hij, if_pos hlt]
            have hhit : instantiate (j + 1) (lift j 1 v) (.bvar i) = .bvar (i - 1) := by
              rw [instantiate, if_neg his, if_pos hlt']
            have hL : instantiate j v (.bvar (i - 1)) = .bvar ((i - 1) - 1) := by
              rw [instantiate, if_neg hne3, if_pos hlt3]
            have hR : instantiate j (instantiate j v a) (.bvar (i - 1)) =
                .bvar ((i - 1) - 1) := by
              rw [instantiate, if_neg hne3, if_pos hlt3]
            rw [hstep, hhit, hL, hR]
          · have hnlt2 : ¬ j + 1 < i := fun h => hlt (Nat.lt_trans (Nat.lt_succ_self j) h)
            have hL : instantiate j a (.bvar i) = .bvar i := by
              rw [instantiate, if_neg hij, if_neg hlt]
            have hR : instantiate (j + 1) (lift j 1 v) (.bvar i) = .bvar i := by
              rw [instantiate, if_neg his, if_neg hnlt2]
            have hL2 : instantiate j v (.bvar i) = .bvar i := by
              rw [instantiate, if_neg hij, if_neg hlt]
            have hR2 : instantiate j (instantiate j v a) (.bvar i) = .bvar i := by
              rw [instantiate, if_neg hij, if_neg hlt]
            rw [hL, hR, hL2, hR2]
  | sort _ => rfl
  | const _ _ => rfl
  | lit _ => rfl
  | app f x ihf ihx =>
      simp only [instantiate]
      rw [ihf j v a, ihx j v a]
  | lam d b ihd ihb =>
      have hbody := ihb (j + 1) (lift 0 1 v) (lift 0 1 a)
      have harg1 : instantiate (1 + j) (lift 0 1 v) (lift 0 1 a) =
          lift 0 1 (instantiate j v a) :=
        (lift_instantiate_high_idx 1 0 j v (Nat.zero_le j) a).symm
      have hrep1 : lift (1 + j) 1 (lift 0 1 v) = lift 0 1 (lift j 1 v) :=
        (lift_lift_permute_idx 1 1 j 0 (Nat.zero_le j) v).symm
      have hcomm : j + 1 = 1 + j := Nat.add_comm j 1
      have harg : instantiate (j + 1) (lift 0 1 v) (lift 0 1 a) =
          lift 0 1 (instantiate j v a) := by
        rw [hcomm]; exact harg1
      have hrep : lift (j + 1) 1 (lift 0 1 v) = lift 0 1 (lift j 1 v) := by
        rw [hcomm]; exact hrep1
      rw [harg, hrep] at hbody
      simp only [instantiate]
      rw [ihd j v a, hbody]
  | pi d b ihd ihb =>
      have hbody := ihb (j + 1) (lift 0 1 v) (lift 0 1 a)
      have harg1 : instantiate (1 + j) (lift 0 1 v) (lift 0 1 a) =
          lift 0 1 (instantiate j v a) :=
        (lift_instantiate_high_idx 1 0 j v (Nat.zero_le j) a).symm
      have hrep1 : lift (1 + j) 1 (lift 0 1 v) = lift 0 1 (lift j 1 v) :=
        (lift_lift_permute_idx 1 1 j 0 (Nat.zero_le j) v).symm
      have hcomm : j + 1 = 1 + j := Nat.add_comm j 1
      have harg : instantiate (j + 1) (lift 0 1 v) (lift 0 1 a) =
          lift 0 1 (instantiate j v a) := by
        rw [hcomm]; exact harg1
      have hrep : lift (j + 1) 1 (lift 0 1 v) = lift 0 1 (lift j 1 v) := by
        rw [hcomm]; exact hrep1
      rw [harg, hrep] at hbody
      simp only [instantiate]
      rw [ihd j v a, hbody]
  | letE d val b ihd ihval ihb =>
      have hbody := ihb (j + 1) (lift 0 1 v) (lift 0 1 a)
      have harg1 : instantiate (1 + j) (lift 0 1 v) (lift 0 1 a) =
          lift 0 1 (instantiate j v a) :=
        (lift_instantiate_high_idx 1 0 j v (Nat.zero_le j) a).symm
      have hrep1 : lift (1 + j) 1 (lift 0 1 v) = lift 0 1 (lift j 1 v) :=
        (lift_lift_permute_idx 1 1 j 0 (Nat.zero_le j) v).symm
      have hcomm : j + 1 = 1 + j := Nat.add_comm j 1
      have harg : instantiate (j + 1) (lift 0 1 v) (lift 0 1 a) =
          lift 0 1 (instantiate j v a) := by
        rw [hcomm]; exact harg1
      have hrep : lift (j + 1) 1 (lift 0 1 v) = lift 0 1 (lift j 1 v) := by
        rw [hcomm]; exact hrep1
      rw [harg, hrep] at hbody
      simp only [instantiate]
      rw [ihd j v a, ihval j v a, hbody]

/- Amounts of `lift 0` add. `lift_shift_comp_idx` is the amount-1 step.
   Not AdeqApp, AdeqLetE, or AdeqConstDelta. -/
theorem lift_add_zero :
    ∀ (j k : Nat) (e : Expr Nat), lift 0 j (lift 0 k e) = lift 0 (k + j) e
  | 0, k, e => by rw [lift_zero_idx, Nat.add_zero]
  | j + 1, k, e => by
      have h1 : lift 0 (j + 1) (lift 0 k e) = lift 0 1 (lift 0 j (lift 0 k e)) :=
        (lift_shift_comp_idx 0 j (lift 0 k e)).symm
      rw [h1, lift_add_zero j k e]
      exact lift_shift_comp_idx 0 (k + j) e

/- Instantiating below a lift that cleared index `c + j` only shortens
   the shift. The binder arm steps the cutoff and lifts the replacement,
   with `(c + j) + 1 = (c + 1) + j`. Not AdeqApp, AdeqLetE, or AdeqConstDelta. -/
theorem instantiate_high_lift :
    ∀ (c j m : Nat) (w e : Expr Nat), j < m →
      instantiate (c + j) w (lift c m e) = lift c (m - 1) e
  | c, j, m, w, .bvar i, h => by
      by_cases hc : c ≤ i
      · have hl : lift c m (Expr.bvar (R := Nat) i) =
            Expr.bvar (R := Nat) (i + m) := by
          simp only [lift, hc, ite_true]
        rw [hl]
        have hlt : c + j < i + m :=
          Nat.lt_of_le_of_lt (Nat.add_le_add_right hc j) (Nat.add_lt_add_left h i)
        have hne : i + m ≠ c + j := Nat.ne_of_gt hlt
        have hstep : instantiate (c + j) w (Expr.bvar (R := Nat) (i + m)) =
            Expr.bvar (R := Nat) (i + m - 1) := by
          rw [instantiate, if_neg hne, if_pos hlt]
        rw [hstep]
        have hr : lift c (m - 1) (Expr.bvar (R := Nat) i) =
            Expr.bvar (R := Nat) (i + (m - 1)) := by
          simp only [lift, hc, ite_true]
        rw [hr]
        have hm : 1 ≤ m := Nat.succ_le_of_lt (Nat.lt_of_le_of_lt (Nat.zero_le j) h)
        exact congrArg (Expr.bvar (R := Nat)) (Nat.add_sub_assoc hm i)
      · have hl : lift c m (Expr.bvar (R := Nat) i) =
            Expr.bvar (R := Nat) i := by
          simp only [lift, hc, ite_false]
        rw [hl]
        have hi : i < c := Nat.not_le.mp hc
        have hlt : i < c + j := Nat.lt_of_lt_of_le hi (Nat.le_add_right c j)
        have hne : i ≠ c + j := Nat.ne_of_lt hlt
        have hnlt : ¬ c + j < i := Nat.not_lt.mpr (Nat.le_of_lt hlt)
        have hstep : instantiate (c + j) w (Expr.bvar (R := Nat) i) =
            Expr.bvar (R := Nat) i := by
          rw [instantiate, if_neg hne, if_neg hnlt]
        rw [hstep]
        have hr : lift c (m - 1) (Expr.bvar (R := Nat) i) =
            Expr.bvar (R := Nat) i := by
          simp only [lift, hc, ite_false]
        rw [hr]
  | _, _, _, _, .sort _, _ => rfl
  | _, _, _, _, .const _ _, _ => rfl
  | _, _, _, _, .lit _, _ => rfl
  | c, j, m, w, .app f x, h => by
      simp only [lift, instantiate, instantiate_high_lift c j m w f h,
        instantiate_high_lift c j m w x h]
  | c, j, m, w, .lam a b, h => by
      have hbody := instantiate_high_lift (c + 1) j m (lift 0 1 w) b h
      have hcj : (c + j) + 1 = (c + 1) + j := Nat.add_right_comm c j 1
      simp only [lift, instantiate]
      rw [instantiate_high_lift c j m w a h, hcj, hbody]
  | c, j, m, w, .pi a b, h => by
      have hbody := instantiate_high_lift (c + 1) j m (lift 0 1 w) b h
      have hcj : (c + j) + 1 = (c + 1) + j := Nat.add_right_comm c j 1
      simp only [lift, instantiate]
      rw [instantiate_high_lift c j m w a h, hcj, hbody]
  | c, j, m, w, .letE a v b, h => by
      have hbody := instantiate_high_lift (c + 1) j m (lift 0 1 w) b h
      have hcj : (c + j) + 1 = (c + 1) + j := Nat.add_right_comm c j 1
      simp only [lift, instantiate]
      rw [instantiate_high_lift c j m w a h, instantiate_high_lift c j m w v h, hcj, hbody]

/- Looking up the tail of a cons is the tail lookup, lifted once.
   `lift_shift_comp_idx` turns `lift 0 ((i + 1) + 1)` into `lift 0 1` of
   `lift 0 (i + 1)`. Not AdeqApp, AdeqLetE, or AdeqConstDelta. -/
theorem lookupType_cons_succ (y : LocalDecl) (Δ : LCtx) (i : Nat) :
    lookupType (y :: Δ) (i + 1) = (lookupType Δ i).map (lift 0 1) := by
  simp only [lookupType, List.get?_cons_succ]
  cases h : Δ.get? i with
  | none => rfl
  | some d =>
      cases d with
      | assumption a =>
          simp only [h, Option.map]
          exact congrArg some (lift_shift_comp_idx 0 (i + 1) a).symm
      | letBinding a _ =>
          simp only [h, Option.map]
          exact congrArg some (lift_shift_comp_idx 0 (i + 1) a).symm

/- `instantiateLevels` does not move de Bruijn indices, so `closedAt` is
   unchanged. A closed member type stays closed after a level instance.
   Not AdeqApp, AdeqLetE, or AdeqConstDelta. -/
theorem closedAt_instantiateLevels (ls : List Level) :
    ∀ (e : Expr Nat) (c : Nat),
      closedAt c (instantiateLevels ls e) = closedAt c e
  | .bvar _, _ => rfl
  | .sort _, _ => rfl
  | .const _ _, _ => rfl
  | .lit _, _ => rfl
  | .app f x, c => by
      simp only [instantiateLevels, closedAt, closedAt_instantiateLevels ls f c,
        closedAt_instantiateLevels ls x c]
  | .lam a b, c => by
      simp only [instantiateLevels, closedAt, closedAt_instantiateLevels ls a c,
        closedAt_instantiateLevels ls b (c + 1)]
  | .pi a b, c => by
      simp only [instantiateLevels, closedAt, closedAt_instantiateLevels ls a c,
        closedAt_instantiateLevels ls b (c + 1)]
  | .letE a v b, c => by
      simp only [instantiateLevels, closedAt, closedAt_instantiateLevels ls a c,
        closedAt_instantiateLevels ls v c, closedAt_instantiateLevels ls b (c + 1)]

/- The syntactic checker on a sort is the successor sort. Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem inferT_sort {E : ResolvedEnv} {n : Nat} (Γ : LCtx) (l : Level) :
    inferT E n Γ (.sort l) = some (.sort (.succ l)) := rfl

/- The syntactic checker on a bound variable is the context lookup.
   The `match` in `checkT` is split, then each branch is the lookup
   equation. Not AdeqApp, AdeqLetE, or AdeqConstDelta. -/
theorem inferT_bvar {E : ResolvedEnv} {n : Nat} (Γ : LCtx) (i : Nat) :
    inferT E n Γ (.bvar i) = lookupType Γ i := by
  unfold inferT checkT
  split <;> simp_all

/- Instantiate one declaration at a de Bruijn index. The prefix walker
   below uses this at the index of the removed assumption. Not AdeqApp. -/
def substDecl (k : Nat) (v : Expr Nat) : LocalDecl → LocalDecl
  | .assumption A => .assumption (instantiate k v A)
  | .letBinding A val => .letBinding (instantiate k v A) (instantiate k v val)

/- Substitute for the assumption just under `Δ`, lifting `v` once per
   newer declaration. `(substPrefix v Δ).length = Δ.length`. Not AdeqApp. -/
def substPrefix (v : Expr Nat) : LCtx → LCtx
  | [] => []
  | d :: Δ => substDecl Δ.length (lift 0 Δ.length v) d :: substPrefix v Δ

theorem substPrefix_length (v : Expr Nat) :
    ∀ Δ : LCtx, (substPrefix v Δ).length = Δ.length
  | [] => rfl
  | _ :: Δ => by
      simp only [substPrefix, List.length_cons, substPrefix_length v Δ]

/- An index below the prefix length ignores the tail. The lift amount is
   `i + 1` on both sides. Not AdeqApp, AdeqLetE, or AdeqConstDelta. -/
theorem lookupType_append_lt (Δ Γ : LCtx) (i : Nat) (hi : i < Δ.length) :
    lookupType (Δ ++ Γ) i = lookupType Δ i := by
  simp only [lookupType]
  rw [List.get?_append hi]

/- An index at or past the prefix reads the tail, then lifts by the
   prefix length. `lift_add_zero` adds that amount to the tail's own
   `i + 1` shift. Not AdeqApp, AdeqLetE, or AdeqConstDelta. -/
theorem lookupType_append_ge (Δ Γ : LCtx) (i : Nat) (hi : Δ.length ≤ i) :
    lookupType (Δ ++ Γ) i =
      (lookupType Γ (i - Δ.length)).map (lift 0 Δ.length) := by
  simp only [lookupType]
  rw [List.get?_append_right hi]
  cases h : Γ.get? (i - Δ.length) with
  | none => rfl
  | some d =>
      cases d with
      | assumption a =>
          simp only [h, Option.map]
          have hidx : (i - Δ.length) + 1 + Δ.length = i + 1 := by
            rw [Nat.add_right_comm, Nat.sub_add_cancel hi]
          rw [lift_add_zero]
          rw [hidx]
      | letBinding a _ =>
          simp only [h, Option.map]
          have hidx : (i - Δ.length) + 1 + Δ.length = i + 1 := by
            rw [Nat.add_right_comm, Nat.sub_add_cancel hi]
          rw [lift_add_zero]
          rw [hidx]

/- Lifting an instantiation at `k` is an instantiation at `k + 1`.
   `lift_instantiate_high_idx` produces index `1 + k`; `Nat.add_comm`
   turns it into `k + 1`. Not AdeqApp, AdeqLetE, or AdeqConstDelta. -/
theorem lift_instantiate_succ (k : Nat) (v A : Expr Nat) :
    lift 0 1 (instantiate k (lift 0 k v) A) =
      instantiate (k + 1) (lift 0 (k + 1) v) (lift 0 1 A) := by
  have h1 : lift 0 1 (instantiate k (lift 0 k v) A) =
      instantiate (1 + k) (lift 0 1 (lift 0 k v)) (lift 0 1 A) :=
    lift_instantiate_high_idx 1 0 k (lift 0 k v) (Nat.zero_le k) A
  have h2 : lift 0 1 (lift 0 k v) = lift 0 (k + 1) v :=
    lift_add_zero 1 k v
  have hcomm : 1 + k = k + 1 := Nat.add_comm 1 k
  rw [h1, h2, hcomm]

/- Lookup in a substituted prefix instantiates the original lookup at
   the prefix length. The head uses `lift_instantiate_succ`; the tail
   is `lookupType_cons_succ` plus the same identity. Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem lookupType_substPrefix (v : Expr Nat) :
    ∀ (Δ : LCtx) (i : Nat), i < Δ.length →
      lookupType (substPrefix v Δ) i =
        (lookupType Δ i).map (instantiate Δ.length (lift 0 Δ.length v))
  | [], _, hi => absurd hi (Nat.not_lt_zero _)
  | d :: Δ, 0, _ => by
      simp only [List.length_cons]
      cases d with
      | assumption a =>
          simp only [substPrefix, substDecl, lookupType, List.get?_cons_zero, Option.map]
          exact congrArg some (lift_instantiate_succ Δ.length v a)
      | letBinding a _ =>
          simp only [substPrefix, substDecl, lookupType, List.get?_cons_zero, Option.map]
          exact congrArg some (lift_instantiate_succ Δ.length v a)
  | d :: Δ, i + 1, hi => by
      have hi' : i < Δ.length := Nat.lt_of_succ_lt_succ hi
      have ih := lookupType_substPrefix v Δ i hi'
      simp only [List.length_cons]
      rw [substPrefix, lookupType_cons_succ, ih, lookupType_cons_succ]
      cases hlook : lookupType Δ i with
      | none => rfl
      | some A =>
          simp only [hlook, Option.map]
          exact congrArg some (lift_instantiate_succ Δ.length v A)

/- Instantiating at `c + j` after instantiating at `c` is one instantiation
   at `c` of the substituted argument, then one at `c + j + 1`. The `c = 0`
   case is what an application type needs. Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem instantiate_dist (c j : Nat) (w a e : Expr Nat) :
    instantiate (c + j) (lift 0 c w) (instantiate c (lift 0 c a) e) =
      instantiate c (lift 0 c (instantiate j w a))
        (instantiate (c + j + 1) (lift 0 (c + 1) w) e) := by
  induction e generalizing c j w a with
  | bvar i =>
      by_cases heq : c = i
      · subst heq
        have hinner : instantiate c (lift 0 c a) (Expr.bvar (R := Nat) c) =
            lift 0 c a := by
          rw [instantiate, if_pos rfl]
        rw [hinner]
        have hL : instantiate (c + j) (lift 0 c w) (lift 0 c a) =
            lift 0 c (instantiate j w a) :=
          (lift_instantiate_high_idx c 0 j w (Nat.zero_le j) a).symm
        have hne : c ≠ c + j + 1 := by
          intro h
          exact Nat.ne_of_lt (Nat.lt_succ_of_le (Nat.le_add_right c j)) h
        have hnlt : ¬ c + j + 1 < c := by
          intro h
          exact Nat.lt_irrefl c (Nat.lt_of_le_of_lt (Nat.le_add_right c j)
            (Nat.lt_trans (Nat.lt_succ_self (c + j)) h))
        have hskip : instantiate (c + j + 1) (lift 0 (c + 1) w) (Expr.bvar (R := Nat) c) =
            Expr.bvar (R := Nat) c := by
          rw [instantiate, if_neg hne, if_neg hnlt]
        rw [hL, hskip, instantiate, if_pos rfl]
      · by_cases hgt : c < i
        · by_cases hhit : i = c + j + 1
          · subst hhit
            have hlt0 : c < c + j + 1 := Nat.lt_succ_of_le (Nat.le_add_right c j)
            have hne0 : c + j + 1 ≠ c := (Nat.ne_of_lt hlt0).symm
            have hsub : (c + j + 1) - 1 = c + j := Nat.add_sub_cancel (c + j) 1
            have hinner : instantiate c (lift 0 c a) (Expr.bvar (R := Nat) (c + j + 1)) =
                Expr.bvar (R := Nat) (c + j) := by
              rw [instantiate, if_neg hne0, if_pos hlt0, hsub]
            rw [hinner]
            have hL : instantiate (c + j) (lift 0 c w) (Expr.bvar (R := Nat) (c + j)) =
                lift 0 c w := by
              rw [instantiate, if_pos rfl]
            have hR1 : instantiate (c + j + 1) (lift 0 (c + 1) w)
                (Expr.bvar (R := Nat) (c + j + 1)) = lift 0 (c + 1) w := by
              rw [instantiate, if_pos rfl]
            have hhigh := instantiate_high_lift 0 c (c + 1)
                (lift 0 c (instantiate j w a)) w (Nat.lt_succ_self c)
            have hsub2 : (c + 1) - 1 = c := Nat.add_sub_cancel c 1
            rw [hL, hR1]
            rw [Nat.zero_add] at hhigh
            rw [hsub2] at hhigh
            exact hhigh.symm
          · by_cases hdec : c + j < i - 1
            · have hpos : 0 < i := Nat.lt_of_le_of_lt (Nat.zero_le c) hgt
              have hone : 1 ≤ i := Nat.succ_le_of_lt hpos
              have hpred : (i - 1) + 1 = i := Nat.sub_add_cancel hone
              have hlt2 : c + j + 1 < i := by
                have h1 : c + j + 1 < (i - 1) + 1 := Nat.add_lt_add_right hdec 1
                rw [hpred] at h1
                exact h1
              have hneL : i - 1 ≠ c + j := Nat.ne_of_gt hdec
              have hneR : i ≠ c + j + 1 := hhit
              have hltL : c + j < i - 1 := hdec
              have hinner : instantiate c (lift 0 c a) (Expr.bvar (R := Nat) i) =
                  Expr.bvar (R := Nat) (i - 1) := by
                rw [instantiate, if_neg (Nat.ne_of_gt hgt), if_pos hgt]
              have hL : instantiate (c + j) (lift 0 c w) (Expr.bvar (R := Nat) (i - 1)) =
                  Expr.bvar (R := Nat) ((i - 1) - 1) := by
                rw [instantiate, if_neg hneL, if_pos hltL]
              have hR1 : instantiate (c + j + 1) (lift 0 (c + 1) w) (Expr.bvar (R := Nat) i) =
                  Expr.bvar (R := Nat) (i - 1) := by
                rw [instantiate, if_neg hneR, if_pos hlt2]
              have hltc : c < i - 1 := Nat.lt_of_le_of_lt (Nat.le_add_right c j) hdec
              have hnec : i - 1 ≠ c := Nat.ne_of_gt hltc
              have hR2 : instantiate c (lift 0 c (instantiate j w a))
                  (Expr.bvar (R := Nat) (i - 1)) =
                  Expr.bvar (R := Nat) ((i - 1) - 1) := by
                rw [instantiate, if_neg hnec, if_pos hltc]
              rw [hinner, hL, hR1, hR2]
            · have hpos : 0 < i := Nat.lt_of_le_of_lt (Nat.zero_le c) hgt
              have hone : 1 ≤ i := Nat.succ_le_of_lt hpos
              have hpred : (i - 1) + 1 = i := Nat.sub_add_cancel hone
              have hle : i - 1 ≤ c + j := Nat.not_lt.mp hdec
              have hne1 : i - 1 ≠ c + j := by
                intro heq1
                have : i = c + j + 1 := by
                  rw [← hpred, heq1]
                exact hhit this
              have hnlt1 : ¬ c + j < i - 1 := hdec
              have hle2 : i ≤ c + j + 1 := by
                rw [← hpred]
                exact Nat.add_le_add_right hle 1
              have hnlt2 : ¬ c + j + 1 < i := Nat.not_lt.mpr hle2
              have hinner : instantiate c (lift 0 c a) (Expr.bvar (R := Nat) i) =
                  Expr.bvar (R := Nat) (i - 1) := by
                rw [instantiate, if_neg (Nat.ne_of_gt hgt), if_pos hgt]
              have hL : instantiate (c + j) (lift 0 c w) (Expr.bvar (R := Nat) (i - 1)) =
                  Expr.bvar (R := Nat) (i - 1) := by
                rw [instantiate, if_neg hne1, if_neg hnlt1]
              have hR1 : instantiate (c + j + 1) (lift 0 (c + 1) w) (Expr.bvar (R := Nat) i) =
                  Expr.bvar (R := Nat) i := by
                rw [instantiate, if_neg hhit, if_neg hnlt2]
              have hnec : i ≠ c := Nat.ne_of_gt hgt
              have hR2 : instantiate c (lift 0 c (instantiate j w a)) (Expr.bvar (R := Nat) i) =
                  Expr.bvar (R := Nat) (i - 1) := by
                rw [instantiate, if_neg hnec, if_pos hgt]
              rw [hinner, hL, hR1, hR2]
        · have hi : i < c := Nat.lt_of_le_of_ne (Nat.le_of_not_lt hgt) (Ne.symm heq)
          have hnei : i ≠ c := Nat.ne_of_lt hi
          have hnlt : ¬ c < i := Nat.not_lt.mpr (Nat.le_of_lt hi)
          have hinner : instantiate c (lift 0 c a) (Expr.bvar (R := Nat) i) =
              Expr.bvar (R := Nat) i := by
            rw [instantiate, if_neg hnei, if_neg hnlt]
          have hltj : i < c + j := Nat.lt_of_lt_of_le hi (Nat.le_add_right c j)
          have hnej : i ≠ c + j := Nat.ne_of_lt hltj
          have hnltj : ¬ c + j < i := Nat.not_lt.mpr (Nat.le_of_lt hltj)
          have hltj1 : i < c + j + 1 := Nat.lt_of_lt_of_le hi (Nat.le_add_right c (j + 1))
          have hnej1 : i ≠ c + j + 1 := Nat.ne_of_lt hltj1
          have hnltj1 : ¬ c + j + 1 < i := Nat.not_lt.mpr (Nat.le_of_lt hltj1)
          have hL : instantiate (c + j) (lift 0 c w) (Expr.bvar (R := Nat) i) =
              Expr.bvar (R := Nat) i := by
            rw [instantiate, if_neg hnej, if_neg hnltj]
          have hR1 : instantiate (c + j + 1) (lift 0 (c + 1) w) (Expr.bvar (R := Nat) i) =
              Expr.bvar (R := Nat) i := by
            rw [instantiate, if_neg hnej1, if_neg hnltj1]
          have hR2 : instantiate c (lift 0 c (instantiate j w a)) (Expr.bvar (R := Nat) i) =
              Expr.bvar (R := Nat) i := by
            rw [instantiate, if_neg hnei, if_neg hnlt]
          rw [hinner, hL, hR1, hR2]
  | sort _ => rfl
  | const _ _ => rfl
  | lit _ => rfl
  | app f x ihf ihx =>
      simp only [instantiate]
      rw [ihf c j w a, ihx c j w a]
  | lam d b ihd ihb =>
      have hbody := ihb (c + 1) j w a
      have hwc : lift 0 1 (lift 0 c w) = lift 0 (c + 1) w := lift_add_zero 1 c w
      have hac : lift 0 1 (lift 0 c a) = lift 0 (c + 1) a := lift_add_zero 1 c a
      have hidx : (c + j) + 1 = (c + 1) + j := Nat.add_right_comm c j 1
      have harg : lift 0 1 (lift 0 c (instantiate j w a)) =
          lift 0 (c + 1) (instantiate j w a) :=
        lift_add_zero 1 c (instantiate j w a)
      have hrep : lift 0 1 (lift 0 (c + 1) w) = lift 0 ((c + 1) + 1) w :=
        lift_add_zero 1 (c + 1) w
      rw [← hwc, ← hac, ← hidx, ← harg, ← hrep] at hbody
      simp only [instantiate]
      rw [ihd c j w a, hbody]
  | pi d b ihd ihb =>
      have hbody := ihb (c + 1) j w a
      have hwc : lift 0 1 (lift 0 c w) = lift 0 (c + 1) w := lift_add_zero 1 c w
      have hac : lift 0 1 (lift 0 c a) = lift 0 (c + 1) a := lift_add_zero 1 c a
      have hidx : (c + j) + 1 = (c + 1) + j := Nat.add_right_comm c j 1
      have harg : lift 0 1 (lift 0 c (instantiate j w a)) =
          lift 0 (c + 1) (instantiate j w a) :=
        lift_add_zero 1 c (instantiate j w a)
      have hrep : lift 0 1 (lift 0 (c + 1) w) = lift 0 ((c + 1) + 1) w :=
        lift_add_zero 1 (c + 1) w
      rw [← hwc, ← hac, ← hidx, ← harg, ← hrep] at hbody
      simp only [instantiate]
      rw [ihd c j w a, hbody]
  | letE d val b ihd ihval ihb =>
      have hbody := ihb (c + 1) j w a
      have hwc : lift 0 1 (lift 0 c w) = lift 0 (c + 1) w := lift_add_zero 1 c w
      have hac : lift 0 1 (lift 0 c a) = lift 0 (c + 1) a := lift_add_zero 1 c a
      have hidx : (c + j) + 1 = (c + 1) + j := Nat.add_right_comm c j 1
      have harg : lift 0 1 (lift 0 c (instantiate j w a)) =
          lift 0 (c + 1) (instantiate j w a) :=
        lift_add_zero 1 c (instantiate j w a)
      have hrep : lift 0 1 (lift 0 (c + 1) w) = lift 0 ((c + 1) + 1) w :=
        lift_add_zero 1 (c + 1) w
      rw [← hwc, ← hac, ← hidx, ← harg, ← hrep] at hbody
      simp only [instantiate]
      rw [ihd c j w a, ihval c j w a, hbody]

theorem instantiate_dist_zero (j : Nat) (w a e : Expr Nat) :
    instantiate j w (instantiate 0 a e) =
      instantiate 0 (instantiate j w a) (instantiate (j + 1) (lift 0 1 w) e) := by
  simpa [Nat.zero_add, lift_zero_idx] using instantiate_dist 0 j w a e

/- A lift commutes with an instantiation at the same index. The body of
   the instantiated term is lifted one cutoff higher, which is what an
   application type needs at cutoff 0. Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem lift_instantiate_shift (c n : Nat) (a e : Expr Nat) :
    lift c n (instantiate c a e) =
      instantiate c (lift c n a) (lift (c + 1) n e) := by
  induction e generalizing c n a with
  | bvar i =>
      by_cases heq : i = c
      · subst heq
        have hL : instantiate i a (Expr.bvar (R := Nat) i) = a := by
          rw [instantiate, if_pos rfl]
        have hskip : lift (i + 1) n (Expr.bvar (R := Nat) i) =
            Expr.bvar (R := Nat) i := by
          have hnle : ¬ i + 1 ≤ i := Nat.not_le.mpr (Nat.lt_succ_self i)
          simp only [lift, hnle, ite_false]
        rw [hL, hskip, instantiate, if_pos rfl]
      · by_cases hlt : c < i
        · have hpos : 0 < i := Nat.lt_of_le_of_lt (Nat.zero_le c) hlt
          have hone : 1 ≤ i := Nat.succ_le_of_lt hpos
          have hsub : (i - 1) + 1 = i := Nat.sub_add_cancel hone
          have hle : c ≤ i - 1 := Nat.le_of_lt_succ (hsub.symm ▸ hlt)
          have hne : i ≠ c := Nat.ne_of_gt hlt
          have hinner : instantiate c a (Expr.bvar (R := Nat) i) =
              Expr.bvar (R := Nat) (i - 1) := by
            rw [instantiate, if_neg hne, if_pos hlt]
          have hLL : lift c n (Expr.bvar (R := Nat) (i - 1)) =
              Expr.bvar (R := Nat) (i - 1 + n) := by
            simp only [lift, hle, ite_true]
          have hle1 : c + 1 ≤ i := Nat.succ_le_of_lt hlt
          have hLR : lift (c + 1) n (Expr.bvar (R := Nat) i) =
              Expr.bvar (R := Nat) (i + n) := by
            simp only [lift, hle1, ite_true]
          have hne2 : i + n ≠ c :=
            Nat.ne_of_gt (Nat.lt_of_lt_of_le hlt (Nat.le_add_right i n))
          have hlt2 : c < i + n := Nat.lt_of_lt_of_le hlt (Nat.le_add_right i n)
          have hstep : instantiate c (lift c n a) (Expr.bvar (R := Nat) (i + n)) =
              Expr.bvar (R := Nat) (i + n - 1) := by
            rw [instantiate, if_neg hne2, if_pos hlt2]
          have hidx : i - 1 + n = i + n - 1 := by
            have h1 : n + (i - 1) = n + i - 1 := (Nat.add_sub_assoc hone n).symm
            rw [← Nat.add_comm n (i - 1), ← Nat.add_comm n i]
            exact h1
          rw [hinner, hLL, hLR, hstep]
          exact congrArg (Expr.bvar (R := Nat)) hidx
        · have hi : i < c := Nat.lt_of_le_of_ne (Nat.le_of_not_lt hlt) heq
          have hne : i ≠ c := Nat.ne_of_lt hi
          have hnlt : ¬ c < i := Nat.not_lt.mpr (Nat.le_of_lt hi)
          have hnle : ¬ c ≤ i := Nat.not_le.mpr hi
          have hnle1 : ¬ c + 1 ≤ i := Nat.not_le.mpr (Nat.lt_trans hi (Nat.lt_succ_self c))
          simp only [instantiate, lift, if_neg hne, if_neg hnlt, hnle, hnle1, ite_false]
  | sort _ => rfl
  | const _ _ => rfl
  | lit _ => rfl
  | app f x ihf ihx =>
      simp only [lift, instantiate, ihf c n a, ihx c n a]
  | lam d b ihd ihb =>
      have hbody := ihb (c + 1) n (lift 0 1 a)
      have hperm : lift 0 1 (lift c n a) = lift (1 + c) n (lift 0 1 a) :=
        lift_lift_permute_idx 1 n c 0 (Nat.zero_le c) a
      have hcomm : c + 1 = 1 + c := Nat.add_comm c 1
      have hperm' : lift 0 1 (lift c n a) = lift (c + 1) n (lift 0 1 a) := by
        rw [hcomm]; exact hperm
      rw [← hperm'] at hbody
      simp only [lift, instantiate]
      rw [ihd c n a, hbody]
  | pi d b ihd ihb =>
      have hbody := ihb (c + 1) n (lift 0 1 a)
      have hperm : lift 0 1 (lift c n a) = lift (1 + c) n (lift 0 1 a) :=
        lift_lift_permute_idx 1 n c 0 (Nat.zero_le c) a
      have hcomm : c + 1 = 1 + c := Nat.add_comm c 1
      have hperm' : lift 0 1 (lift c n a) = lift (c + 1) n (lift 0 1 a) := by
        rw [hcomm]; exact hperm
      rw [← hperm'] at hbody
      simp only [lift, instantiate]
      rw [ihd c n a, hbody]
  | letE d val b ihd ihval ihb =>
      have hbody := ihb (c + 1) n (lift 0 1 a)
      have hperm : lift 0 1 (lift c n a) = lift (1 + c) n (lift 0 1 a) :=
        lift_lift_permute_idx 1 n c 0 (Nat.zero_le c) a
      have hcomm : c + 1 = 1 + c := Nat.add_comm c 1
      have hperm' : lift 0 1 (lift c n a) = lift (c + 1) n (lift 0 1 a) := by
        rw [hcomm]; exact hperm
      rw [← hperm'] at hbody
      simp only [lift, instantiate]
      rw [ihd c n a, ihval c n a, hbody]

/- A term fixed by instantiation at `j`, even when the replacement is a
   `k`-lift, has no free index at `j` or above. The binder steps `k`
   because `instantiate` lifts the replacement. Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem closedAt_of_instantiateLift :
    ∀ (e : Expr Nat) (j k : Nat),
      (∀ v, instantiate j (lift 0 k v) e = e) → closedAt j e = true
  | .bvar i, j, k, h => by
      by_cases heq : i = j
      · have h0 := h (.sort .zero)
        rw [heq] at h0
        simp only [lift, instantiate, if_pos rfl] at h0
        exact Expr.noConfusion h0
      · by_cases hlt : j < i
        · have h0 := h (.sort .zero)
          simp only [instantiate, if_neg heq, if_pos hlt] at h0
          have hpos : i ≠ 0 := Nat.ne_of_gt (Nat.lt_of_le_of_lt (Nat.zero_le j) hlt)
          exact absurd (Expr.bvar.inj h0) (Nat.ne_of_lt (Nat.pred_lt hpos))
        · have hi : i < j := Nat.lt_of_le_of_ne (Nat.le_of_not_lt hlt) heq
          simp only [closedAt, decide_eq_true_eq]
          exact hi
  | .sort _, _, _, _ => rfl
  | .const _ _, _, _, _ => rfl
  | .lit _, _, _, _ => rfl
  | .app f x, j, k, h => by
      have hf : ∀ v, instantiate j (lift 0 k v) f = f := by
        intro v
        have hv := h v
        simp only [instantiate] at hv
        exact (Expr.app.inj hv).1
      have hx : ∀ v, instantiate j (lift 0 k v) x = x := by
        intro v
        have hv := h v
        simp only [instantiate] at hv
        exact (Expr.app.inj hv).2
      simp only [closedAt, closedAt_of_instantiateLift f j k hf,
        closedAt_of_instantiateLift x j k hx, Bool.and_self]
  | .lam a b, j, k, h => by
      have ha : ∀ v, instantiate j (lift 0 k v) a = a := by
        intro v
        have hv := h v
        simp only [instantiate] at hv
        exact (Expr.lam.inj hv).1
      have hb0 : ∀ v, instantiate (j + 1) (lift 0 1 (lift 0 k v)) b = b := by
        intro v
        have hv := h v
        simp only [instantiate] at hv
        exact (Expr.lam.inj hv).2
      have hb : ∀ v, instantiate (j + 1) (lift 0 (k + 1) v) b = b := by
        intro v
        rw [← lift_add_zero 1 k v]
        exact hb0 v
      simp only [closedAt, closedAt_of_instantiateLift a j k ha,
        closedAt_of_instantiateLift b (j + 1) (k + 1) hb, Bool.and_self]
  | .pi a b, j, k, h => by
      have ha : ∀ v, instantiate j (lift 0 k v) a = a := by
        intro v
        have hv := h v
        simp only [instantiate] at hv
        exact (Expr.pi.inj hv).1
      have hb0 : ∀ v, instantiate (j + 1) (lift 0 1 (lift 0 k v)) b = b := by
        intro v
        have hv := h v
        simp only [instantiate] at hv
        exact (Expr.pi.inj hv).2
      have hb : ∀ v, instantiate (j + 1) (lift 0 (k + 1) v) b = b := by
        intro v
        rw [← lift_add_zero 1 k v]
        exact hb0 v
      simp only [closedAt, closedAt_of_instantiateLift a j k ha,
        closedAt_of_instantiateLift b (j + 1) (k + 1) hb, Bool.and_self]
  | .letE a val b, j, k, h => by
      have ha : ∀ v, instantiate j (lift 0 k v) a = a := by
        intro v
        have hv := h v
        simp only [instantiate] at hv
        exact (Expr.letE.inj hv).1
      have hval : ∀ v, instantiate j (lift 0 k v) val = val := by
        intro v
        have hv := h v
        simp only [instantiate] at hv
        exact (Expr.letE.inj hv).2.1
      have hb0 : ∀ v, instantiate (j + 1) (lift 0 1 (lift 0 k v)) b = b := by
        intro v
        have hv := h v
        simp only [instantiate] at hv
        exact (Expr.letE.inj hv).2.2
      have hb : ∀ v, instantiate (j + 1) (lift 0 (k + 1) v) b = b := by
        intro v
        rw [← lift_add_zero 1 k v]
        exact hb0 v
      simp only [closedAt, closedAt_of_instantiateLift a j k ha,
        closedAt_of_instantiateLift val j k hval,
        closedAt_of_instantiateLift b (j + 1) (k + 1) hb, Bool.and_self]

/- `closedAt c` makes a lift at cutoff `c` the identity, for any amount.
   Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem lift_id_of_closedAt :
    ∀ (e : Expr Nat) (c n : Nat), closedAt c e = true → lift c n e = e
  | .bvar i, c, _, h => by
      have hlt : i < c := by simpa [closedAt, decide_eq_true_eq] using h
      have hle : ¬ c ≤ i := Nat.not_le.mpr hlt
      simp only [lift]
      rw [if_neg hle]
  | .sort _, _, _, _ => rfl
  | .const _ _, _, _, _ => rfl
  | .lit _, _, _, _ => rfl
  | .app f x, c, n, h => by
      simp only [closedAt, Bool.and_eq_true] at h
      simp only [lift, lift_id_of_closedAt f c n h.1, lift_id_of_closedAt x c n h.2]
  | .lam a b, c, n, h => by
      simp only [closedAt, Bool.and_eq_true] at h
      simp only [lift, lift_id_of_closedAt a c n h.1, lift_id_of_closedAt b (c + 1) n h.2]
  | .pi a b, c, n, h => by
      simp only [closedAt, Bool.and_eq_true] at h
      simp only [lift, lift_id_of_closedAt a c n h.1, lift_id_of_closedAt b (c + 1) n h.2]
  | .letE a val b, c, n, h => by
      simp only [closedAt, Bool.and_eq_true] at h
      simp only [lift, lift_id_of_closedAt a c n h.1.1, lift_id_of_closedAt val c n h.1.2,
        lift_id_of_closedAt b (c + 1) n h.2]

theorem closedAt_mono :
    ∀ (e : Expr Nat) (c d : Nat), c ≤ d → closedAt c e = true → closedAt d e = true
  | .bvar i, c, d, hle, h => by
      have hlt : i < c := by simpa [closedAt, decide_eq_true_eq] using h
      simp only [closedAt, decide_eq_true_eq]
      exact Nat.lt_of_lt_of_le hlt hle
  | .sort _, _, _, _, _ => rfl
  | .const _ _, _, _, _, _ => rfl
  | .lit _, _, _, _, _ => rfl
  | .app f x, c, d, hle, h => by
      simp only [closedAt, Bool.and_eq_true] at h
      simp only [closedAt, closedAt_mono f c d hle h.1, closedAt_mono x c d hle h.2,
        Bool.and_self]
  | .lam a b, c, d, hle, h => by
      simp only [closedAt, Bool.and_eq_true] at h
      simp only [closedAt, closedAt_mono a c d hle h.1,
        closedAt_mono b (c + 1) (d + 1) (Nat.succ_le_succ hle) h.2, Bool.and_self]
  | .pi a b, c, d, hle, h => by
      simp only [closedAt, Bool.and_eq_true] at h
      simp only [closedAt, closedAt_mono a c d hle h.1,
        closedAt_mono b (c + 1) (d + 1) (Nat.succ_le_succ hle) h.2, Bool.and_self]
  | .letE a v b, c, d, hle, h => by
      simp only [closedAt, Bool.and_eq_true] at h
      simp only [closedAt, closedAt_mono a c d hle h.1.1, closedAt_mono v c d hle h.1.2,
        closedAt_mono b (c + 1) (d + 1) (Nat.succ_le_succ hle) h.2, Bool.and_self]

/- Lifting at cutoff `c + j` after a lift of amount `j` at cutoff `c` is one
   lift of amount `j + n`. Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem lift_add_cut :
    ∀ (c j n : Nat) (e : Expr Nat),
      lift (c + j) n (lift c j e) = lift c (j + n) e
  | c, j, n, .bvar i => by
      by_cases hc : c ≤ i
      · have hcj : c + j ≤ i + j := Nat.add_le_add_right hc j
        simp only [lift, hc, ite_true, hcj, ite_true]
        exact congrArg (Expr.bvar (R := Nat)) (Nat.add_assoc i j n)
      · have hcj : ¬ c + j ≤ i := fun h => hc (Nat.le_trans (Nat.le_add_right c j) h)
        simp only [lift, hc, ite_false, hcj, ite_false]
  | _, _, _, .sort _ => rfl
  | _, _, _, .const _ _ => rfl
  | _, _, _, .lit _ => rfl
  | c, j, n, .app f x => by
      simp only [lift, lift_add_cut c j n f, lift_add_cut c j n x]
  | c, j, n, .lam a b => by
      have hbody := lift_add_cut (c + 1) j n b
      have hcomm : (c + j) + 1 = (c + 1) + j := Nat.add_right_comm c j 1
      simp only [lift, lift_add_cut c j n a, hcomm, hbody]
  | c, j, n, .pi a b => by
      have hbody := lift_add_cut (c + 1) j n b
      have hcomm : (c + j) + 1 = (c + 1) + j := Nat.add_right_comm c j 1
      simp only [lift, lift_add_cut c j n a, hcomm, hbody]
  | c, j, n, .letE a v b => by
      have hbody := lift_add_cut (c + 1) j n b
      have hcomm : (c + j) + 1 = (c + 1) + j := Nat.add_right_comm c j 1
      simp only [lift, lift_add_cut c j n a, lift_add_cut c j n v, hcomm, hbody]

/- A lift at cutoff `k` commutes with instantiation at `c ≤ k`. The body is
   lifted one cutoff higher. At `c = 0` this is application weakening.
   Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem lift_instantiate_above (n : Nat) :
    ∀ (c k : Nat) (a e : Expr Nat), c ≤ k →
      lift k n (instantiate c a e) =
        instantiate c (lift k n a) (lift (k + 1) n e)
  | c, k, a, .bvar i, hck => by
      by_cases heq : i = c
      · subst heq
        have hL : instantiate i a (Expr.bvar (R := Nat) i) = a := by
          rw [instantiate, if_pos rfl]
        have hskip : ¬ k + 1 ≤ i := Nat.not_le.mpr (Nat.lt_succ_of_le hck)
        have hstay : lift (k + 1) n (Expr.bvar (R := Nat) i) =
            Expr.bvar (R := Nat) i := by
          simp only [lift, hskip, ite_false]
        rw [hL, hstay, instantiate, if_pos rfl]
      · by_cases hlt : c < i
        · have hpos : 0 < i := Nat.lt_of_le_of_lt (Nat.zero_le c) hlt
          have hone : 1 ≤ i := Nat.succ_le_of_lt hpos
          have hsub : (i - 1) + 1 = i := Nat.sub_add_cancel hone
          have hne : i ≠ c := Nat.ne_of_gt hlt
          have hinner : instantiate c a (Expr.bvar (R := Nat) i) =
              Expr.bvar (R := Nat) (i - 1) := by
            rw [instantiate, if_neg hne, if_pos hlt]
          by_cases hhi : k ≤ i - 1
          · have hLL : lift k n (Expr.bvar (R := Nat) (i - 1)) =
                Expr.bvar (R := Nat) ((i - 1) + n) := by
              simp only [lift, hhi, ite_true]
            have hle1 : k + 1 ≤ i := by
              have h := Nat.add_le_add_right hhi 1
              rwa [hsub] at h
            have hLR : lift (k + 1) n (Expr.bvar (R := Nat) i) =
                Expr.bvar (R := Nat) (i + n) := by
              simp only [lift, hle1, ite_true]
            have hne2 : i + n ≠ c :=
              Nat.ne_of_gt (Nat.lt_of_lt_of_le hlt (Nat.le_add_right i n))
            have hlt2 : c < i + n := Nat.lt_of_lt_of_le hlt (Nat.le_add_right i n)
            have hstep :
                instantiate c (lift k n a) (Expr.bvar (R := Nat) (i + n)) =
                  Expr.bvar (R := Nat) (i + n - 1) := by
              rw [instantiate, if_neg hne2, if_pos hlt2]
            have hidx : (i - 1) + n = i + n - 1 := by
              have h1 : n + (i - 1) = n + i - 1 := (Nat.add_sub_assoc hone n).symm
              rw [← Nat.add_comm n (i - 1), ← Nat.add_comm n i]
              exact h1
            rw [hinner, hLL, hLR, hstep]
            exact congrArg (Expr.bvar (R := Nat)) hidx
          · have hLL : lift k n (Expr.bvar (R := Nat) (i - 1)) =
                Expr.bvar (R := Nat) (i - 1) := by
              simp only [lift, hhi, ite_false]
            have hnle1 : ¬ k + 1 ≤ i := by
              intro hle
              have h1 : k + 1 ≤ (i - 1) + 1 := by
                rw [hsub]
                exact hle
              exact hhi (Nat.le_of_succ_le_succ h1)
            have hLR : lift (k + 1) n (Expr.bvar (R := Nat) i) =
                Expr.bvar (R := Nat) i := by
              simp only [lift, hnle1, ite_false]
            have hstep : instantiate c (lift k n a) (Expr.bvar (R := Nat) i) =
                Expr.bvar (R := Nat) (i - 1) := by
              rw [instantiate, if_neg hne, if_pos hlt]
            rw [hinner, hLL, hLR, hstep]
        · have hi : i < c := Nat.lt_of_le_of_ne (Nat.le_of_not_lt hlt) heq
          have hne : i ≠ c := heq
          have hnlt : ¬ c < i := Nat.not_lt.mpr (Nat.le_of_lt hi)
          have hnle : ¬ k ≤ i := Nat.not_le.mpr (Nat.lt_of_lt_of_le hi hck)
          have hnle1 : ¬ k + 1 ≤ i :=
            Nat.not_le.mpr (Nat.lt_of_lt_of_le hi (Nat.le_succ_of_le hck))
          simp only [instantiate, lift, if_neg hne, if_neg hnlt, hnle, hnle1, ite_false]
  | _, _, _, .sort _, _ => rfl
  | _, _, _, .const _ _, _ => rfl
  | _, _, _, .lit _, _ => rfl
  | c, k, a, .app f x, hck => by
      simp only [lift, instantiate, lift_instantiate_above n c k a f hck,
        lift_instantiate_above n c k a x hck]
  | c, k, a, .lam d b, hck => by
      have hck' : c + 1 ≤ k + 1 := Nat.succ_le_succ hck
      have hbody := lift_instantiate_above n (c + 1) (k + 1) (lift 0 1 a) b hck'
      have hperm : lift 0 1 (lift k n a) = lift (1 + k) n (lift 0 1 a) :=
        lift_lift_permute_idx 1 n k 0 (Nat.zero_le k) a
      have hcomm : k + 1 = 1 + k := Nat.add_comm k 1
      have hperm' : lift 0 1 (lift k n a) = lift (k + 1) n (lift 0 1 a) := by
        rw [hcomm]
        exact hperm
      rw [← hperm'] at hbody
      simp only [lift, instantiate]
      rw [lift_instantiate_above n c k a d hck, hbody]
  | c, k, a, .pi d b, hck => by
      have hck' : c + 1 ≤ k + 1 := Nat.succ_le_succ hck
      have hbody := lift_instantiate_above n (c + 1) (k + 1) (lift 0 1 a) b hck'
      have hperm : lift 0 1 (lift k n a) = lift (1 + k) n (lift 0 1 a) :=
        lift_lift_permute_idx 1 n k 0 (Nat.zero_le k) a
      have hcomm : k + 1 = 1 + k := Nat.add_comm k 1
      have hperm' : lift 0 1 (lift k n a) = lift (k + 1) n (lift 0 1 a) := by
        rw [hcomm]
        exact hperm
      rw [← hperm'] at hbody
      simp only [lift, instantiate]
      rw [lift_instantiate_above n c k a d hck, hbody]
  | c, k, a, .letE d val b, hck => by
      have hck' : c + 1 ≤ k + 1 := Nat.succ_le_succ hck
      have hbody := lift_instantiate_above n (c + 1) (k + 1) (lift 0 1 a) b hck'
      have hperm : lift 0 1 (lift k n a) = lift (1 + k) n (lift 0 1 a) :=
        lift_lift_permute_idx 1 n k 0 (Nat.zero_le k) a
      have hcomm : k + 1 = 1 + k := Nat.add_comm k 1
      have hperm' : lift 0 1 (lift k n a) = lift (k + 1) n (lift 0 1 a) := by
        rw [hcomm]
        exact hperm
      rw [← hperm'] at hbody
      simp only [lift, instantiate]
      rw [lift_instantiate_above n c k a d hck, lift_instantiate_above n c k a val hck, hbody]


def liftDecl (c amt : Nat) : LocalDecl → LocalDecl
  | .assumption A => .assumption (lift c amt A)
  | .letBinding A val => .letBinding (lift c amt A) (lift c amt val)

def liftPrefix (amt : Nat) : LCtx → LCtx
  | [] => []
  | d :: Δ => liftDecl Δ.length amt d :: liftPrefix amt Δ

theorem liftPrefix_length (amt : Nat) :
    ∀ Δ : LCtx, (liftPrefix amt Δ).length = Δ.length
  | [] => rfl
  | _ :: Δ => by
      simp only [liftPrefix, List.length_cons, liftPrefix_length amt Δ]

theorem lookupType_liftPrefix (amt : Nat) :
    ∀ (Δ : LCtx) (i : Nat), i < Δ.length →
      lookupType (liftPrefix amt Δ) i =
        (lookupType Δ i).map (lift Δ.length amt)
  | [], _, hi => absurd hi (Nat.not_lt_zero _)
  | d :: Δ, 0, _ => by
      simp only [List.length_cons]
      cases d with
      | assumption a =>
          simp only [liftPrefix, liftDecl, lookupType, List.get?_cons_zero, Option.map]
          have hperm : lift 0 1 (lift Δ.length amt a) =
              lift (1 + Δ.length) amt (lift 0 1 a) :=
            lift_lift_permute_idx 1 amt Δ.length 0 (Nat.zero_le _) a
          have hcomm : 1 + Δ.length = Δ.length + 1 := Nat.add_comm 1 Δ.length
          rw [hperm, hcomm]
      | letBinding a _ =>
          simp only [liftPrefix, liftDecl, lookupType, List.get?_cons_zero, Option.map]
          have hperm : lift 0 1 (lift Δ.length amt a) =
              lift (1 + Δ.length) amt (lift 0 1 a) :=
            lift_lift_permute_idx 1 amt Δ.length 0 (Nat.zero_le _) a
          have hcomm : 1 + Δ.length = Δ.length + 1 := Nat.add_comm 1 Δ.length
          rw [hperm, hcomm]
  | d :: Δ, i + 1, hi => by
      have hi' : i < Δ.length := Nat.lt_of_succ_lt_succ hi
      have ih := lookupType_liftPrefix amt Δ i hi'
      simp only [List.length_cons]
      rw [liftPrefix, lookupType_cons_succ, ih, lookupType_cons_succ]
      cases hlook : lookupType Δ i with
      | none => rfl
      | some A =>
          simp only [hlook, Option.map]
          have hperm : lift 0 1 (lift Δ.length amt A) =
              lift (1 + Δ.length) amt (lift 0 1 A) :=
            lift_lift_permute_idx 1 amt Δ.length 0 (Nat.zero_le _) A
          have hcomm : 1 + Δ.length = Δ.length + 1 := Nat.add_comm 1 Δ.length
          rw [hperm, hcomm]


/- `inferT` ignores the local context on a constant: the member type is
   read from the environment. Not AdeqApp, AdeqLetE, or AdeqConstDelta. -/
variable {E : ResolvedEnv} {n : Nat}

theorem checkT_of_inferT {Γ : LCtx} {e T : Expr Nat}
    (h : inferT E n Γ e = some T) : ∃ d, checkT E n Γ e = some ⟨T, d⟩ := by
  unfold inferT at h
  cases hc : checkT E n Γ e with
  | none => simp [hc] at h
  | some s =>
      cases s with
      | mk T' d =>
          have hT : T' = T := by
            have hmap : some T' = some T := by
              simpa [hc, Option.map] using h
            exact Option.some.inj hmap
          refine ⟨hT ▸ d, ?_⟩
          cases hT
          rfl

def constType (E : ResolvedEnv) (n r : Nat) (ls : List Level) : Option (Expr Nat) :=
  match E.members r with
  | none => none
  | some m =>
      if ls.length = m.arity then
        if levelsBounded n ls = true then some (instantiateLevels ls m.mtype) else none
      else none

theorem members_cases (r : Nat) :
    E.members r = none ∨ ∃ m, E.members r = some m := by
  have H : ∀ x, x = E.members r → E.members r = none ∨ ∃ m, E.members r = some m := by
    intro x hx
    cases x with
    | none => exact Or.inl hx.symm
    | some m => exact Or.inr ⟨m, hx.symm⟩
  exact H (E.members r) rfl

theorem inferT_const_eval (Γ : LCtx) (r : Nat) (ls : List Level) :
    inferT E n Γ (.const r ls) = constType E n r ls := by
  unfold inferT checkT checkConstT constType
  split
  · rename_i m hm
    conv =>
      rhs
      rw [hm]
      dsimp
    by_cases hlen : ls.length = m.arity
    · rw [dif_pos hlen, if_pos hlen]
      by_cases hwf : levelsBounded n ls = true
      · rw [dif_pos hwf, if_pos hwf]
        simp only [Option.map]
      · rw [dif_neg hwf, if_neg hwf]
        simp only [Option.map]
    · rw [dif_neg hlen, if_neg hlen]
      simp only [Option.map]
  · rename_i hm
    conv =>
      rhs
      rw [hm]
      dsimp
    simp [Option.map]

theorem inferT_const_indep (Γ1 Γ2 : LCtx) (r : Nat) (ls : List Level) :
    inferT E n Γ1 (.const r ls) = inferT E n Γ2 (.const r ls) := by
  rw [inferT_const_eval Γ1, inferT_const_eval Γ2]

theorem inferT_const_some {Γ : LCtx} {r : Nat} {ls : List Level} {T : Expr Nat} :
    inferT E n Γ (.const r ls) = some T ↔
      ∃ m, E.members r = some m ∧ ls.length = m.arity ∧
        levelsBounded n ls = true ∧ T = instantiateLevels ls m.mtype := by
  constructor
  · intro h
    rw [inferT_const_eval] at h
    rcases members_cases r with hm | ⟨m, hm⟩
    · unfold constType at h
      rw [hm] at h
      simp at h
    · unfold constType at h
      rw [hm] at h
      dsimp at h
      by_cases hlen : ls.length = m.arity
      · rw [if_pos hlen] at h
        by_cases hwf : levelsBounded n ls = true
        · rw [if_pos hwf] at h
          exact ⟨m, hm, hlen, hwf, (Option.some.inj h).symm⟩
        · rw [if_neg hwf] at h
          simp at h
      · rw [if_neg hlen] at h
        simp at h
  · intro ⟨m, hm, hlen, hwf, hT⟩
    subst hT
    rw [inferT_const_eval]
    unfold constType
    rw [hm]
    dsimp
    rw [if_pos hlen, if_pos hwf]

theorem closedAt_member (hS : EnvSubst E) {r : Nat} {m : CheckedMember}
    (hm : E.members r = some m) (c : Nat) : closedAt c m.mtype = true := by
  apply closedAt_of_instantiateLift m.mtype c 0
  intro w
  rw [lift_zero_idx]
  exact (hS r m hm).1 w c

theorem lift_id_closed0 (e : Expr Nat) (c amt : Nat) (h : closedAt 0 e = true) :
    lift c amt e = e :=
  lift_id_of_closedAt e c amt (closedAt_mono e 0 c (Nat.zero_le c) h)

theorem instantiate_id_closed0 (e : Expr Nat) (k : Nat) (w : Expr Nat)
    (h : closedAt 0 e = true) : instantiate k w e = e :=
  instantiate_eq_of_closedAt e k k w (closedAt_mono e 0 k (Nat.zero_le k) h) (Nat.le_refl k)

theorem inferT_pi_some {Γ : LCtx} {A B T : Expr Nat} :
    inferT E n Γ (.pi A B) = some T ↔
      ∃ u v, inferT E n Γ A = some (.sort u) ∧
        inferT E n (.assumption A :: Γ) B = some (.sort v) ∧
        T = .sort (.imax u v) := by
  constructor
  · intro h
    cases hA : checkT E n Γ A with
    | none =>
        unfold inferT checkT at h
        simp [hA] at h
    | some sA =>
        cases sA with
        | mk TA dA =>
            cases TA with
            | sort u =>
                cases hB : checkT E n (.assumption A :: Γ) B with
                | none =>
                    unfold inferT checkT at h
                    simp [hA, hB] at h
                | some sB =>
                    cases sB with
                    | mk TB dB =>
                        cases TB with
                        | sort v =>
                            unfold inferT checkT at h
                            simp only [hA, hB, Option.map] at h
                            refine ⟨u, v, ?_, ?_, (Option.some.inj h).symm⟩
                            · rw [inferT, hA]; rfl
                            · rw [inferT, hB]; rfl
                        | _ =>
                            unfold inferT checkT at h
                            simp [hA, hB] at h
            | _ =>
                unfold inferT checkT at h
                simp [hA] at h
  · intro ⟨u, v, hA, hB, hT⟩
    subst hT
    obtain ⟨_, hAc⟩ := checkT_of_inferT hA
    obtain ⟨_, hBc⟩ := checkT_of_inferT hB
    unfold inferT checkT
    rw [hAc, hBc]
    rfl

theorem inferT_lam_some {Γ : LCtx} {A b T : Expr Nat} :
    inferT E n Γ (.lam A b) = some T ↔
      ∃ u B, inferT E n Γ A = some (.sort u) ∧
        inferT E n (.assumption A :: Γ) b = some B ∧
        T = .pi A B := by
  constructor
  · intro h
    cases hA : checkT E n Γ A with
    | none =>
        unfold inferT checkT at h
        simp [hA] at h
    | some sA =>
        cases sA with
        | mk TA dA =>
            cases TA with
            | sort u =>
                cases hb : checkT E n (.assumption A :: Γ) b with
                | none =>
                    unfold inferT checkT at h
                    simp [hA, hb] at h
                | some sB =>
                    cases sB with
                    | mk B dB =>
                        unfold inferT checkT at h
                        simp only [hA, hb, Option.map] at h
                        refine ⟨u, B, ?_, ?_, (Option.some.inj h).symm⟩
                        · rw [inferT, hA]; rfl
                        · rw [inferT, hb]; rfl
            | _ =>
                unfold inferT checkT at h
                simp [hA] at h
  · intro ⟨u, B, hA, hb, hT⟩
    subst hT
    obtain ⟨_, hAc⟩ := checkT_of_inferT hA
    obtain ⟨_, hbc⟩ := checkT_of_inferT hb
    unfold inferT checkT
    rw [hAc, hbc]
    rfl

theorem inferT_app_some {Γ : LCtx} {f a T : Expr Nat} :
    inferT E n Γ (.app f a) = some T ↔
      ∃ A B, inferT E n Γ f = some (.pi A B) ∧
        inferT E n Γ a = some A ∧
        T = instantiate0 a B := by
  constructor
  · intro h
    cases hf : checkT E n Γ f with
    | none =>
        unfold inferT checkT at h
        simp [hf] at h
    | some sf =>
        cases sf with
        | mk Tf df =>
            cases Tf with
            | pi A B =>
                cases ha : checkT E n Γ a with
                | none =>
                    unfold inferT checkT at h
                    simp [hf, ha] at h
                | some sa =>
                    cases sa with
                    | mk A' da =>
                        unfold inferT checkT at h
                        simp only [hf, ha] at h
                        by_cases heq : A' = A
                        · rw [dif_pos heq] at h
                          simp only [Option.map] at h
                          refine ⟨A, B, ?_, ?_, (Option.some.inj h).symm⟩
                          · rw [inferT, hf]; rfl
                          · rw [inferT, ha]
                            simp only [Option.map]
                            exact congrArg some heq
                        · rw [dif_neg heq] at h
                          simp at h
            | _ =>
                unfold inferT checkT at h
                simp [hf] at h
  · intro ⟨A, B, hf, ha, hT⟩
    subst hT
    obtain ⟨_, hfc⟩ := checkT_of_inferT hf
    obtain ⟨_, hac⟩ := checkT_of_inferT ha
    unfold inferT checkT
    simp [hfc, hac]

theorem inferT_letE_some {Γ : LCtx} {A v b T : Expr Nat} :
    inferT E n Γ (.letE A v b) = some T ↔
      ∃ u B, inferT E n Γ A = some (.sort u) ∧
        inferT E n Γ v = some A ∧
        inferT E n (.letBinding A v :: Γ) b = some B ∧
        T = instantiate0 v B := by
  constructor
  · intro h
    cases hA : checkT E n Γ A with
    | none =>
        unfold inferT checkT at h
        simp [hA] at h
    | some sA =>
        cases sA with
        | mk TA dA =>
            cases TA with
            | sort u =>
                cases hv : checkT E n Γ v with
                | none =>
                    unfold inferT checkT at h
                    simp [hA, hv] at h
                | some sv =>
                    cases sv with
                    | mk A' dv =>
                        cases hb : checkT E n (.letBinding A v :: Γ) b with
                        | none =>
                            unfold inferT checkT at h
                            simp [hA, hv, hb] at h
                        | some sb =>
                            cases sb with
                            | mk B db =>
                                unfold inferT checkT at h
                                simp only [hA, hv, hb] at h
                                by_cases heq : A' = A
                                · rw [dif_pos heq] at h
                                  simp only [Option.map] at h
                                  refine ⟨u, B, ?_, ?_, ?_, (Option.some.inj h).symm⟩
                                  · rw [inferT, hA]; rfl
                                  · rw [inferT, hv]
                                    simp only [Option.map]
                                    exact congrArg some heq
                                  · rw [inferT, hb]; rfl
                                · rw [dif_neg heq] at h
                                  simp at h
            | _ =>
                unfold inferT checkT at h
                simp [hA] at h
  · intro ⟨u, B, hA, hv, hb, hT⟩
    subst hT
    obtain ⟨_, hAc⟩ := checkT_of_inferT hA
    obtain ⟨_, hvc⟩ := checkT_of_inferT hv
    obtain ⟨_, hbc⟩ := checkT_of_inferT hb
    unfold inferT checkT
    simp [hAc, hvc, hbc]

def litSuccType (t : Nat) : Option (Expr Nat) → Option (Expr Nat) → Option (Expr Nat)
  | some (.pi A B), some A' => if A' = A then some (instantiate0 (natExpand t) B) else none
  | _, _ => none

theorem checkLitT_map_step (t : Nat) (Γ : LCtx) :
    (checkLitT E n Γ (t + 1)).map Sigma.fst =
      litSuccType t ((checkConstT E n Γ 2 []).map Sigma.fst)
        ((checkLitT E n Γ t).map Sigma.fst) := by
  simp only [checkLitT]
  cases hc : checkConstT E n Γ 2 [] with
  | none =>
      cases hl : checkLitT E n Γ t with
      | none => simp [hc, hl, litSuccType, Option.map]
      | some q => simp [hc, hl, litSuccType, Option.map]
  | some p =>
      cases hl : checkLitT E n Γ t with
      | none =>
          cases p with
          | mk Tc dc =>
              cases Tc with
              | pi A B => simp [hc, hl, litSuccType, Option.map]
              | _ => simp [hc, hl, litSuccType, Option.map]
      | some q =>
          cases p with
          | mk Tc dc =>
              cases q with
              | mk A' da =>
                  cases Tc with
                  | pi A B =>
                      by_cases heq : A' = A
                      · simp [hc, hl, heq, litSuccType, Option.map, instantiate0]
                      · simp [hc, hl, heq, litSuccType, Option.map]
                  | _ => simp [hc, hl, litSuccType, Option.map]

theorem inferT_lit_expand (t : Nat) (Γ : LCtx) :
    inferT E n Γ (.lit t) = (checkLitT E n Γ t).map Sigma.fst := by
  simp only [inferT, checkT, Option.map_map]
  rfl

theorem inferT_lit_indep (t : Nat) (Γ1 Γ2 : LCtx) :
    inferT E n Γ1 (.lit t) = inferT E n Γ2 (.lit t) := by
  induction t generalizing Γ1 Γ2 with
  | zero =>
      rw [inferT_lit_expand 0 Γ1, inferT_lit_expand 0 Γ2]
      simpa [checkLitT] using inferT_const_indep Γ1 Γ2 1 []
  | succ t ih =>
      rw [inferT_lit_expand (t + 1) Γ1, inferT_lit_expand (t + 1) Γ2,
        checkLitT_map_step t Γ1, checkLitT_map_step t Γ2]
      have hc : (checkConstT E n Γ1 2 []).map Sigma.fst =
          (checkConstT E n Γ2 2 []).map Sigma.fst := by
        simpa [inferT, checkT] using inferT_const_indep Γ1 Γ2 2 []
      have hl : (checkLitT E n Γ1 t).map Sigma.fst =
          (checkLitT E n Γ2 t).map Sigma.fst := by
        simpa [inferT_lit_expand t] using ih Γ1 Γ2
      rw [hc, hl]

theorem closedAt_natExpand (c : Nat) : ∀ t, closedAt c (natExpand t) = true
  | 0 => rfl
  | t + 1 => by
      simp only [natExpand, litSucc, closedAt, closedAt_natExpand c t, Bool.and_true]

theorem closedAt_inferT_lit (hS : EnvSubst E) (t : Nat) (Γ : LCtx) (T : Expr Nat)
    (h : inferT E n Γ (.lit t) = some T) : closedAt 0 T = true := by
  induction t generalizing T with
  | zero =>
      have h0 : inferT E n Γ (.const 1 []) = some T := by
        simpa [inferT, checkT, checkLitT] using h
      obtain ⟨m, hm, _, _, hT⟩ := inferT_const_some.mp h0
      subst hT
      rw [closedAt_instantiateLevels]
      exact closedAt_member hS hm 0
  | succ t _ih =>
      unfold inferT checkT checkLitT at h
      cases hc : checkConstT E n Γ 2 [] with
      | none => simp [hc] at h
      | some p =>
          cases p with
          | mk Tc dc =>
              cases Tc with
              | pi A B =>
                  cases hl : checkLitT E n Γ t with
                  | none => simp [hc, hl] at h
                  | some q =>
                      cases q with
                      | mk A' da =>
                          by_cases heq : A' = A
                          · simp only [hc, hl] at h
                            rw [dif_pos heq] at h
                            simp only [Option.map] at h
                            have hT : T = instantiate0 (natExpand t) B :=
                              (Option.some.inj h).symm
                            have hconst : inferT E n Γ (.const 2 []) = some (.pi A B) := by
                              simp [inferT, checkT, hc]
                            obtain ⟨m, hm, _, _, hTy⟩ := inferT_const_some.mp hconst
                            have hcl : closedAt 0 (.pi A B) = true := by
                              rw [hTy, closedAt_instantiateLevels]
                              exact closedAt_member hS hm 0
                            simp only [closedAt, Bool.and_eq_true] at hcl
                            rw [hT, instantiate0]
                            exact closedAt_instantiate B 0 (natExpand t) hcl.2
                              (closedAt_natExpand 0 t)
                          · simp [hc, hl, heq] at h
              | _ => simp [hc] at h

/- Inserting a prefix `Φ` under `Δ` lifts a derivable type by `|Φ|` at
   cutoff `|Δ|`. Constants stay put because `EnvClosed` makes member types
   closed. Not AdeqApp, AdeqLetE, or AdeqConstDelta. -/
theorem inferT_weaken (hE : EnvClosed E) :
    ∀ (Δ Φ Γ : LCtx) (e T : Expr Nat),
      inferT E n (Δ ++ Γ) e = some T →
      inferT E n (liftPrefix Φ.length Δ ++ Φ ++ Γ)
        (lift Δ.length Φ.length e) =
        some (lift Δ.length Φ.length T) := by
  have hS : EnvSubst E := envSubst_of_envClosed hE
  intro Δ Φ Γ e T he
  induction e generalizing Δ Φ Γ T with
  | sort l =>
      rw [inferT_sort] at he
      have hT : .sort (.succ l) = T := Option.some.inj he
      subst hT
      simp only [lift, inferT_sort]
  | bvar i =>
      rw [inferT_bvar] at he
      by_cases hik : Δ.length ≤ i
      · have hterm : lift Δ.length Φ.length (Expr.bvar (R := Nat) i) =
            Expr.bvar (R := Nat) (i + Φ.length) := by
          simp only [lift, hik, ite_true]
        have hlen : (liftPrefix Φ.length Δ).length = Δ.length :=
          liftPrefix_length Φ.length Δ
        have hpre : (liftPrefix Φ.length Δ ++ Φ).length = Δ.length + Φ.length := by
          simp only [List.length_append, hlen]
        have hik' : (liftPrefix Φ.length Δ ++ Φ).length ≤ i + Φ.length := by
          rw [hpre]
          exact Nat.add_le_add_right hik Φ.length
        cases hlook : lookupType Γ (i - Δ.length) with
        | none =>
            rw [lookupType_append_ge _ _ _ hik, hlook] at he
            simp at he
        | some A0 =>
            rw [lookupType_append_ge _ _ _ hik, hlook] at he
            simp only [Option.map] at he
            have hT : T = lift 0 Δ.length A0 := (Option.some.inj he).symm
            rw [hterm, inferT_bvar, lookupType_append_ge _ _ _ hik', hpre]
            have hsub : i + Φ.length - (Δ.length + Φ.length) = i - Δ.length :=
              Nat.add_sub_add_right i Φ.length Δ.length
            rw [hsub, hlook, hT]
            simp only [Option.map]
            have hcut := (lift_add_cut 0 Δ.length Φ.length A0).symm
            simp only [Nat.zero_add] at hcut
            exact congrArg some hcut
      · have hi : i < Δ.length := Nat.not_le.mp hik
        have hterm : lift Δ.length Φ.length (Expr.bvar (R := Nat) i) =
            Expr.bvar (R := Nat) i := by
          simp only [lift, hik, ite_false]
        rw [hterm, inferT_bvar]
        rw [lookupType_append_lt _ _ _ hi] at he
        have hlen : (liftPrefix Φ.length Δ).length = Δ.length :=
          liftPrefix_length Φ.length Δ
        have hi' : i < (liftPrefix Φ.length Δ).length := by
          rw [hlen]
          exact hi
        have hmid : i < (liftPrefix Φ.length Δ ++ Φ).length := by
          rw [List.length_append, hlen]
          exact Nat.lt_of_lt_of_le hi (Nat.le_add_right _ _)
        rw [lookupType_append_lt (liftPrefix Φ.length Δ ++ Φ) Γ i hmid]
        rw [lookupType_append_lt (liftPrefix Φ.length Δ) Φ i hi']
        rw [lookupType_liftPrefix Φ.length Δ i hi, he]
        simp only [Option.map]
  | const r ls =>
      simp only [lift]
      obtain ⟨m, hm, _, _, hT⟩ := inferT_const_some.mp he
      subst hT
      have hin := inferT_const_indep (E := E) (n := n) (Δ ++ Γ)
        (liftPrefix Φ.length Δ ++ Φ ++ Γ) r ls
      rw [← hin, he]
      exact congrArg some
        (lift_id_closed0 (instantiateLevels ls m.mtype) Δ.length Φ.length
          (by
            rw [closedAt_instantiateLevels]
            exact closedAt_member hS hm _)).symm
  | lit t =>
      simp only [lift]
      have hcl := closedAt_inferT_lit hS t (Δ ++ Γ) T he
      have hin := inferT_lit_indep (E := E) (n := n) t (Δ ++ Γ)
        (liftPrefix Φ.length Δ ++ Φ ++ Γ)
      rw [← hin, he]
      exact congrArg some
        (lift_id_closed0 T Δ.length Φ.length hcl).symm
  | pi dom body ihd ihb =>
      obtain ⟨u, v, hdom, hbody, hT⟩ := inferT_pi_some.mp he
      subst hT
      have hdom' := ihd Δ Φ Γ (.sort u) hdom
      have hbody' := ihb (.assumption dom :: Δ) Φ Γ (.sort v) hbody
      simp only [lift, List.length_cons] at hdom' hbody'
      rw [liftPrefix, liftDecl] at hbody'
      simp only [lift] at hbody' ⊢
      exact inferT_pi_some.mpr ⟨u, v, hdom', hbody', rfl⟩
  | lam dom body ihd ihb =>
      obtain ⟨u, B, hdom, hbody, hT⟩ := inferT_lam_some.mp he
      subst hT
      have hdom' := ihd Δ Φ Γ (.sort u) hdom
      have hbody' := ihb (.assumption dom :: Δ) Φ Γ B hbody
      simp only [lift, List.length_cons] at hdom' hbody'
      rw [liftPrefix, liftDecl] at hbody'
      simp only [lift] at hbody' ⊢
      exact inferT_lam_some.mpr ⟨u, lift (Δ.length + 1) Φ.length B, hdom', hbody', rfl⟩
  | app f a ihf iha =>
      obtain ⟨dom, cod, hf, ha, hT⟩ := inferT_app_some.mp he
      subst hT
      have hf' := ihf Δ Φ Γ (.pi dom cod) hf
      have ha' := iha Δ Φ Γ dom ha
      simp only [lift] at hf' ha' ⊢
      rw [inferT_app_some.mpr ⟨lift Δ.length Φ.length dom,
        lift (Δ.length + 1) Φ.length cod, hf', ha', rfl⟩]
      exact congrArg some
        (lift_instantiate_above Φ.length 0 Δ.length a cod (Nat.zero_le _)).symm
  | letE dom val body ihd ihv ihb =>
      obtain ⟨u, B, hdom, hval, hbody, hT⟩ := inferT_letE_some.mp he
      subst hT
      have hdom' := ihd Δ Φ Γ (.sort u) hdom
      have hval' := ihv Δ Φ Γ dom hval
      have hbody' := ihb (.letBinding dom val :: Δ) Φ Γ B hbody
      simp only [lift, List.length_cons] at hdom' hval' hbody'
      rw [liftPrefix, liftDecl] at hbody'
      simp only [lift] at hdom' hval' hbody' ⊢
      rw [inferT_letE_some.mpr ⟨u, lift (Δ.length + 1) Φ.length B, hdom', hval',
        hbody', rfl⟩]
      exact congrArg some
        (lift_instantiate_above Φ.length 0 Δ.length val B (Nat.zero_le _)).symm

/- `inferT` commutes with substituting an assumption under a prefix.
   `EnvClosed` supplies `EnvSubst`, so a constant's level instance does not
   move. Not AdeqApp, AdeqLetE, or AdeqConstDelta. -/
theorem inferT_instantiate (hE : EnvClosed E) {Γ : LCtx} (v A : Expr Nat)
    (hv : inferT E n Γ v = some A) :
    ∀ (Δ : LCtx) (e T : Expr Nat),
      inferT E n (Δ ++ (.assumption A :: Γ)) e = some T →
      inferT E n (substPrefix v Δ ++ Γ)
        (instantiate Δ.length (lift 0 Δ.length v) e) =
        some (instantiate Δ.length (lift 0 Δ.length v) T) := by
  have hS : EnvSubst E := envSubst_of_envClosed hE
  intro Δ e T he
  induction e generalizing Δ T with
  | sort l =>
      rw [inferT_sort] at he
      have hT : .sort (.succ l) = T := Option.some.inj he
      subst hT
      simp only [instantiate, inferT_sort]
  | bvar i =>
      rw [inferT_bvar] at he
      by_cases hlt : i < Δ.length
      · have hne : i ≠ Δ.length := Nat.ne_of_lt hlt
        have hnge : ¬ Δ.length < i := Nat.not_lt.mpr (Nat.le_of_lt hlt)
        have hterm : instantiate Δ.length (lift 0 Δ.length v)
              (Expr.bvar (R := Nat) i) = Expr.bvar (R := Nat) i := by
          simp only [instantiate, if_neg hne, if_neg hnge]
        rw [hterm, inferT_bvar]
        rw [lookupType_append_lt _ _ _ hlt] at he
        have hlen : (substPrefix v Δ).length = Δ.length := substPrefix_length v Δ
        have hlt' : i < (substPrefix v Δ).length := by
          rw [hlen]
          exact hlt
        rw [lookupType_append_lt _ _ _ hlt', lookupType_substPrefix v Δ i hlt, he]
        simp only [Option.map]
      · by_cases heq : i = Δ.length
        · subst heq
          have hterm : instantiate Δ.length (lift 0 Δ.length v)
                (Expr.bvar (R := Nat) Δ.length) = lift 0 Δ.length v := by
            rw [instantiate, if_pos rfl]
          have hw := inferT_weaken hE [] (substPrefix v Δ) Γ v A hv
          simp only [liftPrefix, List.nil_append, List.length_nil,
            substPrefix_length v Δ] at hw
          rw [hterm, hw]
          have hle : Δ.length ≤ Δ.length := Nat.le_refl _
          rw [lookupType_append_ge _ _ _ hle, Nat.sub_self] at he
          have hhead : lookupType (.assumption A :: Γ) 0 = some (lift 0 1 A) := by
            simp only [lookupType, List.get?_cons_zero]
          rw [hhead, Option.map] at he
          have hT : T = lift 0 Δ.length (lift 0 1 A) := (Option.some.inj he).symm
          have hT2 : T = lift 0 (Δ.length + 1) A := by
            rw [hT, lift_add_zero]
            exact congrArg (fun z => lift 0 z A) (Nat.add_comm 1 Δ.length)
          have hinst := instantiate_high_lift 0 Δ.length (Δ.length + 1)
            (lift 0 Δ.length v) A (Nat.lt_succ_self _)
          simp only [Nat.zero_add, Nat.add_sub_cancel] at hinst
          rw [hT2]
          exact congrArg some hinst.symm
        · have hgt : Δ.length < i :=
            Nat.lt_of_le_of_ne (Nat.le_of_not_lt hlt) (Ne.symm heq)
          have hpos : 0 < i := Nat.lt_of_le_of_lt (Nat.zero_le _) hgt
          have hone : 1 ≤ i := Nat.succ_le_of_lt hpos
          have hsub : (i - 1) + 1 = i := Nat.sub_add_cancel hone
          have hne : i ≠ Δ.length := heq
          have hterm : instantiate Δ.length (lift 0 Δ.length v)
                (Expr.bvar (R := Nat) i) = Expr.bvar (R := Nat) (i - 1) := by
            rw [instantiate, if_neg hne, if_pos hgt]
          rw [hterm, inferT_bvar]
          have hge : Δ.length ≤ i := Nat.le_of_lt hgt
          rw [lookupType_append_ge _ _ _ hge] at he
          have hge1 : 1 ≤ i - Δ.length :=
            Nat.succ_le_of_lt (Nat.sub_pos_of_lt hgt)
          have hidx : (i - Δ.length - 1) + 1 = i - Δ.length :=
            Nat.sub_add_cancel hge1
          have hcons : lookupType (.assumption A :: Γ) (i - Δ.length) =
              (lookupType Γ (i - Δ.length - 1)).map (lift 0 1) := by
            simpa [hidx] using
              lookupType_cons_succ (.assumption A) Γ (i - Δ.length - 1)
          rw [hcons] at he
          have hle' : Δ.length ≤ i - 1 := by
            have h1 : Δ.length + 1 ≤ i := Nat.succ_le_of_lt hgt
            rw [← hsub] at h1
            exact Nat.le_of_succ_le_succ h1
          have hlen : (substPrefix v Δ).length = Δ.length := substPrefix_length v Δ
          have hle'' : (substPrefix v Δ).length ≤ i - 1 := by
            rw [hlen]
            exact hle'
          rw [lookupType_append_ge _ _ _ hle'', hlen]
          have hidx' : (i - 1) - Δ.length = i - Δ.length - 1 := by
            rw [Nat.sub_sub, Nat.sub_sub]
            exact congrArg (fun z => i - z) (Nat.add_comm 1 Δ.length)
          rw [hidx']
          cases hlook : lookupType Γ (i - Δ.length - 1) with
          | none =>
              simp only [hlook, Option.map] at he
              simp at he
          | some A0 =>
              simp only [hlook, Option.map] at he
              have hT : T = lift 0 Δ.length (lift 0 1 A0) := (Option.some.inj he).symm
              have hT2 : T = lift 0 (Δ.length + 1) A0 := by
                rw [hT, lift_add_zero]
                exact congrArg (fun z => lift 0 z A0) (Nat.add_comm 1 Δ.length)
              have hinst := instantiate_high_lift 0 Δ.length (Δ.length + 1)
                (lift 0 Δ.length v) A0 (Nat.lt_succ_self _)
              simp only [Nat.zero_add, Nat.add_sub_cancel] at hinst
              simp only [Option.map]
              rw [hT2]
              exact congrArg some hinst.symm
  | const r ls =>
      simp only [instantiate]
      obtain ⟨m, hm, _, _, hT⟩ := inferT_const_some.mp he
      subst hT
      have hin := inferT_const_indep (E := E) (n := n)
        (Δ ++ (.assumption A :: Γ)) (substPrefix v Δ ++ Γ) r ls
      rw [← hin, he]
      exact congrArg some
        (instantiate_id_closed0 (instantiateLevels ls m.mtype) Δ.length
          (lift 0 Δ.length v)
          (by
            rw [closedAt_instantiateLevels]
            exact closedAt_member hS hm _)).symm
  | lit t =>
      simp only [instantiate]
      have hcl := closedAt_inferT_lit hS t (Δ ++ (.assumption A :: Γ)) T he
      have hin := inferT_lit_indep (E := E) (n := n) t
        (Δ ++ (.assumption A :: Γ)) (substPrefix v Δ ++ Γ)
      rw [← hin, he]
      exact congrArg some
        (instantiate_id_closed0 T Δ.length (lift 0 Δ.length v)
          hcl).symm
  | pi dom body ihd ihb =>
      obtain ⟨u, vl, hdom, hbody, hT⟩ := inferT_pi_some.mp he
      subst hT
      have hdom' := ihd Δ (.sort u) hdom
      have hbody' := ihb (.assumption dom :: Δ) (.sort vl) hbody
      have hw : lift 0 1 (lift 0 Δ.length v) = lift 0 (Δ.length + 1) v :=
        lift_add_zero 1 Δ.length v
      simp only [instantiate, List.length_cons] at hdom' hbody'
      rw [← hw] at hbody'
      rw [substPrefix, substDecl] at hbody'
      simp only [instantiate] at hbody' ⊢
      exact inferT_pi_some.mpr ⟨u, vl, hdom', hbody', rfl⟩
  | lam dom body ihd ihb =>
      obtain ⟨u, B, hdom, hbody, hT⟩ := inferT_lam_some.mp he
      subst hT
      have hdom' := ihd Δ (.sort u) hdom
      have hbody' := ihb (.assumption dom :: Δ) B hbody
      have hw : lift 0 1 (lift 0 Δ.length v) = lift 0 (Δ.length + 1) v :=
        lift_add_zero 1 Δ.length v
      simp only [instantiate, List.length_cons] at hdom' hbody'
      rw [← hw] at hbody'
      rw [substPrefix, substDecl] at hbody'
      simp only [instantiate] at hbody' ⊢
      exact inferT_lam_some.mpr
        ⟨u, instantiate (Δ.length + 1) (lift 0 1 (lift 0 Δ.length v)) B,
          hdom', hbody', rfl⟩
  | app f a ihf iha =>
      obtain ⟨dom, cod, hf, ha, hT⟩ := inferT_app_some.mp he
      subst hT
      have hf' := ihf Δ (.pi dom cod) hf
      have ha' := iha Δ dom ha
      simp only [instantiate] at hf' ha' ⊢
      rw [inferT_app_some.mpr ⟨instantiate Δ.length (lift 0 Δ.length v) dom,
        instantiate (Δ.length + 1) (lift 0 1 (lift 0 Δ.length v)) cod, hf', ha', rfl⟩]
      exact congrArg some
        (instantiate_dist_zero Δ.length (lift 0 Δ.length v) a cod).symm
  | letE dom val body ihd ihv ihb =>
      obtain ⟨u, B, hdom, hval, hbody, hT⟩ := inferT_letE_some.mp he
      subst hT
      have hdom' := ihd Δ (.sort u) hdom
      have hval' := ihv Δ dom hval
      have hbody' := ihb (.letBinding dom val :: Δ) B hbody
      have hw : lift 0 1 (lift 0 Δ.length v) = lift 0 (Δ.length + 1) v :=
        lift_add_zero 1 Δ.length v
      simp only [instantiate, List.length_cons] at hdom' hval' hbody'
      rw [← hw] at hbody'
      rw [substPrefix, substDecl] at hbody'
      simp only [instantiate] at hdom' hval' hbody' ⊢
      rw [inferT_letE_some.mpr ⟨u,
        instantiate (Δ.length + 1) (lift 0 1 (lift 0 Δ.length v)) B,
        hdom', hval', hbody', rfl⟩]
      exact congrArg some
        (instantiate_dist_zero Δ.length (lift 0 Δ.length v) val B).symm

/- A lift of amount zero is the identity at every cutoff. Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem lift_zero_amount :
    ∀ (e : Expr Nat) (c : Nat), lift c 0 e = e
  | .bvar i, c => by
      simp only [lift]
      by_cases h : c ≤ i
      · rw [if_pos h]
        exact congrArg (Expr.bvar (R := Nat)) (Nat.add_zero i)
      · rw [if_neg h]
  | .sort _, _ => rfl
  | .const _ _, _ => rfl
  | .lit _, _ => rfl
  | .app f x, c => by
      simp only [lift, lift_zero_amount f c, lift_zero_amount x c]
  | .lam a b, c => by
      simp only [lift, lift_zero_amount a c, lift_zero_amount b (c + 1)]
  | .pi a b, c => by
      simp only [lift, lift_zero_amount a c, lift_zero_amount b (c + 1)]
  | .letE a v b, c => by
      simp only [lift, lift_zero_amount a c, lift_zero_amount v c,
        lift_zero_amount b (c + 1)]

/- One β at the syntactic checker, in the empty context. The binder type is
   the argument's inferred type. `EnvClosed` is the hypothesis
   `inferT_instantiate` reads. Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem inferT_beta (hE : EnvClosed E) {A B a b : Expr Nat} {u : Level}
    (hdom : inferT E n [] A = some (.sort u))
    (hb : inferT E n (.assumption A :: []) b = some B)
    (ha : inferT E n [] a = some A) :
    inferT E n [] (.app (.lam A b) a) = some (instantiate0 a B) ∧
      inferT E n [] (instantiate0 a b) = some (instantiate0 a B) := by
  refine ⟨?_, ?_⟩
  · exact inferT_app_some.mpr
      ⟨A, B, inferT_lam_some.mpr ⟨u, B, hdom, hb, rfl⟩, ha, rfl⟩
  · have h := inferT_instantiate hE a A ha [] b B hb
    simp only [List.nil_append, List.length_nil, substPrefix] at h
    rw [lift_zero_amount a 0] at h
    simpa [instantiate0] using h

/- The relevance test reads only the inferred type. Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem irrelevant_of_same_type {Γ : LCtx} {e1 e2 T : Expr Nat}
    (h1 : inferT E n Γ e1 = some T) (h2 : inferT E n Γ e2 = some T) :
    irrelevant E n Γ e1 = irrelevant E n Γ e2 := by
  simp only [irrelevant, h1, h2]

/- A relevant β and its reduct are relevant together, because both infer
   to `instantiate0 a B`. Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem irrelevant_beta (hE : EnvClosed E) {A B a b : Expr Nat} {u : Level}
    (hdom : inferT E n [] A = some (.sort u))
    (hb : inferT E n (.assumption A :: []) b = some B)
    (ha : inferT E n [] a = some A) :
    irrelevant E n [] (.app (.lam A b) a) =
      irrelevant E n [] (instantiate0 a b) := by
  obtain ⟨happ, hr⟩ := inferT_beta hE hdom hb ha
  exact irrelevant_of_same_type happ hr

/- `lookupType` reads only the binder's type from a local declaration,
   so a `letBinding` and an `assumption` of the same type agree at
   every index. Not AdeqLetE. -/
theorem lookupType_let_eq_assumption (A v : Expr Nat) (Γ : LCtx) (i : Nat) :
    lookupType (.letBinding A v :: Γ) i = lookupType (.assumption A :: Γ) i := by
  cases i with
  | zero => rfl
  | succ j =>
      rw [lookupType_cons_succ, lookupType_cons_succ]

theorem lookupType_cons_ext (d : LocalDecl) {Γ1 Γ2 : LCtx}
    (h : ∀ i, lookupType Γ1 i = lookupType Γ2 i) (i : Nat) :
    lookupType (d :: Γ1) i = lookupType (d :: Γ2) i := by
  cases i with
  | zero => rfl
  | succ j =>
      rw [lookupType_cons_succ, lookupType_cons_succ, h j]

/- `inferT` depends on the local context only through `lookupType`.
   Not AdeqLetE. -/
theorem inferT_ctx_eq :
    ∀ (e : Expr Nat) {Γ1 Γ2 : LCtx},
      (∀ i, lookupType Γ1 i = lookupType Γ2 i) →
      inferT E n Γ1 e = inferT E n Γ2 e
  | .sort l, _, _, _ => by rw [inferT_sort, inferT_sort]
  | .bvar i, _, _, h => by rw [inferT_bvar, inferT_bvar, h i]
  | .const r ls, Γ1, Γ2, _ => inferT_const_indep Γ1 Γ2 r ls
  | .lit t, Γ1, Γ2, _ => inferT_lit_indep t Γ1 Γ2
  | .app f a, Γ1, Γ2, h => by
      have ihf := inferT_ctx_eq f h
      have iha := inferT_ctx_eq a h
      cases h2 : inferT E n Γ2 (.app f a) with
      | none =>
          cases h1 : inferT E n Γ1 (.app f a) with
          | none => rfl
          | some T =>
              obtain ⟨A, B, hf, ha, hT⟩ := inferT_app_some.mp h1
              rw [ihf] at hf
              rw [iha] at ha
              have h2' := inferT_app_some.mpr ⟨A, B, hf, ha, hT⟩
              rw [h2] at h2'
              exact Option.noConfusion h2'
      | some T =>
          obtain ⟨A, B, hf, ha, hT⟩ := inferT_app_some.mp h2
          rw [← ihf] at hf
          rw [← iha] at ha
          exact inferT_app_some.mpr ⟨A, B, hf, ha, hT⟩
  | .pi A B, Γ1, Γ2, h => by
      have ihA := inferT_ctx_eq A h
      have ihB := inferT_ctx_eq B (lookupType_cons_ext (.assumption A) h)
      cases h2 : inferT E n Γ2 (.pi A B) with
      | none =>
          cases h1 : inferT E n Γ1 (.pi A B) with
          | none => rfl
          | some T =>
              obtain ⟨u, v, hA, hB, hT⟩ := inferT_pi_some.mp h1
              rw [ihA] at hA
              rw [ihB] at hB
              have h2' := inferT_pi_some.mpr ⟨u, v, hA, hB, hT⟩
              rw [h2] at h2'
              exact Option.noConfusion h2'
      | some T =>
          obtain ⟨u, v, hA, hB, hT⟩ := inferT_pi_some.mp h2
          rw [← ihA] at hA
          rw [← ihB] at hB
          exact inferT_pi_some.mpr ⟨u, v, hA, hB, hT⟩
  | .lam A b, Γ1, Γ2, h => by
      have ihA := inferT_ctx_eq A h
      have ihb := inferT_ctx_eq b (lookupType_cons_ext (.assumption A) h)
      cases h2 : inferT E n Γ2 (.lam A b) with
      | none =>
          cases h1 : inferT E n Γ1 (.lam A b) with
          | none => rfl
          | some T =>
              obtain ⟨u, B, hA, hb, hT⟩ := inferT_lam_some.mp h1
              rw [ihA] at hA
              rw [ihb] at hb
              have h2' := inferT_lam_some.mpr ⟨u, B, hA, hb, hT⟩
              rw [h2] at h2'
              exact Option.noConfusion h2'
      | some T =>
          obtain ⟨u, B, hA, hb, hT⟩ := inferT_lam_some.mp h2
          rw [← ihA] at hA
          rw [← ihb] at hb
          exact inferT_lam_some.mpr ⟨u, B, hA, hb, hT⟩
  | .letE A v b, Γ1, Γ2, h => by
      have ihA := inferT_ctx_eq A h
      have ihv := inferT_ctx_eq v h
      have ihb := inferT_ctx_eq b (lookupType_cons_ext (.letBinding A v) h)
      cases h2 : inferT E n Γ2 (.letE A v b) with
      | none =>
          cases h1 : inferT E n Γ1 (.letE A v b) with
          | none => rfl
          | some T =>
              obtain ⟨u, B, hA, hv, hb, hT⟩ := inferT_letE_some.mp h1
              rw [ihA] at hA
              rw [ihv] at hv
              rw [ihb] at hb
              have h2' := inferT_letE_some.mpr ⟨u, B, hA, hv, hb, hT⟩
              rw [h2] at h2'
              exact Option.noConfusion h2'
      | some T =>
          obtain ⟨u, B, hA, hv, hb, hT⟩ := inferT_letE_some.mp h2
          rw [← ihA] at hA
          rw [← ihv] at hv
          rw [← ihb] at hb
          exact inferT_letE_some.mpr ⟨u, B, hA, hv, hb, hT⟩

/- One ζ at the syntactic checker, in the empty context. Not AdeqLetE. -/
theorem inferT_zeta (hE : EnvClosed E) {A B v b : Expr Nat} {u : Level}
    (hdom : inferT E n [] A = some (.sort u))
    (hv : inferT E n [] v = some A)
    (hb : inferT E n (.letBinding A v :: []) b = some B) :
    inferT E n [] (.letE A v b) = some (instantiate0 v B) ∧
      inferT E n [] (instantiate0 v b) = some (instantiate0 v B) := by
  refine ⟨inferT_letE_some.mpr ⟨u, B, hdom, hv, hb, rfl⟩, ?_⟩
  have hb' : inferT E n (.assumption A :: []) b = some B := by
    rw [← inferT_ctx_eq (E := E) (n := n) b (lookupType_let_eq_assumption A v [])]
    exact hb
  exact (inferT_beta hE hdom hb' hv).2

/- A relevant ζ and its reduct are relevant together. Not AdeqLetE. -/
theorem irrelevant_zeta (hE : EnvClosed E) {A B v b : Expr Nat} {u : Level}
    (hdom : inferT E n [] A = some (.sort u))
    (hv : inferT E n [] v = some A)
    (hb : inferT E n (.letBinding A v :: []) b = some B) :
    irrelevant E n [] (.letE A v b) =
      irrelevant E n [] (instantiate0 v b) := by
  obtain ⟨hlet, hr⟩ := inferT_zeta hE hdom hv hb
  exact irrelevant_of_same_type hlet hr

/-! ### Closed ill-typed flip: `EnvClosed` alone does not make the three open
    adequacy statements hold

`closedFlipEnv` has no open member (`closedFlipEnv_closed`), and no
transparent member (`cfBodies`). Member 6 (`cfK`, constructor) has the
closed, ill-typed declared type `Π (x : N), Fam ((λ (_ : P x), _) y)` where
`y : P ((λ z : N, z) 0)` (`closedFlipEnv_member6_illTyped`).
At `cfApp = cfK ((λ z : N, z) 0)` and `cfLet = let x : N := (λ z : N, z) 0 in cfK x`,
instantiating the codomain with the unreduced argument matches `y`'s declared
type syntactically, so `inferT` types the codomain at `Sort 0` and marks the
redex irrelevant (`□`, lowered to `refuse`). Normalizing reduces the argument
to `lit 0`; the instantiated codomain now has a domain mismatch (`P 0 ≠ P cfRedex`),
so `inferT` of the value's type is `none` while `inferT` of the value itself is
`some cfValTy`, making the normal form `cfVal = cfK 0` relevant.
`closedFlipDeltaEnv` adds member 7 (`cfDelta : cfTy := cfApp`), which meets
`BodiesTyped` by `hasTyT_of_inferT` and refutes the `EnvClosed`-only
`AdeqConstDelta`. -/

def cfN : Expr Nat := .const 0 []
def cfRedex : Expr Nat := .app (.lam cfN (.bvar 0)) (.lit 0)
def cfP : Expr Nat := .const 3 []
def cfY : Expr Nat := .const 4 []
def cfFam : Expr Nat := .const 5 []
def cfK : Expr Nat := .const 6 []
def cfKCod : Expr Nat :=
  .app cfFam (.app (.lam (.app cfP (.bvar 0)) (.bvar 0)) cfY)
def cfApp : Expr Nat := .app cfK cfRedex
def cfLet : Expr Nat := .letE cfN cfRedex (.app cfK (.bvar 0))
def cfVal : Expr Nat := .app cfK (.lit 0)
def cfTy : Expr Nat := instantiate0 cfRedex cfKCod
def cfValTy : Expr Nat := instantiate0 (.lit 0) cfKCod
def cfDelta : Expr Nat := .const 7 []

def closedFlipEnv : ResolvedEnv where
  members := fun r =>
    match r with
    | 0 => some ⟨.inductiveM, 0, .sort (.succ .zero), none⟩
    | 1 => some ⟨.constructorM, 0, cfN, none⟩
    | 2 => some ⟨.constructorM, 0, .pi cfN cfN, none⟩
    | 3 => some ⟨.axiomM, 0, .pi cfN (.sort .zero), none⟩
    | 4 => some ⟨.axiomM, 0, .app cfP cfRedex, none⟩
    | 5 => some ⟨.inductiveM, 0, .pi (.app cfP cfRedex) (.sort .zero), none⟩
    | 6 => some ⟨.constructorM, 0, .pi cfN cfKCod, none⟩
    | _ => none

def closedFlipDeltaEnv : ResolvedEnv where
  members := fun r =>
    match r with
    | 0 => some ⟨.inductiveM, 0, .sort (.succ .zero), none⟩
    | 1 => some ⟨.constructorM, 0, cfN, none⟩
    | 2 => some ⟨.constructorM, 0, .pi cfN cfN, none⟩
    | 3 => some ⟨.axiomM, 0, .pi cfN (.sort .zero), none⟩
    | 4 => some ⟨.axiomM, 0, .app cfP cfRedex, none⟩
    | 5 => some ⟨.inductiveM, 0, .pi (.app cfP cfRedex) (.sort .zero), none⟩
    | 6 => some ⟨.constructorM, 0, .pi cfN cfKCod, none⟩
    | 7 => some ⟨.definitionM, 0, cfTy, some cfApp⟩
    | _ => none

theorem closedFlipEnv_closed : EnvClosed closedFlipEnv := by
  intro r m hm
  match r, hm with
  | 0, hm => cases hm; exact ctl_member_closed _ rfl (fun _ hb => nomatch hb)
  | 1, hm => cases hm; exact ctl_member_closed _ rfl (fun _ hb => nomatch hb)
  | 2, hm => cases hm; exact ctl_member_closed _ rfl (fun _ hb => nomatch hb)
  | 3, hm => cases hm; exact ctl_member_closed _ rfl (fun _ hb => nomatch hb)
  | 4, hm => cases hm; exact ctl_member_closed _ rfl (fun _ hb => nomatch hb)
  | 5, hm => cases hm; exact ctl_member_closed _ rfl (fun _ hb => nomatch hb)
  | 6, hm => cases hm; exact ctl_member_closed _ rfl (fun _ hb => nomatch hb)
  | _ + 7, hm => exact Option.noConfusion hm

theorem closedFlipDeltaEnv_closed : EnvClosed closedFlipDeltaEnv := by
  intro r m hm
  match r, hm with
  | 0, hm => cases hm; exact ctl_member_closed _ rfl (fun _ hb => nomatch hb)
  | 1, hm => cases hm; exact ctl_member_closed _ rfl (fun _ hb => nomatch hb)
  | 2, hm => cases hm; exact ctl_member_closed _ rfl (fun _ hb => nomatch hb)
  | 3, hm => cases hm; exact ctl_member_closed _ rfl (fun _ hb => nomatch hb)
  | 4, hm => cases hm; exact ctl_member_closed _ rfl (fun _ hb => nomatch hb)
  | 5, hm => cases hm; exact ctl_member_closed _ rfl (fun _ hb => nomatch hb)
  | 6, hm => cases hm; exact ctl_member_closed _ rfl (fun _ hb => nomatch hb)
  | 7, hm =>
      cases hm
      exact ctl_member_closed _ rfl (fun b hb => by
        cases hb
        rfl)
  | _ + 8, hm => exact Option.noConfusion hm

theorem closedFlipEnv_member6_illTyped :
    inferT closedFlipEnv 0 [] (.pi cfN cfKCod) = none := rfl

theorem closedFlipDeltaEnv_member6_illTyped :
    inferT closedFlipDeltaEnv 0 [] (.pi cfN cfKCod) = none := rfl

theorem cfBodies (n : Nat) : BodiesTyped closedFlipEnv n := by
  intro r m b _ hm _ hb _ _
  match r, hm with
  | 0, hm => cases hm; cases hb
  | 1, hm => cases hm; cases hb
  | 2, hm => cases hm; cases hb
  | 3, hm => cases hm; cases hb
  | 4, hm => cases hm; cases hb
  | 5, hm => cases hm; cases hb
  | 6, hm => cases hm; cases hb
  | _ + 7, hm => exact Option.noConfusion hm

theorem cfData : DataTy closedFlipEnv cfTy :=
  ⟨5, [], [.app (.lam (.app cfP cfRedex) (.bvar 0)) cfY],
    ⟨.inductiveM, 0, .pi (.app cfP cfRedex) (.sort .zero), none⟩, rfl, rfl, rfl⟩

theorem cfDeltaData : DataTy closedFlipDeltaEnv cfTy :=
  ⟨5, [], [.app (.lam (.app cfP cfRedex) (.bvar 0)) cfY],
    ⟨.inductiveM, 0, .pi (.app cfP cfRedex) (.sort .zero), none⟩, rfl, rfl, rfl⟩

theorem cfApp_norm : norm closedFlipEnv 4 cfApp = some cfVal := rfl
theorem cfLet_norm : norm closedFlipEnv 4 cfLet = some cfVal := rfl
theorem cfDelta_norm : norm closedFlipDeltaEnv 5 cfDelta = some cfVal := rfl
theorem cfDelta_tb : transparentBody closedFlipDeltaEnv 7 [] = some cfApp := rfl
theorem cfVal_scm : scmValOf closedFlipEnv 2 cfVal = some (.inj 6 (.list [.int 0])) := rfl
theorem cfVal_scm_delta :
    scmValOf closedFlipDeltaEnv 2 cfVal = some (.inj 6 (.list [.int 0])) := rfl
theorem cfVal_spine : relevantSpine closedFlipEnv 0 2 cfVal = true := rfl
theorem cfVal_spine_delta : relevantSpine closedFlipDeltaEnv 0 2 cfVal = true := rfl

theorem cfTy_infer : inferT closedFlipEnv 0 [] cfTy = some (.sort .zero) := rfl
theorem cfTy_infer_delta :
    inferT closedFlipDeltaEnv 0 [] cfTy = some (.sort .zero) := rfl
theorem cfVal_ty : inferT closedFlipEnv 0 [] cfVal = some cfValTy := rfl
theorem cfVal_ty_delta :
    inferT closedFlipDeltaEnv 0 [] cfVal = some cfValTy := rfl
theorem cfValTy_infer : inferT closedFlipEnv 0 [] cfValTy = none := rfl
theorem cfValTy_infer_delta :
    inferT closedFlipDeltaEnv 0 [] cfValTy = none := rfl
theorem cfVal_vinfer : (inferT closedFlipEnv 0 [] cfVal).isSome = true := by
  rw [cfVal_ty]
  rfl
theorem cfVal_vinfer_delta :
    (inferT closedFlipDeltaEnv 0 [] cfVal).isSome = true := by
  rw [cfVal_ty_delta]
  rfl
theorem cfVal_rel : irrelevant closedFlipEnv 0 [] cfVal = false := rfl
theorem cfVal_rel_delta : irrelevant closedFlipDeltaEnv 0 [] cfVal = false := rfl
theorem cfFits : valFits 2 (sumL 7 .i64) (.inj 6 (.list [.int 0])) = true := by decide

theorem cfApp_infer : inferT closedFlipEnv 0 [] cfApp = some cfTy := rfl
theorem cfLet_infer : inferT closedFlipEnv 0 [] cfLet = some cfTy := rfl
theorem cfDelta_infer : inferT closedFlipDeltaEnv 0 [] cfDelta = some cfTy := rfl
theorem cfApp_body_infer : inferT closedFlipDeltaEnv 0 [] cfApp = some cfTy := rfl

theorem cfApp_irr : irrelevant closedFlipEnv 0 [] cfApp = true :=
  irrelevant_data_tt closedFlipEnv 0 cfApp cfTy (.sort .zero)
    cfApp_infer cfData cfTy_infer rfl

theorem cfLet_irr : irrelevant closedFlipEnv 0 [] cfLet = true :=
  irrelevant_data_tt closedFlipEnv 0 cfLet cfTy (.sort .zero)
    cfLet_infer cfData cfTy_infer rfl

theorem cfDelta_irr : irrelevant closedFlipDeltaEnv 0 [] cfDelta = true :=
  irrelevant_data_tt closedFlipDeltaEnv 0 cfDelta cfTy (.sort .zero)
    cfDelta_infer cfDeltaData cfTy_infer_delta rfl

theorem cfDeltaBodies : BodiesTyped closedFlipDeltaEnv 0 := by
  intro r m b ls hm _ hb hlen _
  match r, hm with
  | 0, hm => cases hm; cases hb
  | 1, hm => cases hm; cases hb
  | 2, hm => cases hm; cases hb
  | 3, hm => cases hm; cases hb
  | 4, hm => cases hm; cases hb
  | 5, hm => cases hm; cases hb
  | 6, hm => cases hm; cases hb
  | 7, hm =>
      cases hm
      cases hb
      cases ls with
      | nil => exact ⟨hasTyT_of_inferT cfApp_body_infer⟩
      | cons _ _ => exact Nat.noConfusion hlen
  | _ + 8, hm => exact Option.noConfusion hm

theorem cfApp_er : Erasable closedFlipEnv 0 cfApp :=
  ⟨1, .box, erase_box_of_irrelevant closedFlipEnv 0 0 [] cfApp cfApp_irr
      (fun k => app_ne_lit cfK cfRedex k)⟩

theorem cfLet_er : Erasable closedFlipEnv 0 cfLet :=
  ⟨1, .box, erase_box_of_irrelevant closedFlipEnv 0 0 [] cfLet cfLet_irr
      (fun k => letE_ne_lit cfN cfRedex (.app cfK (.bvar 0)) k)⟩

theorem cfDelta_er : Erasable closedFlipDeltaEnv 0 cfDelta :=
  ⟨1, .box, erase_box_of_irrelevant closedFlipDeltaEnv 0 0 [] cfDelta cfDelta_irr
      (fun k => const_ne_lit 7 k [])⟩

def AdeqAppClosed {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) : Prop :=
  ∀ E n f a, EnvClosed E → GoodLoose progs E n (.app f a)

def AdeqLetEClosed {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) : Prop :=
  ∀ E n A v b, EnvClosed E → GoodLoose progs E n (.letE A v b)

def AdeqConstDeltaClosed {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) : Prop :=
  ∀ E n r ls b, EnvClosed E →
    transparentBody E r ls = some b → GoodLoose progs E n (.const r ls)

theorem not_adeqAppClosed {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) :
    ¬ AdeqAppClosed progs := by
  intro h
  obtain ⟨F₀, hF⟩ := h closedFlipEnv 0 cfK cfRedex closedFlipEnv_closed 4 2 cfTy cfVal
      (sumL 7 .i64) (.inj 6 (.list [.int 0])) (cfBodies 0) cfApp_infer cfData
      cfApp_norm cfVal_scm cfVal_spine cfVal_rel cfFits
      cfVal_vinfer cfApp_er
  obtain ⟨lf, he⟩ := hF F₀ (Nat.le_refl _)
  exact eval_irrelevant_ne progs closedFlipEnv 0 (sumL 7 .i64) cfApp _
    cfApp_irr (fun k => app_ne_lit cfK cfRedex k) F₀ lf he

theorem not_adeqLetEClosed {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) :
    ¬ AdeqLetEClosed progs := by
  intro h
  obtain ⟨F₀, hF⟩ := h closedFlipEnv 0 cfN cfRedex (.app cfK (.bvar 0))
      closedFlipEnv_closed 4 2 cfTy cfVal (sumL 7 .i64) (.inj 6 (.list [.int 0]))
      (cfBodies 0) cfLet_infer cfData cfLet_norm cfVal_scm cfVal_spine cfVal_rel
      cfFits cfVal_vinfer cfLet_er
  obtain ⟨lf, he⟩ := hF F₀ (Nat.le_refl _)
  exact eval_irrelevant_ne progs closedFlipEnv 0 (sumL 7 .i64) cfLet _
    cfLet_irr (fun k => letE_ne_lit cfN cfRedex (.app cfK (.bvar 0)) k) F₀ lf he

theorem not_adeqConstDeltaClosed {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) :
    ¬ AdeqConstDeltaClosed progs := by
  intro h
  obtain ⟨F₀, hF⟩ := h closedFlipDeltaEnv 0 7 [] cfApp closedFlipDeltaEnv_closed
      cfDelta_tb 5 2 cfTy cfVal (sumL 7 .i64) (.inj 6 (.list [.int 0]))
      cfDeltaBodies cfDelta_infer cfDeltaData cfDelta_norm cfVal_scm_delta
      cfVal_spine_delta cfVal_rel_delta cfFits cfVal_vinfer_delta cfDelta_er
  obtain ⟨lf, he⟩ := hF F₀ (Nat.le_refl _)
  exact eval_irrelevant_ne progs closedFlipDeltaEnv 0 (sumL 7 .i64) cfDelta _
    cfDelta_irr (fun k => const_ne_lit 7 k []) F₀ lf he

/- `ctlEnv` meets `EnvWf`, discharged by `ctlEnv_closed` and the certified
   syntactic checker `inferT` (`hasTyT_of_inferT`). -/
private theorem ctl_member_wf (m : CheckedMember) (u : Level)
    (ht : inferT ctlEnv m.arity [] m.mtype = some (.sort u))
    (hb : ∀ b, m.body = some b → inferT ctlEnv m.arity [] b = some m.mtype) :
    (∃ u, Nonempty (HasTyT ctlEnv m.arity [] m.mtype (.sort u))) ∧
      (∀ b, m.body = some b → Nonempty (HasTyT ctlEnv m.arity [] b m.mtype)) :=
  ⟨⟨u, ⟨hasTyT_of_inferT ht⟩⟩,
   fun b hsome => ⟨hasTyT_of_inferT (hb b hsome)⟩⟩

theorem ctlEnv_wf : EnvWf ctlEnv := by
  refine ⟨ctlEnv_closed, ?_⟩
  intro r m hm
  match r, hm with
  | 0, hm => cases hm; exact ctl_member_wf _ _ rfl (fun _ hb => nomatch hb)
  | 1, hm => cases hm; exact ctl_member_wf _ _ rfl (fun _ hb => nomatch hb)
  | 2, hm => cases hm; exact ctl_member_wf _ _ rfl (fun _ hb => nomatch hb)
  | 3, hm => exact Option.noConfusion hm
  | 4, hm => cases hm; exact ctl_member_wf _ _ rfl (fun _ hb => nomatch hb)
  | 5, hm => cases hm; exact ctl_member_wf _ _ rfl (fun _ hb => nomatch hb)
  | 6, hm => cases hm; exact ctl_member_wf _ _ rfl (fun _ hb => nomatch hb)
  | 7, hm => cases hm; exact ctl_member_wf _ _ rfl (fun _ hb => nomatch hb)
  | 8, hm => cases hm; exact ctl_member_wf _ _ rfl (fun _ hb => nomatch hb)
  | 9, hm => cases hm; exact ctl_member_wf _ _ rfl (fun _ hb => nomatch hb)
  | 10, hm => cases hm; exact ctl_member_wf _ _ rfl (fun _ hb => nomatch hb)
  | 11, hm =>
      cases hm
      exact ctl_member_wf _ _ rfl (fun b hb => by cases hb; rfl)
  | 12, hm =>
      cases hm
      exact ctl_member_wf _ _ rfl (fun b hb => by cases hb; rfl)
  | 13, hm => cases hm; exact ctl_member_wf _ _ rfl (fun _ hb => nomatch hb)
  | 14, hm =>
      cases hm
      exact ctl_member_wf _ _ rfl (fun b hb => by cases hb; rfl)
  | _ + 15, hm => exact Option.noConfusion hm

/-! ### Identity β, code-table shift

`defunc` of `(λ _. 0) arg` converts `arg` against a one-entry prefix whose
body is slot 0 (`defunc_app_lam_bvar0`). `defunc` of `arg` alone starts from
the empty table. The two differ by that prefix: every closure label grows
by the prefix length, and a value with no closure is unchanged.
Reynolds 1972 §8. Not AdeqApp. -/

def shiftD (k : Nat) : DExpr → DExpr
  | .apply f a => .apply (shiftD k f) (shiftD k a)
  | .letE v b => .letE (shiftD k v) (shiftD k b)
  | .clo l caps => .clo (l + k) caps
  | e => e

def shiftCode (k : Nat) (c : Code) : Code :=
  { ncap := c.ncap, body := shiftD k c.body }

mutual
def shiftDVal (k : Nat) : DVal → DVal
  | .box => .box
  | .lit n => .lit n
  | .ctor r xs => .ctor r (shiftDVals k xs)
  | .rigid r xs => .rigid r (shiftDVals k xs)
  | .clo l caps => .clo (l + k) (shiftDVals k caps)

def shiftDVals (k : Nat) : List DVal → List DVal
  | [] => []
  | v :: vs => shiftDVal k v :: shiftDVals k vs
end

def noGlobL : LExpr → Bool
  | .app f a => noGlobL f && noGlobL a
  | .lam b => noGlobL b
  | .letE v b => noGlobL v && noGlobL b
  | .glob _ => false
  | _ => true

def noGlobD : DExpr → Bool
  | .apply f a => noGlobD f && noGlobD a
  | .letE v b => noGlobD v && noGlobD b
  | .glob _ => false
  | _ => true

mutual
def noCloD : DVal → Bool
  | .clo _ _ => false
  | .ctor _ xs => noCloAll xs
  | .rigid _ xs => noCloAll xs
  | _ => true

def noCloAll : List DVal → Bool
  | [] => true
  | v :: vs => noCloD v && noCloAll vs
end

theorem shiftDVals_eq_map (k : Nat) : ∀ xs, shiftDVals k xs = xs.map (shiftDVal k)
  | [] => rfl
  | v :: vs => by
      simp only [shiftDVals, List.map_cons, shiftDVals_eq_map k vs]

theorem shiftDVals_append (k : Nat) :
    ∀ xs ys, shiftDVals k (xs ++ ys) = shiftDVals k xs ++ shiftDVals k ys
  | [], ys => by simp only [shiftDVals, List.nil_append]
  | x :: xs, ys => by
      rw [List.cons_append, shiftDVals, shiftDVals, shiftDVals_append k xs ys, ← List.cons_append]

mutual
theorem shiftDVal_id_of_noClo (k : Nat) : ∀ dv, noCloD dv = true → shiftDVal k dv = dv
  | .box, _ => rfl
  | .lit _, _ => rfl
  | .clo _ _, h => Bool.noConfusion h
  | .ctor _ xs, h => by
      simp only [noCloD] at h
      simp only [shiftDVal]
      exact congrArg (DVal.ctor _) (shiftDVals_id_of_noClo k xs h)
  | .rigid _ xs, h => by
      simp only [noCloD] at h
      simp only [shiftDVal]
      exact congrArg (DVal.rigid _) (shiftDVals_id_of_noClo k xs h)

theorem shiftDVals_id_of_noClo (k : Nat) : ∀ xs, noCloAll xs = true → shiftDVals k xs = xs
  | [], _ => rfl
  | v :: vs, h => by
      simp only [noCloAll, Bool.and_eq_true] at h
      simp only [shiftDVals, shiftDVal_id_of_noClo k v h.1, shiftDVals_id_of_noClo k vs h.2]
end

theorem list_get?_map {α β : Type} (f : α → β) :
    ∀ (xs : List α) (i : Nat), (xs.map f).get? i = (xs.get? i).map f
  | [], _ => rfl
  | _ :: _, 0 => rfl
  | _ :: xs, i + 1 => list_get?_map f xs i

theorem list_get?_append_right {α : Type} :
    ∀ (pre xs : List α) (i : Nat), (pre ++ xs).get? (pre.length + i) = xs.get? i
  | [], xs, i => by
      simp only [List.nil_append, List.length_nil, Nat.zero_add]
  | _ :: pre, xs, i => by
      simp only [List.cons_append, List.length_cons, Nat.succ_add, List.get?_cons_succ]
      exact list_get?_append_right pre xs i

theorem list_get?_append_map {α β : Type} (f : α → β)
    (pre : List β) (xs : List α) (i : Nat) :
    (pre ++ xs.map f).get? (pre.length + i) = (xs.get? i).map f := by
  rw [list_get?_append_right pre (xs.map f) i, list_get?_map f xs i]

theorem list_mem_of_get? {α : Type} : ∀ (xs : List α) (i : Nat) (a : α),
    xs.get? i = some a → a ∈ xs
  | [], _, _, h => Option.noConfusion h
  | _ :: _, 0, _, h => by
      simp only [List.get?] at h
      exact List.mem_cons.mpr (Or.inl (Option.some.inj h.symm))
  | _ :: xs, i + 1, a, h => by
      simp only [List.get?] at h
      exact List.mem_cons.mpr (Or.inr (list_mem_of_get? xs i a h))

theorem noGlobD_of_get? {code : List Code} {i : Nat} {c : Code}
    (hall : ∀ c' ∈ code, noGlobD c'.body = true)
    (hg : code.get? i = some c) : noGlobD c.body = true :=
  hall c (list_mem_of_get? code i c hg)

theorem option_map_some {α β : Type} (f : α → β) (a : α) :
    Option.map f (some a) = some (f a) := rfl

theorem option_map_none {α β : Type} (f : α → β) :
    Option.map f none = none := rfl

theorem list_mapM_shift (k : Nat) (env : List DVal) (caps : List Nat) :
    caps.mapM (fun i => (env.map (shiftDVal k)).get? i) =
      (caps.mapM (fun i => env.get? i)).map (List.map (shiftDVal k)) := by
  induction caps with
  | nil => simp [List.mapM_nil, Option.pure_def]
  | cons i caps ih =>
      rw [List.mapM_cons, List.mapM_cons, list_get?_map (shiftDVal k) env i, ih]
      cases hget : env.get? i with
      | none =>
          simp [Option.map_none', Option.none_bind, Option.bind, bind]
      | some v =>
          cases hrest : caps.mapM (fun j => env.get? j) with
          | none =>
              simp [hrest, Option.map_none', Option.none_bind, Option.some_bind, Option.map_some,
                Option.bind, bind]
          | some vs =>
              simp [hrest, Option.map_some, Option.some_bind, Option.pure_def, Option.bind, bind,
                List.map_cons]

theorem noGlob_conv (cr : List Nat → Nat → Nat) (ρ : Nat → Nat)
    (code : List Code) (l : LExpr)
    (hcode : ∀ c ∈ code, noGlobD c.body = true) (hl : noGlobL l = true) :
    noGlobD (convWith cr ρ code l).1 = true ∧
    ∀ c ∈ (convWith cr ρ code l).2, noGlobD c.body = true := by
  induction l generalizing ρ code with
  | bvar _ =>
      simp only [convWith, noGlobD]
      exact ⟨trivial, hcode⟩
  | box =>
      simp only [convWith, noGlobD]
      exact ⟨trivial, hcode⟩
  | lit _ =>
      simp only [convWith, noGlobD]
      exact ⟨trivial, hcode⟩
  | ctor _ =>
      simp only [convWith, noGlobD]
      exact ⟨trivial, hcode⟩
  | rigid _ =>
      simp only [convWith, noGlobD]
      exact ⟨trivial, hcode⟩
  | glob _ =>
      simp only [noGlobL] at hl
      exact Bool.noConfusion hl
  | app f a ihf iha =>
      simp only [noGlobL, Bool.and_eq_true] at hl
      have hf := ihf ρ code hcode hl.1
      have ha := iha ρ (convWith cr ρ code f).2 hf.2 hl.2
      simp only [convWith, noGlobD, Bool.and_eq_true]
      exact ⟨⟨hf.1, ha.1⟩, ha.2⟩
  | lam b ih =>
      simp only [noGlobL] at hl
      have ihb := ih (cr (freeVars 1 b)) code hcode hl
      simp only [convWith]
      refine ⟨by simp [noGlobD], ?_⟩
      intro c hc
      simp only [List.mem_append, List.mem_singleton] at hc
      cases hc with
      | inl hm => exact ihb.2 c hm
      | inr hm =>
          subst hm
          exact ihb.1
  | letE v b ihv ihb =>
      simp only [noGlobL, Bool.and_eq_true] at hl
      have hv := ihv ρ code hcode hl.1
      have hb := ihb (liftRen ρ) (convWith cr ρ code v).2 hv.2 hl.2
      simp only [convWith, noGlobD, Bool.and_eq_true]
      exact ⟨⟨hv.1, hb.1⟩, hb.2⟩

theorem convWith_shift_start (cr : List Nat → Nat → Nat) (ρ : Nat → Nat)
    (pre base : List Code) (l : LExpr) :
    (convWith cr ρ (pre ++ base.map (shiftCode pre.length)) l).1
      = shiftD pre.length (convWith cr ρ base l).1 ∧
    (convWith cr ρ (pre ++ base.map (shiftCode pre.length)) l).2
      = pre ++ ((convWith cr ρ base l).2.map (shiftCode pre.length)) := by
  induction l generalizing ρ pre base with
  | bvar _ =>
      simp only [convWith, shiftD]
      exact ⟨trivial, trivial⟩
  | box =>
      simp only [convWith, shiftD]
      exact ⟨trivial, trivial⟩
  | lit _ =>
      simp only [convWith, shiftD]
      exact ⟨trivial, trivial⟩
  | ctor _ =>
      simp only [convWith, shiftD]
      exact ⟨trivial, trivial⟩
  | rigid _ =>
      simp only [convWith, shiftD]
      exact ⟨trivial, trivial⟩
  | glob _ =>
      simp only [convWith, shiftD]
      exact ⟨trivial, trivial⟩
  | app f a ihf iha =>
      obtain ⟨hf1, hf2⟩ := ihf ρ pre base
      obtain ⟨ha1, ha2⟩ := iha ρ pre (convWith cr ρ base f).2
      simp only [convWith, shiftD]
      refine ⟨?_, ?_⟩
      · rw [hf1, hf2, ha1]
      · rw [hf2, ha2]
  | lam b ih =>
      let fs := freeVars 1 b
      obtain ⟨hb1, hb2⟩ := ih (cr fs) pre base
      have hlen : (convWith cr (cr fs) (pre ++ base.map (shiftCode pre.length)) b).2.length
          = pre.length + (convWith cr (cr fs) base b).2.length := by
        rw [hb2, List.length_append, List.length_map]
      simp only [convWith, shiftD]
      refine ⟨?_, ?_⟩
      · rw [hlen, Nat.add_comm]
      · rw [hb2, hb1]
        simp only [List.append_assoc, List.map_append, List.map_cons, List.map_nil, shiftCode]
  | letE v b ihv ihb =>
      obtain ⟨hv1, hv2⟩ := ihv ρ pre base
      obtain ⟨hb1, hb2⟩ := ihb (liftRen ρ) pre (convWith cr ρ base v).2
      simp only [convWith, shiftD]
      refine ⟨?_, ?_⟩
      · rw [hv1, hv2, hb1]
      · rw [hv2, hb2]

theorem run_var_eq (code : List Code) (F : Nat) (env : List DVal) (i : Nat) :
    run code (F + 1) env (.var i) = env.get? i := by
  unfold run runWith
  rfl

theorem run_box_eq (code : List Code) (F : Nat) (env : List DVal) :
    run code (F + 1) env .box = some .box := by
  unfold run runWith
  rfl

theorem run_lit_eq (code : List Code) (F : Nat) (env : List DVal) (n : Nat) :
    run code (F + 1) env (.lit n) = some (.lit n) := by
  unfold run runWith
  rfl

theorem run_ctor_eq (code : List Code) (F : Nat) (env : List DVal) (r : Nat) :
    run code (F + 1) env (.ctor r) = some (.ctor r []) := by
  unfold run runWith
  rfl

theorem run_rigid_eq (code : List Code) (F : Nat) (env : List DVal) (r : Nat) :
    run code (F + 1) env (.rigid r) = some (.rigid r []) := by
  unfold run runWith
  rfl

theorem run_clo_eq (code : List Code) (F l : Nat) (caps : List Nat) (env : List DVal) :
    run code (F + 1) env (.clo l caps) =
      (caps.mapM (fun i => env.get? i)).map (DVal.clo l) := by
  unfold run runWith
  rfl

theorem run_shift (k : Nat) :
    ∀ (F : Nat) (pre code : List Code) (env : List DVal) (e : DExpr),
      pre.length = k →
      noGlobD e = true →
      (∀ c ∈ code, noGlobD c.body = true) →
      run (pre ++ code.map (shiftCode k)) F (env.map (shiftDVal k)) (shiftD k e) =
        (run code F env e).map (shiftDVal k) := by
  intro F
  induction F with
  | zero =>
      intro pre code env e _ _ _
      unfold run runWith
      rfl
  | succ F ih =>
      intro pre code env e hk he hcode
      cases e with
      | var i =>
          simp only [shiftD, run_var_eq, list_get?_map]
      | box =>
          simp only [shiftD, run_box_eq]
          rfl
      | lit n =>
          simp only [shiftD, run_lit_eq]
          rfl
      | ctor r =>
          simp only [shiftD, run_ctor_eq]
          rfl
      | rigid r =>
          simp only [shiftD, run_rigid_eq]
          rfl
      | glob _ =>
          simp only [noGlobD] at he
          exact Bool.noConfusion he
      | clo l caps =>
          simp only [shiftD, run_clo_eq]
          rw [list_mapM_shift k env caps]
          cases hrest : caps.mapM (fun i => env.get? i) with
          | none => rfl
          | some vs =>
              change some (DVal.clo (l + k) (List.map (shiftDVal k) vs)) =
                some (shiftDVal k (DVal.clo l vs))
              simp only [shiftDVal, shiftDVals_eq_map]
      | apply g a =>
          simp only [noGlobD, Bool.and_eq_true] at he
          have hg := ih pre code env g hk he.1 hcode
          have ha := ih pre code env a hk he.2 hcode
          simp only [shiftD]
          rw [run_apply_eq, run_apply_eq, hg, ha]
          cases hrg : run code F env g with
          | none =>
              rw [option_map_none (shiftDVal k)]
          | some vg =>
              rw [option_map_some (shiftDVal k) vg]
              cases vg with
              | box =>
                  simp only [shiftDVal]
                  cases hra : run code F env a with
                  | none => rfl
                  | some va =>
                      rw [option_map_some (shiftDVal k) va]
                      rfl
              | lit _ =>
                  simp only [shiftDVal]
                  cases hra : run code F env a with
                  | none => rfl
                  | some va =>
                      rw [option_map_none (shiftDVal k)]
              | ctor r xs =>
                  simp only [shiftDVal]
                  cases hra : run code F env a with
                  | none => rfl
                  | some va =>
                      rw [option_map_some (shiftDVal k) va]
                      rw [option_map_some (shiftDVal k) (DVal.ctor r (xs ++ [va]))]
                      rw [shiftDVal, shiftDVals_append k xs [va], shiftDVals, shiftDVals]
              | rigid r xs =>
                  simp only [shiftDVal]
                  cases hra : run code F env a with
                  | none => rfl
                  | some va =>
                      rw [option_map_some (shiftDVal k) va]
                      rw [option_map_some (shiftDVal k) (DVal.rigid r (xs ++ [va]))]
                      rw [shiftDVal, shiftDVals_append k xs [va], shiftDVals, shiftDVals]
              | clo l caps =>
                  simp only [shiftDVal]
                  cases hra : run code F env a with
                  | none => rfl
                  | some va =>
                      rw [option_map_some (shiftDVal k) va]
                      change (match (pre ++ code.map (shiftCode k)).get? (l + k) with
                          | some c =>
                            run (pre ++ code.map (shiftCode k)) F
                              (bindArg (shiftDVal k va) (shiftDVals k caps)) c.body
                          | none => none) =
                        Option.map (shiftDVal k) (match code.get? l with
                          | some c => run code F (bindArg va caps) c.body
                          | none => none)
                      have hidx : (pre ++ code.map (shiftCode k)).get? (l + k) =
                          (code.get? l).map (shiftCode k) := by
                        have hk' : l + k = pre.length + l := by rw [hk, Nat.add_comm]
                        rw [hk']
                        exact list_get?_append_map (shiftCode k) pre code l
                      cases hc : code.get? l with
                      | none =>
                          rw [hidx, hc]
                          rfl
                      | some c =>
                          have hbody := noGlobD_of_get? hcode hc
                          have ihb := ih pre code (va :: caps) c.body hk hbody hcode
                          rw [hidx, hc, shiftDVals_eq_map]
                          unfold shiftCode
                          simpa only [bindArg, List.map_cons] using ihb
      | letE v b =>
          simp only [noGlobD, Bool.and_eq_true] at he
          have hv := ih pre code env v hk he.1 hcode
          simp only [shiftD]
          rw [run_let_eq, run_let_eq, hv]
          cases hrv : run code F env v with
          | none => rfl
          | some vv =>
              have hb := ih pre code (vv :: env) b hk he.2 hcode
              simpa only [List.map_cons] using hb

/- `run` of the identity λ applied to an argument that itself has no global,
   when that argument's run is a closure-free value. The prefix entry is
   slot 0; `run_shift` says the argument's value is unchanged.
   Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem run_beta_id_shift (la : LExpr) (F : Nat) (dv : DVal)
    (hg : noGlobL la = true) (hc : noCloD dv = true)
    (hr : run (defunc la).2 (F + 1) [] (defunc la).1 = some dv) :
    run (defunc (.app (.lam (.bvar 0)) la)).2 (F + 2) []
      (defunc (.app (.lam (.bvar 0)) la)).1 = some dv := by
  have hclean := noGlob_conv capRen id [] la (fun _ h => nomatch h) hg
  let pre : List Code := [{ ncap := 0, body := .var 0 }]
  have hs := convWith_shift_start capRen id pre [] la
  simp only [List.map_nil, List.append_nil] at hs
  have hr' := run_shift 1 (F + 1) pre (defunc la).2 [] (defunc la).1 rfl hclean.1 hclean.2
  rw [List.map_nil, hr, option_map_some] at hr'
  rw [shiftDVal_id_of_noClo 1 dv hc] at hr'
  rw [defunc_app_lam_bvar0]
  have hc0 : (convWith capRen id pre la).2.get? 0 = some ⟨0, DExpr.var 0⟩ := by
    have hpre : pre = [{ ncap := 0, body := .var 0 }] := rfl
    rw [hs.2, hpre, List.cons_append, List.nil_append]
    rfl
  have hrq : run (convWith capRen id pre la).2 (F + 1) []
      (convWith capRen id pre la).1 = some dv := by
    rw [hs.1, hs.2]
    exact hr'
  exact run_apply_id (convWith capRen id pre la).2 F []
    (convWith capRen id pre la).1 dv hc0 hrq

/- Erasure with the empty global table never builds a `glob`. `noGlobals`
   is `fun _ => none`, so the constant arm cannot take the global branch. -/
theorem noGlobL_eraseWith (irr : LCtx → Expr Nat → Bool) (E : ResolvedEnv) :
    ∀ (F : Nat) (Γ : LCtx) (e : Expr Nat) (l : LExpr),
      eraseWith irr noGlobals E F Γ e = some l → noGlobL l = true := by
  intro F
  induction F with
  | zero =>
      intro Γ e l h
      exact Option.noConfusion h
  | succ F ih =>
      intro Γ e l h
      cases e with
      | sort _ =>
          simp only [eraseWith] at h
          cases h
          rfl
      | pi _ _ =>
          simp only [eraseWith] at h
          cases h
          rfl
      | lit _ =>
          simp only [eraseWith] at h
          cases h
          rfl
      | bvar i =>
          simp only [eraseWith] at h
          cases hi : irr Γ (.bvar i)
          · simp only [hi, Bool.false_eq_true, if_false] at h
            cases h
            rfl
          · simp only [hi, if_true] at h
            cases h
            rfl
      | const r ls =>
          simp only [eraseWith] at h
          cases hi : irr Γ (.const r ls)
          · simp only [hi, Bool.false_eq_true, if_false, noGlobals] at h
            cases hb : transparentBody E r ls with
            | none =>
                rw [hb] at h
                cases hctor : isCtor E r
                · simp only [hctor, ite_false] at h
                  cases h
                  rfl
                · simp only [hctor, ite_true] at h
                  cases h
                  rfl
            | some b =>
                rw [hb] at h
                exact ih [] b l h
          · simp only [hi, if_true] at h
            cases h
            rfl
      | app g a =>
          simp only [eraseWith] at h
          cases hi : irr Γ (.app g a)
          · simp only [hi, Bool.false_eq_true, if_false] at h
            cases hg : eraseWith irr noGlobals E F Γ g with
            | none =>
                simp only [hg] at h
                exact Option.noConfusion h
            | some g' =>
                cases ha : eraseWith irr noGlobals E F Γ a with
                | none =>
                    simp only [hg, ha] at h
                    exact Option.noConfusion h
                | some a' =>
                    simp only [hg, ha] at h
                    cases h
                    simp only [noGlobL, Bool.and_eq_true]
                    exact ⟨ih Γ g g' hg, ih Γ a a' ha⟩
          · simp only [hi, if_true] at h
            cases h
            rfl
      | lam A b =>
          simp only [eraseWith] at h
          cases hi : irr Γ (.lam A b)
          · simp only [hi, Bool.false_eq_true, if_false] at h
            cases hb : eraseWith irr noGlobals E F (.assumption A :: Γ) b with
            | none =>
                simp only [hb, Option.map] at h
                exact Option.noConfusion h
            | some b' =>
                simp only [hb, Option.map] at h
                cases h
                simp only [noGlobL]
                exact ih (.assumption A :: Γ) b b' hb
          · simp only [hi, if_true] at h
            cases h
            rfl
      | letE A v b =>
          simp only [eraseWith] at h
          cases hi : irr Γ (.letE A v b)
          · simp only [hi, Bool.false_eq_true, if_false] at h
            cases hv : eraseWith irr noGlobals E F Γ v with
            | none =>
                simp only [hv] at h
                exact Option.noConfusion h
            | some v' =>
                cases hb : eraseWith irr noGlobals E F (.letBinding A v :: Γ) b with
                | none =>
                    simp only [hv, hb] at h
                    exact Option.noConfusion h
                | some b' =>
                    simp only [hv, hb] at h
                    cases h
                    simp only [noGlobL, Bool.and_eq_true]
                    exact ⟨ih Γ v v' hv, ih (.letBinding A v :: Γ) b b' hb⟩
          · simp only [hi, if_true] at h
            cases h
            rfl

theorem noGlobL_erase (E : ResolvedEnv) (n F : Nat) (Γ : LCtx) (e : Expr Nat) (l : LExpr)
    (h : erase E n F Γ e = some l) : noGlobL l = true :=
  noGlobL_eraseWith (irrelevant E n) E F Γ e l h

/- Eval of an identity β at fuel `F + 3` is eval of the emitted value of the
   argument's erasure, run at fuel `F + 1`. The λ erases to `λ. 0`, and
   `run_beta_id_shift` returns the argument's closure-free value.
   Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem lowerF_beta_id_eval {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n F lf : Nat) (A arg : Expr Nat) (t : BootTy) (w : Val)
    (hirr : irrelevant E n [] (.app (.lam A (.bvar 0)) arg) = false)
    (hirrL : irrelevant E n [] (.lam A (.bvar 0)) = false)
    (hirrB : irrelevant E n (.assumption A :: []) (.bvar 0) = false)
    (la : LExpr)
    (ha : erase E n (F + 1) [] arg = some la)
    (dv : DVal)
    (hr : run (defunc la).2 (F + 1) [] (defunc la).1 = some dv)
    (hc : noCloD dv = true)
    (he : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf []
        (emit (S := S) (G := []) (F + 1) t dv) = some w) :
    Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf []
      (lowerF E n (F + 3) (S := S) t (.app (.lam A (.bvar 0)) arg)) = some w := by
  have ha2 : erase E n (F + 2) [] arg = some la :=
    erase_mono E n (F + 1) (F + 2) [] arg la (Nat.le_succ (F + 1)) ha
  have hB : erase E n (F + 1) (.assumption A :: []) (.bvar 0) = some (.bvar 0) := by
    simp only [erase, eraseWith, hirrB, Bool.false_eq_true, if_false]
  have hLam : erase E n (F + 2) [] (.lam A (.bvar 0)) = some (.lam (.bvar 0)) := by
    rw [erase_lam_keep E n (F + 1) [] A (.bvar 0) hirrL]
    simp only [hB, Option.map]
  have he2 : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf []
      (emit (S := S) (G := []) (F + 2) t dv) = some w :=
    emitWith_evalStable relevantArgs progs lf [] (F + 1) (F + 2) t dv w
      (Nat.le_succ (F + 1)) he
  have hg : noGlobL la = true := noGlobL_erase E n (F + 1) [] arg la ha
  have hrApp : run (defunc (.app (.lam (.bvar 0)) la)).2 (F + 2) []
      (defunc (.app (.lam (.bvar 0)) la)).1 = some dv :=
    run_beta_id_shift la F dv hg hc hr
  exact lowerF_app_eval progs E n (F + 2) lf (.lam A (.bvar 0)) arg t w hirr
    (.lam (.bvar 0)) la hLam ha2 dv hrApp he2

/- A value in a successfully evaluated `listOf` has a successful element eval. -/
theorem eval_listOf_mem {S : SigTable} {τ : BootTy} (progs : Programs S S)
    (g : DVal → BootExpr S [] τ) (lf : Nat) :
    ∀ (xs : List DVal) (x : DVal) (w : Val),
      x ∈ xs →
      Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf [] (listOf (xs.map g)) = some w →
      ∃ u, Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf [] (g x) = some u := by
  intro xs
  induction xs with
  | nil =>
      intro x w hx _
      exact (List.not_mem_nil x hx).elim
  | cons y ys ih =>
      intro x w hx h
      cases lf with
      | zero =>
          rw [eval_fuel0] at h
          exact Option.noConfusion h
      | succ m =>
          change Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs (m + 1) []
            (BootExpr.listAppend (BootExpr.listSingleton (g y)) (listOf (ys.map g))) = some w at h
          simp only [Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval] at h
          cases hy : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs (m + 1) [] (g y) with
          | none =>
              rw [hy] at h
              exact Option.noConfusion h
          | some uy =>
              cases htail : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs (m + 1) []
                  (listOf (ys.map g)) with
              | none =>
                  rw [hy, htail] at h
                  exact Option.noConfusion h
              | some ry =>
                  cases List.mem_cons.mp hx with
                  | inl heq =>
                      subst heq
                      exact ⟨uy, hy⟩
                  | inr hmem =>
                      exact ih x ry hmem htail

theorem eval_listOf_tail {S : SigTable} {τ : BootTy} (progs : Programs S S)
    (g : DVal → BootExpr S [] τ) (lf : Nat) (y : DVal) (ys : List DVal) (w : Val)
    (h : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf []
        (listOf ((y :: ys).map g)) = some w) :
    ∃ w', Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf [] (listOf (ys.map g)) = some w' := by
  cases lf with
  | zero =>
      rw [eval_fuel0] at h
      exact Option.noConfusion h
  | succ m =>
      change Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs (m + 1) []
        (BootExpr.listAppend (BootExpr.listSingleton (g y)) (listOf (ys.map g))) = some w at h
      simp only [Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval] at h
      cases hy : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs (m + 1) [] (g y) with
      | none =>
          rw [hy] at h
          exact Option.noConfusion h
      | some _ =>
          cases htail : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs (m + 1) []
              (listOf (ys.map g)) with
          | none =>
              rw [hy, htail] at h
              exact Option.noConfusion h
          | some ry =>
              exact ⟨ry, rfl⟩

/- `relevantArgs` drops `□` and keeps every other value. -/
theorem relevantArgs_box (vs : List DVal) :
    relevantArgs (.box :: vs) = relevantArgs vs := rfl

theorem relevantArgs_lit (n : Nat) (vs : List DVal) :
    relevantArgs (.lit n :: vs) = .lit n :: relevantArgs vs := rfl

theorem relevantArgs_ctor (r : Nat) (ys vs : List DVal) :
    relevantArgs (.ctor r ys :: vs) = .ctor r ys :: relevantArgs vs := rfl

theorem relevantArgs_rigid (r : Nat) (ys vs : List DVal) :
    relevantArgs (.rigid r ys :: vs) = .rigid r ys :: relevantArgs vs := rfl

theorem relevantArgs_clo (l : Nat) (caps vs : List DVal) :
    relevantArgs (.clo l caps :: vs) = .clo l caps :: relevantArgs vs := rfl

/- Fields that `emit` evaluates contain no closure. The fuel predecessor
   discharges a kept field; a box is dropped before the list eval.
   Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem noCloAll_emitList {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) (F : Nat)
    (ih : ∀ (lf : Nat) (t : BootTy) (dv : DVal) (w : Val),
      Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf []
        (emitWith relevantArgs (S := S) (G := []) F t dv) = some w →
      noCloD dv = true)
    (τ : BootTy) (lf : Nat) :
    ∀ (xs : List DVal) (w : Val),
      Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf []
        (listOf ((relevantArgs xs).map
          (emitWith relevantArgs (S := S) (G := []) F τ))) = some w →
      noCloAll xs = true := by
  intro xs
  induction xs with
  | nil =>
      intro _ _
      rfl
  | cons v vs ihxs =>
      intro w hl
      cases v with
      | box =>
          simp only [noCloAll, noCloD, Bool.true_and]
          rw [relevantArgs_box] at hl
          exact ihxs w hl
      | lit n =>
          simp only [noCloAll, noCloD, Bool.true_and]
          rw [relevantArgs_lit] at hl
          obtain ⟨wt, htail⟩ := eval_listOf_tail progs
            (emitWith relevantArgs (S := S) (G := []) F τ)
            lf (.lit n) (relevantArgs vs) w hl
          exact ihxs wt htail
      | clo l caps =>
          rw [relevantArgs_clo] at hl
          obtain ⟨u, hu⟩ := eval_listOf_mem progs
            (emitWith relevantArgs (S := S) (G := []) F τ)
            lf (.clo l caps :: relevantArgs vs) (.clo l caps) w
            (List.mem_cons_self _ _) hl
          have hnf : noCloD (.clo l caps) = true :=
            ih lf τ (.clo l caps) u hu
          simp only [noCloD] at hnf
          exact Bool.noConfusion hnf
      | ctor r ys =>
          simp only [noCloAll, Bool.and_eq_true]
          rw [relevantArgs_ctor] at hl
          obtain ⟨u, hu⟩ := eval_listOf_mem progs
            (emitWith relevantArgs (S := S) (G := []) F τ)
            lf (.ctor r ys :: relevantArgs vs) (.ctor r ys) w
            (List.mem_cons_self _ _) hl
          obtain ⟨wt, htail⟩ := eval_listOf_tail progs
            (emitWith relevantArgs (S := S) (G := []) F τ)
            lf (.ctor r ys) (relevantArgs vs) w hl
          exact ⟨ih lf τ (.ctor r ys) u hu, ihxs wt htail⟩
      | rigid r ys =>
          simp only [noCloAll, Bool.and_eq_true]
          rw [relevantArgs_rigid] at hl
          obtain ⟨u, hu⟩ := eval_listOf_mem progs
            (emitWith relevantArgs (S := S) (G := []) F τ)
            lf (.rigid r ys :: relevantArgs vs) (.rigid r ys) w
            (List.mem_cons_self _ _) hl
          obtain ⟨wt, htail⟩ := eval_listOf_tail progs
            (emitWith relevantArgs (S := S) (G := []) F τ)
            lf (.rigid r ys) (relevantArgs vs) w hl
          exact ⟨ih lf τ (.rigid r ys) u hu, ihxs wt htail⟩

/- A closure cannot survive `emit`: `refuse` evaluates to `none`. A constructor
   tree that does survive has no closure in any field. Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem noCloD_emitWith {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) :
    ∀ (F lf : Nat) (t : BootTy) (dv : DVal) (w : Val),
      Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf []
        (emitWith relevantArgs (S := S) (G := []) F t dv) = some w →
      noCloD dv = true := by
  intro F
  induction F with
  | zero =>
      intro lf t dv w h
      have href : emitWith relevantArgs (S := S) (G := []) 0 t dv = refuse := by
        cases t <;> cases dv <;> rfl
      rw [href] at h
      exact absurd h (eval_refuse_ne progs lf [] w)
  | succ F ih =>
      intro lf t dv w h
      cases dv with
      | box => rfl
      | lit _ => rfl
      | clo l caps =>
          have href : emitWith relevantArgs (S := S) (G := []) (F + 1) t
              (.clo l caps) = refuse := by
            cases t <;> rfl
          rw [href] at h
          exact absurd h (eval_refuse_ne progs lf [] w)
      | rigid r ys =>
          have href : emitWith relevantArgs (S := S) (G := []) (F + 1) t
              (.rigid r ys) = refuse := by
            cases t <;> rfl
          rw [href] at h
          exact absurd h (eval_refuse_ne progs lf [] w)
      | ctor r xs =>
          cases t with
          | i64 =>
              have href : emitWith relevantArgs (S := S) (G := []) (F + 1) .i64
                  (.ctor r xs) = refuse := rfl
              rw [href] at h
              exact absurd h (eval_refuse_ne progs lf [] w)
          | bool =>
              have href : emitWith relevantArgs (S := S) (G := []) (F + 1) .bool
                  (.ctor r xs) = refuse := rfl
              rw [href] at h
              exact absurd h (eval_refuse_ne progs lf [] w)
          | str =>
              have href : emitWith relevantArgs (S := S) (G := []) (F + 1) .str
                  (.ctor r xs) = refuse := rfl
              rw [href] at h
              exact absurd h (eval_refuse_ne progs lf [] w)
          | bytes =>
              have href : emitWith relevantArgs (S := S) (G := []) (F + 1) .bytes
                  (.ctor r xs) = refuse := rfl
              rw [href] at h
              exact absurd h (eval_refuse_ne progs lf [] w)
          | list τ0 =>
              have href : emitWith relevantArgs (S := S) (G := []) (F + 1) (.list τ0)
                  (.ctor r xs) = refuse := rfl
              rw [href] at h
              exact absurd h (eval_refuse_ne progs lf [] w)
          | pair a b =>
              have href : emitWith relevantArgs (S := S) (G := []) (F + 1) (.pair a b)
                  (.ctor r xs) = refuse := rfl
              rw [href] at h
              exact absurd h (eval_refuse_ne progs lf [] w)
          | record fs =>
              have href : emitWith relevantArgs (S := S) (G := []) (F + 1) (.record fs)
                  (.ctor r xs) = refuse := rfl
              rw [href] at h
              exact absurd h (eval_refuse_ne progs lf [] w)
          | option τ0 =>
              have href : emitWith relevantArgs (S := S) (G := []) (F + 1) (.option τ0)
                  (.ctor r xs) = refuse := rfl
              rw [href] at h
              exact absurd h (eval_refuse_ne progs lf [] w)
          | residue τ0 =>
              have href : emitWith relevantArgs (S := S) (G := []) (F + 1) (.residue τ0)
                  (.ctor r xs) = refuse := rfl
              rw [href] at h
              exact absurd h (eval_refuse_ne progs lf [] w)
          | sum ts =>
              simp only [emitWith] at h
              by_cases hr : r < ts.length
              · rw [dif_pos hr] at h
                split at h
                · rename_i τ hτ
                  cases lf with
                  | zero =>
                      rw [eval_fuel0] at h
                      exact Option.noConfusion h
                  | succ m =>
                      simp only [Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval] at h
                      rw [eval_cast_eq progs (m + 1) [] hτ.symm] at h
                      cases hl : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs (m + 1) []
                          (listOf ((relevantArgs xs).map
                            (emitWith relevantArgs (S := S) (G := []) F τ))) with
                      | none =>
                          rw [hl] at h
                          exact Option.noConfusion h
                      | some lv =>
                          have hall : noCloAll xs = true :=
                            noCloAll_emitList progs F ih τ (m + 1) xs lv hl
                          simp only [noCloD]
                          exact hall
                · exact absurd h (eval_refuse_ne progs lf [] w)
              · rw [dif_neg hr] at h
                exact absurd h (eval_refuse_ne progs lf [] w)

/- Identity β preserves `Good` when the argument's normal form already lowers.
   `norm_beta_id_eq` keeps the value; `lowerF_beta_id_eval` moves the eval.
   The λ, the bound index, and the application are relevant.
   Not the universal AdeqApp. -/
theorem good_beta_id_of_eval {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n : Nat) (A arg : Expr Nat)
    (hirr : irrelevant E n [] (.app (.lam A (.bvar 0)) arg) = false)
    (hirrL : irrelevant E n [] (.lam A (.bvar 0)) = false)
    (hirrB : irrelevant E n (.assumption A :: []) (.bvar 0) = false)
    (harg : ∀ (lf fv : Nat) (v : Expr Nat) (t : BootTy) (w : Val),
      norm E lf arg = some v →
      scmValOf E fv v = some w →
      relevantSpine E n fv v = true →
      irrelevant E n [] v = false →
      valFits fv t w = true →
      (inferT E n [] v).isSome = true →
      ∃ F lf',
        Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf' []
          (lowerF E n F (S := S) t arg) = some w) :
    Good progs E n (.app (.lam A (.bvar 0)) arg) := by
  refine good_of_exists progs E n (.app (.lam A (.bvar 0)) arg) ?_
  intro lf fv T v t w _ _ _ hn hs hrel hirrv hf hvinf _
  cases lf with
  | zero =>
      rw [norm_fuel0] at hn
      exact Option.noConfusion hn
  | succ lf1 =>
      cases lf1 with
      | zero =>
          unfold norm at hn
          rw [whnfFuel_fuel0] at hn
          exact Option.noConfusion hn
      | succ k =>
          have hargn : norm E (k + 2) arg = some v :=
            norm_beta_id_eq E k A arg v hn
          obtain ⟨G, lfe, he⟩ :=
            harg (k + 2) fv v t w hargn hs hrel hirrv hf (by rw [hvinf]; rfl)
          unfold lowerF pipeline at he
          cases ha : erase E n G [] arg with
          | none =>
              simp only [ha] at he
              exact absurd he (eval_refuse_ne progs lfe [] w)
          | some la =>
              simp only [ha] at he
              cases hr : run (defunc la).2 G [] (defunc la).1 with
              | none =>
                  simp only [hr] at he
                  exact absurd he (eval_refuse_ne progs lfe [] w)
              | some dv =>
                  simp only [hr] at he
                  cases G with
                  | zero =>
                      simp only [erase, eraseWith] at ha
                      exact Option.noConfusion ha
                  | succ F =>
                      have hc : noCloD dv = true :=
                        noCloD_emitWith progs (F + 1) lfe t dv w he
                      exact ⟨F + 3, lfe, lowerF_beta_id_eval progs E n F lfe A arg t w
                        hirr hirrL hirrB la ha dv hr hc he⟩

/- Identity ζ preserves `Good` when the bound term's normal form already
   lowers. `norm_let_id_eq` keeps the value; `lowerF_let_id_eval` moves
   the eval. The let and the bound index are relevant.
   Not the universal AdeqLetE. -/
theorem good_let_id_of_eval {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n : Nat) (A bound : Expr Nat)
    (hirr : irrelevant E n [] (.letE A bound (.bvar 0)) = false)
    (hirrB : irrelevant E n (.letBinding A bound :: []) (.bvar 0) = false)
    (hbound : ∀ (lf fv : Nat) (v : Expr Nat) (t : BootTy) (w : Val),
      norm E lf bound = some v →
      scmValOf E fv v = some w →
      relevantSpine E n fv v = true →
      irrelevant E n [] v = false →
      valFits fv t w = true →
      (inferT E n [] v).isSome = true →
      ∃ F lf',
        Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf' []
          (lowerF E n F (S := S) t bound) = some w) :
    Good progs E n (.letE A bound (.bvar 0)) := by
  refine good_of_exists progs E n (.letE A bound (.bvar 0)) ?_
  intro lf fv T v t w _ _ _ hn hs hrel hirrv hf hvinf _
  cases lf with
  | zero =>
      rw [norm_fuel0] at hn
      exact Option.noConfusion hn
  | succ lf1 =>
      cases lf1 with
      | zero =>
          unfold norm at hn
          rw [whnfFuel_fuel0] at hn
          exact Option.noConfusion hn
      | succ k =>
          have hbnd : norm E (k + 2) bound = some v :=
            norm_let_id_eq E k A bound v hn
          obtain ⟨G, lfe, he⟩ :=
            hbound (k + 2) fv v t w hbnd hs hrel hirrv hf (by rw [hvinf]; rfl)
          unfold lowerF pipeline at he
          cases ha : erase E n G [] bound with
          | none =>
              simp only [ha] at he
              exact absurd he (eval_refuse_ne progs lfe [] w)
          | some lv =>
              simp only [ha] at he
              cases hr : run (defunc lv).2 G [] (defunc lv).1 with
              | none =>
                  simp only [hr] at he
                  exact absurd he (eval_refuse_ne progs lfe [] w)
              | some dv =>
                  simp only [hr] at he
                  cases G with
                  | zero =>
                      simp only [erase, eraseWith] at ha
                      exact Option.noConfusion ha
                  | succ F =>
                      exact ⟨F + 3, lfe, lowerF_let_id_eval progs E n F lfe A bound t w
                        hirr hirrB lv ha dv hr he⟩

/- `apply` of a nullary constructor to slot 0. The argument is whatever
   value is already in the environment. Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem run_apply_ctor_var (code : List Code) (F c : Nat) (dv : DVal) :
    run code (F + 2) [dv] (.apply (.ctor c) (.var 0)) = some (.ctor c [dv]) := by
  rw [run_apply_eq code (F + 1) [dv] (.ctor c) (.var 0)]
  rw [run_ctor_any code F c [dv], run_var0 code F [] dv]
  rfl

/- Defunctionalization of a constructor applied to an already erased
   argument. The constructor adds no code entry. Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem defunc_app_ctor (c : Nat) (la : LExpr) :
    defunc (.app (.ctor c) la) =
      (.apply (.ctor c) (defunc la).1, (defunc la).2) := rfl

/- `apply` of a nullary constructor to a closed argument value.
   One fuel runs the constructor head and the argument; the next fuel
   is the application. Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem run_apply_ctor_val (code : List Code) (F c : Nat) (a : DExpr) (dv : DVal)
    (hr : run code (F + 1) [] a = some dv) :
    run code (F + 2) [] (.apply (.ctor c) a) = some (.ctor c [dv]) := by
  rw [run_apply_eq code (F + 1) [] (.ctor c) a]
  rw [run_ctor_any code F c [], hr]
  rfl

/- Eval of a stuck constructor applied to an argument is eval of the
   constructor value whose one field is the argument's run value.
   Letouzey TYPES 2002 keeps a relevant application; the head erases to
   `ctor` because it has no transparent body. Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem lowerF_app_ctor_eval {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n F lf c : Nat) (lsc : List Level) (arg : Expr Nat)
    (t : BootTy) (w : Val)
    (hnone : transparentBody E c lsc = none)
    (hctor : isCtor E c = true)
    (hirr : irrelevant E n [] (.app (.const c lsc) arg) = false)
    (hirrC : irrelevant E n [] (.const c lsc) = false)
    (la : LExpr)
    (ha : erase E n (F + 1) [] arg = some la)
    (dv : DVal)
    (hr : run (defunc la).2 (F + 1) [] (defunc la).1 = some dv)
    (he : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf []
        (emit (S := S) (G := []) (F + 1) t (.ctor c [dv])) = some w) :
    Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf []
      (lowerF E n (F + 2) (S := S) t (.app (.const c lsc) arg)) = some w := by
  have hC1 : erase E n 1 [] (.const c lsc) = some (.ctor c) := by
    simp only [erase, eraseWith, hirrC, Bool.false_eq_true, if_false, noGlobals, hnone,
      hctor, if_true]
  have hC : erase E n (F + 1) [] (.const c lsc) = some (.ctor c) :=
    erase_mono E n 1 (F + 1) [] (.const c lsc) (.ctor c) (Nat.le_add_left 1 F) hC1
  have hee : erase E n (F + 2) [] (.app (.const c lsc) arg) =
      some (.app (.ctor c) la) := by
    simp only [erase_app_keep E n (F + 1) [] (.const c lsc) arg hirr, hC, ha]
  have hrA : run (defunc la).2 (F + 2) []
      (.apply (.ctor c) (defunc la).1) = some (.ctor c [dv]) :=
    run_apply_ctor_val (defunc la).2 F c (defunc la).1 dv hr
  unfold lowerF pipeline
  simp only [hee]
  rw [defunc_app_ctor c la]
  simp only [hrA]
  exact emitWith_evalStable relevantArgs progs lf [] (F + 1) (F + 2) t
    (.ctor c [dv]) w (Nat.le_succ (F + 1)) he

/- β of `λ. c ·` applied to an argument whose run is closure-free.
   The prefix entry is the constructor application; `run_shift` keeps the
   argument's value. The result is that constructor applied to the value,
   not the value itself. Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem run_beta_ctor_shift (c : Nat) (la : LExpr) (F : Nat) (dv : DVal)
    (hg : noGlobL la = true) (hc : noCloD dv = true)
    (hr : run (defunc la).2 (F + 2) [] (defunc la).1 = some dv) :
    run (defunc (.app (.lam (.app (.ctor c) (.bvar 0))) la)).2 (F + 3) []
      (defunc (.app (.lam (.app (.ctor c) (.bvar 0))) la)).1 =
      some (.ctor c [dv]) := by
  have hclean := noGlob_conv capRen id [] la (fun _ h => nomatch h) hg
  let pre : List Code := [{ ncap := 0, body := .apply (.ctor c) (.var 0) }]
  have hs := convWith_shift_start capRen id pre [] la
  simp only [List.map_nil, List.append_nil] at hs
  have hr' := run_shift 1 (F + 2) pre (defunc la).2 [] (defunc la).1 rfl hclean.1 hclean.2
  rw [List.map_nil, hr, option_map_some] at hr'
  rw [shiftDVal_id_of_noClo 1 dv hc] at hr'
  rw [defunc_lam_ctor_bvar]
  have hc0 : (convWith capRen id pre la).2.get? 0 =
      some (⟨0, DExpr.apply (.ctor c) (.var 0)⟩ : Code) := by
    have hpre : pre = [{ ncap := 0, body := .apply (.ctor c) (.var 0) }] := rfl
    rw [hs.2, hpre, List.cons_append, List.nil_append]
    rfl
  have hrq : run (convWith capRen id pre la).2 (F + 2) []
      (convWith capRen id pre la).1 = some dv := by
    rw [hs.1, hs.2]
    exact hr'
  have hb := run_apply_ctor_var (convWith capRen id pre la).2 F c dv
  exact run_apply_clo_nil (convWith capRen id pre la).2 (F + 1) 0 []
    (convWith capRen id pre la).1 (.apply (.ctor c) (.var 0)) dv (.ctor c [dv])
    hc0 hrq hb

/- Eval of `λ. c ·` applied to an argument, at fuel `F + 4`, is eval of
   the constructor value whose one field is the argument's run value.
   The constant is a relevant rigid constructor. Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem lowerF_beta_ctor_eval {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n F lf c : Nat) (lsc : List Level) (A arg : Expr Nat)
    (t : BootTy) (w : Val)
    (hnone : transparentBody E c lsc = none)
    (hctor : isCtor E c = true)
    (hirr : irrelevant E n []
      (.app (.lam A (.app (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0))) arg) = false)
    (hirrL : irrelevant E n [] (.lam A (.app (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0))) = false)
    (hirrBody : irrelevant E n (.assumption A :: [])
      (.app (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0)) = false)
    (hirrC : irrelevant E n (.assumption A :: []) (.const c lsc) = false)
    (hirrB : irrelevant E n (.assumption A :: []) (.bvar 0) = false)
    (la : LExpr)
    (ha : erase E n (F + 2) [] arg = some la)
    (dv : DVal)
    (hr : run (defunc la).2 (F + 2) [] (defunc la).1 = some dv)
    (hc : noCloD dv = true)
    (he : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf []
        (emit (S := S) (G := []) (F + 2) t (.ctor c [dv])) = some w) :
    Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf []
      (lowerF E n (F + 4) (S := S) t
        (.app (.lam A (.app (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0))) arg)) = some w := by
  have ha3 : erase E n (F + 3) [] arg = some la :=
    erase_mono E n (F + 2) (F + 3) [] arg la (Nat.le_succ (F + 2)) ha
  have hB : erase E n (F + 1) (.assumption A :: []) (.bvar 0) = some (.bvar 0) := by
    simp only [erase, eraseWith, hirrB, Bool.false_eq_true, if_false]
  have hC : erase E n (F + 1) (.assumption A :: []) (.const c lsc) = some (.ctor c) := by
    simp only [erase, eraseWith, hirrC, Bool.false_eq_true, if_false, noGlobals, hnone,
      hctor, if_true]
  have hBody : erase E n (F + 2) (.assumption A :: [])
      (.app (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0)) = some (.app (.ctor c) (.bvar 0)) := by
    rw [erase_app_keep E n (F + 1) (.assumption A :: []) (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0) hirrBody]
    simp only [hC, hB]
  have hLam : erase E n (F + 3) [] (.lam A (.app (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0))) =
      some (.lam (.app (.ctor c) (.bvar 0))) := by
    rw [erase_lam_keep E n (F + 2) [] A (.app (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0)) hirrL]
    simp only [hBody, Option.map]
  have he3 : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf []
      (emit (S := S) (G := []) (F + 3) t (.ctor c [dv])) = some w :=
    emitWith_evalStable relevantArgs progs lf [] (F + 2) (F + 3) t (.ctor c [dv]) w
      (Nat.le_succ (F + 2)) he
  have hg : noGlobL la = true := noGlobL_erase E n (F + 2) [] arg la ha
  have hrApp : run (defunc (.app (.lam (.app (.ctor c) (.bvar 0))) la)).2 (F + 3) []
      (defunc (.app (.lam (.app (.ctor c) (.bvar 0))) la)).1 = some (.ctor c [dv]) :=
    run_beta_ctor_shift c la F dv hg hc hr
  exact lowerF_app_eval progs E n (F + 3) lf
    (.lam A (.app (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0))) arg t w hirr
    (.lam (.app (.ctor c) (.bvar 0))) la hLam ha3 (.ctor c [dv]) hrApp he3

/- A stuck constructor applied to an argument whose normal form is
   already known. The application's normal form is the constructor
   applied to that value. Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem norm_app_ctor_arg (E : ResolvedEnv) (k c : Nat) (lsc : List Level)
    (arg varg : Expr Nat)
    (hnone : transparentBody E c lsc = none)
    (harg : norm E (k + 2) arg = some varg) :
    norm E (k + 3) (.app (.const c lsc) arg) =
      some (.app (.const c lsc) varg) := by
  have hwb : whnfFuel E (k + 2) (.app (.const c lsc) arg) =
      some (.app (.const c lsc) arg) := by
    simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine, hnone]
  unfold norm
  rw [hwb]
  have hsp : appsSpine (.app (.const c lsc) arg) =
      (.const c lsc, [arg]) := by
    simp only [appsSpine, List.nil_append]
  simp only [hsp]
  have hm : [arg].mapM (norm E (k + 2)) = some [varg] := by
    rw [List.mapM_cons, harg, List.mapM_nil]
    rfl
  simp only [hm, foldApps]

/- Any successful norm of that stuck application is the constructor
   applied to the argument's normal form, two fuels above zero.
   Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem norm_app_ctor_arg_of_norm (E : ResolvedEnv) (lf c : Nat) (lsc : List Level)
    (arg v : Expr Nat) (hnone : transparentBody E c lsc = none)
    (hn : norm E lf (.app (.const c lsc) arg) = some v) :
    ∃ k varg, lf = k + 2 ∧ norm E (k + 1) arg = some varg ∧
      v = .app (.const c lsc) varg := by
  cases lf with
  | zero =>
      rw [norm_fuel0] at hn
      exact Option.noConfusion hn
  | succ lf1 =>
      cases lf1 with
      | zero =>
          unfold norm at hn
          rw [whnfFuel_fuel0] at hn
          exact Option.noConfusion hn
      | succ k =>
          unfold norm at hn
          have hstuck : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.app (.const c lsc) arg) =
              some (.app (.const c lsc) arg) := by
            simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine, List.nil_append, hnone]
          rw [hstuck] at hn
          have hsp : appsSpine (.app (.const c lsc) arg) =
              (.const c lsc, [arg]) := by
            simp only [appsSpine, List.nil_append]
          simp only [hsp] at hn
          cases hargn : norm E (k + 1) arg with
          | none =>
              have hmap : [arg].mapM (norm E (k + 1)) = none := by
                rw [List.mapM_cons, hargn, List.mapM_nil]
                rfl
              simp only [hmap] at hn
              exact Option.noConfusion hn
          | some varg =>
              have hmap : [arg].mapM (norm E (k + 1)) = some [varg] := by
                rw [List.mapM_cons, hargn, List.mapM_nil]
                rfl
              simp only [hmap, foldApps] at hn
              exact ⟨k, varg, rfl, hargn, (Option.some.inj hn).symm⟩

/- One β whose body is a rigid constructor applied to the bound index.
   The normal form is that constructor applied to the argument's normal
   form. Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem norm_beta_ctor_arg (E : ResolvedEnv) (k c : Nat) (lsc : List Level)
    (A arg v : Expr Nat) (hnone : transparentBody E c lsc = none)
    (ha : norm E (k + 2) arg = some v) :
    norm E (k + 3) (.app (.lam A (.app (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0))) arg) =
      some (.app (.const c lsc) v) := by
  have hsub : (instantiate0 arg (.app (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0)) : Expr Nat) =
      .app (.const c lsc) arg := rfl
  have hbeta : whnfFuel E (k + 2)
      (.app (.lam A (.app (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0))) arg) =
      whnfFuel E (k + 1) (instantiate0 arg (.app (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0))) := by
    simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine, foldApps, List.nil_append]
  have hstuck : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.app (.const c lsc) arg) =
      some (.app (.const c lsc) arg) := by
    simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine, List.nil_append, hnone]
  unfold norm
  rw [hbeta, hsub, hstuck]
  have hsp : appsSpine (.app (.const c lsc) arg) = (.const c lsc, [arg]) := by
    simp only [appsSpine, List.nil_append]
  simp only [hsp]
  have hm : [arg].mapM (norm E (k + 2)) = some [v] := by
    rw [List.mapM_cons, ha, List.mapM_nil]
    rfl
  simp only [hm, foldApps]

/- A successful norm of that β is a successful norm of the argument, and
   the value is the constructor applied to it. Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem norm_beta_ctor_arg_of_norm (E : ResolvedEnv) (lf c : Nat) (lsc : List Level)
    (A arg v : Expr Nat) (hnone : transparentBody E c lsc = none)
    (hn : norm E lf (.app (.lam A (.app (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0))) arg) = some v) :
    ∃ k varg, lf = k + 3 ∧ norm E (k + 2) arg = some varg ∧
      v = .app (.const c lsc) varg := by
  cases lf with
  | zero =>
      rw [norm_fuel0] at hn
      exact Option.noConfusion hn
  | succ lf1 =>
      cases lf1 with
      | zero =>
          unfold norm at hn
          rw [whnfFuel_fuel0] at hn
          exact Option.noConfusion hn
      | succ lf2 =>
          cases lf2 with
          | zero =>
              have hbeta : whnfFuel E 1
                  (.app (.lam A (.app (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0))) arg) =
                  whnfFuel E 0
                    (instantiate0 arg (.app (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0))) := by
                simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine, foldApps, List.nil_append]
              unfold norm at hn
              rw [hbeta, whnfFuel_fuel0] at hn
              exact Option.noConfusion hn
          | succ k =>
              unfold norm at hn
              have hbeta : whnfFuel E (k + 2)
                  (.app (.lam A (.app (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0))) arg) =
                  whnfFuel E (k + 1)
                    (instantiate0 arg (.app (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0))) := by
                simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine, foldApps, List.nil_append]
              have hsub : (instantiate0 arg (.app (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0)) : Expr Nat) =
                  .app (.const c lsc) arg := rfl
              rw [hbeta, hsub] at hn
              have hstuck : whnfFuel E (k + 1) (.app (.const c lsc) arg) =
                  some (.app (.const c lsc) arg) := by
                simp only [whnfFuel, appsSpine, List.nil_append, hnone]
              rw [hstuck] at hn
              have hsp : appsSpine (.app (.const c lsc) arg) =
                  (.const c lsc, [arg]) := by
                simp only [appsSpine, List.nil_append]
              simp only [hsp] at hn
              cases hargn : norm E (k + 2) arg with
              | none =>
                  have hmap : [arg].mapM (norm E (k + 2)) = none := by
                    rw [List.mapM_cons, hargn, List.mapM_nil]
                    rfl
                  simp only [hmap] at hn
                  exact Option.noConfusion hn
              | some varg =>
                  have hmap : [arg].mapM (norm E (k + 2)) = some [varg] := by
                    rw [List.mapM_cons, hargn, List.mapM_nil]
                    rfl
                  simp only [hmap, foldApps] at hn
                  exact ⟨k, varg, rfl, hargn, (Option.some.inj hn).symm⟩

/- Emit of a one-field constructor is the injection of that field's value.
   A `box` field cannot emit, so `relevantArgs` keeps the single field.
   Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem eval_emit_ctor_one {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (F lf c : Nat) (ts : List BootTy) (τ : BootTy) (dv : DVal) (w : Val)
    (hg : ts.get? c = some (.list τ))
    (he : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf []
      (emit (S := S) (G := []) (F + 1) τ dv) = some w) :
    Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf []
      (emit (S := S) (G := []) (F + 2) (.sum ts) (.ctor c [dv])) =
      some (.inj c (.list [w])) := by
  cases lf with
  | zero =>
      rw [eval_fuel0] at he
      exact Option.noConfusion he
  | succ m =>
      obtain ⟨hlt, hget⟩ := list_get?_some ts c (.list τ) hg
      have hkeep : relevantArgs [dv] = [dv] := by
        cases dv with
        | box =>
            have href : emit (S := S) (G := []) (F + 1) τ .box = refuse := by
              cases τ <;> rfl
            rw [href] at he
            exact absurd he (eval_refuse_ne progs (m + 1) [] w)
        | lit n => simpa using relevantArgs_lit n []
        | ctor r ys => simpa using relevantArgs_ctor r ys []
        | rigid r ys => simpa using relevantArgs_rigid r ys []
        | clo l caps => simpa using relevantArgs_clo l caps []
      simp only [emit, emitWith]
      rw [dif_pos hlt]
      split
      · rename_i τ' hτ'
        have hτeq : τ' = τ := BootTy.list.inj (hτ'.symm.trans hget)
        cases hτeq
        simp only [Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval]
        rw [eval_cast_eq progs (m + 1) [] hτ'.symm]
        rw [hkeep, List.map_cons, List.map_nil]
        have hlist : Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs (m + 1) []
            (listOf [emitWith relevantArgs (S := S) (G := []) (F + 1) τ dv]) =
            some (.list [w]) := by
          change Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs (m + 1) []
              (BootExpr.listAppend
                (BootExpr.listSingleton (emit (S := S) (G := []) (F + 1) τ dv))
                (listOf ([] : List (BootExpr S [] τ)))) =
              some (.list [w])
          simp only [listOf, Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval, he, List.append_nil]
          rfl
        rw [hlist]
        rfl
      · rename_i hne
        exact absurd hget (hne τ)

/- `Good` of a stuck constructor applied to an argument whose own
   lowering is given. The scm value is the injection of the field.
   Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem good_app_ctor_of_eval {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n c : Nat) (lsc : List Level) (arg : Expr Nat)
    (hnone : transparentBody E c lsc = none)
    (hirr : irrelevant E n [] (.app (.const c lsc) arg) = false)
    (hirrC : irrelevant E n [] (.const c lsc) = false)
    (harg : ∀ (lf fv : Nat) (v : Expr Nat) (t : BootTy) (w : Val),
      norm E lf arg = some v →
      scmValOf E fv v = some w →
      relevantSpine E n fv v = true →
      irrelevant E n [] v = false →
      valFits fv t w = true →
      ∃ F lf',
        Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf' []
          (lowerF E n F (S := S) t arg) = some w) :
    Good progs E n (.app (.const c lsc) arg) := by
  refine good_of_exists progs E n (.app (.const c lsc) arg) ?_
  intro lf fv T v t w _ _ _ hn hs hrel _ hf _ _
  obtain ⟨k, varg, _, hargn, hv⟩ :=
    norm_app_ctor_arg_of_norm E lf c lsc arg v hnone hn
  subst hv
  cases fv with
  | zero =>
      simp only [scmValOf] at hs
      exact Option.noConfusion hs
  | succ m =>
      cases m with
      | zero =>
          have hs0 : scmValOf E 1 (.app (.const c lsc) varg) = none := by
            simp only [scmValOf, appsSpine, List.nil_append, List.mapM_cons,
              List.mapM_nil, Option.bind, Option.pure_def]
            split
            · rename_i mm hm
              by_cases hc : mm.mclass = .constructorM
              · simp [hm, hc, scmValOf]
              · simp [hm, hc]
            · rename_i hm
              simp [hm]
          rw [hs0] at hs
          exact Option.noConfusion hs
      | succ q =>
          have hs' : (match E.members c with
              | some mm =>
                  if mm.mclass = .constructorM then
                    match List.mapM (scmValOf E (q + 1)) [varg] with
                    | some vs => some (.inj c (.list vs))
                    | none => none
                  else none
              | none => none) = some w := by
            simpa [scmValOf, appsSpine, List.nil_append] using hs
          cases hm : E.members c with
          | none =>
              simp only [hm] at hs'
              exact Option.noConfusion hs'
          | some mm =>
              simp only [hm] at hs'
              by_cases hcm : mm.mclass = .constructorM
              · simp only [hcm, ite_true] at hs'
                rw [List.mapM_cons, List.mapM_nil] at hs'
                cases hfield : scmValOf E (q + 1) varg with
                | none =>
                    simp only [hfield, Option.bind, Option.pure_def] at hs'
                    exact Option.noConfusion hs'
                | some wfield =>
                    simp only [hfield, Option.bind, Option.pure_def] at hs'
                    have hw : w = .inj c (.list [wfield]) := (Option.some.inj hs').symm
                    subst hw
                    have hctor : isCtor E c = true := by simp [isCtor, hm, hcm]
                    have hrel1 :
                        (!irrelevant E n [] varg &&
                          relevantSpine E n (q + 1) varg) = true := by
                      simpa [relevantSpine, appsSpine, List.nil_append, List.all_cons,
                        List.all_nil, Bool.and_true] using hrel
                    cases hirrF : irrelevant E n [] varg with
                    | true =>
                        simp only [hirrF, Bool.not_true, Bool.false_and] at hrel1
                        exact Bool.noConfusion hrel1
                    | false =>
                        simp only [hirrF, Bool.not_false, Bool.true_and] at hrel1
                        cases t with
                        | sum ts =>
                            have hf' : (match ts.get? c with
                                | some (.list τ) =>
                                    valFits (q + 1) τ wfield
                                | _ => false) = true := by
                              simpa [valFits, List.all_cons, List.all_nil, Bool.and_true]
                                using hf
                            split at hf'
                            · rename_i τ hg
                              obtain ⟨G, lfe, he⟩ :=
                                harg (k + 1) (q + 1) varg τ wfield hargn hfield hrel1
                                  hirrF hf'
                              unfold lowerF pipeline at he
                              cases ha : erase E n G [] arg with
                              | none =>
                                  simp only [ha] at he
                                  exact absurd he (eval_refuse_ne progs lfe [] wfield)
                              | some la =>
                                  simp only [ha] at he
                                  cases hr : run (defunc la).2 G [] (defunc la).1 with
                                  | none =>
                                      simp only [hr] at he
                                      exact absurd he (eval_refuse_ne progs lfe [] wfield)
                                  | some dv =>
                                      simp only [hr] at he
                                      cases G with
                                      | zero =>
                                          simp only [erase, eraseWith] at ha
                                          exact Option.noConfusion ha
                                      | succ F =>
                                          have ha2 : erase E n (F + 2) [] arg = some la :=
                                            erase_mono E n (F + 1) (F + 2) [] arg la
                                              (Nat.le_succ (F + 1)) ha
                                          have hr2 : run (defunc la).2 (F + 2) []
                                              (defunc la).1 = some dv :=
                                            run_mono (defunc la).2 (F + 1) (F + 2) []
                                              (defunc la).1 dv (Nat.le_succ (F + 1)) hr
                                          have heC := eval_emit_ctor_one progs F lfe c ts τ
                                            dv wfield hg he
                                          exact ⟨F + 3, lfe,
                                            lowerF_app_ctor_eval progs E n (F + 1) lfe c lsc arg
                                              (.sum ts) (.inj c (.list [wfield])) hnone hctor
                                              hirr hirrC la ha2 dv hr2 heC⟩
                            · exact Bool.noConfusion hf'
                        | i64 | bool | str | bytes | list _ | pair _ _ | record _ |
                          option _ | residue _ =>
                            simp only [valFits] at hf
                            exact Bool.noConfusion hf
              · simp only [hcm, ite_false] at hs'
                exact Option.noConfusion hs'

/- β of `λ. c ·` preserves `Good` when the argument's normal form already
   lowers. The normal form is `c` applied to that value, so the scm value
   is the injection of the field, not the field. Not AdeqApp. -/
theorem good_beta_ctor_of_eval {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n c : Nat) (lsc : List Level) (A arg : Expr Nat)
    (hnone : transparentBody E c lsc = none)
    (hirr : irrelevant E n []
      (.app (.lam A (.app (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0))) arg) = false)
    (hirrL : irrelevant E n [] (.lam A (.app (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0))) = false)
    (hirrBody : irrelevant E n (.assumption A :: [])
      (.app (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0)) = false)
    (hirrC : irrelevant E n (.assumption A :: []) (.const c lsc) = false)
    (hirrB : irrelevant E n (.assumption A :: []) (.bvar 0) = false)
    (harg : ∀ (lf fv : Nat) (v : Expr Nat) (t : BootTy) (w : Val),
      norm E lf arg = some v →
      scmValOf E fv v = some w →
      relevantSpine E n fv v = true →
      irrelevant E n [] v = false →
      valFits fv t w = true →
      ∃ F lf',
        Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf' []
          (lowerF E n F (S := S) t arg) = some w) :
    Good progs E n (.app (.lam A (.app (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0))) arg) := by
  refine good_of_exists progs E n
      (.app (.lam A (.app (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0))) arg) ?_
  intro lf fv T v t w _ _ _ hn hs hrel _ hf _ _
  obtain ⟨k, varg, _, hargn, hv⟩ :=
    norm_beta_ctor_arg_of_norm E lf c lsc A arg v hnone hn
  subst hv
  cases fv with
  | zero =>
      simp only [scmValOf] at hs
      exact Option.noConfusion hs
  | succ m =>
      cases m with
      | zero =>
          have hs0 : scmValOf E 1 (.app (.const c lsc) varg) = none := by
            simp only [scmValOf, appsSpine, List.nil_append, List.mapM_cons,
              List.mapM_nil, Option.bind, Option.pure_def]
            split
            · rename_i mm hm
              by_cases hc : mm.mclass = .constructorM
              · simp [hm, hc, scmValOf]
              · simp [hm, hc]
            · rename_i hm
              simp [hm]
          rw [hs0] at hs
          exact Option.noConfusion hs
      | succ q =>
          have hs' : (match E.members c with
              | some mm =>
                  if mm.mclass = .constructorM then
                    match List.mapM (scmValOf E (q + 1)) [varg] with
                    | some vs => some (.inj c (.list vs))
                    | none => none
                  else none
              | none => none) = some w := by
            simpa [scmValOf, appsSpine, List.nil_append] using hs
          cases hm : E.members c with
          | none =>
              simp only [hm] at hs'
              exact Option.noConfusion hs'
          | some mm =>
              simp only [hm] at hs'
              by_cases hcm : mm.mclass = .constructorM
              · simp only [hcm, ite_true] at hs'
                rw [List.mapM_cons, List.mapM_nil] at hs'
                cases hfield : scmValOf E (q + 1) varg with
                | none =>
                    simp only [hfield, Option.bind, Option.pure_def] at hs'
                    exact Option.noConfusion hs'
                | some wfield =>
                    simp only [hfield, Option.bind, Option.pure_def] at hs'
                    have hw : w = .inj c (.list [wfield]) := (Option.some.inj hs').symm
                    subst hw
                    have hctor : isCtor E c = true := by simp [isCtor, hm, hcm]
                    have hrel1 :
                        (!irrelevant E n [] varg &&
                          relevantSpine E n (q + 1) varg) = true := by
                      simpa [relevantSpine, appsSpine, List.nil_append, List.all_cons,
                        List.all_nil, Bool.and_true] using hrel
                    cases hirrF : irrelevant E n [] varg with
                    | true =>
                        simp only [hirrF, Bool.not_true, Bool.false_and] at hrel1
                        exact Bool.noConfusion hrel1
                    | false =>
                        simp only [hirrF, Bool.not_false, Bool.true_and] at hrel1
                        cases t with
                        | sum ts =>
                            have hf' : (match ts.get? c with
                                | some (.list τ) =>
                                    valFits (q + 1) τ wfield
                                | _ => false) = true := by
                              simpa [valFits, List.all_cons, List.all_nil, Bool.and_true]
                                using hf
                            split at hf'
                            · rename_i τ hg
                              obtain ⟨G, lfe, he⟩ :=
                                harg (k + 2) (q + 1) varg τ wfield hargn hfield hrel1
                                  hirrF hf'
                              unfold lowerF pipeline at he
                              cases ha : erase E n G [] arg with
                              | none =>
                                  simp only [ha] at he
                                  exact absurd he (eval_refuse_ne progs lfe [] wfield)
                              | some la =>
                                  simp only [ha] at he
                                  cases hr : run (defunc la).2 G [] (defunc la).1 with
                                  | none =>
                                      simp only [hr] at he
                                      exact absurd he (eval_refuse_ne progs lfe [] wfield)
                                  | some dv =>
                                      simp only [hr] at he
                                      cases G with
                                      | zero =>
                                          simp only [erase, eraseWith] at ha
                                          exact Option.noConfusion ha
                                      | succ F =>
                                          have hc : noCloD dv = true :=
                                            noCloD_emitWith progs (F + 1) lfe τ dv wfield he
                                          have ha2 : erase E n (F + 2) [] arg = some la :=
                                            erase_mono E n (F + 1) (F + 2) [] arg la
                                              (Nat.le_succ (F + 1)) ha
                                          have hr2 : run (defunc la).2 (F + 2) []
                                              (defunc la).1 = some dv :=
                                            run_mono (defunc la).2 (F + 1) (F + 2) []
                                              (defunc la).1 dv (Nat.le_succ (F + 1)) hr
                                          have heC := eval_emit_ctor_one progs F lfe c ts τ
                                            dv wfield hg he
                                          exact ⟨F + 4, lfe,
                                            lowerF_beta_ctor_eval progs E n F lfe c lsc A arg
                                              (.sum ts) (.inj c (.list [wfield])) hnone hctor
                                              hirr hirrL hirrBody hirrC hirrB la ha2 dv hr2
                                              hc heC⟩
                            · exact Bool.noConfusion hf'
                        | i64 | bool | str | bytes | list _ | pair _ _ | record _ |
                          option _ | residue _ =>
                            simp only [valFits] at hf
                            exact Bool.noConfusion hf
              · simp only [hcm, ite_false] at hs'
                exact Option.noConfusion hs'

/- Open `Good` obligations, named. `none` is a proved head: bvar, sort, Π,
   λ, lit, or a constant with no transparent body (`adeqConstHead`).
   An application, a let, or a transparent constant is refused by the
   open statement's name. This is not a certificate of the chain sources
   in `P1-SOURCE-CERT-CLOSE` (`rsdc/Compile.rsd`, `rsc/rsc.rsd`, `lib/rt`),
   and it is not `source_cert=1`. -/
def certRefusal (E : ResolvedEnv) : Expr Nat → Option String
  | .bvar _ => none
  | .sort _ => none
  | .pi _ _ => none
  | .lam _ _ => none
  | .lit _ => none
  | .const r ls =>
      match transparentBody E r ls with
      | some _ => some "AdeqConstDelta"
      | none => none
  | .app _ _ => some "AdeqApp"
  | .letE _ _ _ => some "AdeqLetE"

theorem certRefusal_bvar (E : ResolvedEnv) (i : Nat) :
    certRefusal E (.bvar i) = none := rfl

theorem certRefusal_sort (E : ResolvedEnv) (l : Level) :
    certRefusal E (.sort l) = none := rfl

theorem certRefusal_pi (E : ResolvedEnv) (A B : Expr Nat) :
    certRefusal E (.pi A B) = none := rfl

theorem certRefusal_lam (E : ResolvedEnv) (A b : Expr Nat) :
    certRefusal E (.lam A b) = none := rfl

theorem certRefusal_lit (E : ResolvedEnv) (k : Nat) :
    certRefusal E (.lit k) = none := rfl

theorem certRefusal_const_head (E : ResolvedEnv) (r : Nat) (ls : List Level)
    (h : transparentBody E r ls = none) :
    certRefusal E (.const r ls) = none := by
  simp only [certRefusal, h]

theorem certRefusal_const_delta (E : ResolvedEnv) (r : Nat) (ls : List Level)
    (b : Expr Nat) (h : transparentBody E r ls = some b) :
    certRefusal E (.const r ls) = some "AdeqConstDelta" := by
  simp only [certRefusal, h]

theorem certRefusal_app (E : ResolvedEnv) (f a : Expr Nat) :
    certRefusal E (.app f a) = some "AdeqApp" := rfl

theorem certRefusal_let (E : ResolvedEnv) (A v b : Expr Nat) :
    certRefusal E (.letE A v b) = some "AdeqLetE" := rfl

/-! ### `HasTyT` vs syntactic `inferT` conversion flip under `EnvWf`

`convFlipEnv` satisfies `EnvWf` (`convFlipEnv_wf`):
- member 0 (`vfI`): universe-polymorphic inductive `I.{u} : Sort u` (arity 1);
- member 1 (`vfK`): constructor `K : I.{max 0 0}` (arity 0);
- member 2 (`vfC`): transparent definition `c : I.{0} := K` (arity 0), whose
  body `K` is typed at `I.{0}` in `HasTyT` via `HasTyT.conv` and `ConvT.consts`
  (`eqN (max 0 0) 0`).

At `vfDelta = c`, `vfApp = (λ x : I.{0}, x) c`, and `vfLet = let x : I.{0} := c in x`,
the syntactic checker `inferT` types the redex at `I.{0}`, whose syntactic type
is `Sort 0` (`isPropSort = true`), so `irrelevant = true` and `lowerF` refuses
at every fuel. The normal form `vfVal = K` has syntactic type `I.{max 0 0}`,
whose syntactic type is `Sort (max 0 0)` (`isPropSort = false`), so
`irrelevant = false` and `scmValOf = some (.inj 1 (.list []))`.
Thus `not_adeqAppWfLoose`, `not_adeqLetEWfLoose`, and
`not_adeqConstDeltaWfLoose` refute `EnvWf` with `GoodLoose`
(`(inferT E n [] v).isSome = true`). Requiring `inferT E n [] v = some T` in
`Good` excludes all three flip witnesses (`vfVal_infer_ne`,
`flipWeird_infer_ne`, `cfVal_infer_ne`) and makes `irrelevant E n [] e = false`
follow from `irrelevant E n [] v = false` (`irrelevant_false_of_same_type`). -/

def vfI : CheckedMember := ⟨.inductiveM, 1, .sort (.param 0), none⟩
def vfK : CheckedMember := ⟨.constructorM, 0, .const 0 [lvl00], none⟩
def vfC : CheckedMember := ⟨.definitionM, 0, .const 0 [.zero], some (.const 1 [])⟩

def convFlipEnv : ResolvedEnv where
  members := fun r =>
    match r with
    | 0 => some vfI
    | 1 => some vfK
    | 2 => some vfC
    | _ => none

def vfTy : Expr Nat := .const 0 [.zero]
def vfValTy : Expr Nat := .const 0 [lvl00]
def vfVal : Expr Nat := .const 1 []
def vfDelta : Expr Nat := .const 2 []
def vfLam : Expr Nat := .lam vfTy (.bvar 0)
def vfApp : Expr Nat := .app vfLam vfDelta
def vfLet : Expr Nat := .letE vfTy vfDelta (.bvar 0)

theorem convFlipEnv_closed : EnvClosed convFlipEnv := by
  intro r m hm
  match r, hm with
  | 0, hm => cases hm; exact ctl_member_closed _ rfl (fun _ hb => nomatch hb)
  | 1, hm => cases hm; exact ctl_member_closed _ rfl (fun _ hb => nomatch hb)
  | 2, hm =>
      cases hm
      exact ctl_member_closed _ rfl (fun b hb => by
        cases hb
        rfl)
  | _ + 3, hm => exact Option.noConfusion hm

theorem vfVal_ty : inferT convFlipEnv 0 [] vfVal = some vfValTy := rfl
theorem vfTy_infer : inferT convFlipEnv 0 [] vfTy = some (.sort .zero) := rfl
theorem vfValTy_infer : inferT convFlipEnv 0 [] vfValTy = some (.sort lvl00) := rfl

def vfKTy : HasTyT convFlipEnv 0 [] vfVal vfValTy :=
  hasTyT_of_inferT vfVal_ty

def vfIConv : ConvT convFlipEnv 0 [] vfValTy vfTy (.sort lvl00) :=
  .consts [] 0 [lvl00] [.zero] vfI rfl rfl rfl rfl ⟨lvl00_eqN, True.intro⟩

def vfCBodyTy : HasTyT convFlipEnv 0 [] vfVal vfTy :=
  .conv [] vfVal vfValTy vfTy lvl00 vfKTy vfIConv

theorem convFlipEnv_wf : EnvWf convFlipEnv := by
  refine ⟨convFlipEnv_closed, ?_⟩
  intro r m hm
  match r, hm with
  | 0, hm =>
      cases hm
      exact ⟨⟨.succ (.param 0), ⟨hasTyT_of_inferT rfl⟩⟩, fun _ hb => nomatch hb⟩
  | 1, hm =>
      cases hm
      exact ⟨⟨lvl00, ⟨hasTyT_of_inferT rfl⟩⟩, fun _ hb => nomatch hb⟩
  | 2, hm =>
      cases hm
      refine ⟨⟨.zero, ⟨hasTyT_of_inferT rfl⟩⟩, fun b hb => ?_⟩
      cases hb
      exact ⟨vfCBodyTy⟩
  | _ + 3, hm => exact Option.noConfusion hm

theorem vfBodies : BodiesTyped convFlipEnv 0 := by
  intro r m b ls hm _ hb hlen _
  match r, hm with
  | 0, hm => cases hm; cases hb
  | 1, hm => cases hm; cases hb
  | 2, hm =>
      cases hm
      cases hb
      cases ls with
      | nil => exact ⟨vfCBodyTy⟩
      | cons _ _ => exact Nat.noConfusion hlen
  | _ + 3, hm => exact Option.noConfusion hm

theorem vfData : DataTy convFlipEnv vfTy :=
  ⟨0, [.zero], [], vfI, rfl, rfl, rfl⟩

theorem vfDelta_tb : transparentBody convFlipEnv 2 [] = some vfVal := rfl
theorem vfDelta_norm : norm convFlipEnv 3 vfDelta = some vfVal := rfl
theorem vfApp_norm : norm convFlipEnv 4 vfApp = some vfVal := rfl
theorem vfLet_norm : norm convFlipEnv 4 vfLet = some vfVal := rfl
theorem vfVal_scm : scmValOf convFlipEnv 1 vfVal = some (.inj 1 (.list [])) := rfl
theorem vfVal_spine : relevantSpine convFlipEnv 0 1 vfVal = true := rfl
theorem vfVal_rel : irrelevant convFlipEnv 0 [] vfVal = false := rfl
theorem vfVal_vinfer : (inferT convFlipEnv 0 [] vfVal).isSome = true := rfl
theorem vfFits : valFits 1 (sumL 2 .i64) (.inj 1 (.list [])) = true := by decide

theorem vfDelta_infer : inferT convFlipEnv 0 [] vfDelta = some vfTy := rfl
theorem vfApp_infer : inferT convFlipEnv 0 [] vfApp = some vfTy := rfl
theorem vfLet_infer : inferT convFlipEnv 0 [] vfLet = some vfTy := rfl

theorem vfDelta_irr : irrelevant convFlipEnv 0 [] vfDelta = true :=
  irrelevant_data_tt convFlipEnv 0 vfDelta vfTy (.sort .zero)
    vfDelta_infer vfData vfTy_infer rfl

theorem vfApp_irr : irrelevant convFlipEnv 0 [] vfApp = true :=
  irrelevant_data_tt convFlipEnv 0 vfApp vfTy (.sort .zero)
    vfApp_infer vfData vfTy_infer rfl

theorem vfLet_irr : irrelevant convFlipEnv 0 [] vfLet = true :=
  irrelevant_data_tt convFlipEnv 0 vfLet vfTy (.sort .zero)
    vfLet_infer vfData vfTy_infer rfl

theorem vfDelta_er : Erasable convFlipEnv 0 vfDelta :=
  ⟨1, .box, erase_box_of_irrelevant convFlipEnv 0 0 [] vfDelta vfDelta_irr
      (fun k => const_ne_lit 2 k [])⟩

theorem vfApp_er : Erasable convFlipEnv 0 vfApp :=
  ⟨1, .box, erase_box_of_irrelevant convFlipEnv 0 0 [] vfApp vfApp_irr
      (fun k => app_ne_lit vfLam vfDelta k)⟩

theorem vfLet_er : Erasable convFlipEnv 0 vfLet :=
  ⟨1, .box, erase_box_of_irrelevant convFlipEnv 0 0 [] vfLet vfLet_irr
      (fun k => letE_ne_lit vfTy vfDelta (.bvar 0) k)⟩

def AdeqAppWfLoose {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) : Prop :=
  ∀ E n f a, EnvWf E → GoodLoose progs E n (.app f a)

def AdeqLetEWfLoose {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) : Prop :=
  ∀ E n A v b, EnvWf E → GoodLoose progs E n (.letE A v b)

def AdeqConstDeltaWfLoose {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) : Prop :=
  ∀ E n r ls b, EnvWf E →
    transparentBody E r ls = some b → GoodLoose progs E n (.const r ls)

theorem not_adeqAppWfLoose {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) :
    ¬ AdeqAppWfLoose progs := by
  intro h
  obtain ⟨F₀, hF⟩ := h convFlipEnv 0 vfLam vfDelta convFlipEnv_wf 4 1 vfTy vfVal
      (sumL 2 .i64) (.inj 1 (.list [])) vfBodies vfApp_infer vfData
      vfApp_norm vfVal_scm vfVal_spine vfVal_rel vfFits
      vfVal_vinfer vfApp_er
  obtain ⟨lf, he⟩ := hF F₀ (Nat.le_refl _)
  exact eval_irrelevant_ne progs convFlipEnv 0 (sumL 2 .i64) vfApp _
    vfApp_irr (fun k => app_ne_lit vfLam vfDelta k) F₀ lf he

theorem not_adeqLetEWfLoose {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) :
    ¬ AdeqLetEWfLoose progs := by
  intro h
  obtain ⟨F₀, hF⟩ := h convFlipEnv 0 vfTy vfDelta (.bvar 0) convFlipEnv_wf 4 1 vfTy
      vfVal (sumL 2 .i64) (.inj 1 (.list [])) vfBodies vfLet_infer vfData
      vfLet_norm vfVal_scm vfVal_spine vfVal_rel vfFits
      vfVal_vinfer vfLet_er
  obtain ⟨lf, he⟩ := hF F₀ (Nat.le_refl _)
  exact eval_irrelevant_ne progs convFlipEnv 0 (sumL 2 .i64) vfLet _
    vfLet_irr (fun k => letE_ne_lit vfTy vfDelta (.bvar 0) k) F₀ lf he

theorem not_adeqConstDeltaWfLoose {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S) :
    ¬ AdeqConstDeltaWfLoose progs := by
  intro h
  obtain ⟨F₀, hF⟩ := h convFlipEnv 0 2 [] vfVal convFlipEnv_wf vfDelta_tb 3 1 vfTy
      vfVal (sumL 2 .i64) (.inj 1 (.list [])) vfBodies vfDelta_infer vfData
      vfDelta_norm vfVal_scm vfVal_spine vfVal_rel vfFits
      vfVal_vinfer vfDelta_er
  obtain ⟨lf, he⟩ := hF F₀ (Nat.le_refl _)
  exact eval_irrelevant_ne progs convFlipEnv 0 (sumL 2 .i64) vfDelta _
    vfDelta_irr (fun k => const_ne_lit 2 k []) F₀ lf he

theorem vfVal_infer_ne : inferT convFlipEnv 0 [] vfVal ≠ some vfTy := by decide
theorem flipWeird_infer_ne : inferT flipEnv 0 [] flipWeird ≠ some flipTrue := by decide
theorem cfVal_infer_ne : inferT closedFlipEnv 0 [] cfVal ≠ some cfTy := by decide

/-! ### Syntactic type-agreement consequences under `Good`

With `inferT E n [] e = some T`, `inferT E n [] v = some T`, and
`irrelevant E n [] v = false` in `Good`, `irrelevant E n [] e = false` holds
for every construct without an external relevance hypothesis on `e`. -/

theorem irrelevant_false_of_same_type {E : ResolvedEnv} {n : Nat} {Γ : LCtx}
    {e v T : Expr Nat}
    (he : inferT E n Γ e = some T) (hv : inferT E n Γ v = some T)
    (hirr : irrelevant E n Γ v = false) :
    irrelevant E n Γ e = false := by
  rw [irrelevant_of_same_type he hv]
  exact hirr

theorem good_const_delta_of_body_eval {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n r : Nat) (ls : List Level) (b : Expr Nat)
    (hb : transparentBody E r ls = some b)
    (hbody : ∀ (lf fv : Nat) (T v : Expr Nat) (t : BootTy) (w : Val),
      BodiesTyped E n →
      inferT E n [] (.const r ls) = some T →
      DataTy E T →
      norm E lf b = some v →
      scmValOf E fv v = some w →
      relevantSpine E n fv v = true →
      irrelevant E n [] v = false →
      valFits fv t w = true →
      inferT E n [] v = some T →
      ∃ F lf',
        Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf' []
          (lowerF E n F (S := S) t b) = some w) :
    Good progs E n (.const r ls) := by
  refine good_of_exists progs E n (.const r ls) ?_
  intro lf fv T v t w hB hi hD hn hs hrel hirrv hf hvinf _
  have hirr : irrelevant E n [] (.const r ls) = false :=
    irrelevant_false_of_same_type hi hvinf hirrv
  cases lf with
  | zero =>
      rw [norm_fuel0] at hn
      exact Option.noConfusion hn
  | succ lf1 =>
      cases lf1 with
      | zero =>
          unfold norm at hn
          rw [whnfFuel_fuel0] at hn
          exact Option.noConfusion hn
      | succ k =>
          have hn' : norm E (k + 2) (foldApps (.const r ls) []) = some v := hn
          have hbn : norm E (k + 2) (foldApps b []) = some v :=
            norm_delta_spine_eq E k r ls b [] v hb hn'
          have hbb : norm E (k + 2) b = some v := hbn
          obtain ⟨F, lfe, he⟩ :=
            hbody (k + 2) fv T v t w hB hi hD hbb hs hrel hirrv hf hvinf
          exact ⟨F + 1, lfe,
            lowerF_const_delta_eval progs E n F r lfe ls b t w hirr hb he⟩

theorem good_const_delta_lit_any {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n r k : Nat) (ls : List Level)
    (hb : transparentBody E r ls = some (.lit k)) :
    Good progs E n (.const r ls) := by
  intro lf fv T v t w hB hi hD hn hs hrel hirrv hf hvinf her
  exact good_const_delta_lit progs E n r k ls hb
    (irrelevant_false_of_same_type hi hvinf hirrv)
    lf fv T v t w hB hi hD hn hs hrel hirrv hf hvinf her

theorem good_const_delta_ctor_any {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n r c : Nat) (ls lsc : List Level)
    (hb : transparentBody E r ls = some (.const c lsc))
    (hnone : transparentBody E c lsc = none) :
    Good progs E n (.const r ls) := by
  intro lf fv T v t w hB hi hD hn hs hrel hirrv hf hvinf her
  exact good_const_delta_ctor progs E n r c ls lsc hb hnone
    (irrelevant_false_of_same_type hi hvinf hirrv)
    lf fv T v t w hB hi hD hn hs hrel hirrv hf hvinf her

theorem good_let_lit_any {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n kv nlit : Nat) (A : Expr Nat) :
    Good progs E n (.letE A (.lit kv) (.lit nlit)) := by
  intro lf fv T v t w hB hi hD hn hs hrel hirrv hf hvinf her
  exact good_let_lit progs E n kv nlit A
    (irrelevant_false_of_same_type hi hvinf hirrv)
    lf fv T v t w hB hi hD hn hs hrel hirrv hf hvinf her

theorem good_let_discard_sort_any {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n kbody : Nat) (A : Expr Nat) (l : Level) :
    Good progs E n (.letE A (.sort l) (.lit kbody)) := by
  intro lf fv T v t w hB hi hD hn hs hrel hirrv hf hvinf her
  exact good_let_discard_sort progs E n kbody A l
    (irrelevant_false_of_same_type hi hvinf hirrv)
    lf fv T v t w hB hi hD hn hs hrel hirrv hf hvinf her

theorem good_let_discard_pi_any {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n kbody : Nat) (A B C : Expr Nat) :
    Good progs E n (.letE A (.pi B C) (.lit kbody)) := by
  intro lf fv T v t w hB hi hD hn hs hrel hirrv hf hvinf her
  exact good_let_discard_pi progs E n kbody A B C
    (irrelevant_false_of_same_type hi hvinf hirrv)
    lf fv T v t w hB hi hD hn hs hrel hirrv hf hvinf her

/-! ### Subterm relevance propagation across application, β, and ζ

When an application `.app f a` is syntactically typed (`inferT E n Γ (.app f a) = some T`)
and relevant (`irrelevant E n Γ (.app f a) = false`, or `isArity T = false`),
its function head `f` is automatically relevant (`irrelevant_fun_false_of_app`),
because `inferT` of a Π-type is always `.sort (.imax u v)` (`isPropSort = false`),
and `isArity (.pi A B) = isArity B` is preserved by `instantiate` (`isArity_instantiate_true`).
Under `EnvClosed E`, a relevant β-redex `.app (.lam A body) arg` also forces
its body `body` to be relevant under `.assumption A` (`irrelevant_body_false_of_beta`),
and a relevant ζ-redex `.letE A val body` forces its body `body` to be relevant
under `.letBinding A val` (`irrelevant_body_false_of_let`), while the bound index
`.bvar 0` under `.assumption A` or `.letBinding A arg` has the same relevance as
`arg` in the empty context (`irrelevant_bvar0_eq_arg`). This eliminates all
external `irrelevant` hypotheses from the β, ζ, and constructor adequacy transports
and slices (`good_beta_id_of_eval_wf`, `good_let_id_of_eval_wf`,
`good_app_ctor_of_eval_any`, `good_beta_ctor_of_eval_wf`, `good_let_bvar_wf`,
`good_beta_lit_wf`, `good_beta_discard_lit_any`, `good_beta_discard_sort_any`,
`good_beta_discard_pi_any`, `good_app_ctor_lit_any`,
`good_const_delta_app_lit_any`, `good_beta_ctor_lit_wf`). -/

theorem isArity_instantiate_true :
    ∀ (B : Expr Nat) (idx : Nat) (a : Expr Nat),
      isArity B = true → isArity (instantiate idx a B) = true
  | .sort _, _, _, _ => rfl
  | .pi _ C, idx, a, h => isArity_instantiate_true C (idx + 1) (lift 0 1 a) h
  | .bvar _, _, _, h => Bool.noConfusion h
  | .const _ _, _, _, h => Bool.noConfusion h
  | .app _ _, _, _, h => Bool.noConfusion h
  | .lam _ _, _, _, h => Bool.noConfusion h
  | .letE _ _ _, _, _, h => Bool.noConfusion h
  | .lit _, _, _, h => Bool.noConfusion h

theorem isArity_false_of_instantiate0 {B a T : Expr Nat}
    (hT : instantiate0 a B = T) (hAr : isArity T = false) :
    isArity B = false := by
  cases hB : isArity B with
  | false => rfl
  | true =>
      have h1 := isArity_instantiate_true B 0 a hB
      rw [← instantiate0, hT, hAr] at h1
      exact Bool.noConfusion h1

theorem inferT_pi_not_propSort {E : ResolvedEnv} {n : Nat} {Γ : LCtx} {A B U : Expr Nat}
    (h : inferT E n Γ (.pi A B) = some U) : isPropSort U = false := by
  obtain ⟨u, v, _, _, hU⟩ := inferT_pi_some.mp h
  subst hU
  rfl

theorem irrelevant_of_inferT_false {E : ResolvedEnv} {n : Nat} {Γ : LCtx} {e T : Expr Nat}
    (hi : inferT E n Γ e = some T) (hirr : irrelevant E n Γ e = false) :
    isArity T = false ∧
      (∀ U, inferT E n Γ T = some U → isPropSort U = false) := by
  simp only [irrelevant, hi, Bool.or_eq_false_iff] at hirr
  refine ⟨hirr.1, fun U hU => ?_⟩
  have h2 := hirr.2
  rw [hU] at h2
  exact h2

theorem irrelevant_fun_false_of_app {E : ResolvedEnv} {n : Nat} {Γ : LCtx}
    {f a T : Expr Nat}
    (hi : inferT E n Γ (.app f a) = some T)
    (hAr : isArity T = false) :
    irrelevant E n Γ f = false := by
  obtain ⟨A, B, hf, _, hT⟩ := inferT_app_some.mp hi
  have hArB : isArity B = false := isArity_false_of_instantiate0 hT.symm hAr
  have hArPi : isArity (.pi A B) = false := hArB
  simp only [irrelevant, hf, hArPi, Bool.false_or]
  cases hpi : inferT E n Γ (.pi A B) with
  | none => rfl
  | some U => exact inferT_pi_not_propSort hpi

theorem irrelevant_fun_false_of_app_irr {E : ResolvedEnv} {n : Nat} {Γ : LCtx}
    {f a T : Expr Nat}
    (hi : inferT E n Γ (.app f a) = some T)
    (hirr : irrelevant E n Γ (.app f a) = false) :
    irrelevant E n Γ f = false :=
  irrelevant_fun_false_of_app hi (irrelevant_of_inferT_false hi hirr).1

theorem isPropSort_eq_true {U : Expr Nat} (h : isPropSort U = true) :
    U = .sort .zero := by
  cases U with
  | sort l =>
      cases l with
      | zero => rfl
      | succ _ => exact Bool.noConfusion h
      | max _ _ => exact Bool.noConfusion h
      | imax _ _ => exact Bool.noConfusion h
      | param _ => exact Bool.noConfusion h
  | bvar _ => exact Bool.noConfusion h
  | const _ _ => exact Bool.noConfusion h
  | app _ _ => exact Bool.noConfusion h
  | lam _ _ => exact Bool.noConfusion h
  | pi _ _ => exact Bool.noConfusion h
  | letE _ _ _ => exact Bool.noConfusion h
  | lit _ => exact Bool.noConfusion h

theorem irrelevant_body_false_of_beta {E : ResolvedEnv} {n : Nat} (hE : EnvClosed E)
    {A body arg T : Expr Nat}
    (hi : inferT E n [] (.app (.lam A body) arg) = some T)
    (hirr : irrelevant E n [] (.app (.lam A body) arg) = false) :
    irrelevant E n (.assumption A :: []) body = false := by
  obtain ⟨hArT, hPropT⟩ := irrelevant_of_inferT_false hi hirr
  obtain ⟨A', B, hlam, harg, hT⟩ := inferT_app_some.mp hi
  obtain ⟨u, B', hA, hbody, hpi⟩ := inferT_lam_some.mp hlam
  injection hpi with hAA hBB
  rw [hAA] at harg
  rw [← hBB] at hbody
  have hArB : isArity B = false := isArity_false_of_instantiate0 hT.symm hArT
  unfold irrelevant
  rw [hbody]
  dsimp only
  rw [hArB, Bool.false_or]
  cases hBU : inferT E n (.assumption A :: []) B with
  | none => rfl
  | some U =>
      dsimp only
      cases hU : isPropSort U with
      | false => rfl
      | true =>
          have hU0 : U = .sort .zero := isPropSort_eq_true hU
          subst hU0
          have hinst := inferT_instantiate hE arg A harg [] B (.sort .zero) hBU
          simp only [List.nil_append, List.length_nil, substPrefix] at hinst
          rw [lift_zero_amount arg 0] at hinst
          have hTU : inferT E n [] T = some (.sort .zero) := by
            rw [hT]
            simpa [instantiate0] using hinst
          exact hPropT (.sort .zero) hTU

theorem irrelevant_ctx_eq {E : ResolvedEnv} {n : Nat} (e : Expr Nat) {Γ1 Γ2 : LCtx}
    (h : ∀ i, lookupType Γ1 i = lookupType Γ2 i) :
    irrelevant E n Γ1 e = irrelevant E n Γ2 e := by
  unfold irrelevant
  rw [inferT_ctx_eq (E := E) (n := n) e h]
  cases inferT E n Γ2 e with
  | none => rfl
  | some T =>
      dsimp only
      rw [inferT_ctx_eq (E := E) (n := n) T h]

theorem irrelevant_body_false_of_let {E : ResolvedEnv} {n : Nat} (hE : EnvClosed E)
    {A val body T : Expr Nat}
    (hi : inferT E n [] (.letE A val body) = some T)
    (hirr : irrelevant E n [] (.letE A val body) = false) :
    irrelevant E n (.letBinding A val :: []) body = false := by
  obtain ⟨u, B, hA, hval, hbody, hT⟩ := inferT_letE_some.mp hi
  have hbody' : inferT E n (.assumption A :: []) body = some B := by
    rw [← inferT_ctx_eq (E := E) (n := n) body (lookupType_let_eq_assumption A val [])]
    exact hbody
  have happ : inferT E n [] (.app (.lam A body) val) = some T :=
    inferT_app_some.mpr ⟨A, B, inferT_lam_some.mpr ⟨u, B, hA, hbody', rfl⟩, hval, hT⟩
  have hirrApp : irrelevant E n [] (.app (.lam A body) val) = false := by
    rw [irrelevant_of_same_type happ hi]
    exact hirr
  rw [irrelevant_ctx_eq body (lookupType_let_eq_assumption A val [])]
  exact irrelevant_body_false_of_beta hE happ hirrApp

theorem isArity_lift :
    ∀ (e : Expr Nat) (c k : Nat), isArity (lift c k e) = isArity e
  | .sort _, _, _ => rfl
  | .pi _ B, c, k => isArity_lift B (c + 1) k
  | .bvar i, c, k => by
      simp only [lift]
      split <;> rfl
  | .const _ _, _, _ => rfl
  | .app _ _, _, _ => rfl
  | .lam _ _, _, _ => rfl
  | .letE _ _ _, _, _ => rfl
  | .lit _, _, _ => rfl

theorem irrelevant_bvar0_eq_arg {E : ResolvedEnv} {n : Nat} (hE : EnvClosed E)
    {A arg : Expr Nat} {u : Level}
    (hA : inferT E n [] A = some (.sort u))
    (harg : inferT E n [] arg = some A) :
    irrelevant E n (.assumption A :: []) (.bvar 0) = irrelevant E n [] arg ∧
      irrelevant E n (.letBinding A arg :: []) (.bvar 0) = irrelevant E n [] arg := by
  have hb0 : inferT E n (.assumption A :: []) (.bvar 0) = some (lift 0 1 A) := rfl
  have hw := inferT_weaken hE [] [.assumption A] [] A (.sort u) hA
  simp only [liftPrefix, List.nil_append, List.append_nil, List.length_cons,
    List.length_nil, lift] at hw
  have h1 : irrelevant E n (.assumption A :: []) (.bvar 0) = irrelevant E n [] arg := by
    unfold irrelevant
    rw [hb0, harg]
    dsimp only
    rw [hw, hA, isArity_lift A 0 1]
  refine ⟨h1, ?_⟩
  rw [irrelevant_ctx_eq (.bvar 0) (lookupType_let_eq_assumption A arg [])]
  exact h1

theorem closedAt_of_lift_one :
    ∀ (e : Expr Nat) (c : Nat),
      closedAt c (lift c 1 e) = true → closedAt c e = true
  | .bvar i, c, h => by
      by_cases hle : c ≤ i
      · simp only [lift, if_pos hle, closedAt, decide_eq_true_eq] at h
        exact False.elim (Nat.not_le.mpr (Nat.lt_of_succ_lt h) hle)
      · simp only [closedAt, decide_eq_true_eq]
        exact Nat.lt_of_not_le hle
  | .sort _, _, _ => rfl
  | .const _ _, _, _ => rfl
  | .lit _, _, _ => rfl
  | .app f x, c, h => by
      simp only [lift, closedAt, Bool.and_eq_true] at h ⊢
      exact ⟨closedAt_of_lift_one f c h.1, closedAt_of_lift_one x c h.2⟩
  | .lam a b, c, h => by
      simp only [lift, closedAt, Bool.and_eq_true] at h ⊢
      exact ⟨closedAt_of_lift_one a c h.1, closedAt_of_lift_one b (c + 1) h.2⟩
  | .pi a b, c, h => by
      simp only [lift, closedAt, Bool.and_eq_true] at h ⊢
      exact ⟨closedAt_of_lift_one a c h.1, closedAt_of_lift_one b (c + 1) h.2⟩
  | .letE a v b, c, h => by
      simp only [lift, closedAt, Bool.and_eq_true] at h ⊢
      exact ⟨⟨closedAt_of_lift_one a c h.1.1, closedAt_of_lift_one v c h.1.2⟩,
        closedAt_of_lift_one b (c + 1) h.2⟩

theorem irrelevant_bvar0_false_of_beta_ctor {E : ResolvedEnv} {n c : Nat}
    {lsc : List Level} {A arg varg T : Expr Nat} (hE : EnvClosed E)
    (hi : inferT E n [] (.app (.lam A (.app (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0))) arg) = some T)
    (hvinf : inferT E n [] (.app (.const c lsc) varg) = some T)
    (hirrF : irrelevant E n [] varg = false) :
    irrelevant E n (.assumption A :: []) (.bvar 0) = false := by
  obtain ⟨A', B, hlam, harg_ty, _⟩ := inferT_app_some.mp hi
  obtain ⟨u, B', hA, hbody, hpi⟩ := inferT_lam_some.mp hlam
  injection hpi with hAA _
  rw [hAA] at harg_ty
  obtain ⟨Ac, Bc, hc_assump, hb0, _⟩ := inferT_app_some.mp hbody
  have hb0_eq : inferT E n (.assumption A :: []) (.bvar 0) = some (lift 0 1 A) := rfl
  rw [hb0_eq] at hb0
  have hAc : Ac = lift 0 1 A := (Option.some.inj hb0).symm
  obtain ⟨Av, Bv, hc_nil, hvarg_ty, _⟩ := inferT_app_some.mp hvinf
  have hcind := inferT_const_indep (E := E) (n := n) (.assumption A :: []) [] c lsc
  rw [hc_assump, hc_nil] at hcind
  injection (Option.some.inj hcind) with hAv _
  have hAv_eq : Av = lift 0 1 A := hAv.symm.trans hAc
  obtain ⟨m, hm, _, _, hTy⟩ := inferT_const_some.mp hc_nil
  have hclPi : closedAt 0 (.pi Av Bv) = true := by
    rw [hTy, closedAt_instantiateLevels]
    exact closedAt_member (envSubst_of_envClosed hE) hm 0
  simp only [closedAt, Bool.and_eq_true] at hclPi
  have hclLift : closedAt 0 (lift 0 1 A) = true := hAv_eq ▸ hclPi.1
  have hclA : closedAt 0 A = true := closedAt_of_lift_one A 0 hclLift
  have hAvA : Av = A := hAv_eq.trans (lift_id_of_closedAt A 0 1 hclA)
  rw [hAvA] at hvarg_ty
  rw [(irrelevant_bvar0_eq_arg hE hA harg_ty).1]
  rw [irrelevant_of_same_type harg_ty hvarg_ty]
  exact hirrF

theorem good_beta_id_of_eval_wf {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n : Nat) (A arg : Expr Nat) (hE : EnvClosed E)
    (harg : ∀ (lf fv : Nat) (v : Expr Nat) (t : BootTy) (w : Val),
      norm E lf arg = some v →
      scmValOf E fv v = some w →
      relevantSpine E n fv v = true →
      irrelevant E n [] v = false →
      valFits fv t w = true →
      (inferT E n [] v).isSome = true →
      ∃ F lf',
        Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf' []
          (lowerF E n F (S := S) t arg) = some w) :
    Good progs E n (.app (.lam A (.bvar 0)) arg) := by
  intro lf fv T v t w hB hi hD hn hs hrel hirrv hf hvinf her
  have hirr : irrelevant E n [] (.app (.lam A (.bvar 0)) arg) = false :=
    irrelevant_false_of_same_type hi hvinf hirrv
  have hirrL : irrelevant E n [] (.lam A (.bvar 0)) = false :=
    irrelevant_fun_false_of_app_irr hi hirr
  have hirrB : irrelevant E n (.assumption A :: []) (.bvar 0) = false :=
    irrelevant_body_false_of_beta hE hi hirr
  exact good_beta_id_of_eval progs E n A arg hirr hirrL hirrB harg
    lf fv T v t w hB hi hD hn hs hrel hirrv hf hvinf her

theorem good_let_id_of_eval_wf {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n : Nat) (A bound : Expr Nat) (hE : EnvClosed E)
    (hbound : ∀ (lf fv : Nat) (v : Expr Nat) (t : BootTy) (w : Val),
      norm E lf bound = some v →
      scmValOf E fv v = some w →
      relevantSpine E n fv v = true →
      irrelevant E n [] v = false →
      valFits fv t w = true →
      (inferT E n [] v).isSome = true →
      ∃ F lf',
        Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf' []
          (lowerF E n F (S := S) t bound) = some w) :
    Good progs E n (.letE A bound (.bvar 0)) := by
  intro lf fv T v t w hB hi hD hn hs hrel hirrv hf hvinf her
  have hirr : irrelevant E n [] (.letE A bound (.bvar 0)) = false :=
    irrelevant_false_of_same_type hi hvinf hirrv
  have hirrB : irrelevant E n (.letBinding A bound :: []) (.bvar 0) = false :=
    irrelevant_body_false_of_let hE hi hirr
  exact good_let_id_of_eval progs E n A bound hirr hirrB hbound
    lf fv T v t w hB hi hD hn hs hrel hirrv hf hvinf her

theorem good_app_ctor_of_eval_any {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n c : Nat) (lsc : List Level) (arg : Expr Nat)
    (hnone : transparentBody E c lsc = none)
    (harg : ∀ (lf fv : Nat) (v : Expr Nat) (t : BootTy) (w : Val),
      norm E lf arg = some v →
      scmValOf E fv v = some w →
      relevantSpine E n fv v = true →
      irrelevant E n [] v = false →
      valFits fv t w = true →
      ∃ F lf',
        Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf' []
          (lowerF E n F (S := S) t arg) = some w) :
    Good progs E n (.app (.const c lsc) arg) := by
  intro lf fv T v t w hB hi hD hn hs hrel hirrv hf hvinf her
  have hirr : irrelevant E n [] (.app (.const c lsc) arg) = false :=
    irrelevant_false_of_same_type hi hvinf hirrv
  have hirrC : irrelevant E n [] (.const c lsc) = false :=
    irrelevant_fun_false_of_app_irr hi hirr
  exact good_app_ctor_of_eval progs E n c lsc arg hnone hirr hirrC harg
    lf fv T v t w hB hi hD hn hs hrel hirrv hf hvinf her

theorem good_beta_ctor_of_eval_wf {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n c : Nat) (lsc : List Level) (A arg : Expr Nat)
    (hE : EnvClosed E)
    (hnone : transparentBody E c lsc = none)
    (harg : ∀ (lf fv : Nat) (v : Expr Nat) (t : BootTy) (w : Val),
      norm E lf arg = some v →
      scmValOf E fv v = some w →
      relevantSpine E n fv v = true →
      irrelevant E n [] v = false →
      valFits fv t w = true →
      ∃ F lf',
        Residua.Bootstrap.Semantics.eval lawsA progs lf' []
          (lowerF E n F (S := S) t arg) = some w) :
    Good progs E n (.app (.lam A (.app (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0))) arg) := by
  intro lf fv T v t w hB hi hD hn hs hrel hirrv hf hvinf her
  have hirr : irrelevant E n []
      (.app (.lam A (.app (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0))) arg) = false :=
    irrelevant_false_of_same_type hi hvinf hirrv
  have hirrL : irrelevant E n [] (.lam A (.app (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0))) = false :=
    irrelevant_fun_false_of_app_irr hi hirr
  have hirrBody : irrelevant E n (.assumption A :: [])
      (.app (.const c lsc) (.bvar 0)) = false :=
    irrelevant_body_false_of_beta hE hi hirr
  obtain ⟨_, _, hlam, _, _⟩ := inferT_app_some.mp hi
  obtain ⟨_, B', _, hbody, _⟩ := inferT_lam_some.mp hlam
  have hirrC : irrelevant E n (.assumption A :: []) (.const c lsc) = false :=
    irrelevant_fun_false_of_app_irr hbody hirrBody
  obtain ⟨_, varg, _, _, hv⟩ :=
    norm_beta_ctor_arg_of_norm E lf c lsc A arg v hnone hn
  have hvinf' : inferT E n [] (.app (.const c lsc) varg) = some T := hv ▸ hvinf
  have hrel' : relevantSpine E n fv (.app (.const c lsc) varg) = true := hv ▸ hrel
  cases fv with
  | zero =>
      simp only [scmValOf] at hs
      exact Option.noConfusion hs
  | succ m =>
      have hrel1 :
          (!irrelevant E n [] varg &&
            relevantSpine E n m varg) = true := by
        simpa [relevantSpine, appsSpine, List.nil_append, List.all_cons,
          List.all_nil, Bool.and_true] using hrel'
      cases hirrF : irrelevant E n [] varg with
      | true =>
          simp only [hirrF, Bool.not_true, Bool.false_and] at hrel1
          exact Bool.noConfusion hrel1
      | false =>
          have hirrB : irrelevant E n (.assumption A :: []) (.bvar 0) = false :=
            irrelevant_bvar0_false_of_beta_ctor hE hi hvinf' hirrF
          exact good_beta_ctor_of_eval progs E n c lsc A arg hnone
            hirr hirrL hirrBody hirrC hirrB harg
            lf (m + 1) T v t w hB hi hD hn hs hrel hirrv hf hvinf her

theorem good_let_bvar_wf {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n kv : Nat) (A : Expr Nat) (hE : EnvClosed E) :
    Good progs E n (.letE A (.lit kv) (.bvar 0)) := by
  intro lf fv T v t w hB hi hD hn hs hrel hirrv hf hvinf her
  have hirr : irrelevant E n [] (.letE A (.lit kv) (.bvar 0)) = false :=
    irrelevant_false_of_same_type hi hvinf hirrv
  have hirrB : irrelevant E n (.letBinding A (.lit kv) :: []) (.bvar 0) = false :=
    irrelevant_body_false_of_let hE hi hirr
  exact good_let_bvar progs E n kv A hirr hirrB
    lf fv T v t w hB hi hD hn hs hrel hirrv hf hvinf her

theorem good_beta_lit_wf {S : SigTable} (progs : Programs S S)
    (E : ResolvedEnv) (n kv : Nat) (A : Expr Nat) (hE : EnvClosed E) :
    Good progs E n (.app (.lam A (.bvar 0)) (.lit kv)) := by
  intro lf fv T v t w hB hi hD hn hs hrel hirrv hf hvinf her
  have hirr : irrelevant E n [] (.app (.lam A (.bvar 0)) (.lit kv)) = false :=
    irrelevant_false_of_same_type hi hvinf hirrv
  have hirrL : irrelevant E n [] (.lam A (.bvar 0)) = false :=
    irrelevant_fun_false_of_app_irr hi hirr
  have hirrB : irrelevant E n (.assumption A :: []) (.bvar 0) = false :=
    irrelevant_body_false_of_beta hE hi hirr
  exact good_beta_lit progs E n kv A hirr hirrL hirrB
    lf fv T v t w hB hi hD hn hs hrel hirrv hf hvinf her

